				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container="">
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
					</div>
					<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"></div></div>
					
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-subjectpageheader">
</div><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha15" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><meta typeof="mw:Includes/NoInclude" id="mwAg"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Short description&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Short_description&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Overview of how Japanese verbs conjugate&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">Overview of how Japanese verbs conjugate</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_is_different_from_Wikidata"></span>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Very long&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Very_long&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 2025&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></span><table class="box-Very_long plainlinks metadata ambox ambox-style ambox-very_long" role="presentation" about="#mwt2"><tbody><tr><td class="mbox-image"><div class="mbox-image-div"><span typeof="mw:File"><span><img alt="" resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Edit-clear.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f2/Edit-clear.svg/40px-Edit-clear.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="48" data-file-height="48" data-file-type="drawing" height="40" width="40" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f2/Edit-clear.svg/120px-Edit-clear.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element"></span></span></div></td><td class="mbox-text"><div class="mbox-text-span">This article <b>may be <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Article_size" title="Wikipedia:Article size">too long</a> to read and navigate comfortably</b>.<span class="hide-when-compact"> Consider <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Splitting" title="Wikipedia:Splitting">splitting</a> content into sub-articles, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Summary_style" title="Wikipedia:Summary style">condensing</a> it, or adding <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Section#Subsections" title="Help:Section">subheadings</a>. Please discuss this issue on the article's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Japanese_conjugation" title="Talk:Japanese conjugation">talk page</a>.</span>  <span class="date-container"><i>(<span class="date">August 2025</span>)</i></span></div></td></tr></tbody></table><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_that_may_be_too_long_from_August_2025"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_that_may_be_too_long"></span><meta typeof="mw:Includes/NoInclude/End" id="mwBQ">
<p id="mwBg"><span typeof="mw:Nowiki mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt4" id="mwBw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Use dmy dates&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Use_dmy_dates&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 2025&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Use_dmy_dates_from_August_2025" about="#mwt4" id="mwCA">
<b id="mwCQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation" class="mw-selflink selflink" id="mwCg">Japanese conjugation</a></b><!--this should be linked, as this section is transcluded on other pages-->, like the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammatical_conjugation" title="Grammatical conjugation" id="mwCw">conjugation</a> of verbs of many other languages, allows verbs to be <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morphology_(linguistics)" title="Morphology (linguistics)" id="mwDA">morphologically</a> modified to change their meaning or grammatical function. In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_language" title="Japanese language" id="mwDQ">Japanese</a>, the beginning of a word (the <i id="mwDg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Word_stem" title="Word stem" id="mwDw">stem</a></i>) is preserved during conjugation, while the ending of the word is altered in some way to change the meaning (this is the <i id="mwEA">inflectional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suffix" title="Suffix" id="mwEQ">suffix</a></i>). Japanese verb conjugations are independent of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammatical_person" title="Grammatical person" id="mwEg">person</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammatical_number" title="Grammatical number" id="mwEw">number</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammatical_gender" title="Grammatical gender" id="mwFA">gender</a> (they do not depend on whether the subject is <i id="mwFQ">I</i>, <i id="mwFg">you</i>, <i id="mwFw">he</i>, <i id="mwGA">she</i>, <i id="mwGQ">we</i>, etc.); the conjugated forms can express meanings such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Affirmation_and_negation" title="Affirmation and negation" id="mwGg">negation</a>, present and past <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammatical_tense" title="Grammatical tense" id="mwGw">tense</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volition_(linguistics)" title="Volition (linguistics)" id="mwHA">volition</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passive_voice" title="Passive voice" id="mwHQ">passive voice</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Causative" title="Causative" id="mwHg">causation</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperative_mood" title="Imperative mood" id="mwHw">imperative</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conditional_mood" title="Conditional mood" id="mwIA">conditional</a> mood, and ability. There are also special forms for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conjunction_(grammar)" title="Conjunction (grammar)" id="mwIQ">conjunction</a> with other verbs, and for combination with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammatical_particle" title="Grammatical particle" id="mwIg">particles</a> for additional meanings.</p>

<p id="mwIw">Japanese verbs have <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agglutination" title="Agglutination" id="mwJA">agglutinating</a> properties: some of the conjugated forms are themselves conjugable verbs (or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_adjectives" title="Japanese adjectives" id="mwJQ"><i id="mwJg">i</i>-adjectives</a>), which can result in several suffixes being strung together in a single verb form to express a combination of meanings.</p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwJw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AMB_Japanese_Verbs.pdf" class="mw-file-description" id="mwKA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AMB_Japanese_Verbs.pdf" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/AMB_Japanese_Verbs.pdf/page1-250px-AMB_Japanese_Verbs.pdf.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="1754" data-file-height="1239" data-file-type="office" height="177" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/AMB_Japanese_Verbs.pdf/page1-500px-AMB_Japanese_Verbs.pdf.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwKQ"></a><figcaption id="mwKg">A revision sheet visually summarizing the conjugations and uses described below</figcaption></figure>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt5" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;TOC limit&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:TOC_limit&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;3&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></span><div class="toclimit-3" about="#mwt5" id="mwLA"><meta property="mw:PageProp/toc"></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwLQ" aria-labelledby="Verb_groups"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Verb_groups">Verb groups</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Verb groups"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt7" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese godan and ichidan verbs&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt7" id="mwLw">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_godan_and_ichidan_verbs" title="Japanese godan and ichidan verbs">Japanese godan and ichidan verbs</a></div>
<span class="skin-invert-image" about="#mwt9" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwMA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Dark mode invert&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Dark_mode_invert&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;image&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;y&quot;},&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[File:Hiragana-Katakana-Gojuuon.jpg|thumb|right|Gojuon Table]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Hiragana-Katakana-Gojuuon.jpg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Hiragana-Katakana-Gojuuon.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Hiragana-Katakana-Gojuuon.jpg/250px-Hiragana-Katakana-Gojuuon.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="699" data-file-height="810" data-file-type="bitmap" height="290" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Hiragana-Katakana-Gojuuon.jpg/500px-Hiragana-Katakana-Gojuuon.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element"></a><figcaption>Gojuon Table</figcaption></figure></span>

<p id="mwMQ">For Japanese verbs, the verb stem remains invariant among all conjugations. However, conjugation patterns vary according to a verb's category. For example, <span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt10" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwMg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo_krt&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;知る&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;shiru&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">知る</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text"> (<span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">shiru</i></span>)</span> and <span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt11" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwMw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo_krt&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;着る&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kiru&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">着る</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text"> (<span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">kiru</i></span>)</span> belong to different verb categories (godan and ichidan, respectively) and therefore follow different conjugation patterns. As such, knowing a verb's category is essential for conjugating Japanese verbs.</p>

<p id="mwNA">Japanese verbs can be allocated into three categories:<sup about="#mwt12" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88&quot;Lesson_3,_Grammar_1:_Verb_Conjugation&quot;_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88\&quot;Lesson 3, Grammar 1: Verb Conjugation\&quot;&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88\&quot;Lesson_3,_Grammar_1:_Verb_Conjugation\&quot;-1&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Banno&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ikeda&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ohno&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Shinagawa&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020a&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;86–88&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Lesson 3, Grammar 1: Verb Conjugation\&quot;&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88&quot;Lesson_3,_Grammar_1:_Verb_Conjugation&quot;-1" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<ol id="mwOQ"><li id="mwOg"><b about="#mwt15" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwOw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''Godan verbs'''&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;五段動詞&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;godan-dōshi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;literally: \&quot;five‑row verbs\&quot;&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">Godan verbs</b><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt15" id="mwPA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">五段動詞</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">, <span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">godan-dōshi</i></span>; literally: "five‑row verbs")</span>, also known as "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_godan_and_ichidan_verbs#Terminology" title="Japanese godan and ichidan verbs" id="mwPQ">pentagrade verbs</a>"</li>
<li id="mwPg"><b about="#mwt16" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwPw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''Ichidan verbs'''&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;一段動詞&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ichidan-dōshi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;literally: \&quot;one‑row verbs\&quot;&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">Ichidan verbs</b><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt16" id="mwQA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">一段動詞</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">, <span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">ichidan-dōshi</i></span>; literally: "one‑row verbs")</span>, also known as "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_godan_and_ichidan_verbs#Terminology" title="Japanese godan and ichidan verbs" id="mwQQ">monograde verbs</a>"</li>
<li id="mwQg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_irregular_verbs" title="Japanese irregular verbs" id="mwQw"><b id="mwRA">Irregular verbs</b></a>, most notably: <span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt17" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwRQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo_krt&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;to do&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;する&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;suru&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">する</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text"> (<span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">suru</i></span>, to do)</span> and <span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt18" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwRg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo_krt&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;to come&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;来る&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kuru&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">来る</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text"> (<span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">kuru</i></span>, to come)</span></li></ol>

<p id="mwRw">Verbs are conjugated from their "<i id="mwSA">dictionary form</i>", where the final <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kana" title="Kana" id="mwSQ">kana</a> is either removed or changed in some way.<sup about="#mwt19" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88&quot;Lesson_3,_Grammar_1:_Verb_Conjugation&quot;_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88\&quot;Lesson 3, Grammar 1: Verb Conjugation\&quot;&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88\&quot;Lesson_3,_Grammar_1:_Verb_Conjugation\&quot;-1&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Banno&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ikeda&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ohno&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Shinagawa&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020a&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;86–88&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Lesson 3, Grammar 1: Verb Conjugation\&quot;&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBannoIkedaOhnoShinagawa2020a86–88&quot;Lesson_3,_Grammar_1:_Verb_Conjugation&quot;-1" id="mwSg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTQ">]</span></span></a></sup> From a technical standpoint, verbs usually require a specific conjugational stem (see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Verb_bases" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwTg">§ Verb bases</a>, below) for any given inflection or suffix. With godan verbs, the conjugational stem can span all five columns of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gojūon#Table" title="Gojūon" id="mwTw">gojūon kana table</a> (hence, the classification as a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_godan_and_ichidan_verbs#Terminology" title="Japanese godan and ichidan verbs" id="mwUA">pentagrade verb</a>). Ichidan verbs are simpler to conjugate: the final kana, which is always <span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt22" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo_krt&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;る&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ru&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">る</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text"> (<span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">ru</i></span>)</span>, is simply removed or replaced with the appropriate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inflectional_suffix" title="Inflectional suffix" class="mw-redirect" id="mwUg">inflectional suffix</a>. This means ichidan verb stems, in themselves, are valid conjugational stems which always end with the same kana (hence, the classification as a monograde verb).</p>

<p id="mwUw">This distinction can be observed by comparing conjugations of the two verb types, within the context of the gojūon table.<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018576–579&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations&quot;_(Verbs)_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018576–579\&quot;Appendix 1 Basic Conjugations\&quot; (Verbs)&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018576–579\&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations\&quot;_(Verbs)-2&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Makino&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tsutsui&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2018&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;576–579&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Appendix 1 Basic Conjugations\&quot; (Verbs)&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018576–579&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations&quot;_(Verbs)-2" id="mwVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwWA">
<tbody id="mwWQ"><tr id="mwWg"><th colspan="2" style="border-bottom:none" id="mwWw">Godan Form</th>
<th id="mwXA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gojūon#Table" title="Gojūon" id="mwXQ">Gojūon table</a><br id="mwXg">'ma' row</th>
<th id="mwXw">Godan Verb<br id="mwYA"><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt26" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwYQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo_krt&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''to read'''&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''読む'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><b>読む</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text"> (<b>to read</b>)</span></th>
<td rowspan="6" id="mwYg"></td>
