<td style="border-left:none;border-right:none" id="mwBT8">[focus particle]</td>
<td style="border-left:none" id="mwBUA"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt422" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBUE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ある&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;aru&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">aru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt422" id="mwBUI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">ある</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<p id="mwBUM">Of focus particles, <i id="mwBUQ">wa</i> ("as for," "speaking of") subdues what comes before it to the background, while throwing focus onto what comes after; and <i id="mwBUU">mo</i> ("even," "too") highlights and raises what comes before it to the foreground.<sup about="#mwt423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004316–322_45-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004316–322&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004316–322-45&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;316–322&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004316–322-45" id="mwBUY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUg">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUk">]</span></span></a></sup> In the following examples, the focused information is underlined in the Japanese original, and put in all caps in the English translations to emulate spoken stress:</p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwBUo">
<tbody id="mwBUs"><tr id="mwBUw">
<th id="mwBU0"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt426" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBU4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;は&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;wa&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">wa</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt426" id="mwBU8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">は</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></th>
<th id="mwBVA"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt427" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBVE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;も&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">mo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt427" id="mwBVI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">も</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></th></tr>
<tr id="mwBVM">
<td id="mwBVQ"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt428" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBVU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;呼びは<u>する</u>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;yobi wa <u>suru</u>&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|I WILL call him}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">yobi wa <u>suru</u></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt428" id="mwBVY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">呼びは<u>する</u></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">I WILL call him</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span></td>
<td id="mwBVc"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt429" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBVg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>呼び</u>もする&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>yobi</u> mo suru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|I'll [even] CALL him}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>yobi</u> mo suru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt429" id="mwBVk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>呼び</u>もする</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">I'll [even] CALL him</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBVo">
<td id="mwBVs"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt430" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBVw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;大きくは<u>ある</u>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ōkiku wa <u>aru</u>&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|it IS big}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ōkiku wa <u>aru</u></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt430" id="mwBV0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">大きくは<u>ある</u></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">it IS big</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span></td>
<td id="mwBV4"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt431" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBV8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>大きく</u>もある&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>ōkiku</u> mo aru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|it's [even] BIG}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>ōkiku</u> mo aru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt431" id="mwBWA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>大きく</u>もある</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">it's [even] BIG</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBWE">
<td id="mwBWI"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt432" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBWM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;本では<u>ある</u>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;hon de wa <u>aru</u>&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|it IS a book}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">hon de wa <u>aru</u></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt432" id="mwBWQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">本では<u>ある</u></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">it IS a book</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span></td>
<td id="mwBWU"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt433" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBWY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>本で</u>もある&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>hon de</u> mo aru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|it's [even] a BOOK}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>hon de</u> mo aru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt433" id="mwBWc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>本で</u>もある</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">it's [even] a BOOK</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<p id="mwBWg"><i id="mwBWk">Wa</i> ("as for," "speaking of"), commonly used to focus on negation,<sup about="#mwt434" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTERubin200436_46-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTERubin200436&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERubin200436-46&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rubin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;36&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTERubin200436-46" id="mwBWo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBWs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWw">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBW0">]</span></span></a></sup> is often taught to foreigners as part of the nucleus, particularly in the negative <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Copulae" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBW4">copula</a>: <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt437" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBW8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;本では<u>ない</u>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Hon de wa <u>nai</u>&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|it's NOT a book}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Hon de wa <u>nai</u></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt437" id="mwBXA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">本では<u>ない</u></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">it's NOT a book</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>. The copular <i id="mwBXE">de wa</i> sequence is used so frequently to focus on negation that it contracts to <i id="mwBXI">ja(a)</i> in speech, and its focusing effect becomes ambiguous (see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Copulae:_Conjugation_table" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBXM">#Copulae: Conjugation table</a> for more). <i id="mwBXQ">De wa</i>/<i id="mwBXU">ja(a)</i> can also be used on their own as a sentence adverbial meaning "in that case" or "well then,"<sup about="#mwt445" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kenkyusha_47-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kenkyusha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-kenkyusha-47&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kenkyusha-47" id="mwBXY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXg">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXk">]</span></span></a></sup> which focuses on the following information in relation to the preceding. <i id="mwBXo">Wa</i> is also used with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Gerund" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwBXs">gerund</a> to form a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Conditional" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBXw">conditional</a> clause:<sup about="#mwt438" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004496_48-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004496&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004496-48&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;496&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004496-48" id="mwBX0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBX4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBX8">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYA">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt441" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBYE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;うちへ帰っては<u>洋服を着替る</u>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Uchi e kaette wa <u>yōfuku o kikaeru</u>&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|When I get home, I'll CHANGE CLOTHES}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Uchi e kaette wa <u>yōfuku o kikaeru</u></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt441" id="mwBYI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">うちへ帰っては<u>洋服を着替る</u></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">When I get home, I'll CHANGE CLOTHES</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>; <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt442" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBYM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;死んでは<u>全てお終いです</u>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Shinde wa <u>subete oshimai desu</u>&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|When you die, it's the END OF EVERYTHING}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Shinde wa <u>subete oshimai desu</u></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt442" id="mwBYQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">死んでは<u>全てお終いです</u></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">When you die, it's the END OF EVERYTHING</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>. Like the aforementioned copular <i id="mwBYU">de wa</i>, the gerundive <i id="mwBYY">‑te/‑de wa</i> also contract to <i id="mwBYc">‑cha/‑ja</i>.</p>

<p id="mwBYg"><i id="mwBYk">Mo</i> ("even," "too") is often used to form concessive clauses:<sup about="#mwt446" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-49&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;A clause that, in English, starts with \&quot;even if/though,\&quot; \&quot;although,\&quot; etc.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-49" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwBYo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYw">[</span>c<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBY0">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt449" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBY4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;それは<u>子供で</u>もできる&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sore wa <u>kodomo de</u> mo dekiru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Even a CHILD can do that}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sore wa <u>kodomo de</u> mo dekiru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt449" id="mwBY8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">それは<u>子供で</u>もできる</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Even a CHILD can do that</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>; <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt450" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBZA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>雨天で</u>も予定時間に出発します&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>Uten de</u> mo yotei jikan ni shuppatsu shimasu&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Even if it RAINS, we'll leave at the scheduled time&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>Uten de</u> mo yotei jikan ni shuppatsu shimasu</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt450" id="mwBZE"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>雨天で</u>も予定時間に出発します</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; Even if it RAINS, we'll leave at the scheduled time)</span>. <i id="mwBZI">De mo</i>, as a sentence adverbial means "but" or "however"<sup about="#mwt456" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kenkyusha_47-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kenkyusha&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kenkyusha-47" id="mwBZM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZU">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZY">]</span></span></a></sup> ("despite what's just been mentioned"). The gerundive <i id="mwBZc">‑te/‑de mo</i> are standard concessive constructions in modern Japanese:<sup about="#mwt451" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010391,_393–395,_401_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010391, 393–395, 401&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010391,_393–395,_401-50&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Frellesvig&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2010&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;391, 393–395, 401&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010391,_393–395,_401-50" id="mwBZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZo">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZs">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt454" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBZw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>雨が降って</u>も行く&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>Ame ga futte</u> mo iku&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Even if it RAINS, I'll go}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>Ame ga futte</u> mo iku</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt454" id="mwBZ0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>雨が降って</u>も行く</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Even if it RAINS, I'll go</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>; <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt455" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBZ4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>いくら飲んで</u>も決して乱れない&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>Ikura nonde</u> mo kesshite midarenai&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|No matter HOW MUCH HE DRINKS, he never loses control}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>Ikura nonde</u> mo kesshite midarenai</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt455" id="mwBZ8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>いくら飲んで</u>も決して乱れない</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">No matter HOW MUCH HE DRINKS, he never loses control</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwBaA" aria-labelledby="Copulae"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Copulae">Copulae</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Copulae"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt457" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBaE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;See also&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:See_also&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese grammar#Copula (だ da)&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt458" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt457" id="mwBaI">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_grammar#Copula_(だ_da)" title="Japanese grammar">Japanese grammar §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Copula (だ da)</a></div>

<p id="mwBaM">The copulae are the basis of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Focus_particles_and_nucleus_splitting" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBaQ">nominal nucleus</a>. It follows a noun, and means "[subject] is &lt;noun&gt;," similarly to the copula <i id="mwBaU">be</i> in English. Certain nouns with descriptive meanings, called "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adjectival_noun_(Japanese)" title="Adjectival noun (Japanese)" id="mwBaY">adjectival nouns</a>," can also precede a copula.</p>

<p id="mwBac">Of the various forms of the copulae, <i id="mwBag">nara(ba)</i> functions as a type of evidential <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Conditional" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBak">conditional</a>. <i id="mwBao">Darō</i> can be added to verbs and adjectives to form the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Hortative" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)" id="mwBas">tentative</a>. <i id="mwBaw">Desu</i> can be used as a meaningless <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Politeness_stylization" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBa0">politeness flourish</a> with word forms that do not readily combine with the politeness auxiliary <i id="mwBa4">‑masu</i>, such as an adjective or a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Negative" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)" id="mwBa8">negative</a> auxiliary. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Perfective" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwBbA">past</a> <i id="mwBbE">deshita</i> and the tentative <i id="mwBbI">deshō</i> are both meaningful and polite extenders to word forms that lack any mechanism to convey pastness and tentativity, namely the western negative <i id="mwBbM">‑n(u)</i>.</p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwBbQ">
<caption id="mwBbU">Copula example sentences</caption>
<tbody id="mwBbY"><tr id="mwBbc">
<th id="mwBbg">English</th>
<th id="mwBbk">Japanese</th>
<th id="mwBbo">Function</th></tr>
<tr id="mwBbs">
<td id="mwBbw">I am<br id="mwBb0">I am<br id="mwBb4">justice‼</td>
<td id="mwBb8"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt459" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBcA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;僕が<br/>私が<br/>'''正義だ'''‼<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:<ruby>僕<rp>(</rp><rt>ぼく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<br/><ruby>私<rp>(</rp><rt>わたし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<br/><ruby>正<rp>(</rp><rt>せい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>義<rp>(</rp><rt>ぎ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>だ‼|trans-quote=I am<br/>I am<br/>justice‼|page=80|script-chapter=ja:ｐａｇｅ．２ <ruby>Ｌ<rp>(</rp><rt>エル</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>|trans-chapter=page.2 L|volume=1|script-title=ja:<ruby>DEATH NOTE<rp>(</rp><rt>デスノート</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>　退屈|trans-title=[[DEATH NOTE]]: boredom|authorlink=Tsugumi Ohba|first1=Tsugumi|last1=Ohba|authorlink2=Takeshi Obata|first2=Takeshi|last2=Obata|date=7 April 2004|editor=Homesha|publisher=Shueisha|location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]|isbn=4-08-873621-4}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Boku ga<br/>Watashi ga<br/>'''seigi da'''‼&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Boku ga<br>Watashi ga<br><b>seigi da</b>‼</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt459" id="mwBcE"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">僕が<br>私が<br><b>正義だ</b>‼<sup about="#mwt462" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-51&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwBcI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBcM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcQ">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcU">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="3" id="mwBcY">copularity with common nouns</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBcc">
<td id="mwBcg">To be, or not to be, that is the question:</td>
<td id="mwBck"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt465" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBco" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;生か死か……それが'''問題だ'''。<ref name=kume-1922/>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sei ka shi ka…… Sore ga '''mondai da'''.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sei ka shi ka…… Sore ga <b>mondai da</b>.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt465" id="mwBcs"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">生か死か……それが<b>問題だ</b>。<sup about="#mwt466" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kume-1922_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kume-1922&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kume-1922-52" id="mwBcw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBc0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBc4">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBc8">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBdA">
<td id="mwBdE">‘I am a servant of the Secret Fire, wielder of the flame of Anor. […]’</td>
<td id="mwBdI"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt468" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBdM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「わしは神秘の火に仕える者、アノールの焰の'''使い手じゃ'''。[…]」<ref name=seta-tanaka-1992-b2-p2/>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Washi wa Shinpi no Hi ni tsukaeru mono, Anōru no honō no '''tsukaite ja'''.”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Washi wa Shinpi no Hi ni tsukaeru mono, Anōru no honō no <b>tsukaite ja</b>.”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt468" id="mwBdQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「わしは神秘の火に仕える者、アノールの焰の<b>使い手じゃ</b>。[…]」<sup about="#mwt469" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-seta-tanaka-1992-b2-p2_53-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;seta-tanaka-1992-b2-p2&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-seta-tanaka-1992-b2-p2-53" id="mwBdU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdc">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdg">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBdk">
<td id="mwBdo">You… Zura Kotarō⁉<br id="mwBds">It’s not Zura, it’s Katsuraaa‼</td>
<td id="mwBdw"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt471" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBd0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;おまっ…ヅラ小太郎か⁉<br/>'''ヅラじゃない　桂だァァ'''‼<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:おまっ…ヅラ<ruby>小<rp>(</rp><rt>こ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>太<rp>(</rp><rt>た</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>郎<rp>(</rp><rt>ろう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>か⁉<br/>ヅラじゃない　<ruby>桂<rp>(</rp><rt>かつら</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>だァァ‼<br/>ぶふォ‼|trans-quote=You… Zura Kotarō⁉<br/>It’s not Zura, it’s Katsuraaa‼<br/>Oof‼|page=142|script-chapter=ja:<ruby>第<rp>(</rp><rt>だい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>五<ruby>訓<rp>(</rp><rt>くん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby> ジジイになってもあだ<ruby>名<rp>(</rp><rt>な</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>で<ruby>呼<rp>(</rp><rt>よ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>び<ruby>合<rp>(</rp><rt>あ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>える<ruby>友<rp>(</rp><rt>とも</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>達<rp>(</rp><rt>だち</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>を<ruby>作<rp>(</rp><rt>つく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>れ|trans-chapter=Lesson 5: Make Friends You Can Go by Nicknames with, Even If They’re a Codger|volume=1|script-title=ja:<ruby>銀魂<rp>(</rp><rt>ぎんたま</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>　<ruby>天<rp>(</rp><rt>てん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>然<rp>(</rp><rt>ねん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>パーマに<ruby>悪<rp>(</rp><rt>わる</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>い<ruby>奴<rp>(</rp><rt>やつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>はいない|trans-title=[[Gintama|Silver Soul]]: No Such Thing as a Bad Guy with a Natural Perm|authorlink=Hideaki Sorachi|first=Hideaki|last=Sorachi|date=7 April 2004|editor=Homesha|publisher=Shueisha|location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]|isbn=4-08-873623-0}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Omah… Zura Kotarō⁉<br/>'''Zura ja nai Katsura daaa'''‼&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Omah… Zura Kotarō⁉<br><b>Zura ja nai Katsura daaa</b>‼</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt471" id="mwBd4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">おまっ…ヅラ小太郎か⁉<br><b>ヅラじゃない　桂だァァ</b>‼<sup about="#mwt474" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-54&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-54" id="mwBd8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBeA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeE">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeI">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="2" id="mwBeM">copularity with proper nouns</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBeQ">
<td id="mwBeU">Look out! It’s the Cat!<br id="mwBeY">[…]<br id="mwBec">Catwoman’s here!</td>
<td id="mwBeg"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt477" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBek" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;気をつけろ！　'''キャットだ'''！<br/>[…]<br/>'''キャットウーマンだ'''ぞ！<ref>{{cite video game|title=[[Batman: Arkham City]]|developer=[[Rocksteady Studios]]|publisher=Warner Bros. Interactive Entertainment|language=en,ja|date=23 November 2011}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ki o tsukero! '''Kyatto da'''!<br/>[…]<br/>'''Kyattoūman da''' zo!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Ki o tsukero! <b>Kyatto da</b>!<br>[…]<br><b>Kyattoūman da</b> zo!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt477" id="mwBeo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">気をつけろ！　<b>キャットだ</b>！<br>[…]<br><b>キャットウーマンだ</b>ぞ！<sup about="#mwt480" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-55&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwBes"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBe0">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBe4">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBe8">
<td id="mwBfA">Batman’s here!</td>
<td id="mwBfE"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt483" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBfI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;バットマンは'''ここだ'''！<ref>{{cite video game|title=[[Batman: Arkham Knight]]|developer=[[Rocksteady Studios]]|publisher=Warner Bros. Interactive Entertainment|language=ja|date=16 July 2015}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Battoman wa '''koko da'''!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Battoman wa <b>koko da</b>!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt483" id="mwBfM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">バットマンは<b>ここだ</b>！<sup about="#mwt486" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-56&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwBfQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfY">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfc">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="2" id="mwBfg">copularity with demonstrative pronouns</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBfk">
<td id="mwBfo">To be, or not to be, I there’s the point,</td>
<td id="mwBfs"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt489" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBfw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;生か死か、問題は'''それだ'''。<ref name=anzai-2010/>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sei ka shi ka, mondai wa '''sore da'''.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sei ka shi ka, mondai wa <b>sore da</b>.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt489" id="mwBf0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">生か死か、問題は<b>それだ</b>。<sup about="#mwt490" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-anzai-2010_57-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;anzai-2010&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-anzai-2010-57" id="mwBf4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBf8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgA">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgE">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBgI">
<td id="mwBgM">‘You were always something of a featherbrain in your youth,’ […] ‘[…] for you were a beauty in your day, Cynthia.’</td>
<td id="mwBgQ"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt492" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBgU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「あなたは頭が'''空っぽでした'''よ、若いころは」[…]「[…]シンシア、あなたも若いころは'''きれいでした'''もの」<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:「あなたは頭が空っぽでしたよ、若いころは」レディ・ウェインライトが言った。マリアンは、そんなことはないと反論しようとしたが、母親は目でそれを押しとどめた。「でもマリアンはわたしたちの家系を代表する美人に育ったわ。あなたの血をひいたのでしょうね。シンシア、あなたも若いころはきれいでしたもの」|quote=‘You were always something of a featherbrain in your youth,’ Lady Wainwright said. Marianne made a movement of protest for it was not the truth, but her mother’s expression prevented her from speaking out. ‘However, we shall not draw comparisons. Marianne is decidedly the beauty of the family, and she does get that from you, for you were a beauty in your day, Cynthia.’|script-chapter=ja:１|chapter=Chapter One|script-title=ja:愛を知らない侯爵|trans-title=A Marquis Who Doesn’t Know of Love|title=Marianne and the Marquis|date=5 July 2008|isbn=978-4-596-32329-3|authorlink=Linda Sole|first=Anne|last=Herries|translator-last=Takada|translator-first=Yū|publisher=HarperCollins Japan}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Anata wa atama ga '''karappo deshita''' yo, wakai koro wa” […] “[…] Shinshia, anata mo wakai koro wa '''kirei deshita''' mono”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Anata wa atama ga <b>karappo deshita</b> yo, wakai koro wa” […] “[…] Shinshia, anata mo wakai koro wa <b>kirei deshita</b> mono”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt492" id="mwBgY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「あなたは頭が<b>空っぽでした</b>よ、若いころは」[…]「[…]シンシア、あなたも若いころは<b>きれいでした</b>もの」<sup about="#mwt495" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-58" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-58&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-58" id="mwBgc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgk">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgo">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="2" id="mwBgs">copularity with adjectival nouns</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBgw">
<td id="mwBg0">“I have sought Mistress Mishley’s aid in tracking down the tomboy who did such a foolish thing as to hide up in a tree”<br id="mwBg4">“What⁉ Don’t give me that baloney!”<br id="mwBg8">[…]<br id="mwBhA">Mishley is the purest of all beings in this world. […]<br id="mwBhE">“I’m so sorry, Mishley! I was an idiot for making you worry!”</td>
<td id="mwBhI"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt498" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBhM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「木の上に隠れるという'''アホな'''ことをしたお転婆様を探し当てるために、ミシュリーお嬢様のお力を借りたのです」<br/>「なっ⁉　'''バカな'''ことを言うな！」<br/>[…]<br/>ミシュリーはこの世で一番'''清らかな'''存在だ。[…]<br/>「ごめんミシュリー！　ミシュリーを心配させるなんて、お姉ちゃん'''バカだった'''！」<ref name=sato-2016>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:「木の上に隠れるというアホなことをしたお<ruby>転婆<rp>(</rp><rt>てんば</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>様を探し当てるために、ミシュリーお嬢様のお力を借りたのです」<br/>「なっ⁉　バカなことを言うな！」<br/>あり得ない説明に声を荒らげた私に対し、マリーワは器用に片<ruby>眉<rp>(</rp><rt>まゆ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>だけ上げて反応した。<br/>「バカなこと、とは？」<br/>「言うまでもない！　<ruby>清廉<rp>(</rp><rt>せいれん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が人の形となったミシュルーが、お前みたいな地獄の使いがたくらんだ計画に手を貸すわけないだろう⁉」<br/>ミシュリーはこの世で一番清らかな存在だ。児童虐待を<ruby>是<rp>(</rp><rt>ぜ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>とする悪魔に<ruby>与<rp>(</rp><rt>くみ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>するはずがない。<br/>「素晴らしい物言いですね、お嬢様。宣言どおり今日の授業は厳しくいきます。地獄をご覧じる覚悟はよろしいですか？」<br/>「黙れ獄卒め！　ミシュリーの行いを偽るような罪を犯したお前はさっさと地獄にかえ――」<br/>「あ、あの、マリーワからおねえさまがまいごになったってきいて、ごはんのじかんにもこないからしんぱいで……」<br/>「ごめんミシュリー！　ミシュリーを心配させるなんて、お姉ちゃんバカだった！」|trans-quote=“I have sought Mistress Mishley’s aid in tracking down the tomboy who did such a foolish thing as to hide up in a tree”<br/>“What⁉ Don’t give me that baloney!”<br/>I raised my voice at her ridiculous claim. In response, Marie-Ois slyly made a face with a single raised eyebrow.<br/>“How do you mean by ‘baloney’?”<br/>“As if I needed to spell it out! There’s no way in hell Mishley, purity in human form, would get in on a plot hatched by a Hell’s messenger like you, now is there⁉”<br/>Mishley is the purest of all beings in this world. No way she would partner with a demon that condones child abuse.<br/>“That was well put, Mistress. As I have announced, today’s lesson will be intense. Are you prepared to face Hell?”<br/>“Shut up, you lowly hellspawn! You’ve committed the offense of lying about what Mishley does, just go straight back to Hell――”<br/>“Sorry, I heard from Marie-Ois you got lost, I was worried ’cause you didn’t even show up for dinner……”<br/>“I’m so sorry, Mishley! I was an idiot for making you worry!”|script-chapter=ja:七歳編|chapter=Age Seven Arc|script-title=ja:ヒロインな妹、悪役令嬢な私|trans-title=My Baby Sister the Heroine, Myself the Villainess|date=29 April 2016|first=Mato|last=Satō|publisher=Shufu-to-Seikatsusha|url=https://ncode.syosetu.com/n4374cs/1/}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Ki no ue ni kakureru to yū '''aho na''' koto o shita otenbasama o sagashiateru tame ni, Mishurī Ojōsama no ochikara o karita no desu”<br/>“Nah⁉ '''Baka na''' koto o yū na!”<br/>[…]<br/>Mishurī wa kono yo de ichiban '''kiyoraka na''' sonzai da. […]<br/>“Gomen Mishurī! Mishurī o shinpai saseru nante, o nēchan '''baka datta'''!”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Ki no ue ni kakureru to yū <b>aho na</b> koto o shita otenbasama o sagashiateru tame ni, Mishurī Ojōsama no ochikara o karita no desu”<br>“Nah⁉ <b>Baka na</b> koto o yū na!”<br>[…]<br>Mishurī wa kono yo de ichiban <b>kiyoraka na</b> sonzai da. […]<br>“Gomen Mishurī! Mishurī o shinpai saseru nante, o nēchan <b>baka datta</b>!”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt498" id="mwBhQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「木の上に隠れるという<b>アホな</b>ことをしたお転婆様を探し当てるために、ミシュリーお嬢様のお力を借りたのです」<br>「なっ⁉　<b>バカな</b>ことを言うな！」<br>[…]<br>ミシュリーはこの世で一番<b>清らかな</b>存在だ。[…]<br>「ごめんミシュリー！　ミシュリーを心配させるなんて、お姉ちゃん<b>バカだった</b>！」<sup about="#mwt501" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sato-2016_59-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sato-2016&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-sato-2016-59&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-sato-2016-59" id="mwBhU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhc">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhg">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBhk">
<td id="mwBho">“As if I needed to spell it out! There’s no way in hell Mishley, purity in human form, would get in on a plot hatched by a Hell’s messenger like you, now is there⁉”<br id="mwBhs">[…]<br id="mwBhw">“Shut up, you lowly hellspawn! You’ve committed the offense of lying about what Mishley does, just go straight back to Hell――”</td>
<td id="mwBh0"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt504" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBh4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「言うまでもない！　清廉が人の形となったミシュリーが、お前'''みたいな'''地獄の使いがたくらんだ計画に手を貸すわけないだろう⁉」<br/>[…]<br/>「黙れ獄卒め！　ミシュリーの行いを偽る'''ような'''罪を犯したお前はさっさと地獄にかえ――」<ref name=sato-2016/>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Yū made mo nai! Seiren ga hito no katachi to natta Mishurī ga, omae '''mitai na''' jigoku no tsukai ga takuranda keikaku ni te o kasu wake nai darō⁉”<br/>[…]<br/>“Damare gokusotsume! Mishurī no okonai o itsuwaru '''yō na''' tsumi o okashita omae wa sassa to jigoku ni kae――”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Yū made mo nai! Seiren ga hito no katachi to natta Mishurī ga, omae <b>mitai na</b> jigoku no tsukai ga takuranda keikaku ni te o kasu wake nai darō⁉”<br>[…]<br>“Damare gokusotsume! Mishurī no okonai o itsuwaru <b>yō na</b> tsumi o okashita omae wa sassa to jigoku ni kae――”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt504" id="mwBh8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「言うまでもない！　清廉が人の形となったミシュリーが、お前<b>みたいな</b>地獄の使いがたくらんだ計画に手を貸すわけないだろう⁉」<br>[…]<br>「黙れ獄卒め！　ミシュリーの行いを偽る<b>ような</b>罪を犯したお前はさっさと地獄にかえ――」<sup about="#mwt505" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sato-2016_59-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sato-2016&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-sato-2016-59" id="mwBiA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBiE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiI">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiM">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="2" id="mwBiQ">copularity with auxiliary nouns</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBiU">
<td id="mwBiY">They say it’s a terrifying place. Many have died there. They say ascetics just keep dying because of the immensely severe asceticism. Do you wish to die too?</td>
<td id="mwBic"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt507" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBig" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;あそこは恐ろしいところだ'''そうだ'''　もう何人も死んでるんだ　'''そうだ'''　あんまりはげしい苦行のために　行者がどんどん死ぬ'''そうだ'''　きみも死にたいのかっ<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:ぼくはあしたウルベーラの苦行林へはいります　当分もう会えないかもしれません<br/>あそこは恐ろしいところだそうだ　もう何人も死んでるんだ　そうだ　あんまりはげしい苦行のために　行者がどんどん死ぬそうだ　きみも死にたいのかっ<br/>死ぬか死なないかは神さまのおぼしめししだいです|trans-quote=I shall enter the ascetic forest of [[Uruvela]] tomorrow. There is no telling if I could see you any time soon.<br/>They say it’s a terrifying place. Many have died there. They say ascetics just keep dying because of the immensely severe asceticism. Do you wish to die too?<br/>Whether or not I die is up to the gods to decide.|pages=131–132|script-chapter=ja:第３部 第７章 苦行林にて|trans-chapter=Part 3, Chapter 7: At the Ascetic Forest|volume=6|series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|手塚治虫漫画全集}}|script-title=ja:ブッダ|trans-title=[[Buddha (manga)|Buddha]]|authorlink=Osamu Tezuka|first=Osamu|last=Tezuka|date=15 June 1999|orig-date=20 July 1983|edition=7th|publisher=Kodansha|location=[[Bunkyō]], Tokyo|isbn=4-06-173292-7}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Asoko wa osoroshii tokoro da '''sō da''' Mō nannin mo shinde ’ru n da '''sō da''' Anmari hageshii kugyō no tame ni gyōja ga dondon shinu '''sō da''' Kimi mo shinitai no kah&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Asoko wa osoroshii tokoro da <b>sō da</b> Mō nannin mo shinde ’ru n da <b>sō da</b> Anmari hageshii kugyō no tame ni gyōja ga dondon shinu <b>sō da</b> Kimi mo shinitai no kah</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt507" id="mwBik"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">あそこは恐ろしいところだ<b>そうだ</b>　もう何人も死んでるんだ　<b>そうだ</b>　あんまりはげしい苦行のために　行者がどんどん死ぬ<b>そうだ</b>　きみも死にたいのかっ<sup about="#mwt510" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-60" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-60&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-60" id="mwBio"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBis"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiw">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBi0">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwBi4">
<td id="mwBi8">“Thank you. You’re cute too, Big Brother!”</td>
<td id="mwBjA"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt513" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBjE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「ありがとうございます。お兄さまも'''可愛いです'''！」<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:「わぁ！　アナ可愛いね！」<br/>真っ先に私を褒めてくれたのは、シルヴェルスお兄さま。<br/>「ありがとうございます。お兄さまも可愛いです！」<br/>[…]<br/>「アナ～！　私は～？」<br/>「ルナティーラお姉さまもとっても可愛いです！」|trans-quote=“Wow! You’re so cute, Anna!”<br/>The very first one to compliment me was Big Brother Silverus.<br/>“Thank you. You’re cute too, Big Brother!”<br/>[…]<br/>“Anna~! What about me~?”<br/>“Big Sister Lunatira is super cute too!”|script-chapter=ja:第一章 新入生歓迎パーティー|trans-chapter=Chapter 1: A Welcome Party for New Students|script-title=ja:私の家族はハイスペックです！　落ちこぼれ転生末姫ですが溺愛されつつ世界救っちゃいます！|trans-title=My Family Is the Best! I’m a Dropout Reincarnated as the Youngest of the Princesses, But I’m Doted on and I’ll Be the One to Save the World|date=30 December 2025|publisher=AlphaPolis|author=Rī-san}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Arigatō gozaimasu. Oniisama mo '''kawaii desu'''!”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Arigatō gozaimasu. Oniisama mo <b>kawaii desu</b>!”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt513" id="mwBjI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「ありがとうございます。お兄さまも<b>可愛いです</b>！」<sup about="#mwt516" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-61&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwBjM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjU">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjY">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td id="mwBjc">politeness</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBjg">
<td id="mwBjk">Well, it wasn't a very successful meeting.</td>
<td id="mwBjo"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt519" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBjs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;そうですね、それはあまり成果のある会議'''ではありませんでした'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sō desu ne, sore wa amari seika no aru kaigi '''de wa arimasen deshita'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sō desu ne, sore wa amari seika no aru kaigi <b>de wa arimasen deshita</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt519" id="mwBjw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">そうですね、それはあまり成果のある会議<b>ではありませんでした</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td id="mwBj0">politeness and pastness</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBj4">
<td id="mwBj8">Might I ask you to go to the hospital with me?</td>
<td id="mwBkA"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt520" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBkE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;私と一緒に病院へ行って'''もらえませんでしょう'''か&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Watashi to issho ni byōin e itte '''moraemasen deshō''' ka&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Watashi to issho ni byōin e itte <b>moraemasen deshō</b> ka</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt520" id="mwBkI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">私と一緒に病院へ行って<b>もらえませんでしょう</b>か</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td id="mwBkM">politeness and tentativity</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBkQ">
<td id="mwBkU">Did you ever run into something like that kind of interest in running one’s own business in your research?</td>
<td id="mwBkY"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt521" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBkc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;そういう個々人の経営への意欲みたいなものは、調査の中で感じられることは'''ありませんでしたでしょう'''か。<ref>{{#invoke:citation|citation|lang=ja|page=23|script-title=ja:ヒラから幹部にまで広がる農業従事の外国人労働力|url=https://www.nohken.or.jp/KOUENKAIKIROKU/No.8_2020/kobetsuPDF/2020-1_horiguchikenji.pdf|last=Yagi|first=Hironori|date=6 July 2020}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sō yū kokojin no keiei e no iyoku mitai na mono wa, chōsa no naka de kanjirareru koto wa '''arimasen deshita deshō''' ka.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sō yū kokojin no keiei e no iyoku mitai na mono wa, chōsa no naka de kanjirareru koto wa <b>arimasen deshita deshō</b> ka.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt521" id="mwBkg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">そういう個々人の経営への意欲みたいなものは、調査の中で感じられることは<b>ありませんでしたでしょう</b>か。<sup about="#mwt524" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-62&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwBkk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBko"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBks">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkw">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td id="mwBk0">politeness, pastness and tentativity</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwBk4" aria-labelledby="Copulae:_Conjugation_table"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Copulae:_Conjugation_table">Copulae: Conjugation table</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Copulae: Conjugation table"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBk8">The copulae of Japanese demonstrate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suppletion" title="Suppletion" id="mwBlA">suppletion</a>, in that they combined different forms from different words into one word. The original copulae were all based on the verb <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt527" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBlE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;あり&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ari&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|to exist}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ari</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt527" id="mwBlI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">あり</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">to exist</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, which evolved into the modern <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt528" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBlM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ある&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;aru&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">aru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt528" id="mwBlQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">ある</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>. It needed to be preceded by one of the three particles, <i id="mwBlU">ni</i>, <i id="mwBlY">nite</i> → <i id="mwBlc">de</i><sup about="#mwt534" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kotobank.jp_63-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kotobank.jp&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kotobank.jp-63" id="mwBlg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlo">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBls">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt529" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004238_64-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004238&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004238-64&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;238&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004238-64" id="mwBlw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBl0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBl4">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBl8">]</span></span></a></sup> and <i id="mwBmA">to</i>, which yielded three variants, <i id="mwBmE">ni ari</i>/<i id="mwBmI">ni aru</i> → <i id="mwBmM">nari</i>/<i id="mwBmQ">naru</i>,<sup about="#mwt537" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-65" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-65&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-65" id="mwBmU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmc">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmg">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwBmk">de ari</i>/<i id="mwBmo">de aru</i> → <i id="mwBms">da</i><sup about="#mwt540" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-66" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-66&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-66" id="mwBmw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBm0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBm4">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBm8">]</span></span></a></sup> and <i id="mwBnA">to ari</i>/<i id="mwBnE">to aru</i> → <i id="mwBnI">tari</i>/<i id="mwBnM">taru</i>, the last of which fell out of use, but did phonetically coincide with <i id="mwBnQ">te ari</i>/<i id="mwBnU">te aru</i> → <i id="mwBnY">tari</i>/<i id="mwBnc">taru</i>,<sup about="#mwt543" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-67" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-67&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-67" id="mwBng"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBno">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBns">]</span></span></a></sup> which in turn evolved into the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Perfective" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwBnw">past</a> auxiliary <i id="mwBn0">ta</i>.<sup about="#mwt546" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-68&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwBn4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBn8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoA">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoE">]</span></span></a></sup> It also combined with adjectival roots to expand their conjugation, for example <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt532" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBoI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;赤かろう&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;akaku arō → akakarō&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">akaku arō → akakarō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt532" id="mwBoM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">赤かろう</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt533" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBoQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;赤かった&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;akaku atta → akakatta&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">akaku atta → akakatta</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt533" id="mwBoU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">赤かった</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, etc.</p>
<ul id="mwBoY"><li id="mwBoc">The original conclusive <i id="mwBog">de ari</i>, was replaced by the attributive <i id="mwBok">de aru</i>, which evolved into the informal conclusive <i id="mwBoo">da</i>, and the formal conclusive <i id="mwBos">de aru</i>. In terms of formality and politeness:
<ul id="mwBow"><li id="mwBo0"><i id="mwBo4">Da</i> is informal and impolite. Depending on specifically what precedes it, <i id="mwBo8">da</i> can be perceived as abrupt or too masculine, and therefore is customarily omitted in some cases.<sup about="#mwt547" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELammers20056–7,_12,_15_69-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTELammers20056–7, 12, 15&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELammers20056–7,_12,_15-69&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Lammers&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2005&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;6–7, 12, 15&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELammers20056–7,_12,_15-69" id="mwBpA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpI">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBpQ"><i id="mwBpU">De aru</i> is formal and nonpolite (with no inherent assumption of politeness).</li>
<li id="mwBpY"><i id="mwBpc">Desu</i> is nonformal (with no inherent assumption of formality) and polite.</li>
<li id="mwBpg"><i id="mwBpk">De arimasu</i> is formal and polite.</li></ul></li>
<li id="mwBpo"><i id="mwBps">Da</i>/<i id="mwBpw">datta</i>/<i id="mwBp0">darō</i> are the colloquial contractions of <i id="mwBp4">de aru</i>/<i id="mwBp8">de atta</i>/<i id="mwBqA">de arō</i> in eastern dialects (including Tokyo Japanese). Their western equivalents include <i id="mwBqE">ja</i>/<i id="mwBqI">jatta</i>/<i id="mwBqM">jarō</i> and <i id="mwBqQ">ya</i>/<i id="mwBqU">yatta</i>/<i id="mwBqY">yarō</i>.<sup about="#mwt550" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004373_70-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004373&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004373-70&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;373&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004373-70" id="mwBqc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqk">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqo">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwBqs">Ja</i>/<i id="mwBqw">jatta</i>/<i id="mwBq0">jarō</i>, along with other western features (<i id="mwBq4">‑n(u)</i>, <i id="mwBq8">‑nanda</i>, <i id="mwBrA">u‑onbin</i>, etc), are occasionally used in faux-archaic speech<sup about="#mwt553" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001336_71-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001336&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001336-71&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;336&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001336-71" id="mwBrE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrM">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrQ">]</span></span></a></sup> or old people's speech rather dialectal speech; for example, the character <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gandalf" title="Gandalf" id="mwBrU">Gandalf</a>, an ancient wizard from <i id="mwBrY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lord_of_the_Rings" title="The Lord of the Rings" id="mwBrc">The Lord of the Rings</a></i>, is made to speak with a few selectively chosen western features,<sup about="#mwt556" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-72&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''Ja''/''jatta''/''jaro'' rather than ''da''/''datta''/''daro'', ''tōsan(u)'' rather than ''tōsanai'', etc.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-72" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwBrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBro">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrs">]</span></span></a></sup> while still retaining some eastern features,<sup about="#mwt559" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-73" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-73&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''Tōku'' rather than ''toō'', ''oyobanakatta'' rather than ''oyobananda'', ''nigero'' rather than ''nigē'', etc.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-73" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwBrw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBr0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr4">[</span>e<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr8">]</span></span></a></sup> in the Japanese translations (see relevant quotations in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Notes" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBsA">footnotes</a>).</li>
<li id="mwBsE"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt562" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBsI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;御座る&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gozaru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;contracted from ''goza aru''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Gozaru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt562" id="mwBsM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">御座る</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; contracted from <i>goza aru</i>)</span> is the honorific version of <i id="mwBsQ">aru</i>, and <i id="mwBsU">goza(r)imasu</i> is the honorific version of <i id="mwBsY">arimasu</i>. <i id="mwBsc">Gozaru</i> has most of the forms that <i id="mwBsg">aru</i> does (<i id="mwBsk">(de (wa)) gozaru</i>, <i id="mwBso">(de (wa)) gozaranu</i>, <i id="mwBss">(de (wa)) gozareba</i>, etc), although it additionally undergoes a minor sound change in the polite conclusive/attributive <i id="mwBsw">gozarimasu</i> → <i id="mwBs0">gozaimasu</i> and the imperative <i id="mwBs4">gozare</i> → <i id="mwBs8">gozai</i>. <i id="mwBtA">Gozaimasu</i> is authentically used in modern Japanese, while <i id="mwBtE">gozaru</i>, <i id="mwBtI">gozarimasu(ru)</i> and <i id="mwBtM">gozaimasuru</i> are used for effect, such as in theatrical or humorous lines.<sup about="#mwt563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin20041035–1036_74-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin20041035–1036&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin20041035–1036-74&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1035–1036&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin20041035–1036-74" id="mwBtQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBtU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtY">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBtg">The current attributive form of <i id="mwBtk">de (wa) aru</i> is still <i id="mwBto">de (wa) aru</i>. <i id="mwBts">Da</i> additionally takes <i id="mwBtw">naru</i> → <i id="mwBt0">na</i> (of said <i id="mwBt4">nari</i>) as its attributive form<sup about="#mwt614" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-75" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-75&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-75" id="mwBt8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuE">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuI">]</span></span></a></sup> only in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adjectival_noun_(Japanese)" title="Adjectival noun (Japanese)" id="mwBuM">adjectival verbs</a>,<sup about="#mwt566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004617_76-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004617&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004617-76&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;617&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004617-76" id="mwBuQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuY">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuc">]</span></span></a></sup> as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt569" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBug" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;綺麗な花&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kirei na hana&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|pretty flower}}, {{lit|a flower, which is pretty}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kirei na hana</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt569" id="mwBuk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">綺麗な花</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">pretty flower</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt570" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBuo\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">a flower, which is pretty</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, and after the auxiliaries <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt571" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBus" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;そう&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sō&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">sō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt571" id="mwBuw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">そう</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt572" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBu0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;よう&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;yō&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">yō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt572" id="mwBu4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">よう</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt573" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBu8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;みたい&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mitai&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">mitai</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt573" id="mwBvA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">みたい</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt574" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBvE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;利口そうな顔&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rikō sō na kao&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|smart-looking face}}, {{lit|a face, which appears smart}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">rikō sō na kao</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt574" id="mwBvI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">利口そうな顔</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">smart-looking face</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt575" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBvM\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">a face, which appears smart</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt576" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBvQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;彼女のような人&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kanojo no yō na hito&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|someone like her}}, {{lit|a person, who is like her}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kanojo no yō na hito</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt576" id="mwBvU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">彼女のような人</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">someone like her</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt577" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBvY\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">a person, who is like her</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>; while the particle <i id="mwBvc">no</i> is used after nouns, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt578" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBvg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;友達の裕子&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;tomodachi no Yūko&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|my friend Yūko}}, {{lit|Yūko, who is my friend}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">tomodachi no Yūko</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt578" id="mwBvk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">友達の裕子</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">my friend Yūko</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt579" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBvo\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Yūko, who is my friend</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> or <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt580" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBvs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;美人のお姉さん&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;bijin no onēsan&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|my beautiful sister}}, {{lit|my sister, who is a beauty}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">bijin no onēsan</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt580" id="mwBvw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">美人のお姉さん</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">my beautiful sister</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt581" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBv0\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">my sister, who is a beauty</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>. However, since <i id="mwBv4">no</i> also expresses possession, this may cause ambiguity, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt582" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBv8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;医者のおじさん&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;isha no ojisan&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|my uncle, who is a doctor; my doctor's uncle}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">isha no ojisan</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt582" id="mwBwA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">医者のおじさん</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt583" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBwE\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">my uncle, who is a doctor; my doctor's uncle</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>;<sup about="#mwt584" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPoser1984168_77-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEPoser1984168&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPoser1984168-77&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Poser&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1984&quot;},&quot;page&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;168&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPoser1984168-77" id="mwBwI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwQ">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwU">]</span></span></a></sup> moreover, some nouns can function as either "adjectival verbs" or "nouns", and take either <i id="mwBwY">na</i> or <i id="mwBwc">no</i>, such as <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt587" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBwg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;色々な物・色々の物&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;iroiro na mono/iroiro no mono&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|various things}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">iroiro na mono/iroiro no mono</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt587" id="mwBwk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">色々な物・色々の物</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">various things</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>. The old <i id="mwBwo">naru</i> (of said <i id="mwBws">nari</i>) and <i id="mwBww">taru</i> (of said <i id="mwBw0">to ari</i>/<i id="mwBw4">to aru</i> → <i id="mwBw8">tari</i>/<i id="mwBxA">taru</i>) can still be used for literary effect, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt588" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBxE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;絶大なるご期待&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;zetsudai naru gokitai&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|the utmost anticipation}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">zetsudai naru gokitai</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt588" id="mwBxI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">絶大なるご期待</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">the utmost anticipation</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt589" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBxM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;北海道なる地方&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Hokkaidō naru chihō&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Hokkaido region}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Hokkaidō naru chihō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt589" id="mwBxQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">北海道なる地方</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Hokkaido region</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt590" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBxU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;医者たる人&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;isha taru hito&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|a person, who is known as a doctor}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">isha taru hito</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt590" id="mwBxY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">医者たる人</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">a person, who is known as a doctor</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt591" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBxc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;教師たるもの&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kyōshi taru mono&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|those who call themselves teachers}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kyōshi taru mono</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt591" id="mwBxg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">教師たるもの</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">those who call themselves teachers</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, or in such idiom as <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt592" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBxk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;聖なる&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sei naru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|holy}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">sei naru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt592" id="mwBxo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">聖なる</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">holy</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> or <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt593" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBxs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;堂々たる&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;dōdō taru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|splendid}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">dōdō taru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt593" id="mwBxw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">堂々たる</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">splendid</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt594" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004617_76-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004617&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004617-76&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;617&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004617-76" id="mwBx0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBx4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBx8">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByA">]</span></span></a></sup> Incidentally, an ancient possessive <i id="mwByE">na</i> was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fossil_word" title="Fossil word" id="mwByI">fossilized</a> in words like <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt597" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwByM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;眼&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ma'''na'''ko&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|eyeball}}, {{lit|eye's child}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ma<b>na</b>ko</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt597" id="mwByQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">眼</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">eyeball</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt598" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwByU\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">eye's child</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt599" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwByY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;港&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mi'''na'''to&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|harbor}}, {{lit|water's door}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">mi<b>na</b>to</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt599" id="mwByc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">港</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">harbor</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt600" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwByg\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">water's door</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt601" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwByk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;掌&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ta'''na'''gokoro&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|palm}}, {{lit|hand's heart}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ta<b>na</b>gokoro</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt601" id="mwByo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">掌</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">palm</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt602" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBys\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">hand's heart</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, etc.<sup about="#mwt603" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001614_78-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001614&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001614-78&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;614&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001614-78" id="mwByw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBy0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBy4">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBy8">]</span></span></a></sup> There is also a niche distinction between <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt606" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBzA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;神戸の人&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kōbe no hito&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|person from [[Kobe]]}}, {{lit|Kobe's person}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kōbe no hito</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt606" id="mwBzE"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">神戸の人</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">person from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobe" title="Kobe">Kobe</a></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt607" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBzI\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Kobe's person</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt608" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBzM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;神戸な人&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kōbe na hito&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|person seeming like they could be from Kobe}}, {{lit|Kobe-ish person}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kōbe na hito</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt608" id="mwBzQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">神戸な人</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">person seeming like they could be from Kobe</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt609" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBzU\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Kobe-ish person</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt617" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-79&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwBzY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzg">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzk">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwBzo">Na</i> is also used before the nominalizer <i id="mwBzs">no</i>, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt610" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBzw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;祖母は100歳なのだ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sobo wa hyakusai na no da&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|it's a fact that my grandma is 100 years old}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">sobo wa hyakusai na no da</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt610" id="mwBz0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">祖母は100歳なのだ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt611" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwBz4\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">it's a fact that my grandma is 100 years old</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.</li>
<li id="mwBz8"><i id="mwB0A">De</i> is morphologically a gerund, for it is constructed by combining its infinitive (<i id="mwB0E">ni</i>) with the gerundive particle <i id="mwB0I">‑te</i> as with any other gerund. In modern Japanese, it itself functions as both an infinitive<sup about="#mwt618" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425_80-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425-80&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;425&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425-80" id="mwB0M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0U">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0Y">]</span></span></a></sup> and a gerund. When combining with <i id="mwB0c">aru</i> to create finite forms, it is <i id="mwB0g">de</i> that is used, not <i id="mwB0k">ni</i> which is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classical_Japanese" title="Classical Japanese" id="mwB0o">classical</a> and merely fossilized in the attributive <i id="mwB0s">na(ru)</i> (← <i id="mwB0w">ni aru</i>) and the provisional <i id="mwB00">nara(ba)</i> (← <i id="mwB04">ni araba</i>). Another gerund, <i id="mwB08">de atte</i> is occasionally found in writing: <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt621" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB1A" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;四人はいずれも人並み以上に強い自我の'''持ち主であって'''、決して妥協などしない&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Yonin wa izure mo hitonami ijō ni tsuyoi jiga no '''mochinushi de atte''', kesshite dakyō nado shinai&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Each of the four is the possessor of a stronger ego than the average man and never makes compromises}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Yonin wa izure mo hitonami ijō ni tsuyoi jiga no <b>mochinushi de atte</b>, kesshite dakyō nado shinai</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt621" id="mwB1E"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">四人はいずれも人並み以上に強い自我の<b>持ち主であって</b>、決して妥協などしない</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Each of the four is the possessor of a stronger ego than the average man and never makes compromises</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt622" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004490_81-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004490&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004490-81&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;490&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004490-81" id="mwB1I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1Q">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1U">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB1Y"><i id="mwB1c">De</i> and <i id="mwB1g">de ari</i> are the more common infinitives: <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt625" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB1k" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;しかし彼らは優れた'''文化であり'''娯楽である映画を一人でも多くの人に見せたいと努力してきただけである&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Shika shi karera wa sugureta '''bunka de ari''' goraku de aru eiga o hitori de mo ōku no hito ni misetai to doryoku shite kita dake de aru&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|But they have only endeavored to show to as many people as possible films that are outstanding culture and are entertainment}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Shika shi karera wa sugureta <b>bunka de ari</b> goraku de aru eiga o hitori de mo ōku no hito ni misetai to doryoku shite kita dake de aru</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt625" id="mwB1o"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">しかし彼らは優れた<b>文化であり</b>娯楽である映画を一人でも多くの人に見せたいと努力してきただけである</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">But they have only endeavored to show to as many people as possible films that are outstanding culture and are entertainment</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>. It is rare to find <i id="mwB1s">ni</i> used alone with an ordinary noun: <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt626" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB1w" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;それが'''無念さに'''若嫁は里へ帰ったきり戻ってこない&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sore ga '''munensa ni''' wakayome wa sato e kaetta kiri modotte konai&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|With that as a resentment, the bride returned to her village and would not return}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sore ga <b>munensa ni</b> wakayome wa sato e kaetta kiri modotte konai</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt626" id="mwB10"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">それが<b>無念さに</b>若嫁は里へ帰ったきり戻ってこない</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">With that as a resentment, the bride returned to her village and would not return</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>; <i id="mwB14">ni</i> meaning "as," however, can be treated as an infinitive: <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt627" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB18" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;うちは'''お客様に'''外人の方が多いんで、アスパラガス、ブロッコリーなどの西洋野菜がよく出ます&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Uchi wa '''okyakusama ni''' gaijin no kata ga ōi n de, asuparagasu, burokkorī nado no seiyō yasai ga yoku demasu&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|As customers we have mostly foreigners, so lots of foreign vegetables like asparagus and broccoli are out for sale}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Uchi wa <b>okyakusama ni</b> gaijin no kata ga ōi n de, asuparagasu, burokkorī nado no seiyō yasai ga yoku demasu</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt627" id="mwB2A"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">うちは<b>お客様に</b>外人の方が多いんで、アスパラガス、ブロッコリーなどの西洋野菜がよく出ます</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">As customers we have mostly foreigners, so lots of foreign vegetables like asparagus and broccoli are out for sale</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt628" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004396_82-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004396&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004396-82&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;396&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004396-82" id="mwB2E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2M">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2Q">]</span></span></a></sup> Other types of nouns, such as adjectival nouns (<span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt631" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB2U" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;平和に&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;heiwa ni&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|peacefully; in a peaceful way}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">heiwa ni</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt631" id="mwB2Y"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">平和に</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">peacefully; in a peaceful way</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>), auxiliary nouns (<span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt632" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB2c" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ように&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;yō ni&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|in a way like}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">yō ni</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt632" id="mwB2g"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">ように</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">in a way like</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>), demonstrative pronouns (<span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt633" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB2k" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ここに&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;koko ni&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|here}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">koko ni</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt633" id="mwB2o"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">ここに</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">here</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>) etc, can be readily paired with <i id="mwB2s">ni</i> when used adverbially.</li>
<li id="mwB2w">The infinitives combine with different words,<sup about="#mwt634" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin200440_83-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin200440&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin200440-83&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;40&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin200440-83" id="mwB20"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB24"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB28">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt637" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425,_502,_507_84-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425, 502, 507&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425,_502,_507-84&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;425, 502, 507&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001425,_502,_507-84" id="mwB3E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3M">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3Q">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt642" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-shinmeikai_85-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;shinmeikai&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-shinmeikai-85&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-shinmeikai-85" id="mwB3U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3c">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3g">]</span></span></a></sup> each with its own parallel:
<ul id="mwB3k"><li id="mwB3o"><i id="mwB3s">de</i> + <i id="mwB3w">aru</i> → <i id="mwB30">de aru</i> ("be"), parallel with <i id="mwB34">akaku</i> + <i id="mwB38">aru</i> → <i id="mwB4A">akaku aru</i> ("be red") and <i id="mwB4E">nomi</i> + <i id="mwB4I">suru</i> → <i id="mwB4M">nomi suru</i> ("drink")</li>
<li id="mwB4Q"><i id="mwB4U">de</i> + <i id="mwB4Y">nai</i> → <i id="mwB4c">de nai</i> ("not be"), parallel with <i id="mwB4g">akaku</i> + <i id="mwB4k">nai</i> → <i id="mwB4o">akaku nai</i> ("not be red") and <i id="mwB4s">nomi</i> + <i id="mwB4w">shinai</i> → <i id="mwB40">nomi shinai</i> ("not drink")</li>
<li id="mwB44"><i id="mwB48">de ari</i> + <i id="mwB5A">‑masu</i> → <i id="mwB5E">de arimasu</i> ("be"),<sup about="#mwt643" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-86" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-86&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Some traditional descriptions also count ''dat'' in ''datta'' (\&quot;was/were\&quot;), which was historically ''de arita'', as well as ''deshi'' in ''deshita''.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-86" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwB5I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5Q">[</span>f<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5U">]</span></span></a></sup> parallel with <i id="mwB5Y">nomi</i> + <i id="mwB5c">‑masu</i> → <i id="mwB5g">nomimasu</i> ("drink")</li></ul></li>
<li id="mwB5k">The above formations allow "splitting",<sup about="#mwt646" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004316_44-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004316&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004316-44&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;316&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004316-44" id="mwB5o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5w">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB50">]</span></span></a></sup> or adding particles like <i id="mwB54">wa</i> or <i id="mwB58">mo</i> between the infinitive forms and the following verbs, which would be impossible with <i id="mwB6A">da</i> ("be"), <i id="mwB6E">akai</i> ("be red") and <i id="mwB6I">nomu</i> ("drink") alone:
<ul id="mwB6M"><li id="mwB6Q"><i id="mwB6U">da</i> ("be"), parallel with <i id="mwB6Y">akai</i> ("be red") and <i id="mwB6c">nomu</i> ("drink")</li>
<li id="mwB6g"><i id="mwB6k">de wa aru</i> ("be …, indeed"), parallel with <i id="mwB6o">akaku wa aru</i> ("be red, indeed") and <i id="mwB6s">nomi wa suru</i> ("drink, indeed")</li>
<li id="mwB6w"><i id="mwB60">de wa nai</i> ("not be …, indeed"), parallel with <i id="mwB64">akaku wa nai</i> ("not be red, indeed") and <i id="mwB68">nomi wa shinai</i> ("not drink, indeed")</li></ul></li>
<li id="mwB7A">The particles <i id="mwB7E">wa</i> and <i id="mwB7I">mo</i> are often added, especially to the negatives, although not required in principle.<sup about="#mwt654" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kotobank.jp_63-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kotobank.jp&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-kotobank.jp-63&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kotobank.jp-63" id="mwB7M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7U">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt657" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-87" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-87&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-87" id="mwB7c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7k">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7o">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwB7s">Wa</i> puts focus on what goes after it, while <i id="mwB7w">mo</i> puts focus what goes before it.<sup about="#mwt649" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004317–322_88-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004317–322&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004317–322-88&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;317–322&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004317–322-88" id="mwB70"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB74"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB78">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8A">]</span></span></a></sup> In the following sentences, the focused information is underlined for the Japanese originals and the literal English translations; for the non-literal English translations, all-caps type emulates how an English speaker would emphasize the focused information.
<ul id="mwB8E"><li id="mwB8I"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt658" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB8M" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>この辺</u>が静かだ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>Kono hen</u> ga shizuka da.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|<u>This area</u>[, not any other area,] is quiet.}}, {{xlat|THIS area is quiet.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>Kono hen</u> ga shizuka da.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt658" id="mwB8Q"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>この辺</u>が静かだ。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt659" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB8U\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text"><u>This area</u>[, not any other area,] is quiet.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt660" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB8Y\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>THIS area is quiet.</span>)</span></li>
<li id="mwB8c"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt661" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB8g" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>この辺</u>も静かだ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>Kono hen</u> mo shizuka da.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|<u>This area</u>, too, [along with at least another area,] is quiet.}}, {{xlat|THIS area's also quiet.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>Kono hen</u> mo shizuka da.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt661" id="mwB8k"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>この辺</u>も静かだ。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt662" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB8o\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text"><u>This area</u>, too, [along with at least another area,] is quiet.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt663" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB8s\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>THIS area's also quiet.</span>)</span></li>
<li id="mwB8w"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt664" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB80" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;この辺は<u>静かだ</u>。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kono hen wa <u>shizuka da</u>.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|This area? <u>It's quiet</u>.}}, {{xlat|This area's QUIET.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kono hen wa <u>shizuka da</u>.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt664" id="mwB84"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">この辺は<u>静かだ</u>。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt665" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB88\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">This area? <u>It's quiet</u>.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt666" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB9A\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>This area's QUIET.</span>)</span></li>
<li id="mwB9E"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt667" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB9I" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;この辺は静かでは<u>ある</u>が、不便だ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kono hen wa shizuka de wa <u>aru</u> ga, fuben da.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|This area? Being quiet? <u>It is indeed</u>, but it's inconvenient.}}, {{xlat|This area IS quiet, but it's inconvenient}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kono hen wa shizuka de wa <u>aru</u> ga, fuben da.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt667" id="mwB9M"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">この辺は静かでは<u>ある</u>が、不便だ。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt668" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB9Q\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">This area? Being quiet? <u>It is indeed</u>, but it's inconvenient.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt669" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB9U\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>This area IS quiet, but it's inconvenient</span>)</span></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwB9Y">Sometimes <i id="mwB9c">de</i> and <i id="mwB9g">aru</i> can be split quite widely:<sup about="#mwt670" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTERubin2004113_89-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTERubin2004113&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERubin2004113-89&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rubin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;113&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTERubin2004113-89" id="mwB9k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9s">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9w">]</span></span></a></sup>
<ul id="mwB90"><li id="mwB94"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt673" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB98" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;意氣地なし！　そして全くその通り'''で'''私は<u>'''あつた'''</u>のだ。<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:<ruby>意<rp>(</rp><rt>い</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>氣<rp>(</rp><rt>く</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>地<rp>(</rp><rt>ぢ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>なし！　そして<ruby>全<rp>(</rp><rt>まつた</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>くその<ruby>通<rp>(</rp><rt>とほ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>りで<ruby>私<rp>(</rp><rt>わたし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>はあつたのだ。|page=13|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1177117/1/10|script-chapter=ja:一 私といふ人間|script-title=ja:苦の世界|series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|改造文庫}}|authorlink=Kōji Uno|first=Kōji|last=Uno|publisher=Kaizōsha|date=11 November 1932|location=[[Shiba, Tokyo]]}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ikuji nashi! So shite mattaku sono tōri '''de''' watashi wa <u>'''atta'''</u> no da.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{xlat|A wuss! I WAS exactly just that.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Ikuji nashi! So shite mattaku sono tōri <b>de</b> watashi wa <u><b>atta</b></u> no da.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt673" id="mwB-A"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">意氣地なし！　そして全くその通り<b>で</b>私は<u><b>あつた</b></u>のだ。<sup about="#mwt676" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-90" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-90&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-90" id="mwB-E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-M">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-Q">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt679" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwB-U\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>A wuss! I WAS exactly just that.</span>)</span></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwB-Y">While <i id="mwB-c">de nai/arimasen</i> are sometimes used in formal contexts, in ordinary speech <i id="mwB-g">ja nai/ja arimasen</i> are used instead. In this case, even though <i id="mwB-k">ja</i> is etymologically a colloquially reduced version of <i id="mwB-o">de wa</i>,<sup about="#mwt680" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018580–581&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations&quot;_(Adjectives)_10-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018580–581\&quot;Appendix 1 Basic Conjugations\&quot; (Adjectives)&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018580–581\&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations\&quot;_(Adjectives)-10&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Makino&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tsutsui&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2018&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;580–581&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Appendix 1 Basic Conjugations\&quot; (Adjectives)&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018580–581&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations&quot;_(Adjectives)-10" id="mwB-s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-0">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-4">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwB-8">ja nai/arimasen</i> are, functionally, colloquial versions of either <i id="mwB_A">de nai/arimasen</i>, which focus on what comes before them, or <i id="mwB_E">de wa nai/arimasen</i> which focus on <i id="mwB_I">nai/arimasen</i>. Some speakers distinguish the short <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt683" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB_M" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;じゃ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ja&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ja</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt683" id="mwB_Q"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">じゃ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> for <i id="mwB_U">de</i> and the long <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt684" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB_Y" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;じゃあ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;jā&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">jā</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt684" id="mwB_c"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">じゃあ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> for <i id="mwB_g">de wa</i>.<sup about="#mwt685" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004239,_373_91-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004239, 373&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004239,_373-91&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;239, 373&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004239,_373-91" id="mwB_k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_s">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_w">]</span></span></a></sup>
<ul id="mwB_0"><li id="mwB_4"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt688" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB_8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>マルクスとレニンの信者</u>でないですか・〜じゃありませんか&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<u>Marukusu to Renin no shinja</u> de nai desu ka /~ ja arimasen ka&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|Are they not <u>believers in Marx and Lenin</u>?}}, {{xlat|Aren't they BELIEVERS in Marx and Lenin?}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><u>Marukusu to Renin no shinja</u> de nai desu ka /~ ja arimasen ka</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt688" id="mwCAA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><u>マルクスとレニンの信者</u>でないですか・〜じゃありませんか</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt689" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwCAE\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Are they not <u>believers in Marx and Lenin</u>?</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt690" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwCAI\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Aren't they BELIEVERS in Marx and Lenin?</span>)</span></li>
<li id="mwCAM"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt691" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCAQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;マルクスとレニンの信者では<u>ない</u>ですか・〜じゃ(あ)<u>ありません</u>か&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Marukusu to Renin no shinja de wa <u>nai</u> desu ka /~ ja(a) <u>arimasen</u> ka&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|Believers in Marx and Lenin? <u>Is that not what they are?</u>}}, {{xlat|Are they NOT believers in Marx and Lenin?}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Marukusu to Renin no shinja de wa <u>nai</u> desu ka /~ ja(a) <u>arimasen</u> ka</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt691" id="mwCAU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">マルクスとレニンの信者では<u>ない</u>ですか・〜じゃ(あ)<u>ありません</u>か</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt692" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwCAY\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Believers in Marx and Lenin? <u>Is that not what they are?</u></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>, <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt693" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwCAc\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Are they NOT believers in Marx and Lenin?</span>)</span></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwCAg">While <i id="mwCAk">de (wa) arimasen</i> and <i id="mwCAo">de (wa) arimasen deshita</i> are often recommended, <i id="mwCAs">de (wa) nai desu</i> and <i id="mwCAw">de (wa) nakatta desu</i> are acceptable colloquial alternatives.<sup about="#mwt694" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004375,_1030_92-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004375, 1030&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004375,_1030-92&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;375, 1030&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004375,_1030-92" id="mwCA0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCA4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA8">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBA">]</span></span></a></sup> For the idiosyncratic <i id="mwCBE">de (wa) aranai</i> and <i id="mwCBI">de (wa) arimashinai</i>, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Negative:_Conjugation_table" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)" id="mwCBM">Negative: Conjugation table</a>.</li>
<li id="mwCBQ"><i id="mwCBU">De (wa) ar<b id="mwCBY">e</b>ba</i> is the regular way of forming <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Conditional" about="#mwt697" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCBc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[#Conditional|conditionals]]&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;仮定形&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kateikei&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">conditionals</a><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt697" id="mwCBg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">仮定形</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">, <span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">kateikei</i></span><span style="margin-left:.09em">)</span></span> in modern Japanese. <i id="mwCBk">Nar<b id="mwCBo">a</b>ba</i> (of said <i id="mwCBs">nari</i>) is kept as the conditional of <i id="mwCBw">da</i>, and along with <i id="mwCB0">tar<b id="mwCB4">a</b>ba</i> (of said <i id="mwCB8">te ari</i>/<i id="mwCCA">te aru</i> → <i id="mwCCE">tari</i>/<i id="mwCCI">taru</i> → <i id="mwCCM">ta</i>), retains the old way of forming conditionals. See <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Conditional:_Conjugation_table" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCCQ">#Conditional: Conjugation table</a> for more.</li>
<li id="mwCCU"><i id="mwCCY">Desu</i>, a copula of uncertain origin, takes its missing forms from <i id="mwCCc">de (wa) aru</i> and <i id="mwCCg">de (wa) arimasu</i>, the latter of which is conceivably the ancestor of <i id="mwCCk">desu</i>.<sup about="#mwt700" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-93" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-93&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-93" id="mwCCo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCw">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCC0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCC4">Although <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt701" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCC8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;なら(ば)&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nara(ba)&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nara(ba)</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt701" id="mwCDA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">なら(ば)</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt702" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCDE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;だろう&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;darō&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">darō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt702" id="mwCDI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">だろう</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt703" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCDM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;でしょう&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;deshō&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">deshō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt703" id="mwCDQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">でしょう</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> were originally conjugations of <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt704" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCDU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;だ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;da&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">da</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt704" id="mwCDY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">だ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt705" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCDc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;です&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;desu&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">desu</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt705" id="mwCDg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">です</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, they are now also used as particles or auxiliaries and can attach directly to other verbs' conclusive/attributive forms, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt706" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCDk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;書くなら(ば)&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kaku nara(ba)&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|if one writes}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kaku nara(ba)</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt706" id="mwCDo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">書くなら(ば)</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">if one writes</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt707" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCDs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;書くだろう・でしょう&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kaku darō/deshō&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|one will probably write}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kaku darō/deshō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt707" id="mwCDw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">書くだろう・でしょう</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">one will probably write</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>. <i id="mwCD0">Desu</i> (or <i id="mwCD4">de arimasu</i> or <i id="mwCD8">de gozaimasu</i>), <i id="mwCEA">deshita</i> and <i id="mwCEE">deshō</i> can add <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Politeness_stylization" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCEI">politeness</a> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Negative" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)" id="mwCEM">negative</a> auxiliaries <i id="mwCEQ">‑n(u)</i> and <i id="mwCEU">‑nai</i>, as well as adjectives:<sup about="#mwt708" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin20041030–1031,_1037_94-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin20041030–1031, 1037&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin20041030–1031,_1037-94&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1030–1031, 1037&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin20041030–1031,_1037-94" id="mwCEY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEg">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEk">]</span></span></a></sup>
<ul id="mwCEo"><li id="mwCEs"><i id="mwCEw">Arimasen/gozaimasen / nai desu/de arimasu/de gozaimasu / naku arimasu / nō gozaimasu</i> ("be not")</li>
<li id="mwCE0"><i id="mwCE4">Arimasen/gozaimasen deshō / nai deshō/de arimashō/de gozaimashō / naku arimashō / nō gozaimashō</i> ("be probably not")</li>
<li id="mwCE8"><i id="mwCFA">Arimasen/gozaimasen deshita / nakatta desu/de arimasu/de gozaimasu / naku arimashita / nō gozaimashita</i> ("were not")</li>
<li id="mwCFE"><i id="mwCFI">Arimasen/gozaimasen deshita deshō / nakatta deshō/de arimasu/de gozaimasu / naku arimashita deshō / nō gozaimashita deshō</i> ("were probably not")</li>
<li id="mwCFM"><i id="mwCFQ">Akai desu/de arimasu/de gozaimasu / akaku arimasu / akō gozaimasu</i> ("be red")</li>
<li id="mwCFU"><i id="mwCFY">Akai deshō/de arimashō/de gozaimashō / akaku arimashō / akō gozaimashō</i> ("be probably red")</li>
<li id="mwCFc"><i id="mwCFg">Akakatta desu/de arimasu/de gozaimasu / akaku arimashita / akō gozaimashita</i> ("were red")</li>
<li id="mwCFk"><i id="mwCFo">Akakatta deshō/de arimasu/de gozaimasu / akaku arimashita deshō / akō gozaimashita deshō</i> ("were probably red")</li></ul></li>
<li id="mwCFs">As shown above, <i id="mwCFw">desu</i> does not have its own negative form, and instead borrows <i id="mwCF0">de (wa) arimasen</i> from <i id="mwCF4">de (wa) arimasu</i>. However, the auxiliary <i id="mwCF8">‑n</i> in <i id="mwCGA">de (wa) arimasen</i> in turn does not have its own past and tentative form, therefore <i id="mwCGE">deshita</i> and <i id="mwCGI">deshō</i> have to be added. The past tentative <i id="mwCGM">‑tarō</i> is infrequent, thus instead of <i id="mwCGQ">deshitarō</i>, <i id="mwCGU">deshita deshō</i> is preferred.<sup about="#mwt713" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-95" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-95&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-95" id="mwCGY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGg">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGk">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwCGo">
<tbody id="mwCGs"><tr id="mwCGw"><th colspan="6" style="border-bottom:none" id="mwCG0">Stems without <i id="mwCG4">aru</i></th></tr>
<tr id="mwCG8">
<th colspan="2" style="border-top:none" id="mwCHA"></th>
<th id="mwCHE">Uncontracted</th>
<th id="mwCHI">Contracted</th>
<td colspan="2" style="border-bottom:none" id="mwCHM"></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCHQ">
<th rowspan="2" colspan="2" id="mwCHU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Infinitive" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwCHY">Infinitive</a></th>
<td id="mwCHc"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt714" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCHg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;に&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ni&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ni</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt714" id="mwCHk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">に</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCHo">
<td id="mwCHs"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt715" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCHw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;で&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;de&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">de</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt715" id="mwCH0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">で</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCH4">
<th colspan="2" id="mwCH8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Gerund" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwCIA">Gerund</a></th>
<td id="mwCIE"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt716" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCII" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;にて&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nite&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nite</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt716" id="mwCIM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">にて</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td id="mwCIQ"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt717" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCIU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;で&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;de&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">de</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt717" id="mwCIY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">で</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCIc">
<th colspan="2" id="mwCIg">Attributive</th>
<td id="mwCIk"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt718" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCIo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:Nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;の&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;no&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">no</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt718" id="mwCIs"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">の</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCIw">
<td colspan="6" style="border-top:none" id="mwCI0"></td></tr>
