</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwDIM" aria-labelledby="Copulae:_Grammatical_compatibility"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Copulae:_Grammatical_compatibility">Copulae: Grammatical compatibility</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Copulae: Grammatical compatibility"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDIQ">Derived from <i id="mwDIU">aru</i> and <i id="mwDIY">arimasu</i>, the copulae can have all the forms that these verbs are capable of having. Certain affirmative conclusive and attributive forms have contracted, especially in speech, such as <i id="mwDIc">de aru</i> → <i id="mwDIg">da</i>/<i id="mwDIk">ja</i> and <i id="mwDIo">de arimasu</i> → <i id="mwDIs">desu</i>; the negative forms remain uncontracted, meaning there is no such form as *<i id="mwDIw">daran</i> or *<i id="mwDI0">desen</i>.</p>

<p id="mwDI4"><span class="anchor" id="mwDI8" about="#mwt1256" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-x-id="終止形" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;anchor&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Anchor&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;終止形&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;shūshikei&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;shushikei&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;conclusive&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;predicative&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;連体形&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rentaikei&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;attributive&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;imperfect&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;辞典形&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;dictionary form&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></span><span class="anchor" id="shūshikei" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="shushikei" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="conclusive" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="predicative" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="連体形" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="rentaikei" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="attributive" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="imperfect" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="辞典形" about="#mwt1256"></span><span class="anchor" id="dictionary_form" about="#mwt1256"></span></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwDJA" aria-labelledby="Imperfective"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Imperfective">Imperfective</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Imperfective"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1257" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDJE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (imperfective form)&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1258" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1257" id="mwDJI">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(imperfective_form)" title="Japanese conjugation (imperfective form)">Japanese conjugation (imperfective form)</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwDJM" aria-labelledby="Negative"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Negative">Negative</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Negative"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1259" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDJQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)#Negative&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1260" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1259" id="mwDJU">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Negative" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)">Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Negative</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwDJY" aria-labelledby="Passive"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Passive">Passive</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Passive"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1261" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDJc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)#Passive&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1262" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1261" id="mwDJg">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Passive" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)">Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Passive</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwDJk" aria-labelledby="Potential"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Potential">Potential</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Potential"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1263" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDJo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)#Potential&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1264" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1263" id="mwDJs">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Potential" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)">Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Potential</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwDJw" aria-labelledby="Causative"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Causative">Causative</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Causative"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1265" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDJ0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)#Causative&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1266" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1265" id="mwDJ4">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Causative" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)">Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Causative</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwDJ8" aria-labelledby="Hortative"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Hortative">Hortative</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: Hortative"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1267" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDKA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)#Hortative&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1268" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1267" id="mwDKE">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Hortative" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)">Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Hortative</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwDKI" aria-labelledby="Infinitive"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Infinitive">Infinitive</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Infinitive"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1269" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDKM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)#Infinitive&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1270" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1269" id="mwDKQ">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Infinitive" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)">Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Infinitive</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwDKU" aria-labelledby="Gerund"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Gerund">Gerund</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section: Gerund"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1271" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDKY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)#Gerund&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1272" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1271" id="mwDKc">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Gerund" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)">Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Gerund</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwDKg" aria-labelledby="Perfective"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Perfective">Perfective</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17" title="Edit section: Perfective"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1273" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDKk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)#Perfective&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt1274" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1273" id="mwDKo">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Perfective" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)">Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base) §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Perfective</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwDKs" aria-labelledby="Imperative"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Imperative">Imperative</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18" title="Edit section: Imperative"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDKw">The <b id="mwDK0">imperative</b> usually expresses the speaker's wish. When directed at a specific sentient <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agent_(grammar)" title="Agent (grammar)" id="mwDK4">agent</a>, such as a human or an animal, it functions as a command, an instruction, or a motivational statement that compels the agent to realize the wish. Plain commands with non-honorific verbs (which are the majority of verbs) towards people in particular are terse, and can be softened by the imperatives of verbs of favor, such as <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1275" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDK8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;(御)呉れ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;(o)kure&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">(o)kure</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1275" id="mwDLA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">(御)呉れ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1276" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDLE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;下さい(ませ)&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kudasai(mase)&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|do me/us a favor!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kudasai(mase)</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1276" id="mwDLI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">下さい(ませ)</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1277" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwDLM\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">do me/us a favor!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> following the main verb's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Gerund:_Grammatical_compatibility" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwDLQ">gerund</a>, although for colloquial brevity, the favor verbs can contract as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1278" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDLU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;行っておくれ→行っとくれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;itte okure → ittokure&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|[do me a favor and] go!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">itte okure → ittokure</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1278" id="mwDLY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">行っておくれ→行っとくれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">[do me a favor and] go!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, or be <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellipsis_(linguistics)" title="Ellipsis (linguistics)" id="mwDLc">elliptically</a> omitted as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1279" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDLg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;行ってください→行って&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;itte kudasai → itte&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|[do me a favor and] please go!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">itte kudasai → itte</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1279" id="mwDLk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">行ってください→行って</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">[do me a favor and] please go!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>. Another option is to use the imperative of the honorific verb <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1280" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDLo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;為さい(ませ)&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nasai(mase)&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{lit|do!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nasai(mase)</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1280" id="mwDLs"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">為さい(ませ)</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1281" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwDLw\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">do!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> following the main verb's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Infinitive:_Grammatical_compatibility" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwDL0">infinitive</a>.</p>

<p id="mwDL4">When not directed at a specific sentient agent, but rather the general idea of an agent ("let women/men/dogs/cats/etc be/do something," "may you rest in peace"), a non-sentient agent ("let rain/snow fall," "let wind blow"), or nothing ("peace be unto you"), the wish becomes impersonal and does not have the abrupt force of a command. Whether the agent is sentient or not, and specific or not, it can be optionally marked with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vocative" title="Vocative" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDL8">vocative</a> particle <i id="mwDMA">yo</i> (similar to the English <i id="mwDME">o</i>). Imperatives can also be part of a concessive clause similarly to the English <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subjunctive" title="Subjunctive" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDMI">subjunctive</a> ("whatever it be", "be it this or that", "come rain or shine").</p>

<table class="wikitable floatleft" id="mwDMM">
<caption style="text-align:left" id="mwDMQ">Imperative form example sentences</caption>
<tbody id="mwDMU"><tr id="mwDMY">
<th id="mwDMc">English</th>
<th id="mwDMg">Japanese</th>
<th id="mwDMk">Function</th></tr>
<tr id="mwDMo">
<td id="mwDMs">“Class started! Sit down, you dogs!”</td>
<td id="mwDMw"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1282" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDM0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「授業を始めるぜ。'''座れ'''！　犬ども！」<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-title=ja:ちゅーちゅーエンジェル|last=Itō|first=Chihaya|publisher=PHP Institute|location=[[Kōtō]], Tokyo|date=9 May 2012|script-chapter=ja:第５章 パンの耳はひのせの主食⁉}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Jugyō o hajimeru ze. '''Suware'''! Inudomo!”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Jugyō o hajimeru ze. <b>Suware</b>! Inudomo!”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1282" id="mwDM4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「授業を始めるぜ。<b>座れ</b>！　犬ども！」<sup about="#mwt1285" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-226" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-226&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-226" id="mwDM8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNE">[</span>213<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNI">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="13" id="mwDNM">plain command</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDNQ">
<td id="mwDNU">“We are camping here tonight. Eat dinner and go to sleep early.”<br id="mwDNY">[…]<br id="mwDNc">“Rise, wake up your men at once. Quietly, without making any noise.”</td>
<td id="mwDNg"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1288" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDNk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「今晩はここで野営とする。早く飯を食って、早く'''寝よ'''」<br/>[…]<br/>「'''起きよ'''、すぐに兵を'''起こせ'''。物音を立てず静かに起こすのだ」<ref name=ito-2010>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:「今晩はここで野営とする。早く飯を食って、早く寝よ」<br/>織田勢の使い番たちは、あまり例のない命令を触れて回った。夜襲を警戒せよとの命令はよく出るが、早く寝よなどという、子どもに注意するような命令は異例であった。<br/>秋の夜は長い、あまり早く寝すぎると、夜中に目が覚めてしまって、そのあと眠ることができなくなり、かえって疲れることも多い。寝るにもころあいの時間というものがあった。<br/>とにかく、早く寝よとの信長の命令であったから、飯を食い終わると早々に誰しもが寝た。<br/><ruby>丑<rp>(</rp><rt>うし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の刻（午前二時ごろ）になると、信長の本営から使いが走り出し、各部隊の責任者を起こして回った。<br/>「起きよ、すぐに兵を起こせ。物音を立てず静かに起こすのだ」<br/>眠気眼をこすっている者たちが、次々と起きだしていく。夜中に起こされたのであるから、次の行動はおおよそ想像が付く。|trans-quote=“We are camping here tonight. Eat dinner and go to sleep early.”<br/>The messengers among the Oda troops passed the highly unprecedented order around. Orders to be on guard against night raids were common, but one to sleep early, as would be issued to children, was unusual.<br/>Autumnal nights were long, thus if one slept too early, one would end up awake in the middle of the night, unable to fall back asleep, and ultimately all the more tired. There was an appropriate time for sleep.<br/>At all events, since Nobunaga’s order was to sleep early, everyone finished dinner and promptly went to sleep.<br/>During the [[Ox (zodiac)#Hour of the Ox|hours of the Ox]] (around 2 AM), a messenger ran out from Nobunaga’s headquarters and woke up the leader of each unit.<br/>“Rise, wake up your men at once. Quietly, without making any noise.”<br/>The men were rubbing their sleepy eyes as they rose one after another. Since they were woken up in the middle of the night, one could imagine what they would be doing next.|script-chapter=ja:第一章 狂虎の咆哮|trans-chapter=Chapter One: The Roar of the Mad Tiger|script-title=ja:安土大乱記　狂気の終焉|trans-title=The Great [[Azuchi]] Rebellion: The End of the Madness|volume=2|series=Rekishi Gunzo Books|first=Hiroshi|last=Itō|publisher=Gakken|year=2010}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Konban wa koko de yaei to suru. Hayaku meshi o kutte, hayaku '''neyo'''”<br/>[…]<br/>“'''Okiyo''', sugu ni hei o '''okose'''. Monooto o tatezu shizuka ni okosu no da”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Konban wa koko de yaei to suru. Hayaku meshi o kutte, hayaku <b>neyo</b>”<br>[…]<br>“<b>Okiyo</b>, sugu ni hei o <b>okose</b>. Monooto o tatezu shizuka ni okosu no da”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1288" id="mwDNo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「今晩はここで野営とする。早く飯を食って、早く<b>寝よ</b>」<br>[…]<br>「<b>起きよ</b>、すぐに兵を<b>起こせ</b>。物音を立てず静かに起こすのだ」<sup about="#mwt1291" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ito-2010_227-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ito-2010&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ito-2010-227&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ito-2010-227" id="mwDNs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDN0">[</span>214<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDN4">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDN8">
<td id="mwDOA">“O wind, blow, rage! Blow!”</td>
<td id="mwDOE"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1294" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDOI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「風よ、'''吹け'''、'''荒れよ'''！　'''吹け'''よ！」――<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-chapter=ja:リヤ王|chapter=King Lear|authorlink=William Shakespeare|first1=William|last1=Shakespeare|last2=Hirata|first2=Tokuboku|script-title=ja:シェイクスピア物語|trans-title=Shakespeare’s Tales|date=30 April 1947|location=[[Chūō, Tokyo]]|publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|文壽堂出版部}}|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1168434/1/80|page=149}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Kaze yo, '''fuke''', '''areyo'''! '''Fuke''' yo!”――&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Kaze yo, <b>fuke</b>, <b>areyo</b>! <b>Fuke</b> yo!”――</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1294" id="mwDOM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「風よ、<b>吹け</b>、<b>荒れよ</b>！　<b>吹け</b>よ！」――<sup about="#mwt1297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-228" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-228&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-228" id="mwDOQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDOU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOY">[</span>215<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOc">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDOg">
<td id="mwDOk">“Wreck that mountain castle! Make it rain! Make the wind blow!”</td>
<td id="mwDOo"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1300" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDOs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「あの山の城を'''くずしてしまへ'''！　雨よ'''降れ'''。風よ'''吹け'''。」<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|page=35|script-chapter=ja:<ruby>龍<rp>(</rp><rt>りう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>宮<rp>(</rp><rt>ぐう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>へ行つた木こり|script-title=ja:南方童話の旅|last=Watanabe|first=Saburō|location=[[Kanda, Tokyo]]|publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|帝敎書房}}|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1717525/1/23|script-quote=ja:山の神樣の仕合せなやうすを見て、ねたましく思つた神さまがあつたのです。それは、水の神樣でした。水の神樣は、多ぜいの<ruby>家<rp>(</rp><rt>け</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>來<rp>(</rp><rt>らい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>命<rp>(</rp><rt>めい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>令<rp>(</rp><rt>れい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>しました。<br/>「あの山の城をくずしてしまへ！　雨よ降れ。風よ吹け。」<br/>さあ、かうなると大へんです。見る見るうちに大空はまつ黑な雲がおひかぶさつて、ドツドツとはげしい風が吹き出し、ザアツザアツと强い雨が振り出しました。}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Ano yama no shiro o '''kuzushite shimae'''! Ame yo '''fure'''. Kaze yo '''fuke'''.”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Ano yama no shiro o <b>kuzushite shimae</b>! Ame yo <b>fure</b>. Kaze yo <b>fuke</b>.”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1300" id="mwDOw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「あの山の城を<b>くずしてしまへ</b>！　雨よ<b>降れ</b>。風よ<b>吹け</b>。」<sup about="#mwt1303" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-229" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-229&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-229" id="mwDO0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDO4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDO8">[</span>216<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPA">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDPE">
<td id="mwDPI">All you bastards that crushed her‼ Die, die, just die‼ Bomba‼ Kill them‼ All of them‼</td>
<td id="mwDPM"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1306" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDPQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;先生をおしつぶしたやつら‼みんな'''死ね　死ね　死んじまえっ'''　ボンバ‼やつらを'''殺せっ'''　ひとリのこらず殺すんだ‼<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:先生……先生――っ！だれが殺した……だれが殺したんだ‼そいつは殺人犯だ　おれが……復讐してやるぞ　先生をおしつぶしたやつら‼みんな死ね　死ね　死んじまえっ　ボンバ‼やつらを殺せっ　ひとリのこらず殺すんだ‼|trans-quote=Miss…… Miss Mizushima――! Who did it…… Who murdered her⁉ They’re murderers! I’ll…… make them pay! All you bastards that [[Crowd collapses and crushes|crushed]] her‼ Die, die, just die‼ Bomba‼ Kill them‼ All of them‼|pages=79–80|script-title=ja:ボンバ！|trans-title=[[Bomba!]]|series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|手塚治虫漫画全集}}|volume=93|date=10 May 2000|edition=8th|publisher=Kodansha|location=[[Bunkyō]], Tokyo|isbn=4-06-108693-6|last=Tezuka|first=Osamu|authorlink=Osamu Tezuka}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sensei o oshitsubushita yatsura‼ Minna '''shine Shine Shinjimaeh''' Bonba‼ Yatsura o '''koroseh''' Hitori nokorazu korosu n da‼&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sensei o oshitsubushita yatsura‼ Minna <b>shine Shine Shinjimaeh</b> Bonba‼ Yatsura o <b>koroseh</b> Hitori nokorazu korosu n da‼</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1306" id="mwDPU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">先生をおしつぶしたやつら‼みんな<b>死ね　死ね　死んじまえっ</b>　ボンバ‼やつらを<b>殺せっ</b>　ひとリのこらず殺すんだ‼<sup about="#mwt1309" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-230" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-230&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-230" id="mwDPY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPg">[</span>217<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPk">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDPo">
<td id="mwDPs">Drop dead, Kenneth! You die too, Doctor‼</td>
<td id="mwDPw"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1312" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDP0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ケネス'''死ね'''　先生も'''死んじゃえ'''‼<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:うそです　先生はお金たくさんもらうからなおすんだ<br/>先生　お金もらうだめ　手術やるだめ　お願いです<br/>先生　悪い人に味方するいけない　あいつ助けないの‼<br/>金をもらうのがなぜ悪い？おおきなお世話だっ<br/>ケネス死ね　先生も死んじゃえ‼|trans-quote=You’re lying! You’re only treating him because he’s paying you a lot of money!<br/>Doctor, don’t take his money, don’t do the surgery, please!<br/>You can’t side with the bad guy! Don’t help him‼<br/>What’s wrong with taking money? It’s none of your damn business!<br/>Drop dead, Kenneth! You die too, Doctor‼|pages=94–95|script-title=ja:ブラック・ジャック|trans-title=[[Black Jack (manga)|Black Jack]]|series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|手塚治虫漫画全集}}|volume=11|date=20 January 2000|edition=8th|publisher=Kodansha|location=[[Bunkyō]], Tokyo|isbn=4-06-108761-4|last=Tezuka|first=Osamu|authorlink=Osamu Tezuka}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kenesu '''shine''' Sensei mo '''shinjae'''‼&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kenesu <b>shine</b> Sensei mo <b>shinjae</b>‼</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1312" id="mwDP4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">ケネス<b>死ね</b>　先生も<b>死んじゃえ</b>‼<sup about="#mwt1315" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-231" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-231&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-231" id="mwDP8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQE">[</span>218<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQI">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDQM">
<td id="mwDQQ">If not, think of your own father for a change!</td>
<td id="mwDQU"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1318" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDQY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;さもなけりや貴樣、自分の父のことを'''考へても見ろ'''！<ref name=\&quot;mori-1943\&quot;>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:「僕は氣持は靜かで、手もとも狂つちやゐない」と彼は四邊を見廻しながら云つた。「先づ、諸君の中で、自分の父を愛さなかつた者があるか、父の想ひ出を嫌ふやうな屈辱な生れかたをした者があるか。見給へ、諸君はこの沈默がお解りだらう？　平和の神の僧となつて、神聖とか宗敎とか年中口にしながら、腹の黑い貴樣のやうな奴は父の何たるを知らないんだ。さもなけりや貴樣、自分の父のことを考へても見ろ！　貴樣が馬鹿にしてる、この會衆の中に貴樣のやうな奴は一人も居ないぞツ。貴樣は奈落の底へ落つべき奴だ！」|trans-quote=“My mind is calm, my hand is steady,” he said, looking around. “First, is there one among you who has not loved his father, who was born in such humiliation that he hates his memory? See? You understand this silence? Priest of a God of peace, your mouth is full of sanctity and religion, yet you black-hearted knave do not know what a father is supposed to be. If not, think of your own father for a change! In this crowd which you scorn there is not a single knave like you. You deserve to go to the depths of hell!”|quote=—Mi corazón late tranquilo, mi mano va segura…<br/>Y mirando alrededor suyo:<br/>—Antes, ¿hay entre vosotros alguno que no haya amado a su padre, que haya odiado su memoria, alguno nacido en la vergüenza y la humillación…? ¿Ves?, ¿oyes ese silencio? Sacerdote de un Dios de paz, que tienes la boca llena de santidad y religión, y el corazón de miseria, tú no debiste conocer lo que es un padre… ¡hubieras pensado en el tuyo! ¿Ves? ¡Entre esa multitud que tú desprecias no hay uno como tú! ¡Estás juzgado!|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1136958/1/174|p=321|script-chapter=ja:34　午餐會|chapter=XXXIV La comida|trans-chapter=34 The Luncheon|title=Noli me tángere|trans-title=[[Noli Me Tángere (novel)|Awaiting Dawn]]|script-title=ja:黎明を待つ|authorlink=José Rizal|first=José Protasio|last=Rizal Mercado y Alonso Realonda|date=20 January 1943|translator-last=Mōri|translator-first=Yasotarō|publisher=Dainippon Shuppan|location=[[Kyōbashi, Tokyo]]}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sa mo nakerya kisama, jibun no chichi no koto o '''kangaete mo miro'''!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sa mo nakerya kisama, jibun no chichi no koto o <b>kangaete mo miro</b>!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1318" id="mwDQc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">さもなけりや貴樣、自分の父のことを<b>考へても見ろ</b>！<sup about="#mwt1321" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-mori-1943_232-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;mori-1943&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-mori-1943-232&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-mori-1943-232" id="mwDQg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQo">[</span>219<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQs">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDQw">
<td id="mwDQ0">[Do me a favor and] stop making things worse, I beg of you!</td>
<td id="mwDQ4"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1324" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDQ8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;これ以上事を'''荒立てないでくれ'''、頼むよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kore ijō koto o '''aradatenai de kure''', tanomu yo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kore ijō koto o <b>aradatenai de kure</b>, tanomu yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1324" id="mwDRA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">これ以上事を<b>荒立てないでくれ</b>、頼むよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDRE">
<td id="mwDRI">[Do me a favor and] please call me “Satchan.”</td>
<td id="mwDRM"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1325" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDRQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;私を「さっちゃん」と'''呼んでください'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Watashi o “Satchan” to '''yonde kudasai'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Watashi o “Satchan” to <b>yonde kudasai</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1325" id="mwDRU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">私を「さっちゃん」と<b>呼んでください</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDRY">
<td id="mwDRc">[Do me a favor and] please make use of this elevator.</td>
<td id="mwDRg"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1326" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDRk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;どうぞこちらのエレベーターを'''ご利用くださいませ'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Dō zo kochira no erebētā '''goriyō kudasaimase'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Dō zo kochira no erebētā <b>goriyō kudasaimase</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1326" id="mwDRo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">どうぞこちらのエレベーターを<b>ご利用くださいませ</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDRs">
<td id="mwDRw">Read the contract well before stamping.</td>
<td id="mwDR0"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1327" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDR4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;押印する前に契約書をよく'''読みなさい'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ōin suru mae ni keiyakusho o yoku '''yominasai'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Ōin suru mae ni keiyakusho o yoku <b>yominasai</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1327" id="mwDR8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">押印する前に契約書をよく<b>読みなさい</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDSA">
<td id="mwDSE">Welcome home!</td>
<td id="mwDSI"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1328" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDSM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''お帰りなさいませ'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''Okaerinasaimase'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><b>Okaerinasaimase</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1328" id="mwDSQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><b>お帰りなさいませ</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span><sup about="#mwt1329" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-241" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-241&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Literally, \&quot;come home, please!\&quot;. ''Okaerinasai(mase)'' is used idiomatically as a greeting to a coresident who has just come home.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E3%81%8A%E5%B8%B0%E3%82%8A%E3%81%AA%E3%81%95%E3%81%84-3227453|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:お帰りなさい}}</ref> It can be colloquially reduced to ''okaennasai'', ''okainnasai'',<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%BE%A1%E5%B8%B0%E3%82%8B%E7%82%BA%E3%81%95%E3%82%8B-451191|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:御帰りなさい}}</ref> or just ''okaeri''.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%BE%A1%E5%B8%B0-2015258|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:御帰}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E3%81%8A%E5%B8%B0%E3%82%8A-451190|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:お帰り}}</ref> Other idiomatic phrases with ''‑nasai(mase)'' include {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||お休み(なさい)|oyasumi(nasai)|{{lit|rest, please!}}; {{xlat|sleep well; good night}}}},<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%BE%A1%E4%BC%91%E3%81%BF%E3%81%AA%E3%81%95%E3%81%84-455049|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:御休みなさい}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%BE%A1%E4%BC%91-2018367|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:御休}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%BE%A1%E4%BC%91%E3%81%BF-455048|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:御休み}}</ref> {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||御免(なさい)|gomen (nasai)|{{lit|forgive me, please!}}; {{xlat|I'm sorry; my apologies}}}},<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%BE%A1%E5%85%8D%E3%81%AA%E3%81%95%E3%81%84-504815|script-work=ja:コトバンク|script-title=ja:御免なさい}}</ref> etc.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-241" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDSU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDSY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSc">[</span>n<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSg">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDSk">
<td id="mwDSo">Don’t make fun of gossip shows. Don’t jeer at the “voyeur’s spirit”.</td>
<td id="mwDSs"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1392" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDSw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ワイドショーをバカにする'''なかれ'''。「やじうま精神」を笑う'''なかれ'''、である。<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:知的好奇心に無縁どころか、人間観察という知的訓練の恰好の機会になると思う。<br/>ワイドショーをバカにするなかれ。「やじうま精神」を笑うなかれ、である。<br/>もちろん、人の不幸を喜ぶようなあさましい気持ちで見るのなら、それこそ最低の「やじうま」だ。<br/>社会に対する関心と問題意識を持って、ことの子細をもっと知りたいと思うかどうかが、ただの「やじうま」と「やじうま精神の持ち主」の違いなのだ。|trans-quote=In my opinion, far from having nothing to do with intellectual curiosity, such activity as observing people will be a great opportunity for intellectual training.<br/>Don’t make fun of gossip shows. Don't jeer at the \&quot;voyeur's spirit\&quot;.<br/>Of course, if all you do is gawk at other people's misfortune with sordid glee, you're nothing but a contemptible \&quot;voyeur\&quot;.<br/>The difference between a mere \&quot;voyeur\&quot; and \&quot;one with the voyeur's spirit\&quot; is whether or not you have an interest in and awareness of society, and you want to learn more about it.|script-chapter=ja:13●やじうま精神を笑うなかれ|trans-chapter=13●Don't jeer at the voyeur's spirit|script-title=ja:<ruby>凛<rp>(</rp><rt>りん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>とした生き方　自分の人生、自分で決める|date=1 March 2011|isbn=978-4-569-67602-9|series=PHP{{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|文庫}}|publisher=PHP Institute|location=[[Kōtō]], Tokyo|authorlink=Birei Kin|first=Birei|last=Kin}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Waido shō o baka ni suru '''nakare'''. “Yajiuma seishin” o warau '''nakare''', de aru.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Waido shō o baka ni suru <b>nakare</b>. “Yajiuma seishin” o warau <b>nakare</b>, de aru.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1392" id="mwDS0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">ワイドショーをバカにする<b>なかれ</b>。「やじうま精神」を笑う<b>なかれ</b>、である。<sup about="#mwt1395" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-242" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-242&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-242" id="mwDS4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDS8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTA">[</span>228<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTE">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDTI">
<td id="mwDTM">STOP<sup about="#mwt1398" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-243" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-243&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;A stop sign.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-243" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTY">[</span>o<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTc">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td id="mwDTg"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1401" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDTk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''止まれ'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'''TOMARE'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn"><b>TOMARE</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1401" id="mwDTo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><b>止まれ</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="3" id="mwDTs">instructional command</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDTw">
<td id="mwDT0">Read the following passage and answer the questions.</td>
<td id="mwDT4"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1402" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDT8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;次の文を読んで問いに'''答えよ'''。<ref>{{citation|lang=ja|title=EurekaⅩⅢ|number=11|date=13 June 2025|url=https://www.mie-mie-h.ed.jp/junior/schoollife/dl_magazine.php?news_id=907|publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|三重高等学校}}}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tsugi no bun o yonde toi ni '''kotaeyo'''.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Tsugi no bun o yonde toi ni <b>kotaeyo</b>.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1402" id="mwDUA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">次の文を読んで問いに<b>答えよ</b>。<sup about="#mwt1405" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-244" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-244&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-244" id="mwDUE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUM">[</span>229<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUQ">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDUU">
<td id="mwDUY">[…] ⑦ Thou shalt not engage in road rage. ⑧ Show proper decorum to thy fellow drivers. […]</td>
<td id="mwDUc"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1408" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDUg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[…]⑦怒る'''なかれ'''．⑧運転者同士礼義'''正しくあれ'''．[…]<ref>{{#invoke:cite|journal|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:四季を通じ，ハイウエイでは次の10箇条を守るべきである，①車にて殺人するなかれ．②ガソリンにアルコールを混合するな．③速度制限を守れ．④前の車にあまり近ずくな．⑤細い小路から小路へ渡り歩くな．⑥シグナルを見損なうな．⑦怒るなかれ．⑧運転者同士礼義正しくあれ．⑨歩行者と自転車に親切に．⑩交通法規を守れ．|trans-quote=The following are the 10 commandments to obey on the highway throughout the seasons: ① Thou shalt not kill by means of a vehicle. ② Thou shalt not mix alcohol with gasoline. ③ Obey the speed limit. ④ Thou shalt not tailgate the vehicle before thee. ⑤ Thou shalt not weave from one narrow lane to another. ⑥ Thou shalt not miss a signal. ⑦ Thou shalt not engage in road rage. ⑧ Show proper decorum to thy fellow drivers. ⑨ Be kind to pedestrians and cyclists. ⑩ Obey traffic law.|page=20|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/7902789/1/14|script-title=ja:交通，運輸，郵便，信号|script-journal=ja:科学技術文献速報|journal=Current Bibliography on Science and Technology|volume=5|number=14|date=25 October 1962|publisher=Japan Information Center of Science and Technology}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[…] ⑦ Okoru '''nakare'''. ⑧ Untensha dōshi reigi '''tadashiku are'''. […]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">[…] ⑦ Okoru <b>nakare</b>. ⑧ Untensha dōshi reigi <b>tadashiku are</b>. […]</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1408" id="mwDUk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">[…]⑦怒る<b>なかれ</b>．⑧運転者同士礼義<b>正しくあれ</b>．[…]<sup about="#mwt1411" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-245" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-245&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-245" id="mwDUo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUw">[</span>230<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDU0">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDU4">
<td id="mwDU8">New PR member, do your best!</td>
<td id="mwDVA"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1414" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDVE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;広報新メンバー'''頑張れ'''！<ref>{{#invoke:cite|journal|lang=ja|last=Takita|first=Hitoshi|script-title=ja:三階席|date=15 July 2023|script-journal=ja:町議会だより おおなん|number=85|url=https://www.town.ohnan.lg.jp/www/contents/1681688489561/simple/gikaidayori85gou.pdf|location=[[Ōnan, Shimane]]|page=4}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kōhō shin-menbā '''ganbare'''!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kōhō shin-menbā <b>ganbare</b>!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1414" id="mwDVI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">広報新メンバー<b>頑張れ</b>！<sup about="#mwt1417" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-246" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-246&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-246" id="mwDVM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVU">[</span>231<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVY">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="5" id="mwDVc">motivational command</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDVg">
<td id="mwDVk">I won’t let you die‼………… Live, for me‼</td>
<td id="mwDVo"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1420" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDVs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;死ぬことは許さん‼…………俺のために'''生きろ'''‼<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-title=ja:がくらん海峡|volume=3|first=Norihiro|last=Nakajima|date=25 March 1980|publisher=Offce MAN}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Shinu koto wa yurusan‼………… Ore no tame ni '''ikiro'''‼&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Shinu koto wa yurusan‼………… Ore no tame ni <b>ikiro</b>‼</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1420" id="mwDVw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">死ぬことは許さん‼…………俺のために<b>生きろ</b>‼<sup about="#mwt1423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-247" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-247&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-247" id="mwDV0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDV4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDV8">[</span>232<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWA">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDWE">
<td id="mwDWI">Stay hungry! Stay foolish!<sup about="#mwt1426" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-248" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-248&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;A quote attributed to [[Steve Jobs]].&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-248" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDWM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWU">[</span>p<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWY">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td id="mwDWc"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1429" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDWg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ハングリー'''であれ'''！愚か'''であれ'''！&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Hangurī '''de are'''! Oroka '''de are'''!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Hangurī <b>de are</b>! Oroka <b>de are</b>!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1429" id="mwDWk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">ハングリー<b>であれ</b>！愚か<b>であれ</b>！</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDWo">
<td id="mwDWs">If you’re strong, stay strong till the end!<br id="mwDWw">If you’re weak, stay weak till the end!</td>
<td id="mwDW0"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1430" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDW4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;强ければ、あくまでも'''强くあれ'''！<br/>弱ければ、飽くまでも'''弱くあれ'''！<ref name=nagai-1948>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1130217/1/66|page=118|script-chapter=ja:日記|script-title=ja:女の幸をしみ〲と思ふ|date=15 November 1948|last=Nagai|first=Tazuko|editor-last=Nagai|editor-first=Hisomu|publisher=Izumo Shobō|location=[[Chūō, Tokyo]]|script-quote=ja:强ければ、あくまでも强くあれ！<br/>弱ければ、飽くまでも弱くあれ！<br/>何事も、徹底しなくてはいけない。善いにしろ、惡いにしろ、何かを完了した人間の活き方は、美しい。<br/>ひた向きな道をゆく人は、自分も樂しからうし、人も亦た、讓らずにはゐられない。}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tsuyokereba, aku made mo '''tsuyoku are'''!<br/>Yowakereba, aku made mo '''yowaku are'''!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Tsuyokereba, aku made mo <b>tsuyoku are</b>!<br>Yowakereba, aku made mo <b>yowaku are</b>!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1430" id="mwDW8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">强ければ、あくまでも<b>强くあれ</b>！<br>弱ければ、飽くまでも<b>弱くあれ</b>！<sup about="#mwt1433" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nagai-1948_249-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nagai-1948&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-nagai-1948-249&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-nagai-1948-249" id="mwDXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXI">[</span>233<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXM">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDXQ">
<td id="mwDXU">[…] Be just!<br id="mwDXY">Be strong! Be good! Show strength!</td>
<td id="mwDXc"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1436" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDXg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[…]'''正しかれ<br/>強かれ 善かれ''' 力'''あれ'''<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.kudamatsu-t.ysn21.jp/songs/yamakou-ouenka.html|script-title=ja:山工応援歌|website=Kudamatsu Technical High School}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[…] '''Tadashikare<br/>Tsuyokare Yokare''' Chikara '''are'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">[…] <b>Tadashikare<br>Tsuyokare Yokare</b> Chikara <b>are</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1436" id="mwDXk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">[…]<b>正しかれ<br>強かれ 善かれ</b> 力<b>あれ</b><sup about="#mwt1439" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-250" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-250&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-250" id="mwDXo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXw">[</span>234<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDX0">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDX4">
<td id="mwDX8">Let it rain‼ […] Rain, storm……‼ One more time………… Keep pouring for just one more time, please‼</td>
<td id="mwDYA"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1442" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDYE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;雨よ'''降れ'''‼[…]雨よ　嵐よ……‼もう一度…………せめてもう一度'''降り続いておくれ'''‼<ref name=ishii-2016>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:<ruby>雨<rp>(</rp><rt>あめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>………どしゃ<ruby>降<rp>(</rp><rt>ぶ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>りの<ruby>雨<rp>(</rp><rt>あめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>……‼ああ　この<ruby>雨<rp>(</rp><rt>あめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が…………あす一<ruby>日<rp>(</rp><rt>にち</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>やまなければいい‼いいえ　あすもあさっても五<ruby>日<rp>(</rp><rt>か</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>も十<ruby>日<rp>(</rp><rt>か</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>も一か<ruby>月<rp>(</rp><rt>げつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>も……<ruby>雨<rp>(</rp><rt>あめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<ruby>降<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>り<ruby>続<rp>(</rp><rt>つづ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>いてくれたら…………<ruby>雨<rp>(</rp><rt>あめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>よ……<ruby>雨<rp>(</rp><rt>あめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>よ<ruby>降<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>れ‼<ruby>大<rp>(</rp><rt>おお</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>昔<rp>(</rp><rt>むかし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>…………………<ruby>何<rp>(</rp><rt>なん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>万<rp>(</rp><rt>まん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>年<rp>(</rp><rt>ねん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>何<rp>(</rp><rt>なん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>千<rp>(</rp><rt>ぜん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>万<rp>(</rp><rt>まん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>年<rp>(</rp><rt>ねん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>もの<ruby>昔<rp>(</rp><rt>むかし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>　<ruby>地<rp>(</rp><rt>ち</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>球<rp>(</rp><rt>きゅう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>全<rp>(</rp><rt>ぜん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>体<rp>(</rp><rt>たい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>をおおいつくしたといわれる　<ruby>雨<rp>(</rp><rt>あめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>よ　<ruby>嵐<rp>(</rp><rt>あらし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>よ……‼もう一<ruby>度<rp>(</rp><rt>ど</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>…………せめてもう一<ruby>度<rp>(</rp><rt>ど</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>降<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>り<ruby>続<rp>(</rp><rt>つづ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>いておくれ‼そして………………そして………………その<ruby>大<rp>(</rp><rt>だい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>洪<rp>(</rp><rt>こう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>水<rp>(</rp><rt>ずい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>中<rp>(</rp><rt>なか</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>で　<ruby>私<rp>(</rp><rt>わたくし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>はノアの<ruby>方<rp>(</rp><rt>はこ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>舟<rp>(</rp><rt>ぶね</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>乗<rp>(</rp><rt>の</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>り　<ruby>私<rp></rp><rt>わたくし</rt><rp></rp></ruby>と……<ruby>私<rp></rp><rt>わたくし</rt><rp></rp></ruby>と…………|script-title=ja:くたばれ‼涙くん|authorlink=Isami Ishii|last=Ishii|first=Isami|publisher=Goma Books|date=1 November 2016|script-chapter=ja:<ruby>第<rp>(</rp><rt>だい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>１<ruby>章<rp>(</rp><rt>しょう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby> <ruby>流<rp>(</rp><rt>なが</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>れる<ruby>白<rp>(</rp><rt>しろ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>い<ruby>雲<rp>(</rp><rt>くも</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ame yo '''fure'''‼ […] Ame yo arashi yo……‼ Mō ichido………… Semete mō ichido '''furitsuzuite okure'''‼&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Ame yo <b>fure</b>‼ […] Ame yo arashi yo……‼ Mō ichido………… Semete mō ichido <b>furitsuzuite okure</b>‼</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1442" id="mwDYI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">雨よ<b>降れ</b>‼[…]雨よ　嵐よ……‼もう一度…………せめてもう一度<b>降り続いておくれ</b>‼<sup about="#mwt1445" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ishii-2016_251-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ishii-2016&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ishii-2016-251&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ishii-2016-251" id="mwDYM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDYQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYU">[</span>235<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYY">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="7" id="mwDYc">literary wish</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDYg">
<td id="mwDYk">God said, “Let there be a great void between the waters, let it separate water from water.”</td>
<td id="mwDYo"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1448" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDYs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;神は言われた。「水の中に大空'''あれ'''。水と水を'''分けよ'''。」<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-chapter=ja:<ruby>創<rp>(</rp><rt>そう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>世<rp>(</rp><rt>せい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>記<rp>(</rp><rt>き</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>|chapter=Book of Genesis|script-title=ja:聖書　新共同訳|author=Executive Committee of The Common Bible Translation|title=[[Japanese New Interconfessional Translation Bible|Old Testament: The New Interconfessional Translation]]|year=1988|publisher=Japan Bible Society|script-quote=ja:<ruby>神<rp>(</rp><rt>かみ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>は<ruby>言<rp>(</rp><rt>い</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>われた。「<ruby>水<rp>(</rp><rt>みず</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>中<rp>(</rp><rt>なか</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>大<rp>(</rp><rt>おお</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>空<rp>(</rp><rt>ぞら</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>あれ。<ruby>水<rp>(</rp><rt>みず</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>と<ruby>水<rp>(</rp><rt>みず</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>を<ruby>分<rp>(</rp><rt>わ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>けよ。」}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kami wa iwareta. “Mizu no naka ni ōzora '''are'''. Mizu to mizu o '''wakeyo'''.”&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kami wa iwareta. “Mizu no naka ni ōzora <b>are</b>. Mizu to mizu o <b>wakeyo</b>.”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1448" id="mwDYw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">神は言われた。「水の中に大空<b>あれ</b>。水と水を<b>分けよ</b>。」<sup about="#mwt1451" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-252" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-252&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-252" id="mwDY0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDY4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDY8">[</span>236<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZA">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDZE">
<td id="mwDZI">[…] heaven bear witness,<br id="mwDZM">[…] God’s peace be with him.<br id="mwDZQ">[…] Heav’n’s peace be with him:<br id="mwDZU">[…] peace be with him.</td>
<td id="mwDZY"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1454" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDZc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;天も照覧'''あれ'''、[…]あゝ、神の平和よ、わが父と共に'''あれ'''！　[…]天の平和よ、彼れと共に'''あれ'''！　[…]あゝ、彼れに平和'''あれ'''！<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:自分は、本日、謀叛人だといふ判決を受けた、で、其罪名で死刑に處せられんければならんのである。然しながら、萬一にもわしが不忠の臣であるなら、天も<ruby>照<rp>(</rp><rt>せう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>覧<rp>(</rp><rt>らん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>あれ、又、わしに良心があるなら、其證人となれ、此身は、斧が下ると共に、永劫に滅亡し了るであらうぞ！　[…]<ruby>先<rp>(</rp><rt>せん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>考<rp>(</rp><rt>かう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>バキンガム公ヘンリーは、<ruby>纂<rp>(</rp><rt>さん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>奪<rp>(</rp><rt>だつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>者<rp>(</rp><rt>しや</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>リチャード（三世王）に眞先に背叛して兵を擧げたが、<ruby>敗<rp>(</rp><rt>はい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>績<rp>(</rp><rt>せき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>して、家來のパニスタといふ者に<ruby>匿<rp>(</rp><rt>かくま</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>はれてゐましたところ、そやつが裏切をした爲、捕へられ、<ruby>審<rp>(</rp><rt>しん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>問<rp>(</rp><rt>もん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>もされないで、刑せられました。あゝ、神の平和よ、わが父と共にあれ！　[…]<br/>'''ウルジ'''　天の平和よ、彼れと共にあれ！　といふ以上の祈りを、わたしはキリスト敎徒として、（彼れの爲に）<ruby>仕<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>樣<rp>(</rp><rt>やう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>もありません。今尙ほぶつくさ申してをる<ruby>輩<rp>(</rp><rt>やから</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に對しては、いづれ叱り附けてくれる<ruby>機<rp>(</rp><rt>をり</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>がありませう。[…]天も照覽あれ！　わらはは<ruby>陛下<rp>(</rp><rt>あなた</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に對して、常に誠實な、謙遜な妻でありました、<ruby>曾<rp>(</rp><rt>つひ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ぞ御意志に<ruby>悖<rp>(</rp><rt>もと</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ったことはございません。お憎しみを受けまするのを常に恐れてをりました。喜ぶにも、悲しむにも、常にお顔色を<ruby>窺<rp>(</rp><rt>うかゞ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ひまして、それに<ruby>倣<rp>(</rp><rt>なら</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ふやうにしてをりました。[…]生存中には最も憎いとも思ってゐた男を、おまひが敬虔な心で、誠實に、穩當にお評しだったので、灰となった今、尊敬する氣になりました。あゝ、彼れに平和あれ！|pages=56, 59, 72–73, 84–85, 152–153|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1664875/1/34|quote=I have this day receiv’d a traitor’s judgment,<br/>And by that name must die; yet, heaven bear witness,<br/>And if I have a conscience, let it sink me,<br/>Even as the axe falls, if I be not faithful.<br/>[…]<br/>My noble father, Henry of Buckingham,<br/>Who first rais’d head against usurping Richard,<br/>Flying for succour to his servant Banister,<br/>Being distress’d, was by that wretch betray’d<br/>And without trial fell; God’s peace be with him.<br/>[…]<br/>'''Wol.''' Heav’n’s peace be with him:<br/>That’s Christian care enough; for living murmurers<br/>There’s places of rebuke. […] Heaven witness,<br/>I have been to you a true and humble wife,<br/>At all times to your will conformable,<br/>Ever in fear to kindle your dislike,<br/>Yea, subject to your countenance, glad or sorry<br/>As I saw it inclin’d. […]<br/>Whom I most hated living, thou hast made me<br/>Now in his ashes honour: peace be with him.|trans-title=[[Henry VIII (play)|Henry VIII]]|script-title=ja:ヘンリー八世|title=King Henry VIII|translator-link=Tsubouchi Shōyō|translator-last=Tsubouchi|translator-first=Shōyō|authorlink=William Shakespeare|first1=William|last1=Shakespeare|authorlink2=John Fletcher (playwright)|first2=John|last2=Fletcher|series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|シェークスピヤ全集}}|publisher=Shinjusha|date=15 October 1958|location=[[Bunkyō]], Tokyo}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[…] ten mo shōran '''are''', […] Ā, Kami no heiwa yo, waga chichi to tomo ni '''are'''! […] Ten no heiwa yo, kare to tomo ni '''are'''! […] Ā, kare ni heiwa '''are'''!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">[…] ten mo shōran <b>are</b>, […] Ā, Kami no heiwa yo, waga chichi to tomo ni <b>are</b>! […] Ten no heiwa yo, kare to tomo ni <b>are</b>! […] Ā, kare ni heiwa <b>are</b>!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1454" id="mwDZg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">天も照覧<b>あれ</b>、[…]あゝ、神の平和よ、わが父と共に<b>あれ</b>！　[…]天の平和よ、彼れと共に<b>あれ</b>！　[…]あゝ、彼れに平和<b>あれ</b>！<sup about="#mwt1457" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-253" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-253&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-253" id="mwDZk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZs">[</span>237<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZw">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDZ0">
<td id="mwDZ4">A plaything let woman be, pure and fine like the precious stone, illumined with the virtues of a world not yet come.<sup about="#mwt1462" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-254" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-254&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-254" id="mwDZ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDaA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaE">[</span>238<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaI">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td id="mwDaM"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1463" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDaQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;女性はおもちゃ'''であれ'''、清く'''美しくあれ'''。まだ存在しない世界の徳によって照らされた宝石に'''ひとしくあれ'''！<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-chapter=ja:老いた女と若い女について|trans-chapter=On Old and Young Women|chapter=Von alten und jungen Weiblein|script-title=ja:ツァラトゥストラはこう語った|trans-title=[[Thus Spoke Zarathustra]]|title=Also sprach Zarathustra|first=Friedrich Wilhelm|last=Nietzsche|authorlink=Friedrich Nietzsche|translator-first=Kenji|translator-last=Takahashi|translator-first2=Hideo|translator-last2=Akiyama|publisher=Gutenberg21|location=[[Setagaya]], Tokyo|date=14 August 2015|script-quote=ja:女性はおもちゃであれ、清く美しくあれ。まだ存在しない世界の徳によって照らされた宝石にひとしくあれ！|quote=Ein Spielzeug sei das Weib, rein und fein, dem Edelsteine gleich, bestrahlt von den Tugenden einer Welt, welche noch nicht da ist.}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Josei wa omocha '''de are''', kiyoku '''utsukushiku are'''. Mada sonzai shinai sekai no toku ni yotte terasareta hōseki ni '''hitoshiku are'''!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Josei wa omocha <b>de are</b>, kiyoku <b>utsukushiku are</b>. Mada sonzai shinai sekai no toku ni yotte terasareta hōseki ni <b>hitoshiku are</b>!</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1463" id="mwDaU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">女性はおもちゃ<b>であれ</b>、清く<b>美しくあれ</b>。まだ存在しない世界の徳によって照らされた宝石に<b>ひとしくあれ</b>！<sup about="#mwt1466" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-255" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-255&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-255" id="mwDaY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDac"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDag">[</span>239<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDak">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDao">
<td id="mwDas">May the victims’ souls rest in eternal peace.</td>
<td id="mwDaw"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1469" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDa0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;犠牲者の御霊よ、永久に'''安かれ'''。<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/9526534/1/2|script-title=ja:伊勢湾台風災害画報|location=[[Mie Prefecture|Mie]]|publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|三重県県民室}}|date=20 March 1960}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Giseisha no mitama yo, eikyū ni '''yasukare'''.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Giseisha no mitama yo, eikyū ni <b>yasukare</b>.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1469" id="mwDa4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">犠牲者の御霊よ、永久に<b>安かれ</b>。<sup about="#mwt1472" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-256" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-256&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-256" id="mwDa8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbE">[</span>240<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbI">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDbM">
<td id="mwDbQ"><i id="mwDbU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lest_Darkness_Fall" title="Lest Darkness Fall" id="mwDbY">Lest Darkness Fall</a></i>; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1475" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:ExpandedAttrs" id="mwDbg" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwDbc\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]],&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lit&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Lit&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''Darkness, Don't Fall''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;" about="#mwt1475"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot" about="#mwt1475">'</span><span class="gloss-text" about="#mwt1475"><i>Darkness, Don't Fall</i></span><span class="gloss-quot" about="#mwt1475" id="mwDbk">'</span></td>
<td id="mwDbo"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1477" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDbs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;闇よ落ちる'''なかれ'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Yami yo ochiru '''nakare'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Yami yo ochiru <b>nakare</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1477" id="mwDbw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">闇よ落ちる<b>なかれ</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDb0">
<td id="mwDb4">believe it or not; would you believe it; lo and behold; wait for it; get this; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1478" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:ExpandedAttrs" id="mwDcA" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwDb8\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]],&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lit&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Lit&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;don't be surprised&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;" about="#mwt1478"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot" about="#mwt1478">'</span><span class="gloss-text" about="#mwt1478">don't be surprised</span><span class="gloss-quot" about="#mwt1478" id="mwDcE">'</span></td>
<td id="mwDcI"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1480" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDcM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;驚く'''なかれ'''<ref name=kenkyusha/>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;odoroku '''nakare'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">odoroku <b>nakare</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1480" id="mwDcQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">驚く<b>なかれ</b><sup about="#mwt1481" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kenkyusha_47-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kenkyusha&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kenkyusha-47" id="mwDcU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDcY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcc">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcg">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDck">
<td id="mwDco">The way of life of someone who has gone all the way through with anything, be it good or bad, is beautiful.</td>
<td id="mwDcs"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1483" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDcw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;善い'''にしろ'''、惡い'''にしろ'''、何かを完了した人間の活き方は、美しい。<ref name=nagai-1948/>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Yoi '''ni shiro''', warui '''ni shiro''', nani ka o kanryō shita ningen no ikikata wa, utsukushii.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Yoi <b>ni shiro</b>, warui <b>ni shiro</b>, nani ka o kanryō shita ningen no ikikata wa, utsukushii.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1483" id="mwDc0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">善い<b>にしろ</b>、惡い<b>にしろ</b>、何かを完了した人間の活き方は、美しい。<sup about="#mwt1484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nagai-1948_249-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nagai-1948&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-nagai-1948-249" id="mwDc4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDc8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdA">[</span>233<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdE">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td>
<td rowspan="7" id="mwDdI">concession</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDdM">
<td id="mwDdQ">Whether it’s the “ability to not miss the moment nature smiles” or “serendipity”, I’d say a state of heightened sensitivity when it happens is essential.</td>
<td id="mwDdU"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1486" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDdY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;この「自然が微笑むときを見逃さない力」'''にせよ'''、「セレンディピティ」'''にせよ'''、その時の感性が高まっているという状態が重要だと思っています。<ref>{{#invoke:cite|AV media|lang=ja|title=Exploring cultural genealogy from the hug of Japanese monkeys {{pipe}} Naofumi NAKAGAWA {{pipe}} TEDxKobe|first=Naofumi|last=Nakagawa|publisher=TEDx Talks|website=YouTube|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RdmwIzMYNgw|date=21 November 2016}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kono “shizen ga hohoemu toki o minogasanai chikara” '''ni seyo''', “serendipiti” '''ni seyo''', sono toki no kansei ga takamatte iru to yū jōtai ga jūyō da to omotte imasu.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kono “shizen ga hohoemu toki o minogasanai chikara” <b>ni seyo</b>, “serendipiti” <b>ni seyo</b>, sono toki no kansei ga takamatte iru to yū jōtai ga jūyō da to omotte imasu.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1486" id="mwDdc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">この「自然が微笑むときを見逃さない力」<b>にせよ</b>、「セレンディピティ」<b>にせよ</b>、その時の感性が高まっているという状態が重要だと思っています。<sup about="#mwt1489" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-257" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-257&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-257" id="mwDdg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdo">[</span>241<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDds">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDdw">
<td id="mwDd0">in any event/case; anyway</td>
<td id="mwDd4"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1492" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDd8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;いずれ'''にしろ'''・'''せよ'''&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;izure '''ni shiro'''/'''seyo'''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">izure <b>ni shiro</b>/<b>seyo</b></i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1492" id="mwDeA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">いずれ<b>にしろ</b>・<b>せよ</b></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDeE">
<td id="mwDeI">Obviously, you’re free to pamper and dote on your own pet however you want to, whether it’s a dog, a cat or any other animal.</td>
<td id="mwDeM"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1493" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDeQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;もちろん、犬'''であれ'''猫'''であれ'''その他の動物'''であれ'''、自分のペットをむやみやたらに甘やかしてかわいがるのは、その人の自由である。<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-chapter=ja:ペットを猫かわいがりする|script-title=ja:〈感じ〉のいい人、悪い人|first=Takeya|last=Yamasaki|date=1 October 2006|publisher=PHP Institute|location=[[Kōtō]], Tokyo}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Mochiron, inu '''de are''' neko '''de are''' sono ta no dōbutsu '''de are''', jibun no petto o muyami yatara ni amayakashite kawaigaru no wa, sono hito no jiyū de aru.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Mochiron, inu <b>de are</b> neko <b>de are</b> sono ta no dōbutsu <b>de are</b>, jibun no petto o muyami yatara ni amayakashite kawaigaru no wa, sono hito no jiyū de aru.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1493" id="mwDeU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">もちろん、犬<b>であれ</b>猫<b>であれ</b>その他の動物<b>であれ</b>、自分のペットをむやみやたらに甘やかしてかわいがるのは、その人の自由である。<sup about="#mwt1496" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-258" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-258&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-258" id="mwDeY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDec"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeg">[</span>242<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDek">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDeo">
<td id="mwDes">[…] knowing full well that whatever they are, be they the Vietnam War or a homicide, won’t just come flying out at you from that convex glass screen that is as warm as a hand warmer if you touch it a little bit, […]</td>
<td id="mwDew"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1499" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDe0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[…]そしてベトナム戰爭'''でござれ'''、人殺し'''でござれ'''、あのちよつと手を觸れると懷爐ほどに熱い凸面ガラスよりこちらへは、絕對に飛び出してくることはないと知つてしまへば、[…]<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|script-quote=ja:この世のことは、みんなブラウン管の中の幻だと思ひ込めれば、そしてベトナム戰爭でござれ、人殺しでござれ、あのちよつと手を觸れると懷爐ほどに熱い凸面ガラスよりこちらへは、絕對に飛び出してくることはないと知つてしまへば、人生を樂に生きられ、人生すべてがたのしみになつてしまふかもしれません。|trans-quote=If you could convince yourself that all life affairs are mere visions in the CRT, knowing full well that whatever they are, be they the Vietnam War or a homicide, won’t just come flying out at you from that convex glass screen that is as warm as a hand warmer if you touch it a little bit, you might just be able to live your life at ease and find joy in every facet of life.|page=155|lang=ja|script-chapter=ja:三島由紀夫レター敎室|trans-chapter=Mishima Yukio’s Letter Classroom|script-title=ja:三島由紀夫全集|trans-title=The Complete Works of Mishima Yukio|volume=16|first=Yukio|last=Mishima|authorlink=Yukio Mishima|date=25 August 1974|publisher=Shinchosha|location=[[Shinjuku]], Tokyo|editor-first=Ishikawa|editor-last=Jun|editor-link=Jun Ishikawa|editor-link2=Yasunari Kawabata|editor-first2=Yasunari|editor-last2=Kawabata|editor-link3=Mitsuo Nakamura|editor-first3=Mitsuo|editor-last3=Nakamura|editor-link4=Taijun Takeda|editor-first4=Taijun|editor-last4=Takeda|editor-first5=Shōichi|editor-last5=Saeki|editor-link6=Donald Keene|editor-first6=Donald Lawrence|editor-last6=Keene|editor-first7=Takeshi|editor-last7=Muramatsu|editor-first8=Miyoko|editor-last8=Tanaka}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[…] so shite Betonamu Sensō '''de gozare''', hitogoroshi '''de gozare''', ano chotto te o fureru to kairo hodo ni atsui totsumen garasu yori kochira e wa, zettai ni tobidashite kuru koto wa nai to shitte shimaeba, […]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">[…] so shite Betonamu Sensō <b>de gozare</b>, hitogoroshi <b>de gozare</b>, ano chotto te o fureru to kairo hodo ni atsui totsumen garasu yori kochira e wa, zettai ni tobidashite kuru koto wa nai to shitte shimaeba, […]</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1499" id="mwDe4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">[…]そしてベトナム戰爭<b>でござれ</b>、人殺し<b>でござれ</b>、あのちよつと手を觸れると懷爐ほどに熱い凸面ガラスよりこちらへは、絕對に飛び出してくることはないと知つてしまへば、[…]<sup about="#mwt1502" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-259" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-259&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-259" id="mwDe8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfE">[</span>243<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfI">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDfM">
<td id="mwDfQ">His elder brothers leave their village with their circles for new settlements, be they far or near.</td>
<td id="mwDfU"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1505" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDfY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;兄たちは仲間たちと一緒に，'''遠かれ近かれ'''，村を離れて新たな土地で生活をする。<ref>{{#invoke:cite|journal|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:カチン人全般がそうであるように，ジンポー族も歓待の心をとても大切にする。友人だけでなく，人種や宗教に関係なく見知らぬ人のおもてなしを拒まない。また，末の男子が本家筋を継いで村に留まる。兄たちは仲間たちと一緒に，遠かれ近かれ，村を離れて新たな土地で生活をする。こうした風習や，人口増加，移動耕作に伴い，何世紀もかけてジンポー族は徐々に南方へ移動してきた。|page=31|script-title=ja:東南アジアの人間像と日本経営史の原像（二）|first=Yoshio|last=Ōba|script-journal=ja:北海学園大学学園論集|number=149|date=25 September 2011|url=http://hokuga.hgu.jp/dspace/bitstream/123456789/1794/1/OOBA1.pdf|issn=0385-7271}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Anitachi wa nakamatachi to issho ni, '''tōkare chikakare''', mura o hanarete arata na tochi de seikatsu o suru.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Anitachi wa nakamatachi to issho ni, <b>tōkare chikakare</b>, mura o hanarete arata na tochi de seikatsu o suru.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1505" id="mwDfc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">兄たちは仲間たちと一緒に，<b>遠かれ近かれ</b>，村を離れて新たな土地で生活をする。<sup about="#mwt1508" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-260" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-260&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-260" id="mwDfg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfo">[</span>244<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfs">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDfw">
<td id="mwDf0">Come rain or wind, as Beethoven roamed the outskirts of Vienna without a care about the weather, […]</td>
<td id="mwDf4"><span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1511" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDf8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;雨よ'''降れ'''、風も'''吹け'''、ウィーンの郊外を、お天氣構はずに彷徨したベートーヴェンは、[…]<ref>{{#invoke:cite|book|lang=ja|script-quote=ja:雨よ降れ、風も吹け、ウィーンの郊外を、お天氣構はずに彷徨したベートーヴェンは、その負けじ魂を至人達人の境地までひた押しに押しあげて居たのである。|trans-quote=Come rain or wind, as Beethoven roamed the outskirts of Vienna without a care about the weather, he pushed his indomitable spirit to the absolute heights of a virtuoso.|page=111|script-chapter=ja:ベートーヴェンの生涯|trans-chapter=The Life of Beethoven|script-title=ja:紙上音樂會　レコードの選び方|trans-title=Concerts on Paper: How to Choose Records|last=Nomura|first=Araebisu|date=5 September 1955|publisher=Ongaku no Tomo Sha|location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]|url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/2475850/1/60}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ame yo '''fure''', kaze mo '''fuke''', Wīn no kōgai o, otenki kamawazu ni hōkō shita Bētōven wa, […]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Ame yo <b>fure</b>, kaze mo <b>fuke</b>, Wīn no kōgai o, otenki kamawazu ni hōkō shita Bētōven wa, […]</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1511" id="mwDgA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">雨よ<b>降れ</b>、風も<b>吹け</b>、ウィーンの郊外を、お天氣構はずに彷徨したベートーヴェンは、[…]<sup about="#mwt1514" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-261" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-261&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-261" id="mwDgE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgM">[</span>245<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDgU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Stop_sign_202412,_Machida.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDgY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Stop_sign_202412,_Machida.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Stop_sign_202412%2C_Machida.jpg/500px-Stop_sign_202412%2C_Machida.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2432" data-file-height="1824" data-file-type="bitmap" height="285" width="380" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Stop_sign_202412%2C_Machida.jpg/960px-Stop_sign_202412%2C_Machida.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1.5" id="mwDgc"></a><figcaption id="mwDgg"><span title="Japanese-language text" about="#mwt1518" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDgk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:lang&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;止まれ&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span lang="ja">止まれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" about="#mwt1518" id="mwDgo"> STOP signs in Japan use the imperative form of <span about="#mwt1519" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDgs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;to stop&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;止まる&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">to stop</span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1519" id="mwDgw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">止まる</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> to command mandatory action.</figcaption></figure><div style="clear:left;" class="" about="#mwt1517" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDg0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;clear&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Clear&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;left&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwDg4" aria-labelledby="Imperative:_Conjugation_table"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Imperative:_Conjugation_table">Imperative: Conjugation table</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Japanese_conjugation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section: Imperative: Conjugation table"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDg8">The honorific <i id="mwDhA">godan</i> verbs are originally <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1520" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDhE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;おっしゃれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;osshare&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">osshare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1520" id="mwDhI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">おっしゃれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1521" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDhM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;下され&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kudasare&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kudasare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1521" id="mwDhQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">下され</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1522" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDhU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;為され&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nasare&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nasare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1522" id="mwDhY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">為され</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1523" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDhc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;御座れ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;gozare&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">gozare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1523" id="mwDhg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">御座れ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, just like other <i id="mwDhk">godan</i>/<span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1524" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDho" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;四段&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;yodan&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">yodan</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1524" id="mwDhs"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">四段</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> verbs, though *<span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1525" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDhw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;いらっしゃれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;irasshare&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">irasshare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1525" id="mwDh0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">いらっしゃれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> was not found. These forms are obsolescent and only used for special effect, such as in advertisements.<sup about="#mwt1526" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004347_262-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004347&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004347-262&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;347&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004347-262" id="mwDh4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDh8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiA">[</span>246<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiE">]</span></span></a></sup> Historically, honorific verbs were <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1529" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDiI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;二段&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nidan&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nidan</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1529" id="mwDiM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">二段</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> rather than <i id="mwDiQ">godan</i>/<i id="mwDiU">yodan</i>, and western imperative forms like <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1530" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDiY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;いらせられよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;iraserareyo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;→ ''irasshai''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">iraserareyo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1530" id="mwDic"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">いらせられよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; → <i>irasshai</i>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1531" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDig" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;仰せられよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ōserareyo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;→ ''osshai''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ōserareyo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1531" id="mwDik"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">仰せられよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; → <i>osshai</i>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1532" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDio" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;下されよ・下されい&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kudasareyo/kudasarei&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;→ ''kudasai''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kudasareyo/kudasarei</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1532" id="mwDis"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">下されよ・下されい</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; → <i>kudasai</i>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1533" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDiw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;為されよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nasareyo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;→ ''nasai''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nasareyo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1533" id="mwDi0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">為されよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; → <i>nasai</i>)</span> are attested. From these <i id="mwDi4">nidan</i> verbs, apart from the <i id="mwDi8">godan</i> offshoots, there still exist <i id="mwDjA">ichidan</i> equivalents. Some rural eastern dialects still have <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1534" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDjE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;為さろ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nasaro&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nasaro</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1534" id="mwDjI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">為さろ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200158–59,_100,_209–210,_557–558_263-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200158–59, 100, 209–210, 557–558&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200158–59,_100,_209–210,_557–558-263&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;58–59, 100, 209–210, 557–558&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200158–59,_100,_209–210,_557–558-263" id="mwDjM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjU">[</span>247<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a12,_157_264-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMinistry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture1935a12, 157&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a12,_157-264&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;12, 157&quot;},&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ministry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1935a&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a12,_157-264" id="mwDjc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjk">[</span>248<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDjs">With non-<i id="mwDjw">godan</i> verbs, there are two imperative forms, one ending in <i id="mwDj0">‑ro</i> and one in <i id="mwDj4">‑yo</i>. <i id="mwDj8">‑Ro</i> has been characterized as used for speech, while <i id="mwDkA">‑yo</i> as used for writing.<sup about="#mwt1541" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018578&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations&quot;_(Verbs:_Footnote_7)_265-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018578\&quot;Appendix 1 Basic Conjugations\&quot; (Verbs: Footnote 7)&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018578\&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations\&quot;_(Verbs:_Footnote_7)-265&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Makino&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tsutsui&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2018&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;578&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Appendix 1 Basic Conjugations\&quot; (Verbs: Footnote 7)&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMakinoTsutsui2018578&quot;Appendix_1_Basic_Conjugations&quot;_(Verbs:_Footnote_7)-265" id="mwDkE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDkI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkM">[</span>249<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In actuality, this corresponds to a difference between <span about="#mwt1544" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDkU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;modern Japanese&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;口語&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kōgo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{lit|oral language}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">modern Japanese</span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1544" id="mwDkY"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">口語</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">, <span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">kōgo</i></span>; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1545" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwDkc\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">oral language</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> based on the eastern Tokyo Japanese dialect,<sup about="#mwt1546" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-267" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-267&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Although ''‑ro'' is not unheard of in western and southern Japan.{{sfnp|Martin|pp=959–961|2004}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-267" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDkg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDkk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDko">[</span>q<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDks">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classical_Japanese" title="Classical Japanese" about="#mwt1552" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDkw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[Classical Japanese]]&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;文語&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;bungo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{lit|literary language}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">Classical Japanese</a><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1552" id="mwDk0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">文語</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">, <span title="Hepburn transliteration"><i lang="ja-Latn">bungo</i></span>; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1553" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwDk4\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">literary language</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, various literary stages of premodern Japanese based on western dialects.<sup about="#mwt1592" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-268" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-268&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-268" id="mwDk8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlE">[</span>251<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1595" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-hoshina-1937_269-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;hoshina-1937&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-hoshina-1937-269&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-hoshina-1937-269" id="mwDlM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlU">[</span>252<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1554" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001777_270-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001777&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001777-270&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;777&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001777-270" id="mwDlc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlk">[</span>253<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlo">]</span></span></a></sup> Both <i id="mwDls">ro</i> and <i id="mwDlw">yo</i> were interjectional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_particles" title="Japanese particles" id="mwDl0">particles</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Japanese" title="Old Japanese" id="mwDl4">Old Japanese</a>,<sup about="#mwt1557" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010133,_154_271-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010133, 154&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010133,_154-271&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Frellesvig&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2010&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;133, 154&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010133,_154-271" id="mwDl8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmE">[</span>254<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-272" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-272&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The author uses the term \&quot;central\&quot; rather than \&quot;western\&quot; for the once capital [[Nara (city)|Nara]], now located in Kansai.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-272" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDmM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmU">[</span>r<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001821–822,_853_273-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001821–822, 853&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001821–822,_853-273&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;821–822, 853&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001821–822,_853-273" id="mwDmc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmk">[</span>255<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143_274-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMinistry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture1935a131–143&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ministry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1935a&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;131–143&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274" id="mwDms"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDm0">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDm4">]</span></span></a></sup> and were sometimes optional, sometimes obligatory with non-<i id="mwDm8">godan</i> verbs. <i id="mwDnA">‑Yo</i> became obligatory with non-<i id="mwDnE">godan</i> verbs toward <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Early_Middle_Japanese" title="Early Middle Japanese" id="mwDnI">Early Middle Japanese</a>, and its reduced variant <i id="mwDnM">‑i</i> arose during <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Middle_Japanese" title="Late Middle Japanese" id="mwDnQ">Late Middle Japanese</a>.<sup about="#mwt1569" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010227_275-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010227&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010227-275&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Frellesvig&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2010&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;227&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010227-275" id="mwDnU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDnY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnc">[</span>257<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDng">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1572" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-276" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-276&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Compare the alternative forms of {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||良い|joi/ii}}, {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||行く|yuku/iku}}.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-276" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDnk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDno"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDns">[</span>s<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnw">]</span></span></a></sup> Historically and dialectally, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1575" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDn0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;見よ・見い・見ろ・見&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mi-yo/mi-i/mi-ro/mi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|look!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">mi-yo/mi-i/mi-ro/mi</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1575" id="mwDn4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">見よ・見い・見ろ・見</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">look!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1576" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDn8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;起きよ・起きい・起きろ・起き&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;oki-yo/oki-i/oki-ro/oki&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|get up!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">oki-yo/oki-i/oki-ro/oki</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1576" id="mwDoA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">起きよ・起きい・起きろ・起き</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">get up!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1577" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDoE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;蹴よ・蹴い・蹴ろ・蹴&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ke-yo/ke-i/ke-ro/ke&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|kick!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ke-yo/ke-i/ke-ro/ke</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1577" id="mwDoI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">蹴よ・蹴い・蹴ろ・蹴</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">kick!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1578" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-277" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-277&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;This verb is primarily ''godan'', therefore the more common imperative is actually ''kere''.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-277" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDoM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoU">[</span>t<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoY">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1581" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDoc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;開けよ・開けい・開けろ・開け&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ake-yo/ake-i/ake-ro/ake&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|open!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ake-yo/ake-i/ake-ro/ake</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1581" id="mwDog"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">開けよ・開けい・開けろ・開け</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">open!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> (all <i id="mwDok">ichidan</i>), <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1582" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDoo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;せよ・しよ・せい・しい・せろ・しろ・せ・し&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;se-yo/shi-yo/se-i/shi-i/se-ro/shi-ro/se/shi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''suru'', {{gloss|do!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">se-yo/shi-yo/se-i/shi-i/se-ro/shi-ro/se/shi</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1582" id="mwDos"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">せよ・しよ・せい・しい・せろ・しろ・せ・し</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <i>suru</i>, <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">do!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1583" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDow" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;来よ・来い・来ろ・来&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ko-yo/ki-yo/ko-i/ki-i/ko-ro/ki-ro/ko/ki&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''kuru'', {{gloss|come!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ko-yo/ki-yo/ko-i/ki-i/ko-ro/ki-ro/ko/ki</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1583" id="mwDo0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">来よ・来い・来ろ・来</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <i>kuru</i>, <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">come!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> were all possible,<sup about="#mwt1584" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010345–346_278-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010345–346&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010345–346-278&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Frellesvig&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2010&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;345–346&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010345–346-278" id="mwDo4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDo8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpA">[</span>258<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1598" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-279" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-279&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-279" id="mwDpI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpQ">[</span>259<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1601" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-280" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-280&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-280" id="mwDpY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpg">[</span>260<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpk">]</span></span></a></sup> with <i id="mwDpo">‑yo</i> and <i id="mwDps">‑i</i> being the western forms, and <i id="mwDpw">‑ro</i> being the eastern form.<sup about="#mwt1604" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-281" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-281&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-281" id="mwDp0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDp4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDp8">[</span>261<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1607" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-282" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-282&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-282" id="mwDqE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqM">[</span>262<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1610" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-283" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-283&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-283" id="mwDqU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqc">[</span>263<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1611" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-matsushita-1929_284-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;matsushita-1929&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-matsushita-1929-284" id="mwDqk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqs">[</span>264<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqw">]</span></span></a></sup> The division between western <i id="mwDq0">‑yo</i>/<i id="mwDq4">‑i</i> and eastern <i id="mwDq8">‑ro</i> still exists today.<sup about="#mwt1587" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010399_285-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010399&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010399-285&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Frellesvig&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2010&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;399&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFrellesvig2010399-285" id="mwDrA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrI">[</span>265<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1614" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-286" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-286&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-286" id="mwDrQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrY">[</span>266<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrc">]</span></span></a></sup> According to a 1991 survey:</p>
<ul id="mwDrg"><li id="mwDrk"><i id="mwDro">‑Ro</i> dominates eastern dialects.<sup about="#mwt1617" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-287" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-287&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-287" id="mwDrs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDr0">[</span>267<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDr4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1620" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-288" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-288&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-288" id="mwDr8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDsA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsE">[</span>268<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1623" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-akero_289-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-akero&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ninjal-akero-289&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-akero-289" id="mwDsM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsU">[</span>269<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDsc"><i id="mwDsg">‑Yo</i> is found mostly in central <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chūbu" title="Chūbu" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDsk">Chūbu</a> and eastern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyushu" title="Kyushu" id="mwDso">Kyushu</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDss"><i id="mwDsw">‑I</i> dominates western dialects in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honshu" title="Honshu" id="mwDs0">Honshu</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shikoku" title="Shikoku" id="mwDs4">Shikoku</a>, and marginally in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shitamachi" title="Shitamachi" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDs8">Shitamachi</a>, Tokyo.<sup about="#mwt1624" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961_266-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;959–961&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266" id="mwDtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDtE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDtI">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDtM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDtQ"><i id="mwDtU">‑Re</i>, likely as a shortened <i id="mwDtY">‑ro‑i</i>,<sup about="#mwt1627" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961_266-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;959–961&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266" id="mwDtc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDtg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDtk">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDto">]</span></span></a></sup> is found in the northernmost dialects in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hokkaido" title="Hokkaido" id="mwDts">Hokkaido</a> and the southernmost ones in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyushu" title="Kyushu" id="mwDtw">Kyushu</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDt0"><i id="mwDt4">Shiro</i> ("do!") dominates eastern dialects, while <i id="mwDt8">sē</i> does western dialects. <i id="mwDuA">Seyo</i> and <i id="mwDuE">shiyo</i> concentrate in central Chūbu, while <i id="mwDuI">sero</i> and <i id="mwDuM">sere</i> do in western Kyushu.<sup about="#mwt1630" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-shiro_38-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-shiro&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-shiro-38" id="mwDuQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDuU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDuY">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDuc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDug">There exist such fused forms as <i id="mwDuk">myo(o)</i> (← <i id="mwDuo">miyo</i>, "look!"), <i id="mwDus">okyo(o)</i> (← <i id="mwDuw">okiyo</i>, "rise!"), <i id="mwDu0">akyo(o)</i> (← <i id="mwDu4">akeyo</i>, "open!") and <i id="mwDu8">sho(o)</i> (← <i id="mwDvA">seyo</i>, "do!") in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shizuoka_Prefecture" title="Shizuoka Prefecture" id="mwDvE">Shizuoka Prefecture</a> and some surrounding areas.</li>
<li id="mwDvI"><i id="mwDvM">Koi</i> ("come!") occurs consistently across Japan, although <i id="mwDvQ">kō</i> has a strong presence in the east. There is a concentration of <i id="mwDvU">kē</i> and <i id="mwDvY">ke</i> in Kyushu. <i id="mwDvc">Koyo</i> is rare in contemporary Japanese dialects,<sup about="#mwt1636" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-koi_290-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-koi&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ninjal-koi-290&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-koi-290" id="mwDvg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDvk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvo">[</span>270<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvs">]</span></span></a></sup> despite being the standard form in classical Japanese. According to another account, <i id="mwDvw">koro</i> occurs in an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akita_Prefecture" title="Akita Prefecture" id="mwDv0">Akita</a> dialect, while <i id="mwDv4">kiro</i> is found in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibaraki_Prefecture" title="Ibaraki Prefecture" id="mwDv8">Ibaraki</a>. Other variants include <i id="mwDwA">kiyo</i>, <i id="mwDwE">kī</i>, <i id="mwDwI">kui</i>, <i id="mwDwM">keyo</i>, etc.<sup about="#mwt1631" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143_274-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMinistry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture1935a131–143&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ministry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1935a&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;131–143&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274" id="mwDwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDwU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwY">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDwg">In some dialects, <i id="mwDwk">okiro(o)</i>, <i id="mwDwo">akero(o)</i>, <i id="mwDws">nero(o)</i>, <i id="mwDww">koro(o)</i>, <i id="mwDw0">shiro(o)</i> are actually <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(mizenkei_base)#Hortative" title="Japanese conjugation (mizenkei base)" id="mwDw4">hortative</a> forms, not imperative forms.<sup about="#mwt1639" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-okiyoo_291-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-okiyoo&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ninjal-okiyoo-291&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-okiyoo-291" id="mwDw8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxE">[</span>271<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1642" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-akeyoo_292-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-akeyoo&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ninjal-akeyoo-292&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-akeyoo-292" id="mwDxM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxU">[</span>272<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1645" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-neyoo_293-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-neyoo&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ninjal-neyoo-293&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-neyoo-293" id="mwDxc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxk">[</span>273<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1648" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-koyoo_294-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-koyoo&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ninjal-koyoo-294&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-koyoo-294" id="mwDxs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDx0">[</span>274<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDx4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1651" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-shiyoo_295-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-shiyoo&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ninjal-shiyoo-295&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-shiyoo-295" id="mwDx8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDyA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyE">[</span>275<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyI">]</span></span></a></sup> The eastern imperative <i id="mwDyM">kō</i> also resembles the western hortative of the same verb.</li></ul>

<p id="mwDyQ">In modern Tokyo Japanese (eastern, specifically <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yamanote" title="Yamanote" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDyU">Yamanote</a> Japanese), <i id="mwDyY">yo</i> largely displaced <i id="mwDyc">ro</i> in non-imperative contexts. <i id="mwDyg">Yo</i> can be optionally added to modern imperative forms with no historical <i id="mwDyk">‑yo</i>, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1652" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDyo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;書けよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kake yo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|write!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kake yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1652" id="mwDys"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">書けよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">write!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1653" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDyw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;見ろよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;miro yo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">miro yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1653" id="mwDy0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">見ろよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1654" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDy4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;しろよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;shiro yo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">shiro yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1654" id="mwDy8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">しろよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1655" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDzA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;来いよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;koi yo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">koi yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1655" id="mwDzE"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">来いよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>; <i id="mwDzI">ro</i> can no longer be used this way, although historically it used to occasionally be, as with <i id="mwDzM">yodan</i> imperatives like <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1656" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDzQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;置けろ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;oke ro&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|put!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">oke ro</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1656" id="mwDzU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">置けろ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">put!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> or <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1657" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDzY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;読めろ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;yome ro&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|read!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">yome ro</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1657" id="mwDzc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">読めろ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">read!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1658" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143_274-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMinistry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture1935a131–143&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ministry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1935a&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;131–143&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274" id="mwDzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDzk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzo">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzs">]</span></span></a></sup> Although <i id="mwDzw">‑yo</i> imperatives already contain <i id="mwDz0">‑yo</i> and are primarily "written," it is not impossible for them to be followed by another colloquial <i id="mwDz4">yo</i>, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1661" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDz8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;倉を開けよよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kura o akeyo yo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|Open the storehouse, would you?}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kura o akeyo yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1661" id="mwD0A"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">倉を開けよよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Open the storehouse, would you?</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span><sup about="#mwt1671" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-296" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-296&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-296" id="mwD0E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD0I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0M">[</span>276<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0Q">]</span></span></a></sup> or <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1662" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD0U" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;もう寝よよ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Mō neyo yo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|Just sleep already, would you?}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Mō neyo yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1662" id="mwD0Y"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">もう寝よよ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Just sleep already, would you?</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1674" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-297" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-297&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-297" id="mwD0c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD0g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0k">[</span>277<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0o">]</span></span></a></sup> Apart from the difference between eastern and western dialects, there exists a register difference between <i id="mwD0s">‑yo</i> and <i id="mwD0w">‑ro</i> within standard Japanese.<sup about="#mwt1677" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-matsushita-1929_284-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;matsushita-1929&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-matsushita-1929-284&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-matsushita-1929-284" id="mwD00"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD04"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD08">[</span>264<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1A">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwD1E">‑Yo</i>, as the more prestigious classical form of the former western capitals (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nara_(city)" title="Nara (city)" id="mwD1I">Nara</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyoto" title="Kyoto" id="mwD1M">Kyoto</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osaka" title="Osaka" id="mwD1Q">Osaka</a>), is still used in formal instructions, such as on test forms,<sup about="#mwt1680" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-298" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-298&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-298" id="mwD1U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD1Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1c">[</span>278<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1g">]</span></span></a></sup> in academic questions,<sup about="#mwt1683" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-299" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-299&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-299" id="mwD1k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD1o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1s">[</span>279<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1w">]</span></span></a></sup> on signage, in formal or polite quoted commands<sup about="#mwt1663" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961_266-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;959–961&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266" id="mwD10"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD14"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD18">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2A">]</span></span></a></sup> or concessive clauses (spoken<sup about="#mwt1686" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-300" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-300&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-300" id="mwD2E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD2I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2M">[</span>280<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2Q">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-301" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-301&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-301" id="mwD2U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD2Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2c">[</span>281<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1692" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-302" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-302&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-302" id="mwD2k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD2o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2s">[</span>282<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1695" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-303" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-303&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-303" id="mwD20"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD24"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD28">[</span>283<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1698" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-304" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-304&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-304" id="mwD3E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD3I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3M">[</span>284<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3Q">]</span></span></a></sup> or written<sup about="#mwt1701" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-305" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-305&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-305" id="mwD3U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD3Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3c">[</span>285<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1704" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-306" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-306&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-306" id="mwD3k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD3o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3s">[</span>286<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1707" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-307" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-307&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-307" id="mwD30"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD34"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD38">[</span>287<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4A">]</span></span></a></sup>), etc. On the other hand, <i id="mwD4E">‑ro</i>, as the more colloquially common form, has a connotation of rudeness.<sup about="#mwt1708" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-matsushita-1929_284-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;matsushita-1929&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-matsushita-1929-284" id="mwD4I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD4M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4Q">[</span>264<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4U">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1666" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-308" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-308&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The author argues that the imperative forms of most verbs are inherently rude in speech, barring those of honorific verbs which are presumed to be polite, such as {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||いらっしゃい|irasshai| {{gloss|come, please!}}}}, {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||遊ばせ|asobase| {{gloss|let do/be, please!}}}}, {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||下さい|kudasai| {{gloss|give me, please!}}}}. The problem is that, with the sole exception of {{#invoke:nihongo|nihongo||御覧じろ|goranjiro| {{gloss|look, please!}}}}, most of these verbs' conjugations (''yodan''/''godan'') have nothing to do with ''‑ro'' (non-''yodan''/''godan'' only), giving ''‑ro'' an unavoidable connotation of rudeness. ''‑Yo'', on the other hand, is associated with classical Japanese (the \&quot;written\&quot; language) and therefore is the only appropriate option in formal contexts, even in speech.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-308" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwD4Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD4c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4g">[</span>u<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4k">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwD4o">Unlike with most <i id="mwD4s">ichidan</i> verbs, <i id="mwD4w">‑ro</i> is optional (possibly dialectal<sup about="#mwt1709" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004960_309-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004960&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004960-309&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;960&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004960-309" id="mwD40"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD44"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD48">[</span>288<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5A">]</span></span></a></sup>) with <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1712" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD5E" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;呉れ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kure&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|give (me/us)!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kure</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1712" id="mwD5I"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">呉れ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">give (me/us)!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> and its honorific version <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1713" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD5M" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;御呉れ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;okure&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">okure</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1713" id="mwD5Q"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">御呉れ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1714" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143_274-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMinistry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture1935a131–143&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ministry of Education, Science, Sports and Culture&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1935a&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;131–143&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinistry_of_Education,_Science,_Sports_and_Culture1935a131–143-274" id="mwD5U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD5Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5c">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1722" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-310" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-310&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-310" id="mwD5k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD5o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5s">[</span>289<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1725" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-311" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-311&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-311" id="mwD50"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD54"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD58">[</span>290<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6A">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwD6E">Kurero</i> emerged in Edo Japanese during the late <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edo_period" title="Edo period" id="mwD6I">Edo period</a>.<sup about="#mwt1717" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001216_312-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001216&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001216-312&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;216&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001216-312" id="mwD6M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD6Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6U">[</span>291<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6Y">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwD6c">Yo</i> and <i id="mwD6g">i</i> are optionally added, just as to any other imperative form.</p>

<p id="mwD6k">Despite originally having the same conjugation as <i id="mwD6o">suru</i>,<sup about="#mwt1740" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-313" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-313&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-313" id="mwD6s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD60">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD64">]</span></span></a></sup> the imperative form of <i id="mwD68">‑masu(ru)</i> is not *<i id="mwD7A">‑mashiro</i>. However, there used to be <i id="mwD7E">‑mase i</i>, with <i id="mwD7I">i</i> being the western reduced form of <i id="mwD7M">yo</i>.<sup about="#mwt1743" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-314" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-314&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-314" id="mwD7Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD7U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7Y">[</span>293<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7c">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwD7g">‑Mase yo</i> exists, though not mandatorily like <i id="mwD7k">seyo</i>, but only as <i id="mwD7o">‑mase</i> optionally followed by <i id="mwD7s">yo</i>. <i id="mwD7w">‑Mashi</i> is a later variant, characteristic of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shitamachi" title="Shitamachi" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD70">Shitamachi</a>.<sup about="#mwt1726" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin20041031_315-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin20041031&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin20041031-315&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1031&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin20041031-315" id="mwD74"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD78"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8A">[</span>294<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8E">]</span></span></a></sup> It used to be common during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meiji_era" title="Meiji era" id="mwD8I">Meiji era</a>, but now has a connotation of unrefined speech. <i id="mwD8M">‑Mase</i> and <i id="mwD8Q">‑mashi</i> are meant to be used with honorific verbs, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1729" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD8U" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;いらっしゃいませ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;irasshaimase&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">irasshaimase</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1729" id="mwD8Y"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">いらっしゃいませ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1730" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD8c" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;為さいませ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nasaimase&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">nasaimase</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1730" id="mwD8g"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">為さいませ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1731" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD8k" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;遊ばしませ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;asobashimase&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">asobashimase</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1731" id="mwD8o"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">遊ばしませ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1732" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD8s" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;召し上がりませ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;meshiagarimase&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">meshiagarimase</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1732" id="mwD8w"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">召し上がりませ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>, etc, and not with ordinary verbs like *<span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1733" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD80" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;書きませ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kakimase&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kakimase</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1733" id="mwD84"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">書きませ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span> or *<span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1734" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD88" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;歩きませ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;arukimase&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">arukimase</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1734" id="mwD9A"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">歩きませ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1735" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001746_316-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001746&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001746-316&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;746&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001746-316" id="mwD9E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD9I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9M">[</span>295<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwD9U">The modern western <i id="mwD9Y">‑i</i> imperative has made its way to Tokyo in the "downtown" region of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shitamachi" title="Shitamachi" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD9c">Shitamachi</a>.<sup about="#mwt1744" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961_266-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;959–961&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266" id="mwD9g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD9k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9o">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1747" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-317" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-317&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin translated ''Shitamachi'' literally as \&quot;downtown,\&quot; but the name is about geographic [[elevation|height]], not southernness as referenced by the English term ''[[downtown]]''. The economic and cultural prestige associated with the English ''downtown'' is actually located in the higher region of [[Yamanote]].&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-317" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwD9w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD90"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD94">[</span>v<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD98">]</span></span></a></sup> It is not as well covered in education materials, although <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001" about="#mwt1750" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwD-A" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;harvcoltxt&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Harvcoltxt&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">Akimoto et al. (2001)</a><span class="error harv-error" style="display: none; font-size:100%" about="#mwt1750"> harvcoltxt error: no target: CITEREFAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001 (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Harv_and_Sfn_template_errors" title="Category:Harv and Sfn template errors">help</a>)</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Harv_and_Sfn_no-target_errors" about="#mwt1750" id="mwD-E"> do sporadically mention it.<sup about="#mwt1751" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001843,_849_318-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001843, 849&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001843,_849-318&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;843, 849&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001843,_849-318" id="mwD-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-Q">[</span>296<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-U">]</span></span></a></sup> When it is preceded by the vowel <i id="mwD-Y">e</i>, the resulting form is <i id="mwD-c">ē</i>, <i id="mwD-g">ei</i> or even <i id="mwD-k">e</i>, in keeping with the common realizations of such combination (see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_phonology#Vowel_sequences_and_long_vowels" title="Japanese phonology" about="#mwt1754" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD-o" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;section link&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Section_link&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Japanese phonology&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Vowel sequences and long vowels&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">Japanese phonology §<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Vowel sequences and long vowels</a>), hence <i id="mwD-s">se(e)/sei</i> (= <i id="mwD-w">shiro/seyo</i>)<sup about="#mwt1771" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-shiro_38-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-shiro&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-shiro-38" id="mwD-0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-8">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_A">]</span></span></a></sup> and <i id="mwD_E">ake(e)/akei</i> (= <i id="mwD_I">akero/akeyo</i>).<sup about="#mwt1772" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-akero_289-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-akero&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-akero-289" id="mwD_M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD_Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_U">[</span>269<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_Y">]</span></span></a></sup> In Kyushu, <i id="mwD_c">koi</i> can be similarly smoothed out into <i id="mwD_g">ke(e)</i><sup about="#mwt1773" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-koi_290-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-koi&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-koi-290" id="mwD_k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD_o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_s">[</span>270<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_w">]</span></span></a></sup> (compare the Tokyo variant <i id="mwD_0">sugē</i> of <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1755" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD_4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;凄い&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sugoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|awesome}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">sugoi</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1755" id="mwD_8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">凄い</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">awesome</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>; more at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Imperfective:_Conjugation_table" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwEAA">#Imperfective: Conjugation table</a>). Like <i id="mwEAE">yo</i>, <i id="mwEAI">i</i> can further attach to, among others, <i id="mwEAM">godan</i>/<i id="mwEAQ">yodan</i> imperatives, as well as eastern <i id="mwEAU">‑ro</i> imperatives, for example in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1756" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEAY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;「や、バッタだ。大バッタとれいッ。」&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;“Ya, batta da. Ōbatta tore ih.”&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|“Look, a grasshopper! Catch the big grasshopper!”}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">“Ya, batta da. Ōbatta tore ih.”</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1756" id="mwEAc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">「や、バッタだ。大バッタとれいッ。」</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">“Look, a grasshopper! Catch the big grasshopper!”</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1776" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-319" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-319&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-319" id="mwEAg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEAk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAo">[</span>297<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAs">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1757" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEAw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;とっととおりろい。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;totto to oriro i.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|get off quickly!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">totto to oriro i.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1757" id="mwEA0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">とっととおりろい。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">get off quickly!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1779" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-yamamoto-1950_320-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;yamamoto-1950&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-yamamoto-1950-320&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-yamamoto-1950-320" id="mwEA4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEA8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBA">[</span>298<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBE">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1758" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEBI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;開けろい&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akero i {{=}} Akero yo&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Open up!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Akero i = Akero yo</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1758" id="mwEBM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">開けろい</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Open up!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, etc; the particle <i id="mwEBQ">ya</i>, which can otherwise follow imperatives just like <i id="mwEBU">yo</i>, with a potential masculine ring, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1759" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEBY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;止せやい&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Yose ya i&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Cut it out!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Yose ya i</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1759" id="mwEBc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">止せやい</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Cut it out!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1760" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEBg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;はっきり言えやい&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Hakkiri ie ya i&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Speak clearly!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Hakkiri ie ya i</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1760" id="mwEBk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">はっきり言えやい</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Speak clearly!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, etc; and negative commands with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Imperfective:_Grammatical_compatibility" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwEBo"><i id="mwEBs">na</i> following conclusives</a>, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1761" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEBw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;よけいな口だしをするない。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Yokei na kuchidashi o suru na i.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{gloss|Don’t butt in needlessly!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Yokei na kuchidashi o suru na i.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1761" id="mwEB0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">よけいな口だしをするない。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Don’t butt in needlessly!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1780" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-yamamoto-1950_320-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;yamamoto-1950&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-yamamoto-1950-320" id="mwEB4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEB8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECA">[</span>298<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1762" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004960_309-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004960&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004960-309&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;960&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004960-309" id="mwECI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwECM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECQ">[</span>288<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200132–33_321-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200132–33&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200132–33-321&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Akimoto&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ishikawa&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Itoi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2001&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;32–33&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi200132–33-321" id="mwECY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwECc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECg">[</span>299<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECk">]</span></span></a></sup> It is also found in non-imperative constructions such as <i id="mwECo">ka i</i> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_particles" title="Japanese particles" id="mwECs">question marker</a>), <i id="mwECw">da i</i> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Copulae" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwEC0">copula</a>), <i id="mwEC4">‑ta/‑da i</i> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_conjugation_(ren'yōkei_base)#Perfective" title="Japanese conjugation (ren'yōkei base)" id="mwEC8">perfect</a>), although it has been said to be a variant of <i id="mwEDA">ne</i> in these cases rather than of <i id="mwEDE">yo</i>.<sup about="#mwt1768" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004934_322-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004934&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004934-322&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;934&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004934-322" id="mwEDI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEDM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDQ">[</span>300<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEDY">The older and more classical <i id="mwEDc">koyo</i> ("come!") is rare in modern spoken dialects,<sup about="#mwt1781" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ninjal-koi_290-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ninjal-koi&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ninjal-koi-290" id="mwEDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEDk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDo">[</span>270<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDs">]</span></span></a></sup> but it was sometimes used as the written version of <i id="mwEDw">koi</i>; for example, the linguist <a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/春日政治" title="ja:春日政治" class="extiw" id="mwED0">Kasuga Masaji</a> used <i id="mwED4">koyo</i> while analyzing nursery rhymes that contain <i id="mwED8">koi</i>.<sup about="#mwt1784" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kasuga-1939_323-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kasuga-1939&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-kasuga-1939-323&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kasuga-1939-323" id="mwEEA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEEE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEI">[</span>301<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEEQ"><i id="mwEEU">Gozai</i> and <i id="mwEEY">gozare</i> are used as a more polite way to say "come!" instead of <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1785" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEEc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;来い&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;koi&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">koi</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1785" id="mwEEg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">来い</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">)</span>. They also occur in the concessive idiom <i id="mwEEk">nan de mo gozai/gozare</i> (<abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1786" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:ExpandedAttrs" id="mwEEs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwEEo\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]],&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lit&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Lit&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;come anything&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;" about="#mwt1786"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot" about="#mwt1786">'</span><span class="gloss-text" about="#mwt1786">come anything</span><span class="gloss-quot" about="#mwt1786" id="mwEEw">'</span>, <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt1788" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:ExpandedAttrs" id="mwEE4" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwEE0\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]],&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;xlat&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Xlat&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;anything goes; anything's good; anything imaginable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">transl.</abbr><span about="#mwt1788" id="mwEE8"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>anything goes; anything's good; anything imaginable</span>),<sup about="#mwt1790" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kenkyusha_47-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kenkyusha&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kenkyusha-47" id="mwEFA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEFE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFI">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFM">]</span></span></a></sup> which is synonymous with <i id="mwEFQ">nan de mo koi</i>.<sup about="#mwt1793" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-324" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-324&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-324" id="mwEFU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEFY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFc">[</span>302<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFg">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwEFk">De gozare</i> is a more polite equivalent to <i id="mwEFo">de are</i>.</p>

<p id="mwEFs"><i id="mwEFw">Are</i> and <i id="mwEF0">de (wa) are</i> have limited use in formal contexts, for example <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1794" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEF4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;神も照覧あれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Kami mo shōran are&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|may God be my witness}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Kami mo shōran are</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1794" id="mwEF8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">神も照覧あれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">may God be my witness</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1795" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961_266-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;959–961&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266" id="mwEGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGI">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGM">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1798" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEGQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[:ja:光あれ|光あれ]]&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;hikari are&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|[[let there be light]]}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">hikari are</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1798" id="mwEGU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja"><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/光あれ" title="ja:光あれ" class="extiw">光あれ</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_there_be_light" title="Let there be light">let there be light</a></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1799" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEGY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;いと高きところには栄光、神にあれ、地には平和、御心に適う人にあれ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ito takaki tokoro ni wa eikō, Kami ni are, chi ni wa heiwa, mikokoro ni kanau hito ni are.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|In the highest realm, glory be unto God, on earth, peace be unto those who earn his grace.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Ito takaki tokoro ni wa eikō, Kami ni are, chi ni wa heiwa, mikokoro ni kanau hito ni are.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1799" id="mwEGc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">いと高きところには栄光、神にあれ、地には平和、御心に適う人にあれ。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">In the highest realm, glory be unto God, on earth, peace be unto those who earn his grace.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1817" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-325" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-325&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-325" id="mwEGg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGo">[</span>303<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGs">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1800" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEGw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;いつも神に従ってあれ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;itsu mo Kami ni shitagatte are.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|always be obedient to God.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">itsu mo Kami ni shitagatte are.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1800" id="mwEG0"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">いつも神に従ってあれ。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">always be obedient to God.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1820" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kaizu_326-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kaizu&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-kaizu-326&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kaizu-326" id="mwEG4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEG8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHA">[</span>304<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHE">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1801" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEHI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;正直であれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;shōjiki de are&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be honest}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">shōjiki de are</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1801" id="mwEHM"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">正直であれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be honest</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1802" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961_266-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;959–961&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004959–961-266" id="mwEHQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEHU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHY">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHc">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwEHg">De (wa) are</i> also has a concessive use, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1805" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEHk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;理由は何であれ，暴力はよくないよ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Riyū wa nan de are, bōryoku wa yoku nai yo.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|No matter the reason, violence is not good.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Riyū wa nan de are, bōryoku wa yoku nai yo.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1805" id="mwEHo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">理由は何であれ，暴力はよくないよ。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">No matter the reason, violence is not good.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1823" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kitazaki_327-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kitazaki&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-kitazaki-327&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kitazaki-327" id="mwEHs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEH0">[</span>305<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEH4">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1806" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEH8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;何の部屋であれ、もうここに泊めてもらうほかはない&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nan no heya de are, mō koko ni tomete morau hoka wa nai&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|Whatever the room may be, we have no choice but to stay here.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Nan no heya de are, mō koko ni tomete morau hoka wa nai</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1806" id="mwEIA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">何の部屋であれ、もうここに泊めてもらうほかはない</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Whatever the room may be, we have no choice but to stay here.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1807" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962_328-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962-328&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;961–962&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962-328" id="mwEIE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEII"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIM">[</span>306<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIQ">]</span></span></a></sup> This has been linked to a probable contraction from the identically sounding <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Conditional" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwEIU">conditional</a> base, <i id="mwEIY">de are</i>, preceding the concessive particle <i id="mwEIc">‑do</i>, as in <i id="mwEIg">de aredo</i>.<sup about="#mwt1810" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962_328-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962-328&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;961–962&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004961–962-328" id="mwEIk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEIo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIs">[</span>306<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIw">]</span></span></a></sup> However, unambiguously imperative bases in <i id="mwEI0">ni seyo</i> and <i id="mwEI4">ni shiro</i> also have concessive uses, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1813" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEI8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;参加するにせよ，しないにせよ，とりあえず連絡を下さい。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sanka suru ni seyo, shinai ni seyo, toriaezu renraku o kudasai.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|Whether you partake or not, please get in touch soon.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sanka suru ni seyo, shinai ni seyo, toriaezu renraku o kudasai.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1813" id="mwEJA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">参加するにせよ，しないにせよ，とりあえず連絡を下さい。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Whether you partake or not, please get in touch soon.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> and <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1814" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEJE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;そばにしろ，うどんにしろ，麺類なら何でもいいんだ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Soba ni shiro, udon ni shiro, menrui nara nan de mo ii n da.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|Soba, udon, whatever, any kind of noodles will do.}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Soba ni shiro, udon ni shiro, menrui nara nan de mo ii n da.</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1814" id="mwEJI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">そばにしろ，うどんにしろ，麺類なら何でもいいんだ。</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">Soba, udon, whatever, any kind of noodles will do.</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span><sup about="#mwt1824" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kitazaki_327-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kitazaki&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kitazaki-327" id="mwEJM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJU">[</span>305<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEJc">Unlike <i id="mwEJg">are</i>, adjectival imperative forms derived from fusions with it (<i id="mwEJk">‑ku are</i> → <i id="mwEJo">‑kare</i>) seem to be used mostly for concession, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1825" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEJs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;多かれ少なかれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ōkare sukunakare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be there more or less}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ōkare sukunakare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1825" id="mwEJw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">多かれ少なかれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be there more or less</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1826" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEJ0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;高かれ安かれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;takakare yasukare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be it expensive or cheap}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">takakare yasukare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1826" id="mwEJ4"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">高かれ安かれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be it expensive or cheap</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1827" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEJ8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;強かれ弱かれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;tsuyokare yowakare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be it strong or weak}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">tsuyokare yowakare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1827" id="mwEKA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">強かれ弱かれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be it strong or weak</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1828" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEKE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;遅かれ早かれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;osokare hayakare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be it later or sooner}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">osokare hayakare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1828" id="mwEKI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">遅かれ早かれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be it later or sooner</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1829" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEKM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;良かれ悪しかれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;yokare ashikare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be it good or bad}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">yokare ashikare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1829" id="mwEKQ"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">良かれ悪しかれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be it good or bad</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>,<sup about="#mwt1830" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004962_329-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004962&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004962-329&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;962&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004962-329" id="mwEKU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEKY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKc">[</span>307<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKg">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1833" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEKk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;遠かれ近かれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;tōkare chikakare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be it far or near}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">tōkare chikakare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1833" id="mwEKo"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">遠かれ近かれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be it far or near</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, etc and occasionally for elevated wishes, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1834" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEKs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;安かれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Yasukare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{xlat|May you be at peace}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Yasukare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1834" id="mwEKw"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">安かれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt1835" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwEK0\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>May you be at peace</span>)</span><sup about="#mwt1861" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kenkyusha_47-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kenkyusha&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kenkyusha-47" id="mwEK4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEK8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELA">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1836" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-331" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;lower-alpha&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-331&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;efn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Efn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''Yasui'' used to mean \&quot;be at peace\&quot;,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|lang=ja|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%AE%89%E3%81%84-648307|script-title=ja:安い|script-work=ja:コトバンク}}</ref> but apart from this imperative form, this meaning is now uncommon.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-331" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwELI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwELM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELQ">[</span>w<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELU">]</span></span></a></sup> or <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1846" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwELY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;幸多かれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sachi ōkare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{xlat|Best of luck to you}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Sachi ōkare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1846" id="mwELc"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">幸多かれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt1847" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwELg\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Best of luck to you</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1864" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-super-daijirin_332-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;super-daijirin&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-super-daijirin-332&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-super-daijirin-332" id="mwELk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwELo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELs">[</span>309<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELw">]</span></span></a></sup> The exceptional <i id="mwEL0">nakare</i> ("let there not be") expresses elevated and/or motivational negative commands or wishes, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1848" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEL4" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;驕るなかれ！自民党&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ogoru nakare! Jimintō&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{xlat|Do not be prideful! O, Liberal Democratic Party}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Ogoru nakare! Jimintō</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1848" id="mwEL8"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">驕るなかれ！自民党</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt1849" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwEMA\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Do not be prideful! O, Liberal Democratic Party</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1850" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEME" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;高が便秘と言うなかれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Taka ga benpi to yū nakare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{xlat|Don't say it's just constipation}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">Taka ga benpi to yū nakare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1850" id="mwEMI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">高が便秘と言うなかれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr title="translation" about="#mwt1851" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwEMM\&quot;>translation</span>&quot;}]]}">transl.</abbr><span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Don't say it's just constipation</span>)</span>, etc. The phrase <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1852" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEMQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;事なかれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;koto nakare&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{lit|let there be no incident}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">koto nakare</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1852" id="mwEMU"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">事なかれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <abbr style="font-size:85%" title="literal translation" about="#mwt1853" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw="{&quot;attribs&quot;:[[{&quot;txt&quot;:&quot;title&quot;},{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;<span typeof=\&quot;mw:Nowiki\&quot; id=\&quot;mwEMY\&quot;>literal translation</span>&quot;}]]}">lit.</abbr><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">let there be no incident</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span> is used in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1854" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEMc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;事なかれ主義&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;koto nakare shugi&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|principle of not rocking the boat}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">koto nakare shugi</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1854" id="mwEMg"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">事なかれ主義</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">principle of not rocking the boat</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1865" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kenkyusha_47-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kenkyusha&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-kenkyusha-47" id="mwEMk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEMo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMs">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMw">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwEM0">Nakare</i> behaves syntactically like the negative imperative particle <i id="mwEM4">na</i>, which is similarly placed after an attributive/conclusive verb, thus <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1855" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEM8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;驕るな&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ogoru na&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|don't be prideful}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">ogoru na</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1855" id="mwENA"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">驕るな</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">don't be prideful</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1856" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwENE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;言うな&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;yū na&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|don't say}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">yū na</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1856" id="mwENI"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">言うな</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">don't say</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>, etc.<sup about="#mwt1857" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004942,_962_333-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMartin2004942, 962&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004942,_962-333&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfnp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfnp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Martin&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;942, 962&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004942,_962-333" id="mwENM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwENQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENU">[</span>310<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENY">]</span></span></a></sup> Unfused <i id="mwENc">‑ku are</i> forms have also been found, as in <span title="Hepburn transliteration" about="#mwt1860" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwENg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:nihongo&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nihongo&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;清くあれ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;kiyoku are&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; {{gloss|be pure!}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i lang="ja-Latn">kiyoku are</i></span><span style="font-weight: normal" about="#mwt1860" id="mwENk"> (<span title="Japanese-language text"><span lang="ja">清くあれ</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text">; <span class="gloss-quot">'</span><span class="gloss-text">be pure!</span><span class="gloss-quot">'</span>)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1868" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-334" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-334&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-334" id="mwENo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwENs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENw">[</span>311<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEN0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

