<li about="#cite_note-479" id="cite_note-479" data-mw-footnote-number="447"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWAw"><a href="#cite_ref-479" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWA0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWA4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-479" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3002" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWA8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:お浄土があると信じればいいのです。「信じること」なんですから、これは妄想ではないのです。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=192&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第九章 お浄土を信じる&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:『歎異抄』を読む&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Suzuki Shuppan&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=February 2008&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;orig-date=January 1993&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;edition=10th&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;author=[[Hiro Sachiya]]&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last2=Go&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first2=Samyeong&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last3=Yamazaki&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first3=Ryūmyō&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHiro_SachiyaGoYamazaki2008" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3002"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hiro_Sachiya" title="Hiro Sachiya" id="mwWBA">Hiro Sachiya</a>; Go, Samyeong; Yamazaki, Ryūmyō (February 2008) [January 1993].  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWBE">第九章 お浄土を信じる</bdi>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWBI">『歎異抄』を読む</bdi> (in Japanese) (10th<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWBM">&nbsp;</span>ed.). Suzuki Shuppan. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWBQ">&nbsp;</span>192.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWBU">お浄土があると信じればいいのです。「信じること」なんですから、これは妄想ではないのです。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E4%B9%9D%E7%AB%A0+%E3%81%8A%E6%B5%84%E5%9C%9F%E3%82%92%E4%BF%A1%E3%81%98%E3%82%8B&amp;rft.btitle=%E3%80%8E%E6%AD%8E%E7%95%B0%E6%8A%84%E3%80%8F%E3%82%92%E8%AA%AD%E3%82%80&amp;rft.pages=192&amp;rft.edition=10th&amp;rft.pub=Suzuki+Shuppan&amp;rft.date=2008-02&amp;rft.au=Hiro+Sachiya&amp;rft.au=Go%2C+Samyeong&amp;rft.au=Yamazaki%2C+Ry%C5%ABmy%C5%8D&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3002" id="mwWBY"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3002" id="mwWBc"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3002" id="mwWBg"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-480" id="cite_note-480" data-mw-footnote-number="448"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWBk"><a href="#cite_ref-480" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWBo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWBs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-480" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3005" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWBw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:人間が信じれば信じるほど神は明確な像を結ぶ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=111&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://koara.lib.keio.ac.jp/xoonips/modules/xoonips/download.php?file_id=39363&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Nishiyama&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Teruo&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:ベルクソンにおける身体の社会性（２）&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=La sociabilité du corps chez Bergson (2ème partie)&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:エティカ&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal=Ethica&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=3&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2010&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFNishiyama2010" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3005">Nishiyama, Teruo (2010). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://koara.lib.keio.ac.jp/xoonips/modules/xoonips/download.php?file_id=39363" class="external text" id="mwWB0">"La sociabilité du corps chez Bergson (2ème partie)" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWB4">ベルクソンにおける身体の社会性（２）</bdi></a>. <i id="mwWB8">Ethica</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWCA">エティカ</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWCE">3</b>: 111.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWCI">人間が信じれば信じるほど神は明確な像を結ぶ。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Ethica&amp;rft.atitle=La+sociabilit%C3%A9+du+corps+chez+Bergson+%282%C3%A8me+partie%29+%E3%83%99%E3%83%AB%E3%82%AF%E3%82%BD%E3%83%B3%E3%81%AB%E3%81%8A%E3%81%91%E3%82%8B%E8%BA%AB%E4%BD%93%E3%81%AE%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E6%80%A7%EF%BC%88%EF%BC%92%EF%BC%89&amp;rft.volume=3&amp;rft.pages=111&amp;rft.date=2010&amp;rft.aulast=Nishiyama&amp;rft.aufirst=Teruo&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fkoara.lib.keio.ac.jp%2Fxoonips%2Fmodules%2Fxoonips%2Fdownload.php%3Ffile_id%3D39363&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3005" id="mwWCM"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3005" id="mwWCQ"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3005" id="mwWCU"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-481" id="cite_note-481" data-mw-footnote-number="449"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWCY"><a href="#cite_ref-481" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWCc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWCg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-481" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3008" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWCk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:そういった中で，何かを信じるための軸はどのように作られるのだろうか，と疑問に思いました．発言している人を信じればよいのでしょうか？&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=273&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/mededjapan/53/3/53_270/_pdf/-char/ja&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Oikawa&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Sayaka&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last2=Kimura&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first2=Takeshi&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last3=Nishigori&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first3=Hiroshi&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:「医学教育研究室の抄読会から」（連載第 13 回）&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:医学教育&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=53&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=3&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2022&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFOikawaKimuraNishigori2022" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3008">Oikawa, Sayaka; Kimura, Takeshi; Nishigori, Hiroshi (2022). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/mededjapan/53/3/53_270/_pdf/-char/ja" class="external text" id="mwWCo"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWCs">「医学教育研究室の抄読会から」（連載第 13 回）</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWCw">医学教育</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWC0">53</b> (3): 273.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWC4">そういった中で，何かを信じるための軸はどのように作られるのだろうか，と疑問に思いました．発言している人を信じればよいのでしょうか？</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E3%80%8C%E5%8C%BB%E5%AD%A6%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6%E5%AE%A4%E3%81%AE%E6%8A%84%E8%AA%AD%E4%BC%9A%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E3%80%8D%EF%BC%88%E9%80%A3%E8%BC%89%E7%AC%AC+13+%E5%9B%9E%EF%BC%89&amp;rft.volume=53&amp;rft.issue=3&amp;rft.pages=273&amp;rft.date=2022&amp;rft.aulast=Oikawa&amp;rft.aufirst=Sayaka&amp;rft.au=Kimura%2C+Takeshi&amp;rft.au=Nishigori%2C+Hiroshi&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jstage.jst.go.jp%2Farticle%2Fmededjapan%2F53%2F3%2F53_270%2F_pdf%2F-char%2Fja&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3008" id="mwWC8"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3008" id="mwWDA"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3008" id="mwWDE"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-482" id="cite_note-482" data-mw-footnote-number="450"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWDI"><a href="#cite_ref-482" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWDM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWDQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-482" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3011" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWDU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:次に青年騎士の選択がこれに絡んでくる。彼の場合は、わりあい簡単に、王女を信じる・信じないの二つのケースになる。そして、王女信ずれば右の扉を開ければよいし、信じない場合は左の扉を開けるであろう。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=24&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:プロローグ●つまるところは諦めか&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:「賭け」と宗教&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=1 June 1995&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Suzuki Shuppan&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;author=[[Hiro Sachiya]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHiro_Sachiya1995" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3011"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hiro_Sachiya" title="Hiro Sachiya" id="mwWDY">Hiro Sachiya</a> (1 June 1995).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWDc">プロローグ●つまるところは諦めか</bdi>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWDg">「賭け」と宗教</bdi> (in Japanese). Suzuki Shuppan. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWDk">&nbsp;</span>24.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWDo">次に青年騎士の選択がこれに絡んでくる。彼の場合は、わりあい簡単に、王女を信じる・信じないの二つのケースになる。そして、王女信ずれば右の扉を開ければよいし、信じない場合は左の扉を開けるであろう。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E3%83%97%E3%83%AD%E3%83%AD%E3%83%BC%E3%82%B0%E2%97%8F%E3%81%A4%E3%81%BE%E3%82%8B%E3%81%A8%E3%81%93%E3%82%8D%E3%81%AF%E8%AB%A6%E3%82%81%E3%81%8B&amp;rft.btitle=%E3%80%8C%E8%B3%AD%E3%81%91%E3%80%8D%E3%81%A8%E5%AE%97%E6%95%99&amp;rft.pages=24&amp;rft.pub=Suzuki+Shuppan&amp;rft.date=1995-06-01&amp;rft.au=Hiro+Sachiya&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3011" id="mwWDs"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3011" id="mwWDw"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3011" id="mwWD0"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-483" id="cite_note-483" data-mw-footnote-number="451"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWD4"><a href="#cite_ref-483" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWD8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWEA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-483" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3014" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWEE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:なぜならば唯物論や弁証法を間違いのない心理であると信ずれば、それを適用してできた唯物史観も、間違いのない心理であると信じるほどかないためである。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=203–204&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第四章 唯物史観の批判とその代案&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:要約　統一思想・勝共理論&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;author={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|鮮文大学校統一思想研究院}}&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Kōgensha&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=1 August 2002&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREF鮮文大学校統一思想研究院Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text2002" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3014"><span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwWEI"><span lang="ja" id="mwWEM">鮮文大学校統一思想研究院</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwWEQ"> (1 August 2002).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWEU">第四章 唯物史観の批判とその代案</bdi>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWEY">要約　統一思想・勝共理論</bdi> (in Japanese). Kōgensha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWEc">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwWEg">203–</span>204.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWEk">なぜならば唯物論や弁証法を間違いのない心理であると信ずれば、それを適用してできた唯物史観も、間違いのない心理であると信じるほどかないためである。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E5%9B%9B%E7%AB%A0+%E5%94%AF%E7%89%A9%E5%8F%B2%E8%A6%B3%E3%81%AE%E6%89%B9%E5%88%A4%E3%81%A8%E3%81%9D%E3%81%AE%E4%BB%A3%E6%A1%88&amp;rft.btitle=%E8%A6%81%E7%B4%84%E3%80%80%E7%B5%B1%E4%B8%80%E6%80%9D%E6%83%B3%E3%83%BB%E5%8B%9D%E5%85%B1%E7%90%86%E8%AB%96&amp;rft.pages=203-204&amp;rft.pub=K%C5%8Dgensha&amp;rft.date=2002-08-01&amp;rft.au=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E9%AE%AE%E6%96%87%E5%A4%A7%E5%AD%A6%E6%A0%A1%E7%B5%B1%E4%B8%80%E6%80%9D%E6%83%B3%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6%E9%99%A2%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3014" id="mwWEo"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3014" id="mwWEs"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3014" id="mwWEw"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-484" id="cite_note-484" data-mw-footnote-number="452"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWE0"><a href="#cite_ref-484" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWE4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWE8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-484" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3017" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWFA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:珍海『三論名教抄』（『大正蔵』Vol. 70、No. 2306, p. 828c12-c13）また、珍海は同抄の第五巻に、吉蔵の『法華義疏』「提婆達多品第十二」の文を引用して、『仁王経』を信じるだけではなく、『法華経』にも一念に信ずれば、八難、三途の難を離れ、地獄に堕ちないと述べている。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=121&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://icabs.repo.nii.ac.jp/?action=repository_uri&amp;item_id=465&amp;file_id=22&amp;file_no=1&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Qi&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Wang&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:珍海の「一念信」について　――『大乗正観略私記』を中心として――&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:仙石山仏教学論集&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=10&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2018&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFWang2018" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3017">Wang, Qi (2018). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://icabs.repo.nii.ac.jp/?action=repository_uri&amp;item_id=465&amp;file_id=22&amp;file_no=1" class="external text" id="mwWFE"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWFI">珍海の「一念信」について　――『大乗正観略私記』を中心として――</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWFM">仙石山仏教学論集</bdi> (in Japanese) (10): 121.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWFQ">珍海『三論名教抄』（『大正蔵』Vol. 70、No. 2306, p. 828c12-c13）また、珍海は同抄の第五巻に、吉蔵の『法華義疏』「提婆達多品第十二」の文を引用して、『仁王経』を信じるだけではなく、『法華経』にも一念に信ずれば、八難、三途の難を離れ、地獄に堕ちないと述べている。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%8F%8D%E6%B5%B7%E3%81%AE%E3%80%8C%E4%B8%80%E5%BF%B5%E4%BF%A1%E3%80%8D%E3%81%AB%E3%81%A4%E3%81%84%E3%81%A6%E3%80%80%E2%80%95%E2%80%95%E3%80%8E%E5%A4%A7%E4%B9%97%E6%AD%A3%E8%A6%B3%E7%95%A5%E7%A7%81%E8%A8%98%E3%80%8F%E3%82%92%E4%B8%AD%E5%BF%83%E3%81%A8%E3%81%97%E3%81%A6%E2%80%95%E2%80%95&amp;rft.issue=10&amp;rft.pages=121&amp;rft.date=2018&amp;rft.aulast=Wang&amp;rft.aufirst=Qi&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Ficabs.repo.nii.ac.jp%2F%3Faction%3Drepository_uri%26item_id%3D465%26file_id%3D22%26file_no%3D1&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3017" id="mwWFU"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3017" id="mwWFY"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3017" id="mwWFc"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-485" id="cite_note-485" data-mw-footnote-number="453"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWFg"><a href="#cite_ref-485" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWFk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWFo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-485" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3044" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWFs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:金銀の持ち合せはないから、進ぜることはできないと刎ね付たのである。[…]それを進ぜれば一厘なしになる、&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=212, 214&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:一〇三、他人に何をも與へ得ない人が貧乏の人である&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1174899/1/119&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:靜心雜記&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Hakuyosha&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Kanda, Tokyo]]&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Daikichirō&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Tagawa&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=14 May 1930&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFTagawa1930" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3044">Tagawa, Daikichirō (14 May 1930).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWFw">一〇三、他人に何をも與へ得ない人が貧乏の人である</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1174899/1/119" class="external text" id="mwWF0"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWF4">靜心雜記</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanda,_Tokyo" title="Kanda, Tokyo" id="mwWF8">Kanda, Tokyo</a>: Hakuyosha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWGA">&nbsp;</span>212, 214.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWGE">金銀の持ち合せはないから、進ぜることはできないと刎ね付たのである。[…]それを進ぜれば一厘なしになる、</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E4%B8%80%E3%80%87%E4%B8%89%E3%80%81%E4%BB%96%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%AB%E4%BD%95%E3%82%92%E3%82%82%E8%88%87%E3%81%B8%E5%BE%97%E3%81%AA%E3%81%84%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%8C%E8%B2%A7%E4%B9%8F%E3%81%AE%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%A7%E3%81%82%E3%82%8B&amp;rft.btitle=%E9%9D%9C%E5%BF%83%E9%9B%9C%E8%A8%98&amp;rft.place=Kanda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=212%2C+214&amp;rft.pub=Hakuyosha&amp;rft.date=1930-05-14&amp;rft.aulast=Tagawa&amp;rft.aufirst=Daikichir%C5%8D&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1174899%2F1%2F119&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3044" id="mwWGI"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3044" id="mwWGM"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3044" id="mwWGQ"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-486" id="cite_note-486" data-mw-footnote-number="454"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWGU"><a href="#cite_ref-486" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWGY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWGc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-486" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3047" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWGg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1939867/1/192&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:『これ<ruby>榊<rp>(</rp><rt>さかき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>原<rp>(</rp><rt>ばら</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>氏<rp>(</rp><rt>うぢ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、この度び、わしの妹を<ruby>濱<rp>(</rp><rt>はま</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>松<rp>(</rp><rt>まつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>殿<rp>(</rp><rt>どの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>へ<ruby>進<rp>(</rp><rt>しん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ぜるにについては、<ruby>是<rp>(</rp><rt>ぜ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>非<rp>(</rp><rt>ひ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ともそなたに親許になつて貰はねばならんぞ』<br/>[…]<br/>『そのように一<ruby>圖<rp>(</rp><rt>づ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に思ひつめては成らん。ようく<ruby>考<rp>(</rp><rt>かんが</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>えて<ruby>見<rp>(</rp><rt>み</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>よ、そちが今、<ruby>秀<rp>(</rp><rt>ひで</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>吉の<ruby>望<rp>(</rp><rt>のぞ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>みを叶へて<ruby>進<rp>(</rp><rt>しん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ずれば、我<ruby>等<rp>(</rp><rt>ら</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>への<ruby>忠<rp>(</rp><rt>ちう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>義<rp>(</rp><rt>ぎ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、まつたその<ruby>身<rp>(</rp><rt>み</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の果<ruby>報<rp>(</rp><rt>はう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>』&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=253, 350&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:太閤記&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Sōun&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Yada&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=30 May 1933&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Hōbunkan&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Nihonbashi]], Tokyo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFYada1933" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3047">Yada, Sōun (30 May 1933). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1939867/1/192" class="external text" id="mwWGk"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWGo">太閤記</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi" title="Nihonbashi" id="mwWGs">Nihonbashi</a>, Tokyo: Hōbunkan. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWGw">&nbsp;</span>253, 350.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWG0">『これ<ruby id="mwWG4">榊<rp id="mwWG8">(</rp><rt id="mwWHA">さかき</rt><rp id="mwWHE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWHI">原<rp id="mwWHM">(</rp><rt id="mwWHQ">ばら</rt><rp id="mwWHU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWHY">氏<rp id="mwWHc">(</rp><rt id="mwWHg">うぢ</rt><rp id="mwWHk">)</rp></ruby>、この度び、わしの妹を<ruby id="mwWHo">濱<rp id="mwWHs">(</rp><rt id="mwWHw">はま</rt><rp id="mwWH0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWH4">松<rp id="mwWH8">(</rp><rt id="mwWIA">まつ</rt><rp id="mwWIE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWII">殿<rp id="mwWIM">(</rp><rt id="mwWIQ">どの</rt><rp id="mwWIU">)</rp></ruby>へ<ruby id="mwWIY">進<rp id="mwWIc">(</rp><rt id="mwWIg">しん</rt><rp id="mwWIk">)</rp></ruby>ぜるにについては、<ruby id="mwWIo">是<rp id="mwWIs">(</rp><rt id="mwWIw">ぜ</rt><rp id="mwWI0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWI4">非<rp id="mwWI8">(</rp><rt id="mwWJA">ひ</rt><rp id="mwWJE">)</rp></ruby>ともそなたに親許になつて貰はねばならんぞ』<br id="mwWJI">[…]<br id="mwWJM">『そのように一<ruby id="mwWJQ">圖<rp id="mwWJU">(</rp><rt id="mwWJY">づ</rt><rp id="mwWJc">)</rp></ruby>に思ひつめては成らん。ようく<ruby id="mwWJg">考<rp id="mwWJk">(</rp><rt id="mwWJo">かんが</rt><rp id="mwWJs">)</rp></ruby>えて<ruby id="mwWJw">見<rp id="mwWJ0">(</rp><rt id="mwWJ4">み</rt><rp id="mwWJ8">)</rp></ruby>よ、そちが今、<ruby id="mwWKA">秀<rp id="mwWKE">(</rp><rt id="mwWKI">ひで</rt><rp id="mwWKM">)</rp></ruby>吉の<ruby id="mwWKQ">望<rp id="mwWKU">(</rp><rt id="mwWKY">のぞ</rt><rp id="mwWKc">)</rp></ruby>みを叶へて<ruby id="mwWKg">進<rp id="mwWKk">(</rp><rt id="mwWKo">しん</rt><rp id="mwWKs">)</rp></ruby>ずれば、我<ruby id="mwWKw">等<rp id="mwWK0">(</rp><rt id="mwWK4">ら</rt><rp id="mwWK8">)</rp></ruby>への<ruby id="mwWLA">忠<rp id="mwWLE">(</rp><rt id="mwWLI">ちう</rt><rp id="mwWLM">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWLQ">義<rp id="mwWLU">(</rp><rt id="mwWLY">ぎ</rt><rp id="mwWLc">)</rp></ruby>、まつたその<ruby id="mwWLg">身<rp id="mwWLk">(</rp><rt id="mwWLo">み</rt><rp id="mwWLs">)</rp></ruby>の果<ruby id="mwWLw">報<rp id="mwWL0">(</rp><rt id="mwWL4">はう</rt><rp id="mwWL8">)</rp></ruby>』</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=%E5%A4%AA%E9%96%A4%E8%A8%98&amp;rft.place=Nihonbashi%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=253%2C+350&amp;rft.pub=H%C5%8Dbunkan&amp;rft.date=1933-05-30&amp;rft.aulast=Yada&amp;rft.aufirst=S%C5%8Dun&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1939867%2F1%2F192&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3047" id="mwWMA"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3047" id="mwWME"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3047" id="mwWMI"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ogawa-1922-487" id="cite_note-ogawa-1922-487" data-mw-footnote-number="455"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWMM"><a href="#cite_ref-ogawa-1922_487-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWMQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWMU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ogawa-1922-487" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3100" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWMY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:しかし彼が長く生くれば生くる程、その靈は一層聲高く談り出で、一層遠く肉體と靈との欲望は離反する。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=But the longer he lives, the more loudly speaks his soul, and the further diverge the desires of his body and of his soul.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/969262/1/86&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;p=161&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:罪、誤謬、及迷信&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;chapter=Sins, Errors and Superstitions&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:愛と智慧との言葉&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=THE PATHWAY OF LIFE: TEACHING LOVE AND WISDOM&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first2=Archibald John&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last2=Wolfe&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Ogawa&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Tatsuhiko&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Leo Tolstoy&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Leo&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Tolstoy&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Rakuyōdō&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=31 July 1922&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Kōjimachi]], Tokyo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFTolstoyWolfe1922" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3100"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_Tolstoy" title="Leo Tolstoy" id="mwWMc">Tolstoy, Leo</a>; Wolfe, Archibald John (31 July 1922). "Sins, Errors and Superstitions" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWMg">罪、誤謬、及迷信</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/969262/1/86" class="external text" id="mwWMk"><i id="mwWMo">THE PATHWAY OF LIFE: TEACHING LOVE AND WISDOM</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWMs">愛と智慧との言葉</bdi></a> (in Japanese). Translated by Ogawa, Tatsuhiko. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kōjimachi" title="Kōjimachi" id="mwWMw">Kōjimachi</a>, Tokyo: Rakuyōdō. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWM0">&nbsp;</span>161. <q id="mwWM4">But the longer he lives, the more loudly speaks his soul, and the further diverge the desires of his body and of his soul.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWM8">しかし彼が長く生くれば生くる程、その靈は一層聲高く談り出で、一層遠く肉體と靈との欲望は離反する。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Sins%2C+Errors+and+Superstitions+%E7%BD%AA%E3%80%81%E8%AA%A4%E8%AC%AC%E3%80%81%E5%8F%8A%E8%BF%B7%E4%BF%A1&amp;rft.btitle=THE+PATHWAY+OF+LIFE%3A+TEACHING+LOVE+AND+WISDOM+%E6%84%9B%E3%81%A8%E6%99%BA%E6%85%A7%E3%81%A8%E3%81%AE%E8%A8%80%E8%91%89&amp;rft.place=K%C5%8Djimachi%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=161&amp;rft.pub=Rakuy%C5%8Dd%C5%8D&amp;rft.date=1922-07-31&amp;rft.aulast=Tolstoy&amp;rft.aufirst=Leo&amp;rft.au=Wolfe%2C+Archibald+John&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F969262%2F1%2F86&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3100" id="mwWNA"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3100" id="mwWNE"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3100" id="mwWNI"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-488" id="cite_note-488" data-mw-footnote-number="456"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWNM"><a href="#cite_ref-488" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWNQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWNU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-488" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3121" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWNY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:然るに近頃王子は憂欝にかゝつて姬を疎んじ、狂人を裝はんと思ひ構へてからは、姬に接する態度が冷淡でやや<ruby>突<rp>(</rp><rt>つく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>慳<rp>(</rp><rt>けん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>貪<rp>(</rp><rt>どん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>である樣にした。然し姬は心麗しくて王子の<ruby>情<rp>(</rp><rt>つれ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>なき素振りに<ruby>怨<rp>(</rp><rt>うらみ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>言を云ふ事もなく、却つて、心に<ruby>病氣<rp>(</rp><rt>いたつき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>あるが爲めで以前よりも我身を<ruby>疎<rp>(</rp><rt>うと</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>んずる<ruby>鬼<rp>(</rp><rt>おに</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>心<rp>(</rp><rt>ごゝろ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>あるが爲めでは無いと思ひ<ruby>諦<rp>(</rp><rt>あき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>らめ、更にまた王子の氣高かりし心、勝れし分別の力も、深き憂鬱に閉されては、本來絕妙なる樂音を發し得る<ruby>妙<rp>(</rp><rt>た</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>へなる鐘鈴も、調子<ruby>構<rp>(</rp><rt>かまは</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ず打ち鳴らされ或は粗暴な<ruby>扱<rp>(</rp><rt>あつか</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ひを受くれば、<ruby>耳<rp>(</rp><rt>みゝ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>障<rp>(</rp><rt>ざは</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>りな不快の狂音を<ruby>放<rp>(</rp><rt>はな</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>つにも比すべきであると考へた。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=But the melancholy which he fell into latterly had made him neglect her, and from the time he conceived the project of counterfeiting madness, he affected to treat her with unkindness, and a sort of rudeness: but she, good lady, rather than reproach him with being false to her, persuaded herself that it was nothing but the disease in his mind, and no settled unkindness, which had made him less observant of her than formerly; and she compared the faculties of his once noble mind and excellent understanding, impaired as they were with the deep melancholy that oppressed him, to sweet bells which in themselves are capable of most exquisite music, but when jangled out of tune, or rudely handled, produce only a harsh and unpleasing sound.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1037405/1/21&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pp=18–19&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;chapter=HAMLET, PRINCE OF DENMARK&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:<ruby>丁<rp>(</rp><rt>デン</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>抹<rp>(</rp><rt>マーク</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>王子ハムレツト物語&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:シェクスピア物語&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=TALES FROM SHAKESPEARE&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Charles Lamb&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Charles&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Lamb&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink2=Mary Lamb&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first2=Mary Anne&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last2=Lamb&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Mineo&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Toshiharu&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Gaigo Kenkyusha&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Hongō, Tokyo]]&quot;},&quot;21&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=25 January 1937&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFLambLamb1937" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3121"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Lamb" title="Charles Lamb" id="mwWNc">Lamb, Charles</a>; <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Lamb" title="Mary Lamb" id="mwWNg">Lamb, Mary Anne</a> (25 January 1937). "HAMLET, PRINCE OF DENMARK" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWNk"><ruby id="mwWNo">丁<rp id="mwWNs">(</rp><rt id="mwWNw">デン</rt><rp id="mwWN0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWN4">抹<rp id="mwWN8">(</rp><rt id="mwWOA">マーク</rt><rp id="mwWOE">)</rp></ruby>王子ハムレツト物語</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1037405/1/21" class="external text" id="mwWOI"><i id="mwWOM">TALES FROM SHAKESPEARE</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWOQ">シェクスピア物語</bdi></a> (in Japanese). Translated by Mineo, Toshiharu. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hongō,_Tokyo" title="Hongō, Tokyo" id="mwWOU">Hongō, Tokyo</a>: Gaigo Kenkyusha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWOY">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwWOc">18–</span>19. <q id="mwWOg">But the melancholy which he fell into latterly had made him neglect her, and from the time he conceived the project of counterfeiting madness, he affected to treat her with unkindness, and a sort of rudeness: but she, good lady, rather than reproach him with being false to her, persuaded herself that it was nothing but the disease in his mind, and no settled unkindness, which had made him less observant of her than formerly; and she compared the faculties of his once noble mind and excellent understanding, impaired as they were with the deep melancholy that oppressed him, to sweet bells which in themselves are capable of most exquisite music, but when jangled out of tune, or rudely handled, produce only a harsh and unpleasing sound.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWOk">然るに近頃王子は憂欝にかゝつて姬を疎んじ、狂人を裝はんと思ひ構へてからは、姬に接する態度が冷淡でやや<ruby id="mwWOo">突<rp id="mwWOs">(</rp><rt id="mwWOw">つく</rt><rp id="mwWO0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWO4">慳<rp id="mwWO8">(</rp><rt id="mwWPA">けん</rt><rp id="mwWPE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWPI">貪<rp id="mwWPM">(</rp><rt id="mwWPQ">どん</rt><rp id="mwWPU">)</rp></ruby>である樣にした。然し姬は心麗しくて王子の<ruby id="mwWPY">情<rp id="mwWPc">(</rp><rt id="mwWPg">つれ</rt><rp id="mwWPk">)</rp></ruby>なき素振りに<ruby id="mwWPo">怨<rp id="mwWPs">(</rp><rt id="mwWPw">うらみ</rt><rp id="mwWP0">)</rp></ruby>言を云ふ事もなく、却つて、心に<ruby id="mwWP4">病氣<rp id="mwWP8">(</rp><rt id="mwWQA">いたつき</rt><rp id="mwWQE">)</rp></ruby>あるが爲めで以前よりも我身を<ruby id="mwWQI">疎<rp id="mwWQM">(</rp><rt id="mwWQQ">うと</rt><rp id="mwWQU">)</rp></ruby>んずる<ruby id="mwWQY">鬼<rp id="mwWQc">(</rp><rt id="mwWQg">おに</rt><rp id="mwWQk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWQo">心<rp id="mwWQs">(</rp><rt id="mwWQw">ごゝろ</rt><rp id="mwWQ0">)</rp></ruby>あるが爲めでは無いと思ひ<ruby id="mwWQ4">諦<rp id="mwWQ8">(</rp><rt id="mwWRA">あき</rt><rp id="mwWRE">)</rp></ruby>らめ、更にまた王子の氣高かりし心、勝れし分別の力も、深き憂鬱に閉されては、本來絕妙なる樂音を發し得る<ruby id="mwWRI">妙<rp id="mwWRM">(</rp><rt id="mwWRQ">た</rt><rp id="mwWRU">)</rp></ruby>へなる鐘鈴も、調子<ruby id="mwWRY">構<rp id="mwWRc">(</rp><rt id="mwWRg">かまは</rt><rp id="mwWRk">)</rp></ruby>ず打ち鳴らされ或は粗暴な<ruby id="mwWRo">扱<rp id="mwWRs">(</rp><rt id="mwWRw">あつか</rt><rp id="mwWR0">)</rp></ruby>ひを受くれば、<ruby id="mwWR4">耳<rp id="mwWR8">(</rp><rt id="mwWSA">みゝ</rt><rp id="mwWSE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWSI">障<rp id="mwWSM">(</rp><rt id="mwWSQ">ざは</rt><rp id="mwWSU">)</rp></ruby>りな不快の狂音を<ruby id="mwWSY">放<rp id="mwWSc">(</rp><rt id="mwWSg">はな</rt><rp id="mwWSk">)</rp></ruby>つにも比すべきであると考へた。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=HAMLET%2C+PRINCE+OF+DENMARK+%3Cruby%3E%E4%B8%81%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%83%87%E3%83%B3%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E6%8A%B9%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%83%9E%E3%83%BC%E3%82%AF%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E7%8E%8B%E5%AD%90%E3%83%8F%E3%83%A0%E3%83%AC%E3%83%84%E3%83%88%E7%89%A9%E8%AA%9E&amp;rft.btitle=TALES+FROM+SHAKESPEARE+%E3%82%B7%E3%82%A7%E3%82%AF%E3%82%B9%E3%83%94%E3%82%A2%E7%89%A9%E8%AA%9E&amp;rft.place=Hong%C5%8D%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=18-19&amp;rft.pub=Gaigo+Kenkyusha&amp;rft.date=1937-01-25&amp;rft.aulast=Lamb&amp;rft.aufirst=Charles&amp;rft.au=Lamb%2C+Mary+Anne&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1037405%2F1%2F21&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3121" id="mwWSo"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3121" id="mwWSs"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3121" id="mwWSw"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-489" id="cite_note-489" data-mw-footnote-number="457"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWS0"><a href="#cite_ref-489" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWS4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWS8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-489" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3151" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWTA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:その時の Rufus の心の中にあったのは，Leona との最初の出会いから，彼女を熱烈に愛し始め，かっ，愛すれば愛するほど，憎んでいった，あの悪夢のような生活のことだったのです。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=28&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://u-kochi.repo.nii.ac.jp/?action=repository_uri&amp;item_id=2542&amp;file_id=22&amp;file_no=1&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Katō&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Tsunehiko&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:“ANOTHER COUNTRY” 論 ――自己の追求という観点から――&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=A Study of \&quot;Another Country\&quot; ―From the Point of View of Self-Recognition―&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=25 November 1977&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:高知女子大学紀要 人文・社会科学編&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=26&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFKatō1977" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3151">Katō, Tsunehiko (25 November 1977). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://u-kochi.repo.nii.ac.jp/?action=repository_uri&amp;item_id=2542&amp;file_id=22&amp;file_no=1" class="external text" id="mwWTE">"A Study of "Another Country" ―From the Point of View of Self-Recognition―" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWTI">“ANOTHER COUNTRY” 論 ――自己の追求という観点から――</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWTM">高知女子大学紀要 人文・社会科学編</bdi> (in Japanese) (26): 28.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWTQ">その時の Rufus の心の中にあったのは，Leona との最初の出会いから，彼女を熱烈に愛し始め，かっ，愛すれば愛するほど，憎んでいった，あの悪夢のような生活のことだったのです。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=A+Study+of+%22Another+Country%22+%E2%80%95From+the+Point+of+View+of+Self-Recognition%E2%80%95+%E2%80%9CANOTHER+COUNTRY%E2%80%9D+%E8%AB%96+%E2%80%95%E2%80%95%E8%87%AA%E5%B7%B1%E3%81%AE%E8%BF%BD%E6%B1%82%E3%81%A8%E3%81%84%E3%81%86%E8%A6%B3%E7%82%B9%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E2%80%95%E2%80%95&amp;rft.issue=26&amp;rft.pages=28&amp;rft.date=1977-11-25&amp;rft.aulast=Kat%C5%8D&amp;rft.aufirst=Tsunehiko&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fu-kochi.repo.nii.ac.jp%2F%3Faction%3Drepository_uri%26item_id%3D2542%26file_id%3D22%26file_no%3D1&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3151" id="mwWTU"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3151" id="mwWTY"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3151" id="mwWTc"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-490" id="cite_note-490" data-mw-footnote-number="458"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWTg"><a href="#cite_ref-490" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWTk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWTo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-490" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3154" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWTs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:愛すれば愛するほど相手の女性が遠ざかっていくとき、愛する者の愛情は自分自身の存在についても憎しみを抱くのである。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=90&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://agu.repo.nii.ac.jp/?action=repository_uri&amp;item_id=783&amp;file_id=22&amp;file_no=1&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Hotta&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Toshiyuki&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:ベケット、不在者の存在&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:愛知学院大学語研紀要&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=45&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=1&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2020&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHotta2020" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3154">Hotta, Toshiyuki (2020). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://agu.repo.nii.ac.jp/?action=repository_uri&amp;item_id=783&amp;file_id=22&amp;file_no=1" class="external text" id="mwWTw"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWT0">ベケット、不在者の存在</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWT4">愛知学院大学語研紀要</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWT8">45</b> (1): 90.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWUA">愛すれば愛するほど相手の女性が遠ざかっていくとき、愛する者の愛情は自分自身の存在についても憎しみを抱くのである。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E3%83%99%E3%82%B1%E3%83%83%E3%83%88%E3%80%81%E4%B8%8D%E5%9C%A8%E8%80%85%E3%81%AE%E5%AD%98%E5%9C%A8&amp;rft.volume=45&amp;rft.issue=1&amp;rft.pages=90&amp;rft.date=2020&amp;rft.aulast=Hotta&amp;rft.aufirst=Toshiyuki&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fagu.repo.nii.ac.jp%2F%3Faction%3Drepository_uri%26item_id%3D783%26file_id%3D22%26file_no%3D1&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3154" id="mwWUE"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3154" id="mwWUI"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3154" id="mwWUM"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-491" id="cite_note-491" data-mw-footnote-number="459"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWUQ"><a href="#cite_ref-491" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWUU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWUY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-491" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3157" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWUc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:彼女は肉体と精神は分けられるものではなくて肉体を愛せば自然に精神をも愛する事になると固く信じているのであった。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=674&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://ocu-omu.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/2004932/files/DBd0271004.pdf&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Miyauchi&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Hiromu&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:「気がふれたジェインの歌」小論&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:人文研究&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=27&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=10&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=1975&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;issn=0491-3329&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|大阪市立大学文学部}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFMiyauchi1975" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3157">Miyauchi, Hiromu (1975). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ocu-omu.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/2004932/files/DBd0271004.pdf" class="external text" id="mwWUg"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWUk">「気がふれたジェインの歌」小論</bdi></a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwWUo">(PDF)</span>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWUs">人文研究</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWUw">27</b> (10). <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwWU0"><span lang="ja" id="mwWU4">大阪市立大学文学部</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwWU8">: 674. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwWVA">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWVE">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0491-3329" class="external text" id="mwWVI">0491-3329</a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWVM">彼女は肉体と精神は分けられるものではなくて肉体を愛せば自然に精神をも愛する事になると固く信じているのであった。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E3%80%8C%E6%B0%97%E3%81%8C%E3%81%B5%E3%82%8C%E3%81%9F%E3%82%B8%E3%82%A7%E3%82%A4%E3%83%B3%E3%81%AE%E6%AD%8C%E3%80%8D%E5%B0%8F%E8%AB%96&amp;rft.volume=27&amp;rft.issue=10&amp;rft.pages=674&amp;rft.date=1975&amp;rft.issn=0491-3329&amp;rft.aulast=Miyauchi&amp;rft.aufirst=Hiromu&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Focu-omu.repo.nii.ac.jp%2Frecord%2F2004932%2Ffiles%2FDBd0271004.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3157" id="mwWVQ"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3157" id="mwWVU"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3157" id="mwWVY"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-492" id="cite_note-492" data-mw-footnote-number="460"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWVc"><a href="#cite_ref-492" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWVg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWVk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-492" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3161" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWVo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:また、自分を愛するように人類を愛せば、その愛は自分中心の利害から離れて正義にかない、その人は公正で有徳になるであろう。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=10–11&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://koara.lib.keio.ac.jp/xoonips/modules/xoonips/download.php?koara_id=AA12362999-20130000-0001&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Yoshida&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Shūma&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:ルソーにおける自尊心の問題&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Le problème de l'amour-propre chez Rousseau&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:エティカ&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal=Ethica&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=6&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2013&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFYoshida2013" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3161">Yoshida, Shūma (2013). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://koara.lib.keio.ac.jp/xoonips/modules/xoonips/download.php?koara_id=AA12362999-20130000-0001" class="external text" id="mwWVs">"Le problème de l'amour-propre chez Rousseau" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWVw">ルソーにおける自尊心の問題</bdi></a>. <i id="mwWV0">Ethica</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWV4">エティカ</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWV8">6</b>: <span class="nowrap" id="mwWWA">10–</span>11.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWWE">また、自分を愛するように人類を愛せば、その愛は自分中心の利害から離れて正義にかない、その人は公正で有徳になるであろう。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Ethica&amp;rft.atitle=Le+probl%C3%A8me+de+l%27amour-propre+chez+Rousseau+%E3%83%AB%E3%82%BD%E3%83%BC%E3%81%AB%E3%81%8A%E3%81%91%E3%82%8B%E8%87%AA%E5%B0%8A%E5%BF%83%E3%81%AE%E5%95%8F%E9%A1%8C&amp;rft.volume=6&amp;rft.pages=10-11&amp;rft.date=2013&amp;rft.aulast=Yoshida&amp;rft.aufirst=Sh%C5%ABma&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fkoara.lib.keio.ac.jp%2Fxoonips%2Fmodules%2Fxoonips%2Fdownload.php%3Fkoara_id%3DAA12362999-20130000-0001&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3161" id="mwWWI"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3161" id="mwWWM"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3161" id="mwWWQ"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-493" id="cite_note-493" data-mw-footnote-number="461"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWWU"><a href="#cite_ref-493" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWWY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWWc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-493" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3179" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWWg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:炉内温度が高いほどＢＰに入る熱量が多く熱分解速度が増し揮発分の単位時間当たりの放出量が多くなり，可燃濃度に速く達するためであるが，粒子サイズの影響が極めて小さいことから，表面部の熱分解が進み，可燃濃度に達すれば着火することが予想される．&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=264&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/jsmemecjo/2005.3/0/2005.3_263/_pdf/-char/ja&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Namba&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Kunihiko&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last2=Ida&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first2=Tamio&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last3=Fuchihata&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first3=Manabu&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last4=Sano&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first4=Hiroshi&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:木質バイオペレットの燃焼特性&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Combustion Characteristics of Woody Bio-pellets&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:年次大会講演論文集&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=19 September 2005&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Japan Society of Mechanical Engineers&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFNambaIdaFuchihataSano2005" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3179">Namba, Kunihiko; Ida, Tamio; Fuchihata, Manabu; Sano, Hiroshi (19 September 2005). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/jsmemecjo/2005.3/0/2005.3_263/_pdf/-char/ja" class="external text" id="mwWWk">"Combustion Characteristics of Woody Bio-pellets" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWWo">木質バイオペレットの燃焼特性</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWWs">年次大会講演論文集</bdi> (in Japanese). Japan Society of Mechanical Engineers: 264.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWWw">炉内温度が高いほどＢＰに入る熱量が多く熱分解速度が増し揮発分の単位時間当たりの放出量が多くなり，可燃濃度に速く達するためであるが，粒子サイズの影響が極めて小さいことから，表面部の熱分解が進み，可燃濃度に達すれば着火することが予想される．</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Combustion+Characteristics+of+Woody+Bio-pellets+%E6%9C%A8%E8%B3%AA%E3%83%90%E3%82%A4%E3%82%AA%E3%83%9A%E3%83%AC%E3%83%83%E3%83%88%E3%81%AE%E7%87%83%E7%84%BC%E7%89%B9%E6%80%A7&amp;rft.pages=264&amp;rft.date=2005-09-19&amp;rft.aulast=Namba&amp;rft.aufirst=Kunihiko&amp;rft.au=Ida%2C+Tamio&amp;rft.au=Fuchihata%2C+Manabu&amp;rft.au=Sano%2C+Hiroshi&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jstage.jst.go.jp%2Farticle%2Fjsmemecjo%2F2005.3%2F0%2F2005.3_263%2F_pdf%2F-char%2Fja&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3179" id="mwWW0"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3179" id="mwWW4"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3179" id="mwWW8"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-494" id="cite_note-494" data-mw-footnote-number="462"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWXA"><a href="#cite_ref-494" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWXE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWXI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-494" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3182" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWXM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:連続照射実験を行う場合，照射期間がある程度経過すれば変異発生頻度は平衡に達する。<br/>一度平衡に達すれば，それ以上長期に照射し続けても頻度の増減は見られず一定のままとなる。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=213&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/jhps/55/4/55_207/_pdf&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Tsunoyama&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Yūichi&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last2=Onoue&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first2=Yōsuke&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last3=Suzuki&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first3=Kazuyo&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last4=Takanishi&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first4=Yasutaka&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last5=Satō&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first5=Joe&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last6=Manabe&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first6=Yūichirō&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last7=Wada&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first7=Takahiro&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last8=Toki&quot;},&quot;21&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first8=Hiroshi&quot;},&quot;22&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last9=Bandō&quot;},&quot;23&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first9=Masako&quot;},&quot;24&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:遺伝的影響予測シミュレータ「WAMSIM」　―動植物への低 LET 放射線照射実験における遺伝的影響を予測するWAM モデルシミュレータ―&quot;},&quot;25&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:保健物理&quot;},&quot;26&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=55&quot;},&quot;27&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=4&quot;},&quot;28&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2020&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFTsunoyamaOnoueSuzukiTakanishi2020" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3182">Tsunoyama, Yūichi; Onoue, Yōsuke; Suzuki, Kazuyo; Takanishi, Yasutaka; Satō, Joe; Manabe, Yūichirō; Wada, Takahiro; Toki, Hiroshi; Bandō, Masako (2020). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/jhps/55/4/55_207/_pdf" class="external text" id="mwWXQ"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWXU">遺伝的影響予測シミュレータ「WAMSIM」　―動植物への低 LET 放射線照射実験における遺伝的影響を予測するWAM モデルシミュレータ―</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWXY">保健物理</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWXc">55</b> (4): 213.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWXg">連続照射実験を行う場合，照射期間がある程度経過すれば変異発生頻度は平衡に達する。<br id="mwWXk">一度平衡に達すれば，それ以上長期に照射し続けても頻度の増減は見られず一定のままとなる。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E9%81%BA%E4%BC%9D%E7%9A%84%E5%BD%B1%E9%9F%BF%E4%BA%88%E6%B8%AC%E3%82%B7%E3%83%9F%E3%83%A5%E3%83%AC%E3%83%BC%E3%82%BF%E3%80%8CWAMSIM%E3%80%8D%E3%80%80%E2%80%95%E5%8B%95%E6%A4%8D%E7%89%A9%E3%81%B8%E3%81%AE%E4%BD%8E+LET+%E6%94%BE%E5%B0%84%E7%B7%9A%E7%85%A7%E5%B0%84%E5%AE%9F%E9%A8%93%E3%81%AB%E3%81%8A%E3%81%91%E3%82%8B%E9%81%BA%E4%BC%9D%E7%9A%84%E5%BD%B1%E9%9F%BF%E3%82%92%E4%BA%88%E6%B8%AC%E3%81%99%E3%82%8BWAM+%E3%83%A2%E3%83%87%E3%83%AB%E3%82%B7%E3%83%9F%E3%83%A5%E3%83%AC%E3%83%BC%E3%82%BF%E2%80%95&amp;rft.volume=55&amp;rft.issue=4&amp;rft.pages=213&amp;rft.date=2020&amp;rft.aulast=Tsunoyama&amp;rft.aufirst=Y%C5%ABichi&amp;rft.au=Onoue%2C+Y%C5%8Dsuke&amp;rft.au=Suzuki%2C+Kazuyo&amp;rft.au=Takanishi%2C+Yasutaka&amp;rft.au=Sat%C5%8D%2C+Joe&amp;rft.au=Manabe%2C+Y%C5%ABichir%C5%8D&amp;rft.au=Wada%2C+Takahiro&amp;rft.au=Toki%2C+Hiroshi&amp;rft.au=Band%C5%8D%2C+Masako&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jstage.jst.go.jp%2Farticle%2Fjhps%2F55%2F4%2F55_207%2F_pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3182" id="mwWXo"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3182" id="mwWXs"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3182" id="mwWXw"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-495" id="cite_note-495" data-mw-footnote-number="463"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWX0"><a href="#cite_ref-495" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWX4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWX8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-495" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3185" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWYA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:（二）州設立豫定區域の男子人口が五千に達するまでは、中央政府より知事及裁判官を派して統治すること、[…]（四）各區の人口が六萬に達せば、自ら憲法を制定し政府を組織し、且つ獨立十三州と同一資格の代表者を議會に送り得ること、これである。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=88–89&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1453563/1/54&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:二 土地政策&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:アメリカ經濟史槪說&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Horie&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Yasuzō&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Yūhikaku&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=20 February 1937&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Kanda, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHorie1937" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3185">Horie, Yasuzō (20 February 1937).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWYE">二 土地政策</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1453563/1/54" class="external text" id="mwWYI"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWYM">アメリカ經濟史槪說</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanda,_Tokyo" title="Kanda, Tokyo" id="mwWYQ">Kanda, Tokyo</a>: Yūhikaku. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWYU">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwWYY">88–</span>89.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWYc">（二）州設立豫定區域の男子人口が五千に達するまでは、中央政府より知事及裁判官を派して統治すること、[…]（四）各區の人口が六萬に達せば、自ら憲法を制定し政府を組織し、且つ獨立十三州と同一資格の代表者を議會に送り得ること、これである。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E4%BA%8C+%E5%9C%9F%E5%9C%B0%E6%94%BF%E7%AD%96&amp;rft.btitle=%E3%82%A2%E3%83%A1%E3%83%AA%E3%82%AB%E7%B6%93%E6%BF%9F%E5%8F%B2%E6%A7%AA%E8%AA%AA&amp;rft.place=Kanda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=88-89&amp;rft.pub=Y%C5%ABhikaku&amp;rft.date=1937-02-20&amp;rft.aulast=Horie&amp;rft.aufirst=Yasuz%C5%8D&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1453563%2F1%2F54&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3185" id="mwWYg"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3185" id="mwWYk"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3185" id="mwWYo"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-496" id="cite_note-496" data-mw-footnote-number="464"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWYs"><a href="#cite_ref-496" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWYw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWY0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-496" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3188" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWY4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:汝等は年尙若きを以つて之を勉むれば自然好樂の境に達するを得ん。已に此域に達せば聲色嗜好凡百の心を蕩かす物は以つて心を動かすに足らないと。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1042221/1/260&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=542&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第二編 鳥取市の沿革&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:鳥取市史&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=7 August 1943&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|鳥取市役所}}&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Tottori (city)|Tottori]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3188" id="mwWY8"> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWZA">第二編 鳥取市の沿革</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1042221/1/260" class="external text" id="mwWZE"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWZI">鳥取市史</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tottori_(city)" title="Tottori (city)" id="mwWZM">Tottori</a>: <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwWZQ"><span lang="ja" id="mwWZU">鳥取市役所</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwWZY">. 7 August 1943. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWZc">&nbsp;</span>542.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWZg">汝等は年尙若きを以つて之を勉むれば自然好樂の境に達するを得ん。已に此域に達せば聲色嗜好凡百の心を蕩かす物は以つて心を動かすに足らないと。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E4%BA%8C%E7%B7%A8+%E9%B3%A5%E5%8F%96%E5%B8%82%E3%81%AE%E6%B2%BF%E9%9D%A9&amp;rft.btitle=%E9%B3%A5%E5%8F%96%E5%B8%82%E5%8F%B2&amp;rft.place=Tottori&amp;rft.pages=542&amp;rft.pub=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E9%B3%A5%E5%8F%96%E5%B8%82%E5%BD%B9%E6%89%80%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.date=1943-08-07&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1042221%2F1%2F260&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3188" id="mwWZk"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3188" id="mwWZo"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3188" id="mwWZs"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-497" id="cite_note-497" data-mw-footnote-number="465"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWZw"><a href="#cite_ref-497" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWZ0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWZ4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-497" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3191" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWZ8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=Достигнув речки Мизы, дорога круто заворачивала влево. Здесь был мост, построенный наискось через реку, и против него городские ворота. […]<br/>- Предательстве? – остановил его Макиавелли. – Когда дело, мессере, идет о спасении отечества, не может быть речи о предательстве и верности, о зле и добре, о милосердии и жестокости, – но все средства равны, только бы цель была достигнута.&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:道路はミザ川に達すると、急に左へ曲つて、こゝには一つの橋が<ruby>斜<rp></rp><rt>はすか</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ひに川に懸かつてゐてその眞向ひが町の城門であつた。[…]<br/>「裏切りですつて？」とマキアヹリが遮つた。「だつて、事が國家の死活にかゝはるやうな場合、裏切りだの誠實だの、善だの惡だの、慈悲だの慘酷だのといふ事は、ぜん〱問題にならないぢやありませんか。方法はどうあらうと同じです、たゞ目的さへ達しればいゝんですよ。」&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-quote=Upon reaching the Misa, the road turned sharply to the left; here, a bridge slanted across the river, directly opposite the gates to the town. […]<br/>“Betrayal?” interrupted Machiavelli. “When it is a matter of the nation’s survival, there must be no question of betrayal or loyalty, of good or evil, of clemency or cruelty. All means are alike, provided the end is met.”&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=209, 214&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1692631/1/109&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第十二編 皇帝か然らずんば無か&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;chapter=Книга двенадцатая. Или Цезарь — или ничто&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-chapter=Book Twelfth. Caesar or Nil&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:神々の復活　―レオナルド・ダ・ヸンチ―&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Воскресшие боги. Леонардо да Винчи&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-title=[[The Romance of Leonardo da Vinci|Resurrection of the Gods: Leonardo da Vinci]]&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Dmitry Merezhkovsky&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Dmitry Sergeyevich&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Merezhkovsky&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=3&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|岩波文庫}}&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Yonekawa&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Masao&quot;},&quot;21&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=25 February 1955&quot;},&quot;22&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;edition=6th&quot;},&quot;23&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;orig-date=15 March 1935&quot;},&quot;24&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Iwanami Shoten&quot;},&quot;25&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFMerezhkovsky1955" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3191"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dmitry_Merezhkovsky" title="Dmitry Merezhkovsky" id="mwWaA">Merezhkovsky, Dmitry Sergeyevich</a> (25 February 1955) [15 March 1935]. "Книга двенадцатая. Или Цезарь — или ничто" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWaE">第十二編 皇帝か然らずんば無か</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWaI">[</span>Book Twelfth. Caesar or Nil<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWaM">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1692631/1/109" class="external text" id="mwWaQ"><i id="mwWaU">Воскресшие боги. Леонардо да Винчи</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWaY">神々の復活　―レオナルド・ダ・ヸンチ―</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWac">[</span><i id="mwWag"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Romance_of_Leonardo_da_Vinci" title="The Romance of Leonardo da Vinci" id="mwWak">Resurrection of the Gods: Leonardo da Vinci</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWao">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwWas"><span lang="ja" id="mwWaw">岩波文庫</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwWa0"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWa4">&nbsp;</span>3. Translated by Yonekawa, Masao (6th<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWa8">&nbsp;</span>ed.). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiyoda,_Tokyo" title="Chiyoda, Tokyo" id="mwWbA">Chiyoda, Tokyo</a>: Iwanami Shoten. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWbE">&nbsp;</span>209, 214. <q id="mwWbI">Достигнув речки Мизы, дорога круто заворачивала влево. Здесь был мост, построенный наискось через реку, и против него городские ворота. […]<br id="mwWbM">- Предательстве? – остановил его Макиавелли. – Когда дело, мессере, идет о спасении отечества, не может быть речи о предательстве и верности, о зле и добре, о милосердии и жестокости, – но все средства равны, только бы цель была достигнута.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWbQ">道路はミザ川に達すると、急に左へ曲つて、こゝには一つの橋が<ruby id="mwWbU">斜<rp id="mwWbY"></rp><rt id="mwWbc">はすか</rt><rp id="mwWbg"></rp></ruby>ひに川に懸かつてゐてその眞向ひが町の城門であつた。[…]<br id="mwWbk">「裏切りですつて？」とマキアヹリが遮つた。「だつて、事が國家の死活にかゝはるやうな場合、裏切りだの誠實だの、善だの惡だの、慈悲だの慘酷だのといふ事は、ぜん〱問題にならないぢやありませんか。方法はどうあらうと同じです、たゞ目的さへ達しればいゝんですよ。」</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWbo">[</span>Upon reaching the Misa, the road turned sharply to the left; here, a bridge slanted across the river, directly opposite the gates to the town. […]<br id="mwWbs">“Betrayal?” interrupted Machiavelli. “When it is a matter of the nation’s survival, there must be no question of betrayal or loyalty, of good or evil, of clemency or cruelty. All means are alike, provided the end is met.”<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWbw">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%D0%9A%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B3%D0%B0+%D0%B4%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B4%D1%86%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%8F.+%D0%98%D0%BB%D0%B8+%D0%A6%D0%B5%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%8C+%E2%80%94+%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B8+%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%87%D1%82%D0%BE+%E7%AC%AC%E5%8D%81%E4%BA%8C%E7%B7%A8+%E7%9A%87%E5%B8%9D%E3%81%8B%E7%84%B6%E3%82%89%E3%81%9A%E3%82%93%E3%81%B0%E7%84%A1%E3%81%8B&amp;rft.btitle=%D0%92%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%81%D1%88%D0%B8%D0%B5+%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%B8.+%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B4%D0%BE+%D0%B4%D0%B0+%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%87%D0%B8+%E7%A5%9E%E3%80%85%E3%81%AE%E5%BE%A9%E6%B4%BB%E3%80%80%E2%80%95%E3%83%AC%E3%82%AA%E3%83%8A%E3%83%AB%E3%83%89%E3%83%BB%E3%83%80%E3%83%BB%E3%83%B8%E3%83%B3%E3%83%81%E2%80%95&amp;rft.place=Chiyoda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E5%B2%A9%E6%B3%A2%E6%96%87%E5%BA%AB%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=209%2C+214&amp;rft.edition=6th&amp;rft.pub=Iwanami+Shoten&amp;rft.date=1955-02-25&amp;rft.aulast=Merezhkovsky&amp;rft.aufirst=Dmitry+Sergeyevich&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1692631%2F1%2F109&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3191" id="mwWb0"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3191" id="mwWb4"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3191" id="mwWb8"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-498" id="cite_note-498" data-mw-footnote-number="466"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWcA"><a href="#cite_ref-498" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWcE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWcI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-498" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3219" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWcM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:私たちが科学を信ずれば宗敎を信ずることができず、反対に<ruby>素<rp></rp><rt>そ</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>朴<rp></rp><rt>ぼく</rt><rp></rp></ruby>な心持で宗敎を信ずれば、科学を信ずることもできないでしょう。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=32&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1168226/1/24&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:２ 近代人に課せられた問題&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:近代を切りひらいた人々&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Hidehiko&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Hori&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=30 March 1950&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Sanseidō&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHori1950" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3219">Hori, Hidehiko (30 March 1950).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWcQ">２ 近代人に課せられた問題</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1168226/1/24" class="external text" id="mwWcU"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWcY">近代を切りひらいた人々</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiyoda,_Tokyo" title="Chiyoda, Tokyo" id="mwWcc">Chiyoda, Tokyo</a>: Sanseidō. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWcg">&nbsp;</span>32.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWck">私たちが科学を信ずれば宗敎を信ずることができず、反対に<ruby id="mwWco">素<rp id="mwWcs"></rp><rt id="mwWcw">そ</rt><rp id="mwWc0"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWc4">朴<rp id="mwWc8"></rp><rt id="mwWdA">ぼく</rt><rp id="mwWdE"></rp></ruby>な心持で宗敎を信ずれば、科学を信ずることもできないでしょう。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%EF%BC%92+%E8%BF%91%E4%BB%A3%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%AB%E8%AA%B2%E3%81%9B%E3%82%89%E3%82%8C%E3%81%9F%E5%95%8F%E9%A1%8C&amp;rft.btitle=%E8%BF%91%E4%BB%A3%E3%82%92%E5%88%87%E3%82%8A%E3%81%B2%E3%82%89%E3%81%84%E3%81%9F%E4%BA%BA%E3%80%85&amp;rft.place=Chiyoda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=32&amp;rft.pub=Sanseid%C5%8D&amp;rft.date=1950-03-30&amp;rft.aulast=Hori&amp;rft.aufirst=Hidehiko&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1168226%2F1%2F24&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3219" id="mwWdI"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3219" id="mwWdM"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3219" id="mwWdQ"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-499" id="cite_note-499" data-mw-footnote-number="467"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWdU"><a href="#cite_ref-499" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWdY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWdc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-499" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3222" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWdg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:唯聞くのみでも之を信ずればよいともいへる。從つて、又、念佛は往生の爲のものでなくして、信ずる時に已に救はれて居るから報恩の爲のものとなす說ともなるのである。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=80&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/3013483/1/55&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第六章 日本佛敎の佛陀觀&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:佛敎汎論&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Iwanami Shoten&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Hakuju&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Ui&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=28 February 1962&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFUi1962" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3222">Ui, Hakuju (28 February 1962).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWdk">第六章 日本佛敎の佛陀觀</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/3013483/1/55" class="external text" id="mwWdo"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWds">佛敎汎論</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiyoda,_Tokyo" title="Chiyoda, Tokyo" id="mwWdw">Chiyoda, Tokyo</a>: Iwanami Shoten. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWd0">&nbsp;</span>80.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWd4">唯聞くのみでも之を信ずればよいともいへる。從つて、又、念佛は往生の爲のものでなくして、信ずる時に已に救はれて居るから報恩の爲のものとなす說ともなるのである。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E5%85%AD%E7%AB%A0+%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%AC%E4%BD%9B%E6%95%8E%E3%81%AE%E4%BD%9B%E9%99%80%E8%A7%80&amp;rft.btitle=%E4%BD%9B%E6%95%8E%E6%B1%8E%E8%AB%96&amp;rft.place=Chiyoda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=80&amp;rft.pub=Iwanami+Shoten&amp;rft.date=1962-02-28&amp;rft.aulast=Ui&amp;rft.aufirst=Hakuju&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F3013483%2F1%2F55&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3222" id="mwWd8"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3222" id="mwWeA"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3222" id="mwWeE"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-500" id="cite_note-500" data-mw-footnote-number="468"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWeI"><a href="#cite_ref-500" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWeM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWeQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-500" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3225" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWeU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:またヨハネは、このことだけを信ずれば救われる、とは言っていない。聖書で信ずることが必要とされているすべてのことを信ずることが必要である。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=192&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://kansai-u.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/18288/files/KU-1100-20020330-05.pdf&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Senoo&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Gōkō&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:同時代人のジョン・ロック批判と擁護&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:社会学部紀要&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Kansai University&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=33&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=3&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2002&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;issn=0287-6817&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Criticisms and Vindications of John Locke by Some Contemporaries&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFSenoo2002" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3225">Senoo, Gōkō (2002). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://kansai-u.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/18288/files/KU-1100-20020330-05.pdf" class="external text" id="mwWeY">"Criticisms and Vindications of John Locke by Some Contemporaries" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWec">同時代人のジョン・ロック批判と擁護</bdi></a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwWeg">(PDF)</span>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWek">社会学部紀要</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWeo">33</b> (3). Kansai University: 192. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwWes">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWew">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0287-6817" class="external text" id="mwWe0">0287-6817</a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWe4">またヨハネは、このことだけを信ずれば救われる、とは言っていない。聖書で信ずることが必要とされているすべてのことを信ずることが必要である。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Criticisms+and+Vindications+of+John+Locke+by+Some+Contemporaries+%E5%90%8C%E6%99%82%E4%BB%A3%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%AE%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A7%E3%83%B3%E3%83%BB%E3%83%AD%E3%83%83%E3%82%AF%E6%89%B9%E5%88%A4%E3%81%A8%E6%93%81%E8%AD%B7&amp;rft.volume=33&amp;rft.issue=3&amp;rft.pages=192&amp;rft.date=2002&amp;rft.issn=0287-6817&amp;rft.aulast=Senoo&amp;rft.aufirst=G%C5%8Dk%C5%8D&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fkansai-u.repo.nii.ac.jp%2Frecord%2F18288%2Ffiles%2FKU-1100-20020330-05.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3225" id="mwWe8"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3225" id="mwWfA"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3225" id="mwWfE"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-501" id="cite_note-501" data-mw-footnote-number="469"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWfI"><a href="#cite_ref-501" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWfM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWfQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-501" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3228" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWfU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:愚かな凡夫だから駄目だとは言わずに、愚かな凡夫が本願を信ずれば、その本願を信ずる心が、もう仏法そのものなのです。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=17&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/shinran/31/0/31_2/_pdf&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Hiroyuki&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Honda&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:金剛心の獲得とは？&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:現代と親鸞&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=31&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=2015&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHonda2015" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3228">Honda, Hiroyuki (2015). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/shinran/31/0/31_2/_pdf" class="external text" id="mwWfY"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWfc">金剛心の獲得とは？</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWfg">現代と親鸞</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwWfk">31</b>: 17.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWfo">愚かな凡夫だから駄目だとは言わずに、愚かな凡夫が本願を信ずれば、その本願を信ずる心が、もう仏法そのものなのです。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E9%87%91%E5%89%9B%E5%BF%83%E3%81%AE%E7%8D%B2%E5%BE%97%E3%81%A8%E3%81%AF%EF%BC%9F&amp;rft.volume=31&amp;rft.pages=17&amp;rft.date=2015&amp;rft.aulast=Honda&amp;rft.aufirst=Hiroyuki&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jstage.jst.go.jp%2Farticle%2Fshinran%2F31%2F0%2F31_2%2F_pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3228" id="mwWfs"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3228" id="mwWfw"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3228" id="mwWf0"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-502" id="cite_note-502" data-mw-footnote-number="470"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWf4"><a href="#cite_ref-502" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWf8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWgA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-502" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3231" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWgE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:まさか神田家の親子が一緖になつて根も葉もない噓をつかうと思ふ人もありますまいし、面と向つて僕に、あなたに隱し子がありますかとか、惡い病氣がありますかとか聞き<ruby>質<rp></rp><rt>たゞ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>し得るものでもなし、一を信じれば十を信じ、十を信じれば百を信ずるといふやうな事になつて行くのです。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=132&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/911642/1/74&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:或る人へ&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;orig-date=January 1919&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=24 August 1919&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:鏡中影&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Ikuma Arishima&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Ikuma&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Arishima&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Shunyodo&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Nihonbashi]], Tokyo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFArishima1919" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3231"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ikuma_Arishima" title="Ikuma Arishima" id="mwWgI">Arishima, Ikuma</a> (24 August 1919) [January 1919].  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWgM">或る人へ</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/911642/1/74" class="external text" id="mwWgQ"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWgU">鏡中影</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi" title="Nihonbashi" id="mwWgY">Nihonbashi</a>, Tokyo: Shunyodo. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWgc">&nbsp;</span>132.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWgg">まさか神田家の親子が一緖になつて根も葉もない噓をつかうと思ふ人もありますまいし、面と向つて僕に、あなたに隱し子がありますかとか、惡い病氣がありますかとか聞き<ruby id="mwWgk">質<rp id="mwWgo"></rp><rt id="mwWgs">たゞ</rt><rp id="mwWgw"></rp></ruby>し得るものでもなし、一を信じれば十を信じ、十を信じれば百を信ずるといふやうな事になつて行くのです。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E6%88%96%E3%82%8B%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%B8&amp;rft.btitle=%E9%8F%A1%E4%B8%AD%E5%BD%B1&amp;rft.place=Nihonbashi%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=132&amp;rft.pub=Shunyodo&amp;rft.date=1919-08-24&amp;rft.aulast=Arishima&amp;rft.aufirst=Ikuma&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F911642%2F1%2F74&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3231" id="mwWg0"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3231" id="mwWg4"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3231" id="mwWg8"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-503" id="cite_note-503" data-mw-footnote-number="471"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWhA"><a href="#cite_ref-503" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWhE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWhI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-503" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3234" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWhM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:<ruby>要<rp></rp><rt>えう</rt><rp></rp></ruby>するにその<ruby>心<rp></rp><rt>こゝろ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>開<rp></rp><rt>ひら</rt><rp></rp></ruby>いて、<ruby>神<rp></rp><rt>かみ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>信<rp></rp><rt>しん</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ずる<ruby>者<rp></rp><rt>もの</rt><rp></rp></ruby>は、より<ruby>多<rp></rp><rt>おほ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>く、その<ruby>力<rp></rp><rt>ちから</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>受<rp></rp><rt>う</rt><rp></rp></ruby>け、<ruby>惠<rp></rp><rt>めぐみ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>受<rp></rp><rt>う</rt><rp></rp></ruby>けるのである。<br/><ruby>心<rp></rp><rt>こゝろ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>空<rp></rp><rt>むな</rt><rp></rp></ruby>しうして、つまり<ruby>邪<rp></rp><rt>じや</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>念<rp></rp><rt>ねん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>惡<rp></rp><rt>あく</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>想<rp></rp><rt>さう</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>去<rp></rp><rt>さ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>つて<ruby>神<rp></rp><rt>かみ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>信<rp></rp><rt>しん</rt><rp></rp></ruby>じれば、<ruby>神<rp></rp><rt>かみ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>の<ruby>愛<rp></rp><rt>あい</rt><rp></rp></ruby>とめぐみは、その<ruby>空<rp></rp><rt>むな</rt><rp></rp></ruby>しき<ruby>心<rp></rp><rt>こゝろ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>滿<rp></rp><rt>み</rt><rp></rp></ruby>たし<ruby>玉<rp></rp><rt>たま</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ふのである。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=171&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/969246/1/95&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:'''八''' 信仰と幸福&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:人生を超越する力&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Leo&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Tolstoy&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Leo Tolstoy&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=28 June 1922&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Uchida&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Shizue&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Chuoh Publishing Co.&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Hongō, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFTolstoy1922" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3234"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_Tolstoy" title="Leo Tolstoy" id="mwWhQ">Tolstoy, Leo</a> (28 June 1922).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWhU"><b id="mwWhY">八</b> 信仰と幸福</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/969246/1/95" class="external text" id="mwWhc"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWhg">人生を超越する力</bdi></a> (in Japanese). Translated by Uchida, Shizue. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hongō,_Tokyo" title="Hongō, Tokyo" id="mwWhk">Hongō, Tokyo</a>: Chuoh Publishing Co. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWho">&nbsp;</span>171.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWhs"><ruby id="mwWhw">要<rp id="mwWh0"></rp><rt id="mwWh4">えう</rt><rp id="mwWh8"></rp></ruby>するにその<ruby id="mwWiA">心<rp id="mwWiE"></rp><rt id="mwWiI">こゝろ</rt><rp id="mwWiM"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWiQ">開<rp id="mwWiU"></rp><rt id="mwWiY">ひら</rt><rp id="mwWic"></rp></ruby>いて、<ruby id="mwWig">神<rp id="mwWik"></rp><rt id="mwWio">かみ</rt><rp id="mwWis"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWiw">信<rp id="mwWi0"></rp><rt id="mwWi4">しん</rt><rp id="mwWi8"></rp></ruby>ずる<ruby id="mwWjA">者<rp id="mwWjE"></rp><rt id="mwWjI">もの</rt><rp id="mwWjM"></rp></ruby>は、より<ruby id="mwWjQ">多<rp id="mwWjU"></rp><rt id="mwWjY">おほ</rt><rp id="mwWjc"></rp></ruby>く、その<ruby id="mwWjg">力<rp id="mwWjk"></rp><rt id="mwWjo">ちから</rt><rp id="mwWjs"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWjw">受<rp id="mwWj0"></rp><rt id="mwWj4">う</rt><rp id="mwWj8"></rp></ruby>け、<ruby id="mwWkA">惠<rp id="mwWkE"></rp><rt id="mwWkI">めぐみ</rt><rp id="mwWkM"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWkQ">受<rp id="mwWkU"></rp><rt id="mwWkY">う</rt><rp id="mwWkc"></rp></ruby>けるのである。<br id="mwWkg"><ruby id="mwWkk">心<rp id="mwWko"></rp><rt id="mwWks">こゝろ</rt><rp id="mwWkw"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWk0">空<rp id="mwWk4"></rp><rt id="mwWk8">むな</rt><rp id="mwWlA"></rp></ruby>しうして、つまり<ruby id="mwWlE">邪<rp id="mwWlI"></rp><rt id="mwWlM">じや</rt><rp id="mwWlQ"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWlU">念<rp id="mwWlY"></rp><rt id="mwWlc">ねん</rt><rp id="mwWlg"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWlk">惡<rp id="mwWlo"></rp><rt id="mwWls">あく</rt><rp id="mwWlw"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWl0">想<rp id="mwWl4"></rp><rt id="mwWl8">さう</rt><rp id="mwWmA"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWmE">去<rp id="mwWmI"></rp><rt id="mwWmM">さ</rt><rp id="mwWmQ"></rp></ruby>つて<ruby id="mwWmU">神<rp id="mwWmY"></rp><rt id="mwWmc">かみ</rt><rp id="mwWmg"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWmk">信<rp id="mwWmo"></rp><rt id="mwWms">しん</rt><rp id="mwWmw"></rp></ruby>じれば、<ruby id="mwWm0">神<rp id="mwWm4"></rp><rt id="mwWm8">かみ</rt><rp id="mwWnA"></rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwWnE">愛<rp id="mwWnI"></rp><rt id="mwWnM">あい</rt><rp id="mwWnQ"></rp></ruby>とめぐみは、その<ruby id="mwWnU">空<rp id="mwWnY"></rp><rt id="mwWnc">むな</rt><rp id="mwWng"></rp></ruby>しき<ruby id="mwWnk">心<rp id="mwWno"></rp><rt id="mwWns">こゝろ</rt><rp id="mwWnw"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWn0">滿<rp id="mwWn4"></rp><rt id="mwWn8">み</rt><rp id="mwWoA"></rp></ruby>たし<ruby id="mwWoE">玉<rp id="mwWoI"></rp><rt id="mwWoM">たま</rt><rp id="mwWoQ"></rp></ruby>ふのである。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E5%85%AB+%E4%BF%A1%E4%BB%B0%E3%81%A8%E5%B9%B8%E7%A6%8F&amp;rft.btitle=%E4%BA%BA%E7%94%9F%E3%82%92%E8%B6%85%E8%B6%8A%E3%81%99%E3%82%8B%E5%8A%9B&amp;rft.place=Hong%C5%8D%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=171&amp;rft.pub=Chuoh+Publishing+Co.&amp;rft.date=1922-06-28&amp;rft.aulast=Tolstoy&amp;rft.aufirst=Leo&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F969246%2F1%2F95&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3234" id="mwWoU"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3234" id="mwWoY"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3234" id="mwWoc"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-504" id="cite_note-504" data-mw-footnote-number="472"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWog"><a href="#cite_ref-504" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWok"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWoo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-504" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWos" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:Ｒ・Ｎの<ruby>言<rp></rp><rt>い</rt><rp></rp></ruby>つた<ruby>事<rp></rp><rt>こと</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を、<ruby>私<rp></rp><rt>わたし</rt><rp></rp></ruby>はどこまで<ruby>信<rp></rp><rt>しん</rt><rp></rp></ruby>じればよいのであらう。<ruby>船<rp></rp><rt>せん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>室<rp></rp><rt>しつ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>の<ruby>圓<rp></rp><rt>ゑん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>形<rp></rp><rt>けい</rt><rp></rp></ruby>の<ruby>窓<rp></rp><rt>まど</rt><rp></rp></ruby>からは<ruby>船<rp></rp><rt>ふね</rt><rp></rp></ruby>の<ruby>搖<rp></rp><rt>ゆ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>れるまにまに<ruby>月<rp></rp><rt>つき</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>夜<rp></rp><rt>よ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>の<ruby>海<rp></rp><rt>うみ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>が<span style=\&quot;text-emphasis:sesame\&quot;>ちらちら</span>と<ruby>見<rp></rp><rt>み</rt><rp></rp></ruby>えて、それがＲ・Ｎの<ruby>語<rp></rp><rt>かた</rt><rp></rp></ruby>つた<ruby>幻<rp></rp><rt>げん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>想<rp></rp><rt>さう</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>的<rp></rp><rt>てき</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ないろいろの<ruby>光<rp></rp><rt>くわう</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>景<rp></rp><rt>けい</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を、<ruby>私<rp></rp><rt>わたし</rt><rp></rp></ruby>に<ruby>暗<rp></rp><rt>あん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>示<rp></rp><rt>じ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>した。……だんだんそれを<ruby>信<rp></rp><rt>しん</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ずる<ruby>度<rp></rp><rt>ど</rt><rp></rp></ruby>が<ruby>多<rp></rp><rt>おほ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>くなれば、<ruby>最<rp></rp><rt>もつと</rt><rp></rp></ruby>も<ruby>多<rp></rp><rt>おほ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>くなつた<ruby>頂<rp></rp><rt>ちやう</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>上<rp></rp><rt>じやう</rt><rp></rp></ruby>では、<ruby>彼<rp></rp><rt>かれ</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>自<rp></rp><rt>じ</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>身<rp></rp><rt>しん</rt><rp></rp></ruby>が<ruby>彼<rp></rp><rt>かれ</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>自<rp></rp><rt>じ</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>身<rp></rp><rt>しん</rt><rp></rp></ruby>を<ruby>信<rp></rp><rt>しん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>用<rp></rp><rt>よう</rt><rp></rp></ruby>する<ruby>最<rp></rp><rt>さい</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>大<rp></rp><rt>だい</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>限<rp></rp><rt>げん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>度<rp></rp><rt>ど</rt><rp></rp></ruby>の<ruby>時<rp></rp><rt>とき</rt><rp></rp></ruby>と<ruby>同<rp></rp><rt>おな</rt><rp></rp></ruby>じやうに、<ruby>遂<rp></rp><rt>つひ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>には「ウヰリアム、ウヰルスンガ<ruby>長<rp></rp><rt>なが</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>崎<rp></rp><rt>さき</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ノ<ruby>阿<rp></rp><rt>ア</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>片<rp></rp><rt>ヘン</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>窟<rp></rp><rt>くつ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ノ<ruby>殺<rp></rp><rt>さつ</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>人<rp></rp><rt>じん</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>者<rp></rp><rt>しや</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ニ<ruby>相<rp></rp><rt>さう</rt><rp></rp></ruby><ruby>違<rp></rp><rt>ゐ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>ナイ」といふところまで<ruby>彼<rp></rp><rt>かれ</rt><rp></rp></ruby>に一<ruby>致<rp></rp><rt>ち</rt><rp></rp></ruby>するであらう？……&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=72&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/3430366/1/41&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:指紋&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Haruo Satō (novelist)&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Haruo&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Satō&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:佐藤春夫集　芥川龍之介集&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|日本探偵小說全集}}&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=20&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Kaizōsha&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=25 June 1929&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Shiba, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFSatō1929" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3237"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haruo_Satō_(novelist)" title="Haruo Satō (novelist)" id="mwWow">Satō, Haruo</a> (25 June 1929).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWo0">指紋</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/3430366/1/41" class="external text" id="mwWo4"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwWo8">佐藤春夫集　芥川龍之介集</bdi></a>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwWpA"><span lang="ja" id="mwWpE">日本探偵小說全集</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwWpI"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWpM">&nbsp;</span>20. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiba,_Tokyo" title="Shiba, Tokyo" id="mwWpQ">Shiba, Tokyo</a>: Kaizōsha. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwWpU">&nbsp;</span>72.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwWpY">Ｒ・Ｎの<ruby id="mwWpc">言<rp id="mwWpg"></rp><rt id="mwWpk">い</rt><rp id="mwWpo"></rp></ruby>つた<ruby id="mwWps">事<rp id="mwWpw"></rp><rt id="mwWp0">こと</rt><rp id="mwWp4"></rp></ruby>を、<ruby id="mwWp8">私<rp id="mwWqA"></rp><rt id="mwWqE">わたし</rt><rp id="mwWqI"></rp></ruby>はどこまで<ruby id="mwWqM">信<rp id="mwWqQ"></rp><rt id="mwWqU">しん</rt><rp id="mwWqY"></rp></ruby>じればよいのであらう。<ruby id="mwWqc">船<rp id="mwWqg"></rp><rt id="mwWqk">せん</rt><rp id="mwWqo"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWqs">室<rp id="mwWqw"></rp><rt id="mwWq0">しつ</rt><rp id="mwWq4"></rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwWq8">圓<rp id="mwWrA"></rp><rt id="mwWrE">ゑん</rt><rp id="mwWrI"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWrM">形<rp id="mwWrQ"></rp><rt id="mwWrU">けい</rt><rp id="mwWrY"></rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwWrc">窓<rp id="mwWrg"></rp><rt id="mwWrk">まど</rt><rp id="mwWro"></rp></ruby>からは<ruby id="mwWrs">船<rp id="mwWrw"></rp><rt id="mwWr0">ふね</rt><rp id="mwWr4"></rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwWr8">搖<rp id="mwWsA"></rp><rt id="mwWsE">ゆ</rt><rp id="mwWsI"></rp></ruby>れるまにまに<ruby id="mwWsM">月<rp id="mwWsQ"></rp><rt id="mwWsU">つき</rt><rp id="mwWsY"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWsc">夜<rp id="mwWsg"></rp><rt id="mwWsk">よ</rt><rp id="mwWso"></rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwWss">海<rp id="mwWsw"></rp><rt id="mwWs0">うみ</rt><rp id="mwWs4"></rp></ruby>が<span style="text-emphasis:sesame" id="mwWs8">ちらちら</span>と<ruby id="mwWtA">見<rp id="mwWtE"></rp><rt id="mwWtI">み</rt><rp id="mwWtM"></rp></ruby>えて、それがＲ・Ｎの<ruby id="mwWtQ">語<rp id="mwWtU"></rp><rt id="mwWtY">かた</rt><rp id="mwWtc"></rp></ruby>つた<ruby id="mwWtg">幻<rp id="mwWtk"></rp><rt id="mwWto">げん</rt><rp id="mwWts"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWtw">想<rp id="mwWt0"></rp><rt id="mwWt4">さう</rt><rp id="mwWt8"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWuA">的<rp id="mwWuE"></rp><rt id="mwWuI">てき</rt><rp id="mwWuM"></rp></ruby>ないろいろの<ruby id="mwWuQ">光<rp id="mwWuU"></rp><rt id="mwWuY">くわう</rt><rp id="mwWuc"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWug">景<rp id="mwWuk"></rp><rt id="mwWuo">けい</rt><rp id="mwWus"></rp></ruby>を、<ruby id="mwWuw">私<rp id="mwWu0"></rp><rt id="mwWu4">わたし</rt><rp id="mwWu8"></rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwWvA">暗<rp id="mwWvE"></rp><rt id="mwWvI">あん</rt><rp id="mwWvM"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWvQ">示<rp id="mwWvU"></rp><rt id="mwWvY">じ</rt><rp id="mwWvc"></rp></ruby>した。……だんだんそれを<ruby id="mwWvg">信<rp id="mwWvk"></rp><rt id="mwWvo">しん</rt><rp id="mwWvs"></rp></ruby>ずる<ruby id="mwWvw">度<rp id="mwWv0"></rp><rt id="mwWv4">ど</rt><rp id="mwWv8"></rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwWwA">多<rp id="mwWwE"></rp><rt id="mwWwI">おほ</rt><rp id="mwWwM"></rp></ruby>くなれば、<ruby id="mwWwQ">最<rp id="mwWwU"></rp><rt id="mwWwY">もつと</rt><rp id="mwWwc"></rp></ruby>も<ruby id="mwWwg">多<rp id="mwWwk"></rp><rt id="mwWwo">おほ</rt><rp id="mwWws"></rp></ruby>くなつた<ruby id="mwWww">頂<rp id="mwWw0"></rp><rt id="mwWw4">ちやう</rt><rp id="mwWw8"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWxA">上<rp id="mwWxE"></rp><rt id="mwWxI">じやう</rt><rp id="mwWxM"></rp></ruby>では、<ruby id="mwWxQ">彼<rp id="mwWxU"></rp><rt id="mwWxY">かれ</rt><rp id="mwWxc"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWxg">自<rp id="mwWxk"></rp><rt id="mwWxo">じ</rt><rp id="mwWxs"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWxw">身<rp id="mwWx0"></rp><rt id="mwWx4">しん</rt><rp id="mwWx8"></rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwWyA">彼<rp id="mwWyE"></rp><rt id="mwWyI">かれ</rt><rp id="mwWyM"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWyQ">自<rp id="mwWyU"></rp><rt id="mwWyY">じ</rt><rp id="mwWyc"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWyg">身<rp id="mwWyk"></rp><rt id="mwWyo">しん</rt><rp id="mwWys"></rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwWyw">信<rp id="mwWy0"></rp><rt id="mwWy4">しん</rt><rp id="mwWy8"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWzA">用<rp id="mwWzE"></rp><rt id="mwWzI">よう</rt><rp id="mwWzM"></rp></ruby>する<ruby id="mwWzQ">最<rp id="mwWzU"></rp><rt id="mwWzY">さい</rt><rp id="mwWzc"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWzg">大<rp id="mwWzk"></rp><rt id="mwWzo">だい</rt><rp id="mwWzs"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwWzw">限<rp id="mwWz0"></rp><rt id="mwWz4">げん</rt><rp id="mwWz8"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW0A">度<rp id="mwW0E"></rp><rt id="mwW0I">ど</rt><rp id="mwW0M"></rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwW0Q">時<rp id="mwW0U"></rp><rt id="mwW0Y">とき</rt><rp id="mwW0c"></rp></ruby>と<ruby id="mwW0g">同<rp id="mwW0k"></rp><rt id="mwW0o">おな</rt><rp id="mwW0s"></rp></ruby>じやうに、<ruby id="mwW0w">遂<rp id="mwW00"></rp><rt id="mwW04">つひ</rt><rp id="mwW08"></rp></ruby>には「ウヰリアム、ウヰルスンガ<ruby id="mwW1A">長<rp id="mwW1E"></rp><rt id="mwW1I">なが</rt><rp id="mwW1M"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW1Q">崎<rp id="mwW1U"></rp><rt id="mwW1Y">さき</rt><rp id="mwW1c"></rp></ruby>ノ<ruby id="mwW1g">阿<rp id="mwW1k"></rp><rt id="mwW1o">ア</rt><rp id="mwW1s"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW1w">片<rp id="mwW10"></rp><rt id="mwW14">ヘン</rt><rp id="mwW18"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW2A">窟<rp id="mwW2E"></rp><rt id="mwW2I">くつ</rt><rp id="mwW2M"></rp></ruby>ノ<ruby id="mwW2Q">殺<rp id="mwW2U"></rp><rt id="mwW2Y">さつ</rt><rp id="mwW2c"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW2g">人<rp id="mwW2k"></rp><rt id="mwW2o">じん</rt><rp id="mwW2s"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW2w">者<rp id="mwW20"></rp><rt id="mwW24">しや</rt><rp id="mwW28"></rp></ruby>ニ<ruby id="mwW3A">相<rp id="mwW3E"></rp><rt id="mwW3I">さう</rt><rp id="mwW3M"></rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW3Q">違<rp id="mwW3U"></rp><rt id="mwW3Y">ゐ</rt><rp id="mwW3c"></rp></ruby>ナイ」といふところまで<ruby id="mwW3g">彼<rp id="mwW3k"></rp><rt id="mwW3o">かれ</rt><rp id="mwW3s"></rp></ruby>に一<ruby id="mwW3w">致<rp id="mwW30"></rp><rt id="mwW34">ち</rt><rp id="mwW38"></rp></ruby>するであらう？……</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E6%8C%87%E7%B4%8B&amp;rft.btitle=%E4%BD%90%E8%97%A4%E6%98%A5%E5%A4%AB%E9%9B%86%E3%80%80%E8%8A%A5%E5%B7%9D%E9%BE%8D%E4%B9%8B%E4%BB%8B%E9%9B%86&amp;rft.place=Shiba%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%AC%E6%8E%A2%E5%81%B5%E5%B0%8F%E8%AA%AA%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=72&amp;rft.pub=Kaiz%C5%8Dsha&amp;rft.date=1929-06-25&amp;rft.aulast=Sat%C5%8D&amp;rft.aufirst=Haruo&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F3430366%2F1%2F41&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3237" id="mwW4A"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3237" id="mwW4E"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3237" id="mwW4I"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-505" id="cite_note-505" data-mw-footnote-number="473"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwW4M"><a href="#cite_ref-505" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwW4Q"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwW4U">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-505" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3240" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwW4Y" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:フォースを信じないで、何を信ずるのだということです。信じれば、フォースは共にあるので、ルークを導いてくれるのです。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=131&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第４章 自動化の夜明け&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:サラリーマンは寝ながらお金を増やしなさい&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Katō&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Takayuki&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Shūwa System&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=21 January 2020&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFKatō2020" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3240">Katō, Takayuki (21 January 2020).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwW4c">第４章 自動化の夜明け</bdi>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwW4g">サラリーマンは寝ながらお金を増やしなさい</bdi> (in Japanese). Shūwa System. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwW4k">&nbsp;</span>131.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwW4o">フォースを信じないで、何を信ずるのだということです。信じれば、フォースは共にあるので、ルークを導いてくれるのです。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%EF%BC%94%E7%AB%A0+%E8%87%AA%E5%8B%95%E5%8C%96%E3%81%AE%E5%A4%9C%E6%98%8E%E3%81%91&amp;rft.btitle=%E3%82%B5%E3%83%A9%E3%83%AA%E3%83%BC%E3%83%9E%E3%83%B3%E3%81%AF%E5%AF%9D%E3%81%AA%E3%81%8C%E3%82%89%E3%81%8A%E9%87%91%E3%82%92%E5%A2%97%E3%82%84%E3%81%97%E3%81%AA%E3%81%95%E3%81%84&amp;rft.pages=131&amp;rft.pub=Sh%C5%ABwa+System&amp;rft.date=2020-01-21&amp;rft.aulast=Kat%C5%8D&amp;rft.aufirst=Takayuki&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3240" id="mwW4s"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3240" id="mwW4w"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3240" id="mwW40"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-506" id="cite_note-506" data-mw-footnote-number="474"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwW44"><a href="#cite_ref-506" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwW48"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwW5A">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-506" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3286" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwW5E" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-quote=If all the savants, philosophers and prison wardens from the world over should gather in her cell, lay out books, scalpels, axes and nooses before her, and prove that death exists, that when a human dies their life disappears, that there is no such thing as immortality, she would only stare at that with ''amazement''… How could there be no immortality, since she was already immortal?… What could it be to speak of death or immortality, when she had already been killed and yet was immortal, alive in death, as she had been alive in life?…&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=И если бы собрались к ней в камеру со всего света ученые, философы и палачи, разложили перед нею книги, скальпели, топоры и петли и стали доказывать, что смерть существует, что человек умирает и убивается, что бессмертия нет, — они только удивили бы ее. Как бессмертия нет, когда уже сейчас она бессмертна? О каком же еще бессмертии, о какой еще смерти можно говорить, когда уже сейчас она мертва и бессмертна, жива в смерти, как была жива в жизни?&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:<ruby>若<rp>(</rp><rt>も</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>し<ruby>彼<rp>(</rp><rt>かの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>女<rp>(</rp><rt>ぢよ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>檻<rp>(</rp><rt>かん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>房<rp>(</rp><rt>ばう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>世<rp>(</rp><rt>せ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>界<rp>(</rp><rt>かい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>中<rp>(</rp><rt>ぢう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>悉<rp>(</rp><rt>あら</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ゆる<ruby>碩<rp>(</rp><rt>せき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>學<rp>(</rp><rt>がく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>者<rp>(</rp><rt>しや</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、<ruby>哲<rp>(</rp><rt>てつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>學<rp>(</rp><rt>がく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>者<rp>(</rp><rt>しや</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、<ruby>司<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>獄<rp>(</rp><rt>ごく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>官<rp>(</rp><rt>くわん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<ruby>集<rp>(</rp><rt>あつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>まつて<ruby>彼<rp>(</rp><rt>かの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>女<rp>(</rp><rt>ぢよ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>前<rp>(</rp><rt>まへ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>書<rp>(</rp><rt>しよ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>籍<rp>(</rp><rt>じやく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、<ruby>解<rp>(</rp><rt>かい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>剖<rp>(</rp><rt>ばう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>刀<rp>(</rp><rt>たう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、<ruby>斧<rp>(</rp><rt>おの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、<ruby>繩<rp>(</rp><rt>なは</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>を<ruby>擴<rp>(</rp><rt>ひろ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>げて、<ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>存<rp>(</rp><rt>そん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>在<rp>(</rp><rt>ざい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>すること、<ruby>人<rp>(</rp><rt>にん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>間<rp>(</rp><rt>げん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ぬれば<ruby>其<rp>(</rp><rt>そ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>生<rp>(</rp><rt>せい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<ruby>消<rp>(</rp><rt>き</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>えること、<ruby>不<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>なるものの<ruby>決<rp>(</rp><rt>けつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>してないことを<ruby>示<rp>(</rp><rt>しめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>したとすれば、<ruby>彼<rp>(</rp><rt>かの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>女<rp>(</rp><rt>ぢよ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>は<ruby>只<rp>(</rp><rt>たゞ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>之<rp>(</rp><rt>これ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>を<span style=text-emphasis:sesame>あきれ</span>て<ruby>眺<rp>(</rp><rt>なが</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>めたであらう………<ruby>彼<rp>(</rp><rt>かの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>女<rp>(</rp><rt>ぢよ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<ruby>現<rp>(</rp><rt>げん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>不<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>である<ruby>以<rp>(</rp><rt>い</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>上<rp>(</rp><rt>じやう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>、<ruby>不<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>なるものが<ruby>決<rp>(</rp><rt>けつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>してあるべきでないとは<ruby>何<rp>(</rp><rt>なに</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>事<rp>(</rp><rt>ごと</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>だ？……<ruby>彼<rp>(</rp><rt>かの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>女<rp>(</rp><rt>ぢよ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<ruby>旣<rp>(</rp><rt>すで</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>殺<rp>(</rp><rt>ころ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>されて<ruby>而<rp>(</rp><rt>しか</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>も<ruby>不<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>で、<ruby>生<rp>(</rp><rt>せい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>在<rp>(</rp><rt>あつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>て<ruby>活<rp>(</rp><rt>いき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>々<rp>(</rp><rt>〱</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>としてゐるやう、<ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>於<rp>(</rp><rt>おい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ても<ruby>活<rp>(</rp><rt>いき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>々<rp>(</rp><rt>〱</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>としてゐたなら、<ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>とか<ruby>不<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>とは<ruby>何<rp>(</rp><rt>なん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>話<rp>(</rp><rt>はなし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>だらう………&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;p=185&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1016971/1/98&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:<ruby>死<rp>(</rp><rt>し</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>刑<rp>(</rp><rt>けい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>七<rp>(</rp><rt>しち</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>人<rp>(</rp><rt>にん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>物<rp>(</rp><rt>もの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>語<rp>(</rp><rt>がたり</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;chapter=Рассказ о семи повешенных&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-chapter=[[The Seven Who Were Hanged|The Tale of the Seven on Death Row]]&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Leonid Andreyev&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Leonid Nikolaievich&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Andreyev&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:<ruby>闇<rp>(</rp><rt>やみ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>國<rp>(</rp><rt>くに</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-title=[[Peasants (novella)|The Dark Country]]&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Мужики&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Shun'yōsha&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=8 June 1925&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Toichi&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Kubota&quot;},&quot;21&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Ushigome]], Tokyo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFAndreyev1925" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3286"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonid_Andreyev" title="Leonid Andreyev" id="mwW5I">Andreyev, Leonid Nikolaievich</a> (8 June 1925). "Рассказ о семи повешенных" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwW5M"><ruby id="mwW5Q">死<rp id="mwW5U">(</rp><rt id="mwW5Y">し</rt><rp id="mwW5c">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW5g">刑<rp id="mwW5k">(</rp><rt id="mwW5o">けい</rt><rp id="mwW5s">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW5w">七<rp id="mwW50">(</rp><rt id="mwW54">しち</rt><rp id="mwW58">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW6A">人<rp id="mwW6E">(</rp><rt id="mwW6I">にん</rt><rp id="mwW6M">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW6Q">物<rp id="mwW6U">(</rp><rt id="mwW6Y">もの</rt><rp id="mwW6c">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW6g">語<rp id="mwW6k">(</rp><rt id="mwW6o">がたり</rt><rp id="mwW6s">)</rp></ruby></bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwW6w">[</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Seven_Who_Were_Hanged" title="The Seven Who Were Hanged" id="mwW60">The Tale of the Seven on Death Row</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwW64">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1016971/1/98" class="external text" id="mwW68"><i id="mwW7A">Мужики</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwW7E"><ruby id="mwW7I">闇<rp id="mwW7M">(</rp><rt id="mwW7Q">やみ</rt><rp id="mwW7U">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwW7Y">國<rp id="mwW7c">(</rp><rt id="mwW7g">くに</rt><rp id="mwW7k">)</rp></ruby></bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwW7o">[</span><i id="mwW7s"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peasants_(novella)" title="Peasants (novella)" id="mwW7w">The Dark Country</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwW70">]</span> (in Japanese). Translated by Kubota, Toichi. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ushigome" title="Ushigome" id="mwW74">Ushigome</a>, Tokyo: Shun'yōsha. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwW78">&nbsp;</span>185. <q id="mwW8A">И если бы собрались к ней в камеру со всего света ученые, философы и палачи, разложили перед нею книги, скальпели, топоры и петли и стали доказывать, что смерть существует, что человек умирает и убивается, что бессмертия нет, — они только удивили бы ее. Как бессмертия нет, когда уже сейчас она бессмертна? О каком же еще бессмертии, о какой еще смерти можно говорить, когда уже сейчас она мертва и бессмертна, жива в смерти, как была жива в жизни?</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwW8E"><ruby id="mwW8I">若<rp id="mwW8M">(</rp><rt id="mwW8Q">も</rt><rp id="mwW8U">)</rp></ruby>し<ruby id="mwW8Y">彼<rp id="mwW8c">(</rp><rt id="mwW8g">かの</rt><rp id="mwW8k">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW8o">女<rp id="mwW8s">(</rp><rt id="mwW8w">ぢよ</rt><rp id="mwW80">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwW84">檻<rp id="mwW88">(</rp><rt id="mwW9A">かん</rt><rp id="mwW9E">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW9I">房<rp id="mwW9M">(</rp><rt id="mwW9Q">ばう</rt><rp id="mwW9U">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwW9Y">世<rp id="mwW9c">(</rp><rt id="mwW9g">せ</rt><rp id="mwW9k">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW9o">界<rp id="mwW9s">(</rp><rt id="mwW9w">かい</rt><rp id="mwW90">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW94">中<rp id="mwW98">(</rp><rt id="mwW-A">ぢう</rt><rp id="mwW-E">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwW-I">悉<rp id="mwW-M">(</rp><rt id="mwW-Q">あら</rt><rp id="mwW-U">)</rp></ruby>ゆる<ruby id="mwW-Y">碩<rp id="mwW-c">(</rp><rt id="mwW-g">せき</rt><rp id="mwW-k">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW-o">學<rp id="mwW-s">(</rp><rt id="mwW-w">がく</rt><rp id="mwW-0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW-4">者<rp id="mwW-8">(</rp><rt id="mwW_A">しや</rt><rp id="mwW_E">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwW_I">哲<rp id="mwW_M">(</rp><rt id="mwW_Q">てつ</rt><rp id="mwW_U">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW_Y">學<rp id="mwW_c">(</rp><rt id="mwW_g">がく</rt><rp id="mwW_k">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwW_o">者<rp id="mwW_s">(</rp><rt id="mwW_w">しや</rt><rp id="mwW_0">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwW_4">司<rp id="mwW_8">(</rp><rt id="mwXAA">し</rt><rp id="mwXAE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXAI">獄<rp id="mwXAM">(</rp><rt id="mwXAQ">ごく</rt><rp id="mwXAU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXAY">官<rp id="mwXAc">(</rp><rt id="mwXAg">くわん</rt><rp id="mwXAk">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwXAo">集<rp id="mwXAs">(</rp><rt id="mwXAw">あつ</rt><rp id="mwXA0">)</rp></ruby>まつて<ruby id="mwXA4">彼<rp id="mwXA8">(</rp><rt id="mwXBA">かの</rt><rp id="mwXBE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXBI">女<rp id="mwXBM">(</rp><rt id="mwXBQ">ぢよ</rt><rp id="mwXBU">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXBY">前<rp id="mwXBc">(</rp><rt id="mwXBg">まへ</rt><rp id="mwXBk">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXBo">書<rp id="mwXBs">(</rp><rt id="mwXBw">しよ</rt><rp id="mwXB0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXB4">籍<rp id="mwXB8">(</rp><rt id="mwXCA">じやく</rt><rp id="mwXCE">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwXCI">解<rp id="mwXCM">(</rp><rt id="mwXCQ">かい</rt><rp id="mwXCU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXCY">剖<rp id="mwXCc">(</rp><rt id="mwXCg">ばう</rt><rp id="mwXCk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXCo">刀<rp id="mwXCs">(</rp><rt id="mwXCw">たう</rt><rp id="mwXC0">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwXC4">斧<rp id="mwXC8">(</rp><rt id="mwXDA">おの</rt><rp id="mwXDE">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwXDI">繩<rp id="mwXDM">(</rp><rt id="mwXDQ">なは</rt><rp id="mwXDU">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwXDY">擴<rp id="mwXDc">(</rp><rt id="mwXDg">ひろ</rt><rp id="mwXDk">)</rp></ruby>げて、<ruby id="mwXDo">死<rp id="mwXDs">(</rp><rt id="mwXDw">し</rt><rp id="mwXD0">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXD4">存<rp id="mwXD8">(</rp><rt id="mwXEA">そん</rt><rp id="mwXEE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXEI">在<rp id="mwXEM">(</rp><rt id="mwXEQ">ざい</rt><rp id="mwXEU">)</rp></ruby>すること、<ruby id="mwXEY">人<rp id="mwXEc">(</rp><rt id="mwXEg">にん</rt><rp id="mwXEk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXEo">間<rp id="mwXEs">(</rp><rt id="mwXEw">げん</rt><rp id="mwXE0">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwXE4">死<rp id="mwXE8">(</rp><rt id="mwXFA">し</rt><rp id="mwXFE">)</rp></ruby>ぬれば<ruby id="mwXFI">其<rp id="mwXFM">(</rp><rt id="mwXFQ">そ</rt><rp id="mwXFU">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXFY">生<rp id="mwXFc">(</rp><rt id="mwXFg">せい</rt><rp id="mwXFk">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwXFo">消<rp id="mwXFs">(</rp><rt id="mwXFw">き</rt><rp id="mwXF0">)</rp></ruby>えること、<ruby id="mwXF4">不<rp id="mwXF8">(</rp><rt id="mwXGA">ふ</rt><rp id="mwXGE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXGI">死<rp id="mwXGM">(</rp><rt id="mwXGQ">し</rt><rp id="mwXGU">)</rp></ruby>なるものの<ruby id="mwXGY">決<rp id="mwXGc">(</rp><rt id="mwXGg">けつ</rt><rp id="mwXGk">)</rp></ruby>してないことを<ruby id="mwXGo">示<rp id="mwXGs">(</rp><rt id="mwXGw">しめ</rt><rp id="mwXG0">)</rp></ruby>したとすれば、<ruby id="mwXG4">彼<rp id="mwXG8">(</rp><rt id="mwXHA">かの</rt><rp id="mwXHE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXHI">女<rp id="mwXHM">(</rp><rt id="mwXHQ">ぢよ</rt><rp id="mwXHU">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwXHY">只<rp id="mwXHc">(</rp><rt id="mwXHg">たゞ</rt><rp id="mwXHk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXHo">之<rp id="mwXHs">(</rp><rt id="mwXHw">これ</rt><rp id="mwXH0">)</rp></ruby>を<span style="text-emphasis:sesame" id="mwXH4">あきれ</span>て<ruby id="mwXH8">眺<rp id="mwXIA">(</rp><rt id="mwXIE">なが</rt><rp id="mwXII">)</rp></ruby>めたであらう………<ruby id="mwXIM">彼<rp id="mwXIQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXIU">かの</rt><rp id="mwXIY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXIc">女<rp id="mwXIg">(</rp><rt id="mwXIk">ぢよ</rt><rp id="mwXIo">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwXIs">現<rp id="mwXIw">(</rp><rt id="mwXI0">げん</rt><rp id="mwXI4">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXI8">不<rp id="mwXJA">(</rp><rt id="mwXJE">ふ</rt><rp id="mwXJI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXJM">死<rp id="mwXJQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXJU">し</rt><rp id="mwXJY">)</rp></ruby>である<ruby id="mwXJc">以<rp id="mwXJg">(</rp><rt id="mwXJk">い</rt><rp id="mwXJo">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXJs">上<rp id="mwXJw">(</rp><rt id="mwXJ0">じやう</rt><rp id="mwXJ4">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwXJ8">不<rp id="mwXKA">(</rp><rt id="mwXKE">ふ</rt><rp id="mwXKI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXKM">死<rp id="mwXKQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXKU">し</rt><rp id="mwXKY">)</rp></ruby>なるものが<ruby id="mwXKc">決<rp id="mwXKg">(</rp><rt id="mwXKk">けつ</rt><rp id="mwXKo">)</rp></ruby>してあるべきでないとは<ruby id="mwXKs">何<rp id="mwXKw">(</rp><rt id="mwXK0">なに</rt><rp id="mwXK4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXK8">事<rp id="mwXLA">(</rp><rt id="mwXLE">ごと</rt><rp id="mwXLI">)</rp></ruby>だ？……<ruby id="mwXLM">彼<rp id="mwXLQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXLU">かの</rt><rp id="mwXLY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXLc">女<rp id="mwXLg">(</rp><rt id="mwXLk">ぢよ</rt><rp id="mwXLo">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwXLs">旣<rp id="mwXLw">(</rp><rt id="mwXL0">すで</rt><rp id="mwXL4">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXL8">殺<rp id="mwXMA">(</rp><rt id="mwXME">ころ</rt><rp id="mwXMI">)</rp></ruby>されて<ruby id="mwXMM">而<rp id="mwXMQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXMU">しか</rt><rp id="mwXMY">)</rp></ruby>も<ruby id="mwXMc">不<rp id="mwXMg">(</rp><rt id="mwXMk">ふ</rt><rp id="mwXMo">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXMs">死<rp id="mwXMw">(</rp><rt id="mwXM0">し</rt><rp id="mwXM4">)</rp></ruby>で、<ruby id="mwXM8">生<rp id="mwXNA">(</rp><rt id="mwXNE">せい</rt><rp id="mwXNI">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXNM">在<rp id="mwXNQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXNU">あつ</rt><rp id="mwXNY">)</rp></ruby>て<ruby id="mwXNc">活<rp id="mwXNg">(</rp><rt id="mwXNk">いき</rt><rp id="mwXNo">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXNs">々<rp id="mwXNw">(</rp><rt id="mwXN0">〱</rt><rp id="mwXN4">)</rp></ruby>としてゐるやう、<ruby id="mwXN8">死<rp id="mwXOA">(</rp><rt id="mwXOE">し</rt><rp id="mwXOI">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXOM">於<rp id="mwXOQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXOU">おい</rt><rp id="mwXOY">)</rp></ruby>ても<ruby id="mwXOc">活<rp id="mwXOg">(</rp><rt id="mwXOk">いき</rt><rp id="mwXOo">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXOs">々<rp id="mwXOw">(</rp><rt id="mwXO0">〱</rt><rp id="mwXO4">)</rp></ruby>としてゐたなら、<ruby id="mwXO8">死<rp id="mwXPA">(</rp><rt id="mwXPE">し</rt><rp id="mwXPI">)</rp></ruby>とか<ruby id="mwXPM">不<rp id="mwXPQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXPU">ふ</rt><rp id="mwXPY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXPc">死<rp id="mwXPg">(</rp><rt id="mwXPk">し</rt><rp id="mwXPo">)</rp></ruby>とは<ruby id="mwXPs">何<rp id="mwXPw">(</rp><rt id="mwXP0">なん</rt><rp id="mwXP4">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXP8">話<rp id="mwXQA">(</rp><rt id="mwXQE">はなし</rt><rp id="mwXQI">)</rp></ruby>だらう………</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXQM">[</span>If all the savants, philosophers and prison wardens from the world over should gather in her cell, lay out books, scalpels, axes and nooses before her, and prove that death exists, that when a human dies their life disappears, that there is no such thing as immortality, she would only stare at that with <i id="mwXQQ">amazement</i>… How could there be no immortality, since she was already immortal?… What could it be to speak of death or immortality, when she had already been killed and yet was immortal, alive in death, as she had been alive in life?…<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXQU">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%D0%A0%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%B7+%D0%BE+%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BC%D0%B8+%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%88%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BD%D1%8B%D1%85+%3Cruby%3E%E6%AD%BB%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%97%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E5%88%91%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%91%E3%81%84%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E4%B8%83%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%97%E3%81%A1%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E4%BA%BA%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%AB%E3%82%93%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E7%89%A9%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%82%82%E3%81%AE%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E8%AA%9E%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%8C%E3%81%9F%E3%82%8A%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E&amp;rft.btitle=%D0%9C%D1%83%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B8+%3Cruby%3E%E9%97%87%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%82%84%E3%81%BF%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%81%AE%3Cruby%3E%E5%9C%8B%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%8F%E3%81%AB%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E&amp;rft.place=Ushigome%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=185&amp;rft.pub=Shun%27y%C5%8Dsha&amp;rft.date=1925-06-08&amp;rft.aulast=Andreyev&amp;rft.aufirst=Leonid+Nikolaievich&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1016971%2F1%2F98&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3286" id="mwXQY"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3286" id="mwXQc"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3286" id="mwXQg"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-shimamura-katagami-1915-dewaarimasenanda-rureba-508" id="cite_note-shimamura-katagami-1915-dewaarimasenanda-rureba-508" data-mw-footnote-number="475"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXQk"><a href="#cite_ref-shimamura-katagami-1915-dewaarimasenanda-rureba_508-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXQo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXQs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-shimamura-katagami-1915-dewaarimasenanda-rureba-508" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3309" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXQw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=No fueron tan vanas nueſtras oraciones que no fueſſen oydas del cielo, que en nueſtro fauor luego boluio el viento tranquilo el mar, combidandonos a que tornaſſemos alegres a proſeguir nueſtro començado viage. […] Dificil ſeñor ſe hizo de creer la cõtinencia del moço, pero ella lo afirmò con tantas veras, que fueron parte para que el deſconſolado padre ſe conſolaſſe, no haziendo cuẽta de las riquezas q̃ le lleuauan: pues le auian dexado a ſu hija con la joya, que ſi vna vez ſe pierde no dexa eſperança de que jamas ſe cobre.&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:<ruby>私<rp>(</rp><rt>わたし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>たちの<ruby>祈<rp>(</rp><rt>いの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>りは<ruby>天<rp>(</rp><rt>てん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>屆<rp>(</rp><rt>とゞ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>かぬほどに<ruby>效<rp>(</rp><rt>かひ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ないものではありませなんだ。<ruby>間<rp>(</rp><rt>ま</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>もなく<ruby>風<rp>(</rp><rt>かぜ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>は<ruby>順<rp>(</rp><rt>じゆん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>風<rp>(</rp><rt>ぷう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>變<rp>(</rp><rt>へん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>じ、<ruby>海<rp>(</rp><rt>うみ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>は<ruby>靜<rp>(</rp><rt>しづ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>まつて、<ruby>私<rp>(</rp><rt>わたし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>たちを<ruby>元<rp>(</rp><rt>げん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>氣<rp>(</rp><rt>き</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>よく<ruby>再<rp>(</rp><rt>ふたゝ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>び<ruby>航<rp>(</rp><rt>かう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>海<rp>(</rp><rt>かい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>をつゞけるように<ruby>誘<rp>(</rp><rt>さそ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ひました。[…]<ruby>私<rp>(</rp><rt>わたし</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>たちに<ruby>取<rp>(</rp><rt>と</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>つてはその<ruby>若<rp>(</rp><rt>わか</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>者<rp>(</rp><rt>もの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>節<rp>(</rp><rt>せつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>慾<rp>(</rp><rt>よく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>を<ruby>信<rp>(</rp><rt>しん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>ずることは<ruby>容<rp>(</rp><rt>よう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>易<rp>(</rp><rt>い</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>でありませなんだ。しかしレアンドラは一<ruby>生<rp>(</rp><rt>せい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>懸<rp>(</rp><rt>けん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>命<rp>(</rp><rt>めい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>にそれを<ruby>辯<rp>(</rp><rt>べん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>護<rp>(</rp><rt>ご</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>しましたので、その<ruby>落<rp>(</rp><rt>らく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>膽<rp>(</rp><rt>たん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>してゐる<ruby>父<rp>(</rp><rt>ちゝ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>親<rp>(</rp><rt>おや</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>もそれをせめてもの<ruby>慰<rp>(</rp><rt>なぐさ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>めとしました。<ruby>父<rp>(</rp><rt>ちゝ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>親<rp>(</rp><rt>おや</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>は、一<ruby>度<rp>(</rp><rt>ど</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>失<rp>(</rp><rt>うしな</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>はるれば<ruby>未<rp>(</rp><rt>み</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>來<rp>(</rp><rt>らい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>永<rp>(</rp><rt>えい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>劫<rp>(</rp><rt>がふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>囘<rp>(</rp><rt>くわい</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>復<rp>(</rp><rt>ふく</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>されない<ruby>寶<rp>(</rp><rt>たから</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>が<ruby>自<rp>(</rp><rt>じ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>分<rp>(</rp><rt>ぶん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>娘<rp>(</rp><rt>むすめ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に<ruby>殘<rp>(</rp><rt>のこ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>されてある<ruby>以<rp>(</rp><rt>い</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>上<rp>(</rp><rt>じやう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>は、その<ruby>外<rp>(</rp><rt>ほか</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>盜<rp>(</rp><rt>ぬす</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>まれた<ruby>物<rp>(</rp><rt>もの</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>は<ruby>何<rp>(</rp><rt>なん</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>とも<ruby>思<rp>(</rp><rt>おも</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>はなんだのです。&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-quote=Our prayers were not so in vain as not to reach Heaven. In our favor the wind soon changed, the sea calmed, inviting us again to resume our voyage with good vigor. […] It was not easy for us to credit the young man’s continence. But Leandra affirmed it so earnestly that at least her disconsolate father found it consoling. Since the jewel, which would be forever unrecoverable once lost, had been left to his daughter, he did not think much of his other stolen goods.&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;p=752, 906&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/945515/1/424&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:ドン・キホーテ&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-title=[[Don Quixote]]&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=EL INGENIOSO HIDALGO DON QVIXOTE DE LA MANCHA&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Miguel&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=de Cervantes Saavedra&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Miguel de Cervantes&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=1&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=13 November 1915&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;edition=2nd&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-link=Hōgetsu Shimamura&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Hōgetsu&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Shimamura&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-link2=Noburu Katagami&quot;},&quot;21&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first2=Noburu&quot;},&quot;22&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last2=Katagami&quot;},&quot;23&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Uetake Shoin&quot;},&quot;24&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Kōjimachi]], Tokyo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="mwXQ0" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3309" data-x-id="CITEREFde_Cervantes_Saavedra1915"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miguel_de_Cervantes" title="Miguel de Cervantes" id="mwXQ4">de Cervantes Saavedra, Miguel</a> (13 November 1915). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/945515/1/424" class="external text" id="mwXQ8"><i id="mwXRA">EL INGENIOSO HIDALGO DON QVIXOTE DE LA MANCHA</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXRE">ドン・キホーテ</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXRI">[</span><i id="mwXRM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Quixote" title="Don Quixote" id="mwXRQ">Don Quixote</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXRU">]</span> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXRY">&nbsp;</span>1. Translated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hōgetsu_Shimamura" title="Hōgetsu Shimamura" id="mwXRc">Shimamura, Hōgetsu</a>; <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noburu_Katagami" title="Noburu Katagami" id="mwXRg">Katagami, Noburu</a> (2nd<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXRk">&nbsp;</span>ed.). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kōjimachi" title="Kōjimachi" id="mwXRo">Kōjimachi</a>, Tokyo: Uetake Shoin. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXRs">&nbsp;</span>752, 906. <q id="mwXRw">No fueron tan vanas nueſtras oraciones que no fueſſen oydas del cielo, que en nueſtro fauor luego boluio el viento tranquilo el mar, combidandonos a que tornaſſemos alegres a proſeguir nueſtro començado viage. […] Dificil ſeñor ſe hizo de creer la cõtinencia del moço, pero ella lo afirmò con tantas veras, que fueron parte para que el deſconſolado padre ſe conſolaſſe, no haziendo cuẽta de las riquezas q̃ le lleuauan: pues le auian dexado a ſu hija con la joya, que ſi vna vez ſe pierde no dexa eſperança de que jamas ſe cobre.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXR0"><ruby id="mwXR4">私<rp id="mwXR8">(</rp><rt id="mwXSA">わたし</rt><rp id="mwXSE">)</rp></ruby>たちの<ruby id="mwXSI">祈<rp id="mwXSM">(</rp><rt id="mwXSQ">いの</rt><rp id="mwXSU">)</rp></ruby>りは<ruby id="mwXSY">天<rp id="mwXSc">(</rp><rt id="mwXSg">てん</rt><rp id="mwXSk">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXSo">屆<rp id="mwXSs">(</rp><rt id="mwXSw">とゞ</rt><rp id="mwXS0">)</rp></ruby>かぬほどに<ruby id="mwXS4">效<rp id="mwXS8">(</rp><rt id="mwXTA">かひ</rt><rp id="mwXTE">)</rp></ruby>ないものではありませなんだ。<ruby id="mwXTI">間<rp id="mwXTM">(</rp><rt id="mwXTQ">ま</rt><rp id="mwXTU">)</rp></ruby>もなく<ruby id="mwXTY">風<rp id="mwXTc">(</rp><rt id="mwXTg">かぜ</rt><rp id="mwXTk">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwXTo">順<rp id="mwXTs">(</rp><rt id="mwXTw">じゆん</rt><rp id="mwXT0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXT4">風<rp id="mwXT8">(</rp><rt id="mwXUA">ぷう</rt><rp id="mwXUE">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXUI">變<rp id="mwXUM">(</rp><rt id="mwXUQ">へん</rt><rp id="mwXUU">)</rp></ruby>じ、<ruby id="mwXUY">海<rp id="mwXUc">(</rp><rt id="mwXUg">うみ</rt><rp id="mwXUk">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwXUo">靜<rp id="mwXUs">(</rp><rt id="mwXUw">しづ</rt><rp id="mwXU0">)</rp></ruby>まつて、<ruby id="mwXU4">私<rp id="mwXU8">(</rp><rt id="mwXVA">わたし</rt><rp id="mwXVE">)</rp></ruby>たちを<ruby id="mwXVI">元<rp id="mwXVM">(</rp><rt id="mwXVQ">げん</rt><rp id="mwXVU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXVY">氣<rp id="mwXVc">(</rp><rt id="mwXVg">き</rt><rp id="mwXVk">)</rp></ruby>よく<ruby id="mwXVo">再<rp id="mwXVs">(</rp><rt id="mwXVw">ふたゝ</rt><rp id="mwXV0">)</rp></ruby>び<ruby id="mwXV4">航<rp id="mwXV8">(</rp><rt id="mwXWA">かう</rt><rp id="mwXWE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXWI">海<rp id="mwXWM">(</rp><rt id="mwXWQ">かい</rt><rp id="mwXWU">)</rp></ruby>をつゞけるように<ruby id="mwXWY">誘<rp id="mwXWc">(</rp><rt id="mwXWg">さそ</rt><rp id="mwXWk">)</rp></ruby>ひました。[…]<ruby id="mwXWo">私<rp id="mwXWs">(</rp><rt id="mwXWw">わたし</rt><rp id="mwXW0">)</rp></ruby>たちに<ruby id="mwXW4">取<rp id="mwXW8">(</rp><rt id="mwXXA">と</rt><rp id="mwXXE">)</rp></ruby>つてはその<ruby id="mwXXI">若<rp id="mwXXM">(</rp><rt id="mwXXQ">わか</rt><rp id="mwXXU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXXY">者<rp id="mwXXc">(</rp><rt id="mwXXg">もの</rt><rp id="mwXXk">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXXo">節<rp id="mwXXs">(</rp><rt id="mwXXw">せつ</rt><rp id="mwXX0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXX4">慾<rp id="mwXX8">(</rp><rt id="mwXYA">よく</rt><rp id="mwXYE">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwXYI">信<rp id="mwXYM">(</rp><rt id="mwXYQ">しん</rt><rp id="mwXYU">)</rp></ruby>ずることは<ruby id="mwXYY">容<rp id="mwXYc">(</rp><rt id="mwXYg">よう</rt><rp id="mwXYk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXYo">易<rp id="mwXYs">(</rp><rt id="mwXYw">い</rt><rp id="mwXY0">)</rp></ruby>でありませなんだ。しかしレアンドラは一<ruby id="mwXY4">生<rp id="mwXY8">(</rp><rt id="mwXZA">せい</rt><rp id="mwXZE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXZI">懸<rp id="mwXZM">(</rp><rt id="mwXZQ">けん</rt><rp id="mwXZU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXZY">命<rp id="mwXZc">(</rp><rt id="mwXZg">めい</rt><rp id="mwXZk">)</rp></ruby>にそれを<ruby id="mwXZo">辯<rp id="mwXZs">(</rp><rt id="mwXZw">べん</rt><rp id="mwXZ0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXZ4">護<rp id="mwXZ8">(</rp><rt id="mwXaA">ご</rt><rp id="mwXaE">)</rp></ruby>しましたので、その<ruby id="mwXaI">落<rp id="mwXaM">(</rp><rt id="mwXaQ">らく</rt><rp id="mwXaU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXaY">膽<rp id="mwXac">(</rp><rt id="mwXag">たん</rt><rp id="mwXak">)</rp></ruby>してゐる<ruby id="mwXao">父<rp id="mwXas">(</rp><rt id="mwXaw">ちゝ</rt><rp id="mwXa0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXa4">親<rp id="mwXa8">(</rp><rt id="mwXbA">おや</rt><rp id="mwXbE">)</rp></ruby>もそれをせめてもの<ruby id="mwXbI">慰<rp id="mwXbM">(</rp><rt id="mwXbQ">なぐさ</rt><rp id="mwXbU">)</rp></ruby>めとしました。<ruby id="mwXbY">父<rp id="mwXbc">(</rp><rt id="mwXbg">ちゝ</rt><rp id="mwXbk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXbo">親<rp id="mwXbs">(</rp><rt id="mwXbw">おや</rt><rp id="mwXb0">)</rp></ruby>は、一<ruby id="mwXb4">度<rp id="mwXb8">(</rp><rt id="mwXcA">ど</rt><rp id="mwXcE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXcI">失<rp id="mwXcM">(</rp><rt id="mwXcQ">うしな</rt><rp id="mwXcU">)</rp></ruby>はるれば<ruby id="mwXcY">未<rp id="mwXcc">(</rp><rt id="mwXcg">み</rt><rp id="mwXck">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXco">來<rp id="mwXcs">(</rp><rt id="mwXcw">らい</rt><rp id="mwXc0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXc4">永<rp id="mwXc8">(</rp><rt id="mwXdA">えい</rt><rp id="mwXdE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXdI">劫<rp id="mwXdM">(</rp><rt id="mwXdQ">がふ</rt><rp id="mwXdU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXdY">囘<rp id="mwXdc">(</rp><rt id="mwXdg">くわい</rt><rp id="mwXdk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXdo">復<rp id="mwXds">(</rp><rt id="mwXdw">ふく</rt><rp id="mwXd0">)</rp></ruby>されない<ruby id="mwXd4">寶<rp id="mwXd8">(</rp><rt id="mwXeA">たから</rt><rp id="mwXeE">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwXeI">自<rp id="mwXeM">(</rp><rt id="mwXeQ">じ</rt><rp id="mwXeU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXeY">分<rp id="mwXec">(</rp><rt id="mwXeg">ぶん</rt><rp id="mwXek">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXeo">娘<rp id="mwXes">(</rp><rt id="mwXew">むすめ</rt><rp id="mwXe0">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwXe4">殘<rp id="mwXe8">(</rp><rt id="mwXfA">のこ</rt><rp id="mwXfE">)</rp></ruby>されてある<ruby id="mwXfI">以<rp id="mwXfM">(</rp><rt id="mwXfQ">い</rt><rp id="mwXfU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXfY">上<rp id="mwXfc">(</rp><rt id="mwXfg">じやう</rt><rp id="mwXfk">)</rp></ruby>は、その<ruby id="mwXfo">外<rp id="mwXfs">(</rp><rt id="mwXfw">ほか</rt><rp id="mwXf0">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXf4">盜<rp id="mwXf8">(</rp><rt id="mwXgA">ぬす</rt><rp id="mwXgE">)</rp></ruby>まれた<ruby id="mwXgI">物<rp id="mwXgM">(</rp><rt id="mwXgQ">もの</rt><rp id="mwXgU">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwXgY">何<rp id="mwXgc">(</rp><rt id="mwXgg">なん</rt><rp id="mwXgk">)</rp></ruby>とも<ruby id="mwXgo">思<rp id="mwXgs">(</rp><rt id="mwXgw">おも</rt><rp id="mwXg0">)</rp></ruby>はなんだのです。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXg4">[</span>Our prayers were not so in vain as not to reach Heaven. In our favor the wind soon changed, the sea calmed, inviting us again to resume our voyage with good vigor. […] It was not easy for us to credit the young man’s continence. But Leandra affirmed it so earnestly that at least her disconsolate father found it consoling. Since the jewel, which would be forever unrecoverable once lost, had been left to his daughter, he did not think much of his other stolen goods.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXg8">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=EL+INGENIOSO+HIDALGO+DON+QVIXOTE+DE+LA+MANCHA+%E3%83%89%E3%83%B3%E3%83%BB%E3%82%AD%E3%83%9B%E3%83%BC%E3%83%86&amp;rft.place=K%C5%8Djimachi%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=752%2C+906&amp;rft.edition=2nd&amp;rft.pub=Uetake+Shoin&amp;rft.date=1915-11-13&amp;rft.aulast=de+Cervantes+Saavedra&amp;rft.aufirst=Miguel&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F945515%2F1%2F424&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3309" id="mwXhA"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3309" id="mwXhE"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3309" id="mwXhI"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-fukami-1931-509" id="cite_note-fukami-1931-509" data-mw-footnote-number="476"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXhM"><a href="#cite_ref-fukami-1931_509-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXhQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXhU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-fukami-1931-509" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3312" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXhY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:率直に言ふことを許さるれば、スミスに於ける自由貿易理論は尚ほ未だ全きものではあらなかつた。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=23–24&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1272097/1/19&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第二章 世界經濟思想の由來&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=10 October 1931&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Fukami&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Giichi&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:世界經濟總論&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|世界經濟硏究}}&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=1&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Kanda, Tokyo]]&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|瞭文堂}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="mwXhc" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3312" data-x-id="CITEREFFukami1931">Fukami, Giichi (10 October 1931).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXhg">第二章 世界經濟思想の由來</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1272097/1/19" class="external text" id="mwXhk"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwXho">世界經濟總論</bdi></a>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXhs"><span lang="ja" id="mwXhw">世界經濟硏究</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXh0"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXh4">&nbsp;</span>1. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanda,_Tokyo" title="Kanda, Tokyo" id="mwXh8">Kanda, Tokyo</a>: <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXiA"><span lang="ja" id="mwXiE">瞭文堂</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXiI">. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXiM">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwXiQ">23–</span>24.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXiU">率直に言ふことを許さるれば、スミスに於ける自由貿易理論は尚ほ未だ全きものではあらなかつた。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E4%BA%8C%E7%AB%A0+%E4%B8%96%E7%95%8C%E7%B6%93%E6%BF%9F%E6%80%9D%E6%83%B3%E3%81%AE%E7%94%B1%E4%BE%86&amp;rft.btitle=%E4%B8%96%E7%95%8C%E7%B6%93%E6%BF%9F%E7%B8%BD%E8%AB%96&amp;rft.place=Kanda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E4%B8%96%E7%95%8C%E7%B6%93%E6%BF%9F%E7%A1%8F%E7%A9%B6%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=23-24&amp;rft.pub=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E7%9E%AD%E6%96%87%E5%A0%82%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.date=1931-10-10&amp;rft.aulast=Fukami&amp;rft.aufirst=Giichi&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1272097%2F1%2F19&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3312" id="mwXiY"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3312" id="mwXic"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3312" id="mwXig"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-511" id="cite_note-511" data-mw-footnote-number="477"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXik"><a href="#cite_ref-511" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXio"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXis">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-511" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3343" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXiw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:『併し君は餘り早く來過ぎたよ。君は私と同樣、日の出る二時間前、見張をすることであつた。これは私の最初の出陣で、名を揚げるか、<ruby>隕<rp>(</rp><rt>おど</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>すか、此の一擧にかゝつてをる。敵は老練なリシンガムとブラックリイ（ダニエル）の二將に率ゐられて、なか〱手剛い。だが、彼等は兩面海と川とに圍まれて、<ruby>退<rp>(</rp><rt>のき</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>路<rp>(</rp><rt>みち</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>がない。だから、<ruby>窃<rp>(</rp><rt>ひそか</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>に立つて不意打を食はすれば、大打擊を與へることが出來ようと思ふ』&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=“Ye come too soon,” he said; “but why should I complain? Ye are like me, that was here at watch two hours before the day. But this is the first sally of mine arms; upon this adventure, Master Shelton, shall I make or mar the quality of my renown. There lie mine enemies, under two old, skilled captains, Risingham and Brackley, well posted for strength, I do believe, but yet upon two sides without retreat, enclosed betwixt the sea, the harbour, and the river. Methinks, Shelton, here were a great blow to be stricken, an we could strike it silently and suddenly.”&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;p=264&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1689407/1/144&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:'''一'''　<ruby>銳<rp>(</rp><rt>するど</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>い<ruby>喇<rp>(</rp><rt>らつ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>叭<rp>(</rp><rt>ぱ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>の<ruby>音<rp>(</rp><rt>ね</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;chapter=CHAPTER I. <span style=font-variant:small-caps>the shrill trumpet.</span>&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-chapter='''I.''' The Sound of the Trumpet&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:黑矢物語&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-title=[[The Black Arrow: A Tale of the Two Roses|Tale of the Black Arrow]]&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=The Black Arrow: A Tale of the Two Roses&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|世界名作物語}}&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Robert Louis Stevenson&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Robert Louis&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Stevenson&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Kōichirō&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Miyahara&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=10 October 1940&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Dōwa Shunjusha&quot;},&quot;21&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Nihonbashi]], Tokyo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFStevenson1940" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3343"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Louis_Stevenson" title="Robert Louis Stevenson" id="mwXi0">Stevenson, Robert Louis</a> (10 October 1940). "CHAPTER I. <span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwXi4">the shrill trumpet.</span>" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXi8"><b id="mwXjA">一</b>　<ruby id="mwXjE">銳<rp id="mwXjI">(</rp><rt id="mwXjM">するど</rt><rp id="mwXjQ">)</rp></ruby>い<ruby id="mwXjU">喇<rp id="mwXjY">(</rp><rt id="mwXjc">らつ</rt><rp id="mwXjg">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXjk">叭<rp id="mwXjo">(</rp><rt id="mwXjs">ぱ</rt><rp id="mwXjw">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwXj0">音<rp id="mwXj4">(</rp><rt id="mwXj8">ね</rt><rp id="mwXkA">)</rp></ruby></bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXkE">[</span><b id="mwXkI">I.</b> The Sound of the Trumpet<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXkM">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1689407/1/144" class="external text" id="mwXkQ"><i id="mwXkU">The Black Arrow: A Tale of the Two Roses</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXkY">黑矢物語</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXkc">[</span><i id="mwXkg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Black_Arrow:_A_Tale_of_the_Two_Roses" title="The Black Arrow: A Tale of the Two Roses" id="mwXkk">Tale of the Black Arrow</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXko">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXks"><span lang="ja" id="mwXkw">世界名作物語</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXk0"> (in Japanese). Translated by Miyahara, Kōichirō. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi" title="Nihonbashi" id="mwXk4">Nihonbashi</a>, Tokyo: Dōwa Shunjusha. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXk8">&nbsp;</span>264. <q id="mwXlA"><span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwXlE"></span>"Ye come too soon," he said; "but why should I complain? Ye are like me, that was here at watch two hours before the day. But this is the first sally of mine arms; upon this adventure, Master Shelton, shall I make or mar the quality of my renown. There lie mine enemies, under two old, skilled captains, Risingham and Brackley, well posted for strength, I do believe, but yet upon two sides without retreat, enclosed betwixt the sea, the harbour, and the river. Methinks, Shelton, here were a great blow to be stricken, an we could strike it silently and suddenly."<span class="cs1-kern-right" id="mwXlI"></span></q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXlM">『併し君は餘り早く來過ぎたよ。君は私と同樣、日の出る二時間前、見張をすることであつた。これは私の最初の出陣で、名を揚げるか、<ruby id="mwXlQ">隕<rp id="mwXlU">(</rp><rt id="mwXlY">おど</rt><rp id="mwXlc">)</rp></ruby>すか、此の一擧にかゝつてをる。敵は老練なリシンガムとブラックリイ（ダニエル）の二將に率ゐられて、なか〱手剛い。だが、彼等は兩面海と川とに圍まれて、<ruby id="mwXlg">退<rp id="mwXlk">(</rp><rt id="mwXlo">のき</rt><rp id="mwXls">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwXlw">路<rp id="mwXl0">(</rp><rt id="mwXl4">みち</rt><rp id="mwXl8">)</rp></ruby>がない。だから、<ruby id="mwXmA">窃<rp id="mwXmE">(</rp><rt id="mwXmI">ひそか</rt><rp id="mwXmM">)</rp></ruby>に立つて不意打を食はすれば、大打擊を與へることが出來ようと思ふ』</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=CHAPTER+I.+%3Cspan+style%3Dfont-variant%3Asmall-caps%3Ethe+shrill+trumpet.%3C%2Fspan%3E+%E4%B8%80%E3%80%80%3Cruby%3E%E9%8A%B3%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%99%E3%82%8B%E3%81%A9%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%81%84%3Cruby%3E%E5%96%87%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%82%89%E3%81%A4%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E5%8F%AD%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%B1%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%81%AE%3Cruby%3E%E9%9F%B3%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%AD%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E&amp;rft.btitle=The+Black+Arrow%3A+A+Tale+of+the+Two+Roses+%E9%BB%91%E7%9F%A2%E7%89%A9%E8%AA%9E&amp;rft.place=Nihonbashi%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E4%B8%96%E7%95%8C%E5%90%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%89%A9%E8%AA%9E%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=264&amp;rft.pub=D%C5%8Dwa+Shunjusha&amp;rft.date=1940-10-10&amp;rft.aulast=Stevenson&amp;rft.aufirst=Robert+Louis&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1689407%2F1%2F144&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3343" id="mwXmQ"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3343" id="mwXmU"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3343" id="mwXmY"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-nakayama-1951-513" id="cite_note-nakayama-1951-513" data-mw-footnote-number="478"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXmc"><a href="#cite_ref-nakayama-1951_513-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXmg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXmk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-nakayama-1951-513" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3366" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXmo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-quote=“I myself know there have been a great many crimes just as horrific before. I recently visited a prison and was able to get close to some convicted and unconvicted inmates. There were some among them far more horrible than this one, offenders who have killed ten people without the least remorse. But I noticed this: even the most hardened and remorseless murderer still knows he’s a ''criminal''. That means he’s still conscious he’s done a bad thing, even if he has no remorse. And they were all like this. Yet the people Yevgeny Pavlovich spoke of don’t even have the slightest inkling they’re criminals, in their guts they just had a right to do what they did… they did a good thing,… that’s mostly how they feel, isn’t it? If you ask me, that there is the major difference. And get this, they’re all youths, you know, the age group hopelessly susceptible to the distortion of ideas.”&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:「それは、僕も犯罪が以前にもこういう怖ろしいのが非常に多かつたということは、自分でも知つています。つい先ごろ僕は監獄へ參りまして、いくたりかの囚人や未決囚と近づきになることができました。中には今度のよりはずつと怖ろしいのがいて、十人も殺しておきながら、一寸も後悔していないような犯人もいました。しかし、僕はその時こんな事に氣がつきました。それはこの上もなく頑强な、そして一寸も後悔をしていない殺人犯でも、やはり自分が<span style=text-emphasis:sesame>罪人</span>であるということは知つている。つまり、良心的に、たとい後悔などはしていないにしても、自分が良くないことをしたのだということだけは考えているということです。そして彼等は悉くそうなのです。ところがエヴゲニイ・パーヴロヰッチさんがお話しになつたような人たちは、自分のことを罪人だということを考えて見る氣持さえもなく、肚の中では、當然そうする權利があつたのだ……よいことをしたのだと、……つまり大體がそういう氣持でいるんじやありませんか。僕をして言わしむれば、ここにこそ非常な相違があるのです。しかも注意しなければならないのは、これがみんな靑年であるということつまり何よりもたやすく、あつさりと觀念の曲解に陷ることのできる年頃の連中であることです。」&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=— Я сам знаю, что преступлений и прежде было очень много, и таких же ужасных; я еще недавно в острогах был, и с некоторыми преступниками и подсудимыми мне удалось познакомиться. Есть даже страшнее преступники, чем этот, убившие по десяти человек, совсем не раскаиваясь. Но я вот что заметил при этом: что самый закоренелый и нераскаянный убийца все-таки знает, что он преступник, то есть по совести считает, что он нехорошо поступил, хоть и безо всякого раскаяния. И таков всякий из них; а эти ведь, о которых Евгений Павлыч заговорил, не хотят себя даже считать преступниками и думают про себя, что право имели и… даже хорошо поступили, то есть почти ведь так. Вот в этом-то и состоит, по-моему, ужасная разница. И заметьте, всё это молодежь, то есть именно такой возраст, в котором всего легче и беззащитнее можно подпасть под извращение идей.&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;p=17&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1690459/1/13&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第三編&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-chapter=Part III&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;chapter=Часть III&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:白痴&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-title=[[The Idiot]]&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Идиот&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Fyodor Dostoevsky&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Fyodor Mikhailovich&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Dostoevsky&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Shōzaburō&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Nakayama&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|世界文學選書}}&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=3&quot;},&quot;21&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Mikasa Shobo&quot;},&quot;22&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=30 June 1951&quot;},&quot;23&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFDostoevsky1951" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3366"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fyodor_Dostoevsky" title="Fyodor Dostoevsky" id="mwXms">Dostoevsky, Fyodor Mikhailovich</a> (30 June 1951). "Часть III" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXmw">第三編</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXm0">[</span>Part III<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXm4">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1690459/1/13" class="external text" id="mwXm8"><i id="mwXnA">Идиот</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXnE">白痴</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXnI">[</span><i id="mwXnM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Idiot" title="The Idiot" id="mwXnQ">The Idiot</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXnU">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXnY"><span lang="ja" id="mwXnc">世界文學選書</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXng"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXnk">&nbsp;</span>3. Translated by Nakayama, Shōzaburō. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiyoda,_Tokyo" title="Chiyoda, Tokyo" id="mwXno">Chiyoda, Tokyo</a>: Mikasa Shobo. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXns">&nbsp;</span>17. <q id="mwXnw">— Я сам знаю, что преступлений и прежде было очень много, и таких же ужасных; я еще недавно в острогах был, и с некоторыми преступниками и подсудимыми мне удалось познакомиться. Есть даже страшнее преступники, чем этот, убившие по десяти человек, совсем не раскаиваясь. Но я вот что заметил при этом: что самый закоренелый и нераскаянный убийца все-таки знает, что он преступник, то есть по совести считает, что он нехорошо поступил, хоть и безо всякого раскаяния. И таков всякий из них; а эти ведь, о которых Евгений Павлыч заговорил, не хотят себя даже считать преступниками и думают про себя, что право имели и… даже хорошо поступили, то есть почти ведь так. Вот в этом-то и состоит, по-моему, ужасная разница. И заметьте, всё это молодежь, то есть именно такой возраст, в котором всего легче и беззащитнее можно подпасть под извращение идей.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXn0">「それは、僕も犯罪が以前にもこういう怖ろしいのが非常に多かつたということは、自分でも知つています。つい先ごろ僕は監獄へ參りまして、いくたりかの囚人や未決囚と近づきになることができました。中には今度のよりはずつと怖ろしいのがいて、十人も殺しておきながら、一寸も後悔していないような犯人もいました。しかし、僕はその時こんな事に氣がつきました。それはこの上もなく頑强な、そして一寸も後悔をしていない殺人犯でも、やはり自分が<span style="text-emphasis:sesame" id="mwXn4">罪人</span>であるということは知つている。つまり、良心的に、たとい後悔などはしていないにしても、自分が良くないことをしたのだということだけは考えているということです。そして彼等は悉くそうなのです。ところがエヴゲニイ・パーヴロヰッチさんがお話しになつたような人たちは、自分のことを罪人だということを考えて見る氣持さえもなく、肚の中では、當然そうする權利があつたのだ……よいことをしたのだと、……つまり大體がそういう氣持でいるんじやありませんか。僕をして言わしむれば、ここにこそ非常な相違があるのです。しかも注意しなければならないのは、これがみんな靑年であるということつまり何よりもたやすく、あつさりと觀念の曲解に陷ることのできる年頃の連中であることです。」</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXn8">[</span>“I myself know there have been a great many crimes just as horrific before. I recently visited a prison and was able to get close to some convicted and unconvicted inmates. There were some among them far more horrible than this one, offenders who have killed ten people without the least remorse. But I noticed this: even the most hardened and remorseless murderer still knows he’s a <i id="mwXoA">criminal</i>. That means he’s still conscious he’s done a bad thing, even if he has no remorse. And they were all like this. Yet the people Yevgeny Pavlovich spoke of don’t even have the slightest inkling they’re criminals, in their guts they just had a right to do what they did… they did a good thing,… that’s mostly how they feel, isn’t it? If you ask me, that there is the major difference. And get this, they’re all youths, you know, the age group hopelessly susceptible to the distortion of ideas.”<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXoE">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%D0%A7%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C+III+%E7%AC%AC%E4%B8%89%E7%B7%A8&amp;rft.btitle=%D0%98%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BE%D1%82+%E7%99%BD%E7%97%B4&amp;rft.place=Chiyoda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E4%B8%96%E7%95%8C%E6%96%87%E5%AD%B8%E9%81%B8%E6%9B%B8%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=17&amp;rft.pub=Mikasa+Shobo&amp;rft.date=1951-06-30&amp;rft.aulast=Dostoevsky&amp;rft.aufirst=Fyodor+Mikhailovich&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1690459%2F1%2F13&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3366" id="mwXoI"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3366" id="mwXoM"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3366" id="mwXoQ"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-514" id="cite_note-514" data-mw-footnote-number="479"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXoU"><a href="#cite_ref-514" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXoY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXoc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-514" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3380" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXog" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;citation&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Citation&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ja&quot;},&quot;script-quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ja:この病気の原因を研究いたし，これを予防することができますれば，日本国民および医学にたずさわる者の名誉でございます．[…]脚気病の原因は，高木の研究によりますれば，栄養の調合が悪いためであります．&quot;},&quot;pages&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;444–445&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://ir.jikei.ac.jp/record/1710/files/TK_igaku_444.pdf&quot;},&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Matsuda&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Makoto&quot;},&quot;script-title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ja:切腹してお詫びする&quot;},&quot;year&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2007&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFMatsuda2007" class="citation cs2 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3380">Matsuda, Makoto (2007), <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ir.jikei.ac.jp/record/1710/files/TK_igaku_444.pdf" class="external text" id="mwXok"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwXoo">切腹してお詫びする</bdi></a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwXos">(PDF)</span> (in Japanese), pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXow">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwXo0">444–</span>445,  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXo4">この病気の原因を研究いたし，これを予防することができますれば，日本国民および医学にたずさわる者の名誉でございます．[…]脚気病の原因は，高木の研究によりますれば，栄養の調合が悪いためであります．</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=%E5%88%87%E8%85%B9%E3%81%97%E3%81%A6%E3%81%8A%E8%A9%AB%E3%81%B3%E3%81%99%E3%82%8B&amp;rft.pages=444-445&amp;rft.date=2007&amp;rft.aulast=Matsuda&amp;rft.aufirst=Makoto&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fir.jikei.ac.jp%2Frecord%2F1710%2Ffiles%2FTK_igaku_444.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3380" id="mwXo8"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3380" id="mwXpA"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3380" id="mwXpE"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-515" id="cite_note-515" data-mw-footnote-number="480"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXpI"><a href="#cite_ref-515" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXpM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXpQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-515" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3383" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXpU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:「年上を正室とした前例がございますれば、問題ないかと」&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:王宮の事件&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|おかしな転生}}&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=V&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:レーズンパンの恋模様&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=TO Books&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Koryū&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Nozomu&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=10 November 2016&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFKoryū2016" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3383">Koryū, Nozomu (10 November 2016).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXpY">王宮の事件</bdi>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXpc">レーズンパンの恋模様</bdi>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXpg"><span lang="ja" id="mwXpk">おかしな転生</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXpo"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXps">&nbsp;</span>V. TO Books.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXpw">「年上を正室とした前例がございますれば、問題ないかと」</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%8E%8B%E5%AE%AE%E3%81%AE%E4%BA%8B%E4%BB%B6&amp;rft.btitle=%E3%83%AC%E3%83%BC%E3%82%BA%E3%83%B3%E3%83%91%E3%83%B3%E3%81%AE%E6%81%8B%E6%A8%A1%E6%A7%98&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E3%81%8A%E3%81%8B%E3%81%97%E3%81%AA%E8%BB%A2%E7%94%9F%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pub=TO+Books&amp;rft.date=2016-11-10&amp;rft.aulast=Kory%C5%AB&amp;rft.aufirst=Nozomu&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3383" id="mwXp0"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3383" id="mwXp4"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3383" id="mwXp8"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-516" id="cite_note-516" data-mw-footnote-number="481"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXqA"><a href="#cite_ref-516" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXqE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXqI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-516" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3386" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXqM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:しかしながら、私のような外部の者から見ますれば、この内容と申しますのは、いささか他律的事由を中心とする形式的あるいは手続的な改正が多く、実質的な内容の修正・変更を伴うものではなかったということです。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=6&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=August 2022&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:公害等調整委員会設立 50 周年記念シンポジウム「50 年を迎える公害等調整委員会」（第 1 回基調講演）&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Yoshinobu&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Kitamura&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|総務省公害等調整委員会}}&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:ちょうせい&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=110&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.soumu.go.jp/main_content/000832390.pdf&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFKitamura2022" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3386">Kitamura, Yoshinobu (August 2022). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.soumu.go.jp/main_content/000832390.pdf" class="external text" id="mwXqQ"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwXqU">公害等調整委員会設立 50 周年記念シンポジウム「50 年を迎える公害等調整委員会」（第 1 回基調講演）</bdi></a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwXqY">(PDF)</span>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXqc">ちょうせい</bdi> (in Japanese) (110). <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXqg"><span lang="ja" id="mwXqk">総務省公害等調整委員会</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXqo">: 6.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXqs">しかしながら、私のような外部の者から見ますれば、この内容と申しますのは、いささか他律的事由を中心とする形式的あるいは手続的な改正が多く、実質的な内容の修正・変更を伴うものではなかったということです。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E5%85%AC%E5%AE%B3%E7%AD%89%E8%AA%BF%E6%95%B4%E5%A7%94%E5%93%A1%E4%BC%9A%E8%A8%AD%E7%AB%8B+50+%E5%91%A8%E5%B9%B4%E8%A8%98%E5%BF%B5%E3%82%B7%E3%83%B3%E3%83%9D%E3%82%B8%E3%82%A6%E3%83%A0%E3%80%8C50+%E5%B9%B4%E3%82%92%E8%BF%8E%E3%81%88%E3%82%8B%E5%85%AC%E5%AE%B3%E7%AD%89%E8%AA%BF%E6%95%B4%E5%A7%94%E5%93%A1%E4%BC%9A%E3%80%8D%EF%BC%88%E7%AC%AC+1+%E5%9B%9E%E5%9F%BA%E8%AA%BF%E8%AC%9B%E6%BC%94%EF%BC%89&amp;rft.issue=110&amp;rft.pages=6&amp;rft.date=2022-08&amp;rft.aulast=Kitamura&amp;rft.aufirst=Yoshinobu&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.soumu.go.jp%2Fmain_content%2F000832390.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3386" id="mwXqw"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3386" id="mwXq0"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3386" id="mwXq4"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-517" id="cite_note-517" data-mw-footnote-number="482"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXq8"><a href="#cite_ref-517" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXrA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXrE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-517" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3389" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXrI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:何しろ、修辞学のいわゆる<ruby>転換法<rp>(</rp><rt>メタレプシス</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>というものを用いませば、そうしたことにもなるわけでございますよ。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=100&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第一四章 パニュルジュの見た夢と、当人の解釈&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:第三之書　パンタグリュエル物語&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=3&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Iwanami Shoten&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;series={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|岩波文庫}}&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-title=The Third Book: The Tales of [[Pantagruel]]&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Tiers liure des <span style=font-variant:small-caps>faictz et dictz</span> H''eroïques du noble'' P''antagruel''.&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=François&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Rabelais&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=François Rabelais&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Kazuo&quot;},&quot;16&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Watanabe&quot;},&quot;17&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=20 August 1975&quot;},&quot;18&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;orig-date=18 March 1974&quot;},&quot;19&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;edition=3rd&quot;},&quot;20&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Chiyoda, Tokyo]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="mwXrM" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3389" data-x-id="CITEREFRabelais1975"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/François_Rabelais" title="François Rabelais" id="mwXrQ">Rabelais, François</a> (20 August 1975) [18 March 1974].  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXrU">第一四章 パニュルジュの見た夢と、当人の解釈</bdi>. <i id="mwXrY">Tiers liure des <span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwXrc">faictz et dictz</span> H</i>eroïques du noble<i id="mwXrg"> P</i>antagruel<i id="mwXrk"><span id="mwXro"></span></i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXrs">第三之書　パンタグリュエル物語</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXrw">[</span><i id="mwXr0">The Third Book: The Tales of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantagruel" title="Pantagruel" class="mw-redirect" id="mwXr4">Pantagruel</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXr8">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXsA"><span lang="ja" id="mwXsE">岩波文庫</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXsI"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXsM">&nbsp;</span>3. Translated by Watanabe, Kazuo (3rd<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXsQ">&nbsp;</span>ed.). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiyoda,_Tokyo" title="Chiyoda, Tokyo" id="mwXsU">Chiyoda, Tokyo</a>: Iwanami Shoten. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXsY">&nbsp;</span>100.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXsc">何しろ、修辞学のいわゆる<ruby id="mwXsg">転換法<rp id="mwXsk">(</rp><rt id="mwXso">メタレプシス</rt><rp id="mwXss">)</rp></ruby>というものを用いませば、そうしたことにもなるわけでございますよ。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E4%B8%80%E5%9B%9B%E7%AB%A0+%E3%83%91%E3%83%8B%E3%83%A5%E3%83%AB%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A5%E3%81%AE%E8%A6%8B%E3%81%9F%E5%A4%A2%E3%81%A8%E3%80%81%E5%BD%93%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%AE%E8%A7%A3%E9%87%88&amp;rft.btitle=Tiers+liure+des+%3Cspan+style%3Dfont-variant%3Asmall-caps%3Efaictz+et+dictz%3C%2Fspan%3E+Hero%C3%AFques+du+noble+Pantagruel.+%E7%AC%AC%E4%B8%89%E4%B9%8B%E6%9B%B8%E3%80%80%E3%83%91%E3%83%B3%E3%82%BF%E3%82%B0%E3%83%AA%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A8%E3%83%AB%E7%89%A9%E8%AA%9E&amp;rft.place=Chiyoda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E5%B2%A9%E6%B3%A2%E6%96%87%E5%BA%AB%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=100&amp;rft.edition=3rd&amp;rft.pub=Iwanami+Shoten&amp;rft.date=1975-08-20&amp;rft.aulast=Rabelais&amp;rft.aufirst=Fran%C3%A7ois&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3389" id="mwXsw"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3389" id="mwXs0"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3389" id="mwXs4"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-518" id="cite_note-518" data-mw-footnote-number="483"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXs8"><a href="#cite_ref-518" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXtA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXtE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-518" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3461" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXtI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;journal&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:その結果富士山に行かねば、主任検定員の資格も取らねば鎌田現道岳連会長並びに菅野道岳連指導委員長にお返し出来ないと考えて参加しました。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;page=9&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:氷雪技術に関する指導員の教育と研修　参加者の感想&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Nobuo&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Nakai&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-journal=ja:登山月報&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;number=459&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=15 June 2007&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/11722106/1/1&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Japan Mountaineering Association&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=[[Shibuya]], Tokyo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFNakai2007" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3461">Nakai, Nobuo (15 June 2007). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/11722106/1/1" class="external text" id="mwXtM"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwXtQ">氷雪技術に関する指導員の教育と研修　参加者の感想</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXtU">登山月報</bdi> (in Japanese) (459). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shibuya" title="Shibuya" id="mwXtY">Shibuya</a>, Tokyo: Japan Mountaineering Association: 9.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXtc">その結果富士山に行かねば、主任検定員の資格も取らねば鎌田現道岳連会長並びに菅野道岳連指導委員長にお返し出来ないと考えて参加しました。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=%E6%B0%B7%E9%9B%AA%E6%8A%80%E8%A1%93%E3%81%AB%E9%96%A2%E3%81%99%E3%82%8B%E6%8C%87%E5%B0%8E%E5%93%A1%E3%81%AE%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2%E3%81%A8%E7%A0%94%E4%BF%AE%E3%80%80%E5%8F%82%E5%8A%A0%E8%80%85%E3%81%AE%E6%84%9F%E6%83%B3&amp;rft.issue=459&amp;rft.pages=9&amp;rft.date=2007-06-15&amp;rft.aulast=Nakai&amp;rft.aufirst=Nobuo&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F11722106%2F1%2F1&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3461" id="mwXtg"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3461" id="mwXtk"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3461" id="mwXto"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-519" id="cite_note-519" data-mw-footnote-number="484"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXts"><a href="#cite_ref-519" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXtw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXt0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-519" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3464" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXt4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:くそ婆ァが何をぬかしやがると嘲笑いつつ、いくら偉い者でも飯を食わねば死んでしまうのだというお夏の言葉には妙な含畜があり、若い新吉ではあるが、人間の真理を<ruby>衝<rp>(</rp><rt>つ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby>かれたような気がしたのである。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:第一話 けちな飯&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:居酒屋お夏&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;volume=1&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Satoru&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Okamoto&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=5 June 2014&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Gentosha&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFOkamoto2014" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3464">Okamoto, Satoru (5 June 2014).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXt8">第一話 けちな飯</bdi>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXuA">居酒屋お夏</bdi> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXuE">&nbsp;</span>1. Gentosha.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXuI">くそ婆ァが何をぬかしやがると嘲笑いつつ、いくら偉い者でも飯を食わねば死んでしまうのだというお夏の言葉には妙な含畜があり、若い新吉ではあるが、人間の真理を<ruby id="mwXuM">衝<rp id="mwXuQ">(</rp><rt id="mwXuU">つ</rt><rp id="mwXuY">)</rp></ruby>かれたような気がしたのである。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E4%B8%80%E8%A9%B1+%E3%81%91%E3%81%A1%E3%81%AA%E9%A3%AF&amp;rft.btitle=%E5%B1%85%E9%85%92%E5%B1%8B%E3%81%8A%E5%A4%8F&amp;rft.pub=Gentosha&amp;rft.date=2014-06-05&amp;rft.aulast=Okamoto&amp;rft.aufirst=Satoru&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3464" id="mwXuc"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3464" id="mwXug"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3464" id="mwXuk"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-520" id="cite_note-520" data-mw-footnote-number="485"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXuo"><a href="#cite_ref-520" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXus"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXuw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-520" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3467" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXu0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;lang=ja&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-quote=ja:ハギスとはどこで食べられるものなのだろうか。早速、現地でできた友人らに、片っ端から「ハギスはどこで食べるべきでしょうか？」と聞き、あたりをつけた店に予約を入れる。とにかくやはり、ハギスを食べねば帰国できん。&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-quote=I wondered where I could eat haggis. I immediately asked the friends I made there, one after another, “Where should I get some haggis?” and then made a reservation at the restaurant I managed to find. At any rate, I couldn’t just left if I hadn’t had haggis.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-chapter=ja:スコットランドの食事なら、ソウルフード「ハギス」一択&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-chapter=When It Comes Mealtime in Scotland, Pick the Soul Food Called “Haggis”&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pages=74–75&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Isa&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Tomomi&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;script-title=ja:旅の賢人たちがつくった海外グルメ旅最強ナビ&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;trans-title=The Ultimate Guide to Gourmet Travel Abroad, by Travel Connoiseurs&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=24 December 2020&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;editor={{#invoke:lang|lang|ja|丸山ゴンザレス&amp;世界トラベラー情報研究会}}&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Tatsumi Publishing&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFIsa2020" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" about="#mwt3467">Isa, Tomomi (24 December 2020).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXu4">スコットランドの食事なら、ソウルフード「ハギス」一択</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXu8">[</span>When It Comes Mealtime in Scotland, Pick the Soul Food Called “Haggis”<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXvA">]</span>. In <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwXvE"><span lang="ja" id="mwXvI">丸山ゴンザレス&amp;世界トラベラー情報研究会</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwXvM"> (ed.).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXvQ">旅の賢人たちがつくった海外グルメ旅最強ナビ</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXvU">[</span><i id="mwXvY">The Ultimate Guide to Gourmet Travel Abroad, by Travel Connoiseurs</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXvc">]</span> (in Japanese). Tatsumi Publishing. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXvg">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwXvk">74–</span>75.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXvo">ハギスとはどこで食べられるものなのだろうか。早速、現地でできた友人らに、片っ端から「ハギスはどこで食べるべきでしょうか？」と聞き、あたりをつけた店に予約を入れる。とにかくやはり、ハギスを食べねば帰国できん。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXvs">[</span>I wondered where I could eat haggis. I immediately asked the friends I made there, one after another, “Where should I get some haggis?” and then made a reservation at the restaurant I managed to find. At any rate, I couldn’t just left if I hadn’t had haggis.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXvw">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E3%82%B9%E3%82%B3%E3%83%83%E3%83%88%E3%83%A9%E3%83%B3%E3%83%89%E3%81%AE%E9%A3%9F%E4%BA%8B%E3%81%AA%E3%82%89%E3%80%81%E3%82%BD%E3%82%A6%E3%83%AB%E3%83%95%E3%83%BC%E3%83%89%E3%80%8C%E3%83%8F%E3%82%AE%E3%82%B9%E3%80%8D%E4%B8%80%E6%8A%9E&amp;rft.btitle=%E6%97%85%E3%81%AE%E8%B3%A2%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%9F%E3%81%A1%E3%81%8C%E3%81%A4%E3%81%8F%E3%81%A3%E3%81%9F%E6%B5%B7%E5%A4%96%E3%82%B0%E3%83%AB%E3%83%A1%E6%97%85%E6%9C%80%E5%BC%B7%E3%83%8A%E3%83%93&amp;rft.pages=74-75&amp;rft.pub=Tatsumi+Publishing&amp;rft.date=2020-12-24&amp;rft.aulast=Isa&amp;rft.aufirst=Tomomi&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3467" id="mwXv0"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" about="#mwt3467" id="mwXv4"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" about="#mwt3467" id="mwXv8"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001359-521" id="cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001359-521" data-mw-footnote-number="486"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXwA"><a href="#cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001359_521-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXwE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXwI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001359-521" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwXwM">Akimoto et al. (2001)</a>, p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXwQ">&nbsp;</span>359.<span class="error harv-error" style="display: none; font-size:100%" id="mwXwU"> sfnp error: no target: CITEREFAkimotoAkimotoIshikawaItoi2001 (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Harv_and_Sfn_template_errors" title="Category:Harv and Sfn template errors" id="mwXwY">help</a>)</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Harv_and_Sfn_no-target_errors" id="mwXwc"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004559-522" id="cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004559-522" data-mw-footnote-number="487"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXwg"><a href="#cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMartin2004559_522-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXwk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXwo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMartin2004559-522" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFMartin2004" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwXws">Martin (2004)</a>, p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXww">&nbsp;</span>559.<span class="error harv-error" style="display: none; font-size:100%" id="mwXw0"> sfnp error: no target: CITEREFMartin2004 (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Harv_and_Sfn_template_errors" title="Category:Harv and Sfn template errors" id="mwXw4">help</a>)</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Harv_and_Sfn_no-target_errors" id="mwXw8"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKaiserIchikawaKobayashiYamamoto2013572–573-523" id="cite_note-FOOTNOTEKaiserIchikawaKobayashiYamamoto2013572–573-523" data-mw-footnote-number="488"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXxA"><a href="#cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKaiserIchikawaKobayashiYamamoto2013572–573_523-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXxE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXxI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKaiserIchikawaKobayashiYamamoto2013572–573-523" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFKaiserIchikawaKobayashiYamamoto2013" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwXxM">Kaiser et al. (2013)</a>, p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXxQ">&nbsp;</span>572–573.<span class="error harv-error" style="display: none; font-size:100%" id="mwXxU"> sfnp error: no target: CITEREFKaiserIchikawaKobayashiYamamoto2013 (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Harv_and_Sfn_template_errors" title="Category:Harv and Sfn template errors" id="mwXxY">help</a>)</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Harv_and_Sfn_no-target_errors" id="mwXxc"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-528" id="cite_note-528" data-mw-footnote-number="489"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXxg"><a href="#cite_ref-528" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXxk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXxo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-528" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3518" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwXxs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFSmith2013" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._E._Smith" title="E. E. Smith" id="mwXxw">Smith, Edward Elmer</a> (29 March 2013). "Chapter 12: Flying Visits—Via Projection" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXx0">一二　<ruby id="mwXx4">立体投映<rp id="mwXx8">(</rp><rt id="mwXyA">プロジェクション</rt><rp id="mwXyE">)</rp></ruby>でこんにちは！</bdi>. <i id="mwXyI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skylark_Three" title="Skylark Three" id="mwXyM">Skylark Three</a></i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXyQ">スカイラーク３</bdi> (in Japanese). Translated by Kawaguchi, Shōkichi. Gutenber21. <q id="mwXyU"><span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwXyY"></span>"That is, of course, true, and is a point I was careless enough to overlook." Rovol thought for a moment, then got up, crossed the room to his control desk, and continued, "We shall dismantle the machine and rebuild it at once."<br id="mwXyc">"Oh, no—too much work!" protested Seaton. "You've got it about done, haven't you?"<br id="mwXyg">"It is hardly started. Two hundred thousand bands of force must be linked to it, each in its proper place, and it is necessary that you should understand thoroughly every detail of this entire projector."<span class="cs1-kern-right" id="mwXyk"></span></q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwXyo">「もちろん――それは<ruby id="mwXys">真実<rp id="mwXyw">(</rp><rt id="mwXy0">ほんと</rt><rp id="mwXy4">)</rp></ruby>です。わたし自身もうっかりその点を見逃していた」ロヴォレはちょっと考えこんだ。それから座席から立ち、部屋を横切って制御デスクのほうへ行き、「機械をとりこわし、それと平行してもう一度作りなおさなければならん」<br id="mwXy8">「そんな、だめです――大変な仕事になりますよ。もうほとんど終りかけているんじゃないですか、そうでしょう？」<br id="mwXzA">「いや、まだ手をつけていないも同然です。これに二十万個からの超エネルギー周波帯を連絡しなければならん。一個一個が正しい場所に接続されなければならん。しかもあなたに、この投映器の細々したところまで、徹底的に理解してもらわなくっちゃ意味がない」</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Chapter+12%3A+Flying+Visits%E2%80%94Via+Projection+%E4%B8%80%E4%BA%8C%E3%80%80%3Cruby%3E%E7%AB%8B%E4%BD%93%E6%8A%95%E6%98%A0%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%83%97%E3%83%AD%E3%82%B8%E3%82%A7%E3%82%AF%E3%82%B7%E3%83%A7%E3%83%B3%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%81%A7%E3%81%93%E3%82%93%E3%81%AB%E3%81%A1%E3%81%AF%EF%BC%81&amp;rft.btitle=Skylark+Three+%E3%82%B9%E3%82%AB%E3%82%A4%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%82%AF%EF%BC%93&amp;rft.pub=Gutenber21&amp;rft.date=2013-03-29&amp;rft.aulast=Smith&amp;rft.aufirst=Edward+Elmer&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwXzE"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwXzI"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwXzM"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-529" id="cite_note-529" data-mw-footnote-number="490"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwXzQ"><a href="#cite_ref-529" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwXzU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwXzY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-529" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3522" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwXzc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;book&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Wisdom and Destiny&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;authorlink=Maurice Maeterlinck&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Maurice Polydore Marie Bernard&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Maeterlinck&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-link=Alfred Sutro&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-first=Alfred&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;translator-last=Sutro&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;location=New York&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=Dodd, Mead and Company&quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=Till reality confront us, it is well, it may be, to cherish ideals that we hold to surpass it in beauty ; but once face to face with reality, then must the ideal flame that has fed on our noblest desires be content to throw faithful light on the less fragile, less tender beauty of the mighty mass that crushes these desires.&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;chapter=§ 4.&quot;},&quot;13&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;year=1989&quot;},&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;p=18&quot;},&quot;15&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://archive.org/details/wisdomdestiny00maet_0/page/18/mode/2up&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFMaeterlinck1989" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt3522"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurice_Maeterlinck" title="Maurice Maeterlinck" id="mwXzg">Maeterlinck, Maurice Polydore Marie Bernard</a> (1989). "§ 4.". <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://archive.org/details/wisdomdestiny00maet_0/page/18/mode/2up" class="external text" id="mwXzk"><i id="mwXzo">Wisdom and Destiny</i></a>. Translated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfred_Sutro" title="Alfred Sutro" id="mwXzs">Sutro, Alfred</a>. New York: Dodd, Mead and Company. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwXzw">&nbsp;</span>18. <q id="mwXz0">Till reality confront us, it is well, it may be, to cherish ideals that we hold to surpass it in beauty<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwXz4">&nbsp;</span>; but once face to face with reality, then must the ideal flame that has fed on our noblest desires be content to throw faithful light on the less fragile, less tender beauty of the mighty mass that crushes these desires.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%C2%A7+4.&amp;rft.btitle=Wisdom+and+Destiny&amp;rft.place=New+York&amp;rft.pages=18&amp;rft.pub=Dodd%2C+Mead+and+Company&amp;rft.date=1989&amp;rft.aulast=Maeterlinck&amp;rft.aufirst=Maurice+Polydore+Marie+Bernard&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.org%2Fdetails%2Fwisdomdestiny00maet_0%2Fpage%2F18%2Fmode%2F2up&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3522" id="mwXz8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-otani-1913-530" id="cite_note-otani-1913-530" data-mw-footnote-number="491"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwX0A"><a href="#cite_ref-otani-1913_530-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwX0E"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwX0I">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-otani-1913-530" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3527" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwX0M" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFMaeterlinck1913" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurice_Maeterlinck" title="Maurice Maeterlinck" id="mwX0Q">Maeterlinck, Maurice Polydore Marie Bernard</a> (30 December 1913). "IV" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX0U">四</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX0Y">[</span>§ 4.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX0c">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/951871/1/17" class="external text" id="mwX0g"><i id="mwX0k">La sagesse et la destinée</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX0o">智慧と運命</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX0s">[</span><i id="mwX0w">Wisdom and Destiny</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX00">]</span> (in Japanese). Translated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfred_Sutro" title="Alfred Sutro" id="mwX04">Sutro, Alfred</a>; Ōtani, Jōseki. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ushigome" title="Ushigome" id="mwX08">Ushigome</a>, Tokyo: Nanbokusha. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX1A">&nbsp;</span>27. <q id="mwX1E">En attendant que la réalité se manifeste, il est peut-être salutaire d'entretenir un idéal qu'on s'imagine plus beau que la réalité; mais après que celle-ci s'est enfin révélée, il devient nécessaire que la flamme idéale que nous avons nourrie de nos meilleurs désirs, ne serve plus qu'à éclairer loyalement les beautés moins fragiles et moins complaisantes de la masse imposante qui écrase ces désirs.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX1I">現實が面と向つて我々に對する迄は、美の點で之に優ると思ふ理想を抱くのが善くはなからうか。が一旦現實と面と向ひ合へば、我々の最高の願望を油として燃えて居た理想の炎は、そんな願望を紛碎する偉大な現實の、自己よりも脆からぬ、自己よりも弱からぬその美に對して、自己の有の儘の光を投ずるに滿足しなきやならぬ。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX1M">[</span>Till reality confront us, it is well, it may be, to cherish ideals that we hold to surpass it in beauty<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwX1Q">&nbsp;</span>; but once face to face with reality, then must the ideal flame that has fed on our noblest desires be content to throw faithful light on the less fragile, less tender beauty of the mighty mass that crushes these desires.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX1U">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=IV+%E5%9B%9B&amp;rft.btitle=La+sagesse+et+la+destin%C3%A9e+%E6%99%BA%E6%85%A7%E3%81%A8%E9%81%8B%E5%91%BD&amp;rft.place=Ushigome%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=27&amp;rft.pub=Nanbokusha&amp;rft.date=1913-12-30&amp;rft.aulast=Maeterlinck&amp;rft.aufirst=Maurice+Polydore+Marie+Bernard&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F951871%2F1%2F17&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwX1Y"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwX1c"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwX1g"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-531" id="cite_note-531" data-mw-footnote-number="492"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwX1k"><a href="#cite_ref-531" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwX1o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwX1s">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-531" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3533" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwX1w" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFAlain1960" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alain_(philosopher)" title="Alain (philosopher)" id="mwX10">Alain</a> (20 April 1960). "VIII. La métaphore est proprement religieuse" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX14">第八章　<ruby id="mwX18">暗喩表現<rp id="mwX2A">(</rp><rt id="mwX2E">メタフオール</rt><rp id="mwX2I">)</rp></ruby>は本来宗教的なものである</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX2M">[</span>Chapter VIII. Metaphor is properly religious<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX2Q">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1336772/1/19" class="external text" id="mwX2U"><i id="mwX2Y">Propos de littérature</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX2c">文学論</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX2g">[</span><i id="mwX2k">On Literature</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX2o">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwX2s"><span lang="ja" id="mwX2w">新潮文庫</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwX20"> (in Japanese). Translated by Katayama, Toshihiko. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinjuku" title="Shinjuku" id="mwX24">Shinjuku</a>, Tokyo: Shinchosha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX28">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwX3A">34–</span>35. <q id="mwX3E">La métaphore est proprement religieuse. Elle soutient nos pensées et nos sentiments par une description ample ou brève, mais qui veut être vraie. Le lac de Lamartine est un vrai lac<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwX3I">&nbsp;</span>; observez comme les moindres traits font apparaître la loi des eaux et des rochers. Dans l'éclair lyrique les choses de nature apparaissent solides et suffisantes, nullement transformées à l'image de nos instables pensées. Et il faut distinguer le lyrique, qui s'appuie sur l'ordre des choses, de tous les genres de fantastique.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX3M"><ruby id="mwX3Q">暗喩表現<rp id="mwX3U">(</rp><rt id="mwX3Y">メタフオール</rt><rp id="mwX3c">)</rp></ruby>は本来宗教的なものである。それは、或いは詳しい、或いは簡潔な叙述――しかしいずれにせよ真実の叙述たることを志すところの表現によって、われわれ人間の思想と感情とに支柱を与える。ラマルチーヌの『みずうみ』は、一つの真実なみずうみである。どんなに最微の表現の筆致が、水や巖の法則を顕現させているかに注目したまえ。抒情の閃光に照らされて、自然のさまざまの存在物が確固として且つ十全にあらわされている。――少しもわれわれ人間のはかない思想の形象に変形されることなしに。さてまた、抒情的なもの――事物の秩序に依拠する抒情的なものと、あらゆる種類の幻想的なものとを区別せねばならない。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX3g">[</span>Metaphor is properly religious. It sustains our thoughts and our feelings by an ample or brief description—but one which wants to be true. <i id="mwX3k"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Lac_(poem)" title="Le Lac (poem)" id="mwX3o">The Lake</a></i> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamartine" title="Lamartine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwX3s">Lamartine</a> is a true lake. Observe how the slightest traits make appear the law of waters and rocks. In the lyric flash the things of nature appear solid and sufficient—not at all transformed into the image of our unstable thoughts. And one must distinguish lyricism—which relies on the order of things—from all genres of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fantastique" title="Fantastique" id="mwX3w">fantastique</a>.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX30">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=VIII.+La+m%C3%A9taphore+est+proprement+religieuse+%E7%AC%AC%E5%85%AB%E7%AB%A0%E3%80%80%3Cruby%3E%E6%9A%97%E5%96%A9%E8%A1%A8%E7%8F%BE%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%83%A1%E3%82%BF%E3%83%95%E3%82%AA%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AB%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%81%AF%E6%9C%AC%E6%9D%A5%E5%AE%97%E6%95%99%E7%9A%84%E3%81%AA%E3%82%82%E3%81%AE%E3%81%A7%E3%81%82%E3%82%8B&amp;rft.btitle=Propos+de+litt%C3%A9rature+%E6%96%87%E5%AD%A6%E8%AB%96&amp;rft.place=Shinjuku%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E6%96%B0%E6%BD%AE%E6%96%87%E5%BA%AB%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=34-35&amp;rft.pub=Shinchosha&amp;rft.date=1960-04-20&amp;rft.au=Alain&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1336772%2F1%2F19&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwX34"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwX38"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwX4A"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-532" id="cite_note-532" data-mw-footnote-number="493"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwX4E"><a href="#cite_ref-532" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwX4I"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwX4M">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-532" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3539" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwX4Q" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFRasmusson2011" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Rasmusson, Jonathan (16 July 2011). "Master Sensei and the aspiring warrior" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX4U">マスター・センセイと熱心な弟子</bdi>. In Pfalzer, Susannah Davidson; Nishimura, Naoto; Kakutani, Shintarō (eds.). <i id="mwX4Y">The Agile Samurai: How Agile Masters Deliver Great Software</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX4c">アジャイルサムライ――達人開発者への道</bdi> (in Japanese). Translated by Kondō, Shūhei; Tsunokake, Takumi. Ohmsha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX4g">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwX4k">271–</span>272. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwX4o">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX4s">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-4-274-06856-0" title="Special:BookSources/978-4-274-06856-0" id="mwX4w"><bdi id="mwX40">978-4-274-06856-0</bdi></a>. <q id="mwX44"><i id="mwX48"><b id="mwX5A">STUDENT:</b> So, TDD is really about design and not testing?<br id="mwX5E"><b id="mwX5I">MASTER:</b>  That would be an oversimplification. Testing is a core part of TDD, because we use tests to prove that the code we produce works. But we cannot complete the tests without first doing some design and showing our intent through the code.<br id="mwX5M"><b id="mwX5Q">STUDENT:</b> Thank you, Master. I must think on this more.</i></q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX5U">弟子　　　では、ＴＤＤは本当は設計手法であって、テスト手法ではないのですか？<br id="mwX5Y">センセイ　それは言い過ぎかもしれん。テストはＴＤＤの核心だ。我われはテストすることを通じて、プロダクトコードがきちんと動いていることを確かめているのだからな。だが、そのテストを完了させるためには、プログラムを設計せねばならんだろうし、その設計の意図をコードとして示さねばならんはずだ。<br id="mwX5c">弟子　　　ありがとうございます、マスター。自分でもよく考えてみます。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Master+Sensei+and+the+aspiring+warrior+%E3%83%9E%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BF%E3%83%BC%E3%83%BB%E3%82%BB%E3%83%B3%E3%82%BB%E3%82%A4%E3%81%A8%E7%86%B1%E5%BF%83%E3%81%AA%E5%BC%9F%E5%AD%90&amp;rft.btitle=The+Agile+Samurai%3A+How+Agile+Masters+Deliver+Great+Software+%E3%82%A2%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A3%E3%82%A4%E3%83%AB%E3%82%B5%E3%83%A0%E3%83%A9%E3%82%A4%E2%80%95%E2%80%95%E9%81%94%E4%BA%BA%E9%96%8B%E7%99%BA%E8%80%85%E3%81%B8%E3%81%AE%E9%81%93&amp;rft.pages=271-272&amp;rft.pub=Ohmsha&amp;rft.date=2011-07-16&amp;rft.isbn=978-4-274-06856-0&amp;rft.aulast=Rasmusson&amp;rft.aufirst=Jonathan&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwX5g"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwX5k"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwX5o"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-kikuchi-1939-535" id="cite_note-kikuchi-1939-535" data-mw-footnote-number="494"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwX5s"><a href="#cite_ref-kikuchi-1939_535-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwX5w"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwX50">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-kikuchi-1939-535" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3552" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwX54" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFMalot1939" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hector_Malot" title="Hector Malot" id="mwX58">Malot, Hector-Henri</a> (11 April 1939). "Mes débuts" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX6A"><ruby id="mwX6E">初<rp id="mwX6I">(</rp><rt id="mwX6M">はつ</rt><rp id="mwX6Q">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX6U">御<rp id="mwX6Y">(</rp><rt id="mwX6c">お</rt><rp id="mwX6g">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX6k">目<rp id="mwX6o">(</rp><rt id="mwX6s">め</rt><rp id="mwX6w">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX60">見<rp id="mwX64">(</rp><rt id="mwX68">みえ</rt><rp id="mwX7A">)</rp></ruby></bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX7E">[</span>Débuts<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX7I">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1037600/1/36" class="external text" id="mwX7M"><i id="mwX7Q">Sans famille</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX7U">家なき兒</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX7Y">[</span><i id="mwX7c"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sans_famille" title="Sans famille" class="mw-redirect" id="mwX7g">A Boy without Home</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX7k">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwX7o"><span lang="ja" id="mwX7s">世界大衆文學名作選集</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwX7w"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX70">&nbsp;</span>2. Translated by Kikuchi, Yūhō. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiba,_Tokyo" title="Shiba, Tokyo" id="mwX74">Shiba, Tokyo</a>: Kaizōsha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwX78">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwX8A">64–</span>65. <q id="mwX8E">«<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwX8I">&nbsp;</span>Que sommes-nous? Des artistes, n'est-ce pas? des comédiens qui par leur seul aspect doivent provoquer la curiosité. Crois-tu que, si nous allions tantôt sur la place publique habillés comme des bourgeois ou des paysans, nous forcerions les gens à nous regarder et à s'arrêter autour de nous? Non, n'est-ce pas? Apprends donc que dans la vie le paraître est quelquefois indispensable; cela est fâcheux, mais nous n'y pouvons rien.<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwX8M">&nbsp;</span>»</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwX8Q">「お<ruby id="mwX8U">前<rp id="mwX8Y">(</rp><rt id="mwX8c">まへ</rt><rp id="mwX8g">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwX8k">乃公<rp id="mwX8o">(</rp><rt id="mwX8s">わし</rt><rp id="mwX8w">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX80">共<rp id="mwX84">(</rp><rt id="mwX88">ども</rt><rp id="mwX9A">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwX9E">何<rp id="mwX9I">(</rp><rt id="mwX9M">なん</rt><rp id="mwX9Q">)</rp></ruby>ぢやと<ruby id="mwX9U">思<rp id="mwX9Y">(</rp><rt id="mwX9c">おも</rt><rp id="mwX9g">)</rp></ruby>ふ。<ruby id="mwX9k">藝<rp id="mwX9o">(</rp><rt id="mwX9s">げい</rt><rp id="mwX9w">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX90">人<rp id="mwX94">(</rp><rt id="mwX98">にん</rt><rp id="mwX-A">)</rp></ruby>ぢや、なりやア<ruby id="mwX-E">一<rp id="mwX-I">(</rp><rt id="mwX-M">ひと</rt><rp id="mwX-Q">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX-U">目<rp id="mwX-Y">(</rp><rt id="mwX-c">め</rt><rp id="mwX-g">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwX-k">惹<rp id="mwX-o">(</rp><rt id="mwX-s">ひ</rt><rp id="mwX-w">)</rp></ruby>く<ruby id="mwX-0">眼<rp id="mwX-4">(</rp><rt id="mwX-8">み</rt><rp id="mwX_A">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX_E">裝<rp id="mwX_I">(</rp><rt id="mwX_M">なり</rt><rp id="mwX_Q">)</rp></ruby>をせにやアならん。<ruby id="mwX_U">喃<rp id="mwX_Y">(</rp><rt id="mwX_c">なう</rt><rp id="mwX_g">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwX_k">世<rp id="mwX_o">(</rp><rt id="mwX_s">せ</rt><rp id="mwX_w">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwX_0">間<rp id="mwX_4">(</rp><rt id="mwX_8">けん</rt><rp id="mwYAA">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYAE">竝<rp id="mwYAI">(</rp><rt id="mwYAM">なみ</rt><rp id="mwYAQ">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYAU">姿<rp id="mwYAY">(</rp><rt id="mwYAc">すがた</rt><rp id="mwYAg">)</rp></ruby>や<ruby id="mwYAk">百<rp id="mwYAo">(</rp><rt id="mwYAs">ひやく</rt><rp id="mwYAw">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYA0">姓<rp id="mwYA4">(</rp><rt id="mwYA8">しやう</rt><rp id="mwYBA">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYBE">風<rp id="mwYBI">(</rp><rt id="mwYBM">ふう</rt><rp id="mwYBQ">)</rp></ruby>をして、<ruby id="mwYBU">公<rp id="mwYBY">(</rp><rt id="mwYBc">こう</rt><rp id="mwYBg">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYBk">園<rp id="mwYBo">(</rp><rt id="mwYBs">ゑん</rt><rp id="mwYBw">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYB0">地<rp id="mwYB4">(</rp><rt id="mwYB8">ち</rt><rp id="mwYCA">)</rp></ruby>へ<ruby id="mwYCE">出<rp id="mwYCI">(</rp><rt id="mwYCM">で</rt><rp id="mwYCQ">)</rp></ruby>かけたところで、<ruby id="mwYCU">人<rp id="mwYCY">(</rp><rt id="mwYCc">ひと</rt><rp id="mwYCg">)</rp></ruby>ツ<ruby id="mwYCk">子<rp id="mwYCo">(</rp><rt id="mwYCs">こ</rt><rp id="mwYCw">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYC0">一<rp id="mwYC4">(</rp><rt id="mwYC8">ひと</rt><rp id="mwYDA">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYDE">人<rp id="mwYDI">(</rp><rt id="mwYDM">り</rt><rp id="mwYDQ">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYDU">乃公<rp id="mwYDY">(</rp><rt id="mwYDc">わし</rt><rp id="mwYDg">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYDk">等<rp id="mwYDo">(</rp><rt id="mwYDs">ら</rt><rp id="mwYDw">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYD0">周圍<rp id="mwYD4">(</rp><rt id="mwYD8">ぐるり</rt><rp id="mwYEA">)</rp></ruby>へ<ruby id="mwYEE">集<rp id="mwYEI">(</rp><rt id="mwYEM">たか</rt><rp id="mwYEQ">)</rp></ruby>つては<ruby id="mwYEU">來<rp id="mwYEY">(</rp><rt id="mwYEc">こ</rt><rp id="mwYEg">)</rp></ruby>まいがの。そこぢやて。<ruby id="mwYEk">世<rp id="mwYEo">(</rp><rt id="mwYEs">よ</rt><rp id="mwYEw">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYE0">渡<rp id="mwYE4">(</rp><rt id="mwYE8">わた</rt><rp id="mwYFA">)</rp></ruby>りをして<ruby id="mwYFE">行<rp id="mwYFI">(</rp><rt id="mwYFM">ゆ</rt><rp id="mwYFQ">)</rp></ruby>かうと<ruby id="mwYFU">思<rp id="mwYFY">(</rp><rt id="mwYFc">おも</rt><rp id="mwYFg">)</rp></ruby>へば<ruby id="mwYFk">異<rp id="mwYFo">(</rp><rt id="mwYFs">かは</rt><rp id="mwYFw">)</rp></ruby>つた<ruby id="mwYF0">姿<rp id="mwYF4">(</rp><rt id="mwYF8">なり</rt><rp id="mwYGA">)</rp></ruby>も<ruby id="mwYGE">必<rp id="mwYGI">(</rp><rt id="mwYGM">ひつ</rt><rp id="mwYGQ">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYGU">要<rp id="mwYGY">(</rp><rt id="mwYGc">えう</rt><rp id="mwYGg">)</rp></ruby>ぢや。<ruby id="mwYGk">何<rp id="mwYGo">(</rp><rt id="mwYGs">なに</rt><rp id="mwYGw">)</rp></ruby>もすき<ruby id="mwYG0">好<rp id="mwYG4">(</rp><rt id="mwYG8">この</rt><rp id="mwYHA">)</rp></ruby>んでするのではない。<ruby id="mwYHE">合<rp id="mwYHI">(</rp><rt id="mwYHM">が</rt><rp id="mwYHQ">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYHU">點<rp id="mwYHY">(</rp><rt id="mwYHc">てん</rt><rp id="mwYHg">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwYHk">行<rp id="mwYHo">(</rp><rt id="mwYHs">い</rt><rp id="mwYHw">)</rp></ruby>たかの。」</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYH0">[</span>“What do you think we are? We’re artists, so we have to put on eye-catching outfits. Right, if we went out to the public square, looking ordinary or like peasants, would a single soul come and crowd around us? There it is. If we wish to make our way in life, distinct appearance, too, is indispensable. We don’t do it just for the fun of it. Does that make sense, now?”<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYH4">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Mes+d%C3%A9buts+%3Cruby%3E%E5%88%9D%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%AF%E3%81%A4%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E5%BE%A1%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%8A%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E7%9B%AE%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%82%81%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E8%A6%8B%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%BF%E3%81%88%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E&amp;rft.btitle=Sans+famille+%E5%AE%B6%E3%81%AA%E3%81%8D%E5%85%92&amp;rft.place=Shiba%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E4%B8%96%E7%95%8C%E5%A4%A7%E8%A1%86%E6%96%87%E5%AD%B8%E5%90%8D%E4%BD%9C%E9%81%B8%E9%9B%86%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=64-65&amp;rft.pub=Kaiz%C5%8Dsha&amp;rft.date=1939-04-11&amp;rft.aulast=Malot&amp;rft.aufirst=Hector-Henri&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1037600%2F1%2F36&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYH8"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYIA"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYIE"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-536" id="cite_note-536" data-mw-footnote-number="495"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYII"><a href="#cite_ref-536" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYIM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYIQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-536" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3558" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYIU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFHemingway2014" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernest_Hemingway" title="Ernest Hemingway" id="mwYIY">Hemingway, Ernest Miller</a> (29 August 2014). "Hunger Was Good Discipline" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYIc">飢えは良い修行だった</bdi>. <i id="mwYIg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Moveable_Feast" title="A Moveable Feast" id="mwYIk">A Moveable Feast</a>: Sketches of the Author's Life in Paris in the Twenties</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYIo">移動祝祭日　回想のパリ</bdi> (in Japanese). Translated by Fukuda, Rikutarō. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Setagaya" title="Setagaya" id="mwYIs">Setagaya</a>, Tokyo: Gutenberg21. <q id="mwYIw">I knew it was probably a good thing that it was lost, but I knew too that I must write a novel. I would put it off though until I could not help doing it. I was damned if I would write one because it was what I should do if we were to eat regularly. When I had to write it, then it would be the only thing to do and there would be no choice.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYI0">それが失われたことは、たぶん良いことだとは、わかっていたが、また小説を書かねばならぬということもわかっていた。けれど、そうしなければいられなくなるまで、書くのをのばそう。私たちが規則正しく食事しようとするなら、私は小説を書かねばならない――そんな理由で、小説を書くなんてまっぴらだ。私が書かねばならぬときは、それしかできなくて、他に選択の余地のないときなのだ。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Hunger+Was+Good+Discipline+%E9%A3%A2%E3%81%88%E3%81%AF%E8%89%AF%E3%81%84%E4%BF%AE%E8%A1%8C%E3%81%A0%E3%81%A3%E3%81%9F&amp;rft.btitle=A+Moveable+Feast%3A+Sketches+of+the+Author%27s+Life+in+Paris+in+the+Twenties+%E7%A7%BB%E5%8B%95%E7%A5%9D%E7%A5%AD%E6%97%A5%E3%80%80%E5%9B%9E%E6%83%B3%E3%81%AE%E3%83%91%E3%83%AA&amp;rft.place=Setagaya%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pub=Gutenberg21&amp;rft.date=2014-08-29&amp;rft.aulast=Hemingway&amp;rft.aufirst=Ernest+Miller&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYI4"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYI8"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYJA"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-537" id="cite_note-537" data-mw-footnote-number="496"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYJE"><a href="#cite_ref-537" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYJI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYJM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-537" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3564" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYJQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFHesse2015" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann_Hesse" title="Hermann Hesse" id="mwYJU">Hesse, Hermann Karl</a> (22 May 2015). "Am Flusse" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYJY">川のほとりで</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYJc">[</span>By the River<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYJg">]</span>. <i id="mwYJk">Siddhartha. Eine indische Dichtung</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYJo">シッダールタ</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYJs">[</span><i id="mwYJw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siddhartha_(novel)" title="Siddhartha (novel)" id="mwYJ0">Siddhartha</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYJ4">]</span> (in Japanese). Translated by Akiyama, Hideo. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Setagaya" title="Setagaya" id="mwYJ8">Setagaya</a>, Tokyo: Gutenberg21. <q id="mwYKA">Darum hatte er in die Welt gehen müssen, sich an Lust und Macht, an Weib und Geld verlieren müssen, hatte ein Händler, ein Würfelspieler, Trinker und Habgieriger werden müssen, bis der Priester und Samana in ihm tot war. Darum hatte er weiter diese häßlichen Jahre ertragen müssen, den Ekel ertragen, die Lehre, die Sinnlosigkeit eines öden und verlorenen Lebens, bis zum Ende, bis zur bittern Verzweiflung, bis auch der Lüstling Siddhartha, der Habgierige Siddhartha sterben konnte.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYKE">だからこそ、彼は俗世へ出て行かねばならなかったのだ。そして彼の心に巣くっている司祭と沙門が死んでしまうまで、享楽と権勢、女と金のために自分の本筋を見失い、商人となり賭博者となり、酒飲みとなり欲ばりとならねばならなかったのだ。だからこそ、彼はなおもこの醜悪な年月に耐え、嘔吐に耐え、荒涼とした堕落した生活の空虚と無意義に耐えねばならなかったのだ。どたん場に行きつくまで、にがい絶望に行きつくまで、遊蕩児シッダールタ、欲ばりシッダールタが死んでしまうまで。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYKI">[</span>Therefore, he had to go out into the world, and until the priest and samana dwelling within his heart finally died, he had to lose himself to lust and power, to women and money, and become a merchant, a gambler, a drinker and a greedy man. Therefore, he still had to bear these ugly years, bear the disgust, bear the emptiness and meaninglessness of a drearily forlorn life, to the last ditch, to bitter despair, until the lustful Siddhartha, the greedy Siddhartha finally died.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYKM">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Am+Flusse+%E5%B7%9D%E3%81%AE%E3%81%BB%E3%81%A8%E3%82%8A%E3%81%A7&amp;rft.btitle=Siddhartha.+Eine+indische+Dichtung+%E3%82%B7%E3%83%83%E3%83%80%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AB%E3%82%BF&amp;rft.place=Setagaya%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pub=Gutenberg21&amp;rft.date=2015-05-22&amp;rft.aulast=Hesse&amp;rft.aufirst=Hermann+Karl&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYKQ"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYKU"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYKY"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-539" id="cite_note-539" data-mw-footnote-number="497"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYKc"><a href="#cite_ref-539" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYKg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYKk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-539" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3573" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYKo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFMaugham1966" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W._Somerset_Maugham" title="W. Somerset Maugham" id="mwYKs">Maugham, William Somerset</a> (20 March 1966) [5 July 1956]. "The Door of Opportunity" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYKw">機械の扉</bdi>. <i id="mwYK0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Vessel_of_Wrath" title="The Vessel of Wrath" id="mwYK4">The Vessel of Wrath</a></i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYK8">怒りの器</bdi>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwYLA"><span lang="ja" id="mwYLE">Ｗ・サマセット・モーム全集</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwYLI"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYLM">&nbsp;</span>18. Translated by Masuno, Masae (7th<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYLQ">&nbsp;</span>ed.). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinjuku" title="Shinjuku" id="mwYLU">Shinjuku</a>, Tokyo: Shinchosha.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=The+Door+of+Opportunity+%E6%A9%9F%E6%A2%B0%E3%81%AE%E6%89%89&amp;rft.btitle=The+Vessel+of+Wrath+%E6%80%92%E3%82%8A%E3%81%AE%E5%99%A8&amp;rft.place=Shinjuku%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%EF%BC%B7%E3%83%BB%E3%82%B5%E3%83%9E%E3%82%BB%E3%83%83%E3%83%88%E3%83%BB%E3%83%A2%E3%83%BC%E3%83%A0%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.edition=7th&amp;rft.pub=Shinchosha&amp;rft.date=1966-03-20&amp;rft.aulast=Maugham&amp;rft.aufirst=William+Somerset&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYLY"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYLc"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYLg"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-nobori-1948-541" id="cite_note-nobori-1948-541" data-mw-footnote-number="498"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYLk"><a href="#cite_ref-nobori-1948_541-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYLo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYLs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-nobori-1948-541" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3582" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYLw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFTolstoy1948" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_Tolstoy" title="Leo Tolstoy" id="mwYL0">Tolstoy, Leo</a> (1 July 1948). "Власть тьмы, или «Коготок увяз, всей птичке пропасть». Драма в пяти действиях" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYL4">闇の力（五幕）　<small id="mwYL8">別名（爪が一本罠にかかつたら、その小鳥はもうおしまひだ。）</small></bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYMA">[</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Power_of_Darkness" title="The Power of Darkness" id="mwYME">The Power of Darkness</a> (five acts) <small id="mwYMI">Or (If a Claw Is Caught, the Bird Is Lost.)</small><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYMM">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1132851/1/32" class="external text" id="mwYMQ"><i id="mwYMU">Власть тьмы. Живой труп</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYMY">闇の力・生ける屍</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYMc">[</span><i id="mwYMg">The Power of Darkness. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Living_Corpse" title="The Living Corpse" id="mwYMk">The Living Corpse</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYMo">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwYMs"><span lang="ja" id="mwYMw">改造選書</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwYM0"> (in Japanese). Translated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shomu_Nobori" title="Shomu Nobori" id="mwYM4">Nobori, Shomu</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chūō,_Tokyo" title="Chūō, Tokyo" id="mwYM8">Chūō, Tokyo</a>: Kaizōsha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYNA">&nbsp;</span>58, 62, 80, 91, 148. <q id="mwYNE">Матрена (садится). И то уморилась, миленькие; А что соборовать — это беспременно надо. Люди говорят — тоже душе на пользу.<br id="mwYNI">[…]<br id="mwYNM">Анисья. Уже и сама не знаю. Измучал он меня.<br id="mwYNQ">[…]<br id="mwYNU">Анисья. Что ж, я нагрешила, а он да что с деньгами…<br id="mwYNY">[…]<br id="mwYNc">Митрич (слезает). И не видал, как заснул. О господи, Микола-угодник! Здорово, дядя Аким.<br id="mwYNg">[…]<br id="mwYNk">Анютка. Да хоть бы и я померла. (Хнычет.)<br id="mwYNo">Митрич. Помрешь, из счета вон.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYNs">マトリョーナ　<small id="mwYNw">（腰を下ろす）</small>本當に草臥れちもうただよ。ところで聖油禮は、どうあつても受けにやなるめえ。皆の話によれあ――魂がしあはせになると言ふだからね。<br id="mwYN0">[…]<br id="mwYN4">アニーシャ　わしあもう自分でも分んなくなつちもうただ。あの<ruby id="mwYN8">爺<rp id="mwYOA">(</rp><rt id="mwYOE">おやぢ</rt><rp id="mwYOI">)</rp></ruby>にやさんざ苦しめられただ。<br id="mwYOM">[…]<br id="mwYOQ">アニーシャ　ああこれでわしァ罪深けえことをやつちもうただ。それだのに、あの人ァ金もつて行つちまつて、どうするだ。<br id="mwYOU">[…]<br id="mwYOY">ミートリッチ<small id="mwYOc">（下りる）</small>何時寢込んぢまうたか分んねえだ。おお神樣、お慈悲深けえミコラ樣！　今日は、アキーム叔父さん。<br id="mwYOg">[…]<br id="mwYOk">アニュートカ　わしも死んでしまへたらなあ。<small id="mwYOo">（泣く）</small><br id="mwYOs">ミートリッチ　死んぢまうたら――此の世から除けもんになるだけだ！</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYOw">[</span><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYO0">Matryona</span>. <small id="mwYO4">(sits down)</small> I’m really exhausted. But still, I can’t do without Holy Unction. Everybody says it’s good for the soul.<br id="mwYO8">[…]<br id="mwYPA"><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYPE">Anisya</span>. I don’t even know anymore. I’m awfully worn out because of him.<br id="mwYPI">[…]<br id="mwYPM"><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYPQ">Anisya</span>. Oh, I’ve done a sinful thing now. And yet, he’s gone with the money, what do I do?<br id="mwYPU">[…]<br id="mwYPY"><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYPc">Mitritch</span>. <small id="mwYPg">(gets down)</small> I didn’t notice when I fell asleep. Oh my God, oh merciful Nicholas! Good day, Uncle Akim.<br id="mwYPk">[…]<br id="mwYPo"><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYPs">Anyutka</span>. If only I could die too. <small id="mwYPw">(cries)</small><br id="mwYP0"><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYP4">Mitritch</span>. If you died――you’d only become an outcast from this world!<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYP8">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%D0%92%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C+%D1%82%D1%8C%D0%BC%D1%8B%2C+%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B8+%C2%AB%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BA+%D1%83%D0%B2%D1%8F%D0%B7%2C+%D0%B2%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%B9+%D0%BF%D1%82%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B5+%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C%C2%BB.+%D0%94%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0+%D0%B2+%D0%BF%D1%8F%D1%82%D0%B8+%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%B9%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%8F%D1%85+%E9%97%87%E3%81%AE%E5%8A%9B%EF%BC%88%E4%BA%94%E5%B9%95%EF%BC%89%E3%80%80%3Csmall%3E%E5%88%A5%E5%90%8D%EF%BC%88%E7%88%AA%E3%81%8C%E4%B8%80%E6%9C%AC%E7%BD%A0%E3%81%AB%E3%81%8B%E3%81%8B%E3%81%A4%E3%81%9F%E3%82%89%E3%80%81%E3%81%9D%E3%81%AE%E5%B0%8F%E9%B3%A5%E3%81%AF%E3%82%82%E3%81%86%E3%81%8A%E3%81%97%E3%81%BE%E3%81%B2%E3%81%A0%E3%80%82%EF%BC%89%3C%2Fsmall%3E&amp;rft.btitle=%D0%92%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C+%D1%82%D1%8C%D0%BC%D1%8B.+%D0%96%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B9+%D1%82%D1%80%D1%83%D0%BF+%E9%97%87%E3%81%AE%E5%8A%9B%E3%83%BB%E7%94%9F%E3%81%91%E3%82%8B%E5%B1%8D&amp;rft.place=Ch%C5%AB%C5%8D%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E6%94%B9%E9%80%A0%E9%81%B8%E6%9B%B8%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=58%2C+62%2C+80%2C+91%2C+148&amp;rft.pub=Kaiz%C5%8Dsha&amp;rft.date=1948-07-01&amp;rft.aulast=Tolstoy&amp;rft.aufirst=Leo&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1132851%2F1%2F32&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYQA"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYQE"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYQI"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-544" id="cite_note-544" data-mw-footnote-number="499"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYQM"><a href="#cite_ref-544" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYQQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYQU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-544" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3605" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYQY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFIshii1924" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Ishii, Mitsuru (25 November 1924).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYQc">⒊自動車の洪水</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYQg">[</span>3. Car Flooding<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYQk">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/983094/1/128" class="external text" id="mwYQo"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwYQs">金と女の國のうらおもて</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYQw">[</span><i id="mwYQ0">A Land of Money and Women: The Ins and Outs</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYQ4">]</span> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koishikawa" title="Koishikawa" id="mwYQ8">Koishikawa</a>, Tokyo: Hinoeuma Shuppansha. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYRA">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwYRE">235–</span>236.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYRI">元來、繁華な市街で交通の頻繁な場所では自動車は、何百臺と列をしてあとからあとからとやつて來る。それだから、あれ程の大きいものを廻はしたり停めたりすることは大事業である。それ故に一寸目と鼻のところへゆくにも、自動車なら却つて大迂回しなければゆけないことがある。お上りさんがこんな目に遭ふと、運轉手が料金を高くとる爲めにわざと大迂回をしたのだと思つて憤慨したりするが、實は決して左樣ではない。また市街地の空地と云ふ空地は悉く有料自動車置場になつてゐる。四時間廿五仙、土曜の午後や日曜には其の倍額をもとられる。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYRM">[</span>It used to be that, in traffic-heavy spots on bustling streets, cars would line up and arrive one after another in the hundreds, and manoeuvring and parking in such massive traffic was a huge undertaking. Consequently, one would have to take a large detour by car just to go to a place only a short stone’s throw away. When experiencing this, visitors from out of town would take umbrage because they thought cab drivers were taking large detours on purpose to overcharge them, even though it was by no means the case. Add to that, all the vacant parts of street space were turning into paid parking lots, which cost twenty-five cents for four hours, and double that on Saturday afternoons and Sundays.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYRQ">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E2%92%8A%E8%87%AA%E5%8B%95%E8%BB%8A%E3%81%AE%E6%B4%AA%E6%B0%B4&amp;rft.btitle=%E9%87%91%E3%81%A8%E5%A5%B3%E3%81%AE%E5%9C%8B%E3%81%AE%E3%81%86%E3%82%89%E3%81%8A%E3%82%82%E3%81%A6&amp;rft.place=Koishikawa%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=235-236&amp;rft.pub=Hinoeuma+Shuppansha&amp;rft.date=1924-11-25&amp;rft.aulast=Ishii&amp;rft.aufirst=Mitsuru&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F983094%2F1%2F128&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYRU"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYRY"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYRc"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-545" id="cite_note-545" data-mw-footnote-number="500"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYRg"><a href="#cite_ref-545" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYRk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYRo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-545" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3611" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYRs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFYanagisawa2016" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimio_Yanagisawa" title="Kimio Yanagisawa" id="mwYRw">Yanagisawa, Kimio</a> (17 November 2016).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYR0">●第73話●結婚について</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYR4">[</span>●Chapter 73●On Marriage<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYR8">]</span>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYSA">大市民</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYSE">[</span><i id="mwYSI">The Great Citizen</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYSM">]</span> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYSQ">&nbsp;</span>7. CoMax.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYSU">どうして 日本人は 何に考えず 右にならえ してしまうのか⁉ という事だ アッというまに みんな同じ服装に なってしまう そして そうする事に 疑問を何も感じてない カラオケやゴルフを 私が嫌うのも そういう理由があるからだ どうして 日本人は みんなで同じ行動を とるのかと……… なぜ 結婚式に 白と黒の服装で 出席せねばいけないのか なぜ そろいもそろって みんな ゴルフとカラオケをやらねばいけないのか 毎日のひとつひとつの事に <b id="mwYSY">疑問と反発</b>を抱かぬ 日本の大人に <b id="mwYSc">私は怒りを感じるからだ</b></bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYSg">[</span>Why do Japanese people just mindlessly follow the crowd⁉ Before you know it, everybody ends up dressing the same, and they don’t feel like questioning that. That’s why I hate karaoke and golf. How come Japanese people all act the same……… Why is it you must wear black and white to weddings? Why must everybody agree to play golf or sing karaoke together? Grown Japanese, who can’t be bothered to <b id="mwYSk">question and oppose</b> every single thing they do every day, they <b id="mwYSo">piss me off</b>.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYSs">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E2%97%8F%E7%AC%AC73%E8%A9%B1%E2%97%8F%E7%B5%90%E5%A9%9A%E3%81%AB%E3%81%A4%E3%81%84%E3%81%A6&amp;rft.btitle=%E5%A4%A7%E5%B8%82%E6%B0%91&amp;rft.pub=CoMax&amp;rft.date=2016-11-17&amp;rft.aulast=Yanagisawa&amp;rft.aufirst=Kimio&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYSw"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYS0"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYS4"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-547" id="cite_note-547" data-mw-footnote-number="501"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYS8"><a href="#cite_ref-547" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYTA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYTE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-547" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3620" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYTI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFItō1929" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masanori_Itō_(journalist)" title="Masanori Itō (journalist)" id="mwYTM">Itō, Masanori</a>, ed. (30 March 1929).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYTQ"><b id="mwYTU">第二章</b>　趣味生活</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYTY">[</span><b id="mwYTc">Chapter 2</b> A Life of Interests<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYTg">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1240825/1/413" class="external text" id="mwYTk"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwYTo">加藤高明</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYTs">[</span><i id="mwYTw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katō_Takaaki" title="Katō Takaaki" id="mwYT0">Katō Takaaki</a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYT4">]</span> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYT8">&nbsp;</span>2. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hongō,_Tokyo" title="Hongō, Tokyo" id="mwYUA">Hongō, Tokyo</a>: <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwYUE"><span lang="ja" id="mwYUI">加藤伯傳記編纂委員會</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwYUM">. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYUQ">&nbsp;</span>754.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYUU">結城　加藤高明さんが、馬車は宮中から下の方に來た、ところが自動車は下の方から上に行つた、變遷から反感が多い、といつた。<br id="mwYUY">生田　日本に初めて自動車の來た時、加藤さんは、この自動車を注意せねばいけん、これが社會主義を招徠する一番の原因だ、といつた。その通りのやうだ。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYUc">[</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyotarō_Yūki" title="Toyotarō Yūki" id="mwYUg"><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYUk">Yūki</span></a>. Mr Katō Takaaki said that horse-drawn carriages came from the Palace to the common folk, but automobiles went upwards from the common folk, and there was much antipathy due to this shift.<br id="mwYUo"><span style="font-variant:small-caps" id="mwYUs">Ikuta</span>. When automobiles first came to Japan, Mr Katō said that we had to keep watch of them, these were the primary factor that gives rise to socialism. That seems to be the case.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYUw">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E4%BA%8C%E7%AB%A0%E3%80%80%E8%B6%A3%E5%91%B3%E7%94%9F%E6%B4%BB&amp;rft.btitle=%E5%8A%A0%E8%97%A4%E9%AB%98%E6%98%8E&amp;rft.place=Hong%C5%8D%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=754&amp;rft.pub=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E5%8A%A0%E8%97%A4%E4%BC%AF%E5%82%B3%E8%A8%98%E7%B7%A8%E7%BA%82%E5%A7%94%E5%93%A1%E6%9C%83%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.date=1929-03-30&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1240825%2F1%2F413&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYU0"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYU4"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYU8"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-549" id="cite_note-549" data-mw-footnote-number="502"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYVA"><a href="#cite_ref-549" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYVE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYVI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-549" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3629" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYVM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFNishinoMorihara2026" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Nishino, Murasaki; Morihara, Yōka (9 January 2026).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYVQ">【一章】</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYVU">[</span>[1st Chapter]<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYVY">]</span>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYVc">エリート海上自衛官のひたむきな独占求愛～恋に臆病な彼女は蕩けるほど甘やかされる～</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYVg">[</span><i id="mwYVk">An Elite Maritime Self-Defense Officer’s Earnest and Exclusive Courtship: A Timid Girlfriend in Love Is Pampered So Much She Melts</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYVo">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwYVs"><span lang="ja" id="mwYVw">極上自衛官</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwYV0"> (in Japanese). HarperCollins Japan. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwYV4">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYV8">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-4-302-11187-9" title="Special:BookSources/978-4-302-11187-9" id="mwYWA"><bdi id="mwYWE">978-4-302-11187-9</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYWI">にへら、と笑う彼の背後に「桃届いたんじゃろうか？」という声がかかる。おばあちゃんだ。日傘を閉じ、しっかりとした歩調で歩いてくる。<br id="mwYWM">「お隣にもおすそ分けせにゃいけんねえ」<br id="mwYWQ">「おばあちゃん、違うって。いや、桃は届いてるんだけど」<br id="mwYWU">「ん？　年寄りにも分かるように説明せえ」</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYWY">[</span>As he grinned from ear to ear, a voice came up from behind, “Did the peaches arrive?” It was Granny. She closed her parasol, and walked up at a steady pace.<br id="mwYWc">“We gotta share with the neighbors.”<br id="mwYWg">“No, granny. The peaches are still on the way, though.”<br id="mwYWk">“Hm? Explain so an old lady could understand.”<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYWo">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E3%80%90%E4%B8%80%E7%AB%A0%E3%80%91&amp;rft.btitle=%E3%82%A8%E3%83%AA%E3%83%BC%E3%83%88%E6%B5%B7%E4%B8%8A%E8%87%AA%E8%A1%9B%E5%AE%98%E3%81%AE%E3%81%B2%E3%81%9F%E3%82%80%E3%81%8D%E3%81%AA%E7%8B%AC%E5%8D%A0%E6%B1%82%E6%84%9B%EF%BD%9E%E6%81%8B%E3%81%AB%E8%87%86%E7%97%85%E3%81%AA%E5%BD%BC%E5%A5%B3%E3%81%AF%E8%95%A9%E3%81%91%E3%82%8B%E3%81%BB%E3%81%A9%E7%94%98%E3%82%84%E3%81%8B%E3%81%95%E3%82%8C%E3%82%8B%EF%BD%9E&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E6%A5%B5%E4%B8%8A%E8%87%AA%E8%A1%9B%E5%AE%98%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pub=HarperCollins+Japan&amp;rft.date=2026-01-09&amp;rft.isbn=978-4-302-11187-9&amp;rft.aulast=Nishino&amp;rft.aufirst=Murasaki&amp;rft.au=Morihara%2C+Y%C5%8Dka&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYWs"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYWw"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYW0"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-hirata-1918-550" id="cite_note-hirata-1918-550" data-mw-footnote-number="503"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYW4"><a href="#cite_ref-hirata-1918_550-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYW8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYXA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-hirata-1918-550" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3635" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYXE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="mwYXI" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source" data-x-id="CITEREFMeredith1918"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Meredith" title="George Meredith" id="mwYXM">Meredith, George</a> (15 June 1918). "Chapter XLII. Shows the Divining Arts of a Perceptive Mind" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYXQ"><b id="mwYXU"><ruby id="mwYXY">第<rp id="mwYXc">(</rp><rt id="mwYXg">だい</rt><rp id="mwYXk">)</rp></ruby>四十二<ruby id="mwYXo">章<rp id="mwYXs">(</rp><rt id="mwYXw">しやう</rt><rp id="mwYX0">)</rp></ruby></b>　<small id="mwYX4">覺りの早き人の透視術</small></bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/953545/1/171" class="external text" id="mwYX8"><i id="mwYYA">The Egoist: A Comedy in Narrative</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYYE"><ruby id="mwYYI">我意の人<rp id="mwYYM">(</rp><rt id="mwYYQ">エゴイスト</rt><rp id="mwYYU">)</rp></ruby></bdi></a> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYYY">&nbsp;</span>3. Translated by Hirata, Tokuboku. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanda,_Tokyo" title="Kanda, Tokyo" id="mwYYc">Kanda, Tokyo</a>: <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwYYg"><span lang="ja" id="mwYYk">國民文庫刊行會</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwYYo">. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYYs">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwYYw">332–</span>333. <q id="mwYY0">He who can watch circling above it awhile, quietly viewing, and collecting in his eye, gathers matter that makes the secret thing discourse to the brain by weight and balance; he will get either the right clue or none; more frequently none; but he will escape the entanglement of his own cleverness, he will always be nearer to the enigma than the guesser or the calculator, and he will retain a breadth of vision forfeited by them. He must, however, to have his chance of success, be acutely besides calmly perceptive, a reader of features, audacious at the proper moment.</q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYY4"><ruby id="mwYY8">暫時<rp id="mwYZA">(</rp><rt id="mwYZE">しばらく</rt><rp id="mwYZI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYZM">高<rp id="mwYZQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYZU">たか</rt><rp id="mwYZY">)</rp></ruby>くその<ruby id="mwYZc">上<rp id="mwYZg">(</rp><rt id="mwYZk">うへ</rt><rp id="mwYZo">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwYZs">飛<rp id="mwYZw">(</rp><rt id="mwYZ0">ひ</rt><rp id="mwYZ4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYZ8">揚<rp id="mwYaA">(</rp><rt id="mwYaE">やう</rt><rp id="mwYaI">)</rp></ruby>して、ぢつとその<ruby id="mwYaM">觀<rp id="mwYaQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYaU">くわん</rt><rp id="mwYaY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYac">察<rp id="mwYag">(</rp><rt id="mwYak">さつ</rt><rp id="mwYao">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYas">擅<rp id="mwYaw">(</rp><rt id="mwYa0">ほしいま</rt><rp id="mwYa4">)</rp></ruby>まにし、<ruby id="mwYa8">靜<rp id="mwYbA">(</rp><rt id="mwYbE">しづ</rt><rp id="mwYbI">)</rp></ruby>かに<ruby id="mwYbM">見<rp id="mwYbQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYbU">み</rt><rp id="mwYbY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYbc">渡<rp id="mwYbg">(</rp><rt id="mwYbk">わた</rt><rp id="mwYbo">)</rp></ruby>し、<ruby id="mwYbs">物<rp id="mwYbw">(</rp><rt id="mwYb0">もの</rt><rp id="mwYb4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYb8">皆<rp id="mwYcA">(</rp><rt id="mwYcE">みな</rt><rp id="mwYcI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYcM">悉<rp id="mwYcQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYcU">こと〲</rt><rp id="mwYcY">)</rp></ruby>く<ruby id="mwYcc">我<rp id="mwYcg">(</rp><rt id="mwYck">わ</rt><rp id="mwYco">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwYcs">眼<rp id="mwYcw">(</rp><rt id="mwYc0">め</rt><rp id="mwYc4">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYc8">中<rp id="mwYdA">(</rp><rt id="mwYdE">うち</rt><rp id="mwYdI">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwYdM">收<rp id="mwYdQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYdU">をさ</rt><rp id="mwYdY">)</rp></ruby>めようといふ<ruby id="mwYdc">人<rp id="mwYdg">(</rp><rt id="mwYdk">ひと</rt><rp id="mwYdo">)</rp></ruby>こそ、<ruby id="mwYds">秘<rp id="mwYdw">(</rp><rt id="mwYd0">ひ</rt><rp id="mwYd4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYd8">密<rp id="mwYeA">(</rp><rt id="mwYeE">みつ</rt><rp id="mwYeI">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYeM">事<rp id="mwYeQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYeU">じ</rt><rp id="mwYeY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYec">物<rp id="mwYeg">(</rp><rt id="mwYek">ぶつ</rt><rp id="mwYeo">)</rp></ruby>をして、よくその<ruby id="mwYes">輕<rp id="mwYew">(</rp><rt id="mwYe0">けい</rt><rp id="mwYe4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYe8">重<rp id="mwYfA">(</rp><rt id="mwYfE">ぢう</rt><rp id="mwYfI">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYfM">量<rp id="mwYfQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYfU">はか</rt><rp id="mwYfY">)</rp></ruby>つて<ruby id="mwYfc">頭<rp id="mwYfg">(</rp><rt id="mwYfk">づ</rt><rp id="mwYfo">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYfs">腦<rp id="mwYfw">(</rp><rt id="mwYf0">なう</rt><rp id="mwYf4">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwYf8">吿<rp id="mwYgA">(</rp><rt id="mwYgE">つ</rt><rp id="mwYgI">)</rp></ruby>げしむるやうになす、<ruby id="mwYgM">數多<rp id="mwYgQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYgU">あまた</rt><rp id="mwYgY">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYgc">材<rp id="mwYgg">(</rp><rt id="mwYgk">ざい</rt><rp id="mwYgo">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYgs">料<rp id="mwYgw">(</rp><rt id="mwYg0">れう</rt><rp id="mwYg4">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYg8">蒐<rp id="mwYhA">(</rp><rt id="mwYhE">しう</rt><rp id="mwYhI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYhM">集<rp id="mwYhQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYhU">しふ</rt><rp id="mwYhY">)</rp></ruby>するのである。<ruby id="mwYhc">確<rp id="mwYhg">(</rp><rt id="mwYhk">たし</rt><rp id="mwYho">)</rp></ruby>かに<ruby id="mwYhs">手<rp id="mwYhw">(</rp><rt id="mwYh0">て</rt><rp id="mwYh4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYh8">掛<rp id="mwYiA">(</rp><rt id="mwYiE">がゝり</rt><rp id="mwYiI">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYiM">得<rp id="mwYiQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYiU">え</rt><rp id="mwYiY">)</rp></ruby>るか、<ruby id="mwYic">全<rp id="mwYig">(</rp><rt id="mwYik">ぜん</rt><rp id="mwYio">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYis">然<rp id="mwYiw">(</rp><rt id="mwYi0">〱</rt><rp id="mwYi4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYi8">左<rp id="mwYjA">(</rp><rt id="mwYjE">さ</rt><rp id="mwYjI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYjM">樣<rp id="mwYjQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYjU">う</rt><rp id="mwYjY">)</rp></ruby>したものを<ruby id="mwYjc">手<rp id="mwYjg">(</rp><rt id="mwYjk">て</rt><rp id="mwYjo">)</rp></ruby>にせぬか<ruby id="mwYjs">二<rp id="mwYjw">(</rp><rt id="mwYj0">ふた</rt><rp id="mwYj4">)</rp></ruby>つ<ruby id="mwYj8">一<rp id="mwYkA">(</rp><rt id="mwYkE">ひと</rt><rp id="mwYkI">)</rp></ruby>つである、<ruby id="mwYkM">多<rp id="mwYkQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYkU">おほ</rt><rp id="mwYkY">)</rp></ruby>くは<ruby id="mwYkc">何<rp id="mwYkg">(</rp><rt id="mwYkk">なに</rt><rp id="mwYko">)</rp></ruby>をも<ruby id="mwYks">得<rp id="mwYkw">(</rp><rt id="mwYk0">え</rt><rp id="mwYk4">)</rp></ruby>られぬが<ruby id="mwYk8">普<rp id="mwYlA">(</rp><rt id="mwYlE">ふ</rt><rp id="mwYlI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYlM">通<rp id="mwYlQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYlU">つう</rt><rp id="mwYlY">)</rp></ruby>である、が、<ruby id="mwYlc">彼<rp id="mwYlg">(</rp><rt id="mwYlk">かれ</rt><rp id="mwYlo">)</rp></ruby>はそれに<ruby id="mwYls">依<rp id="mwYlw">(</rp><rt id="mwYl0">よ</rt><rp id="mwYl4">)</rp></ruby>つて<ruby id="mwYl8">我<rp id="mwYmA">(</rp><rt id="mwYmE">わ</rt><rp id="mwYmI">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwYmM">巧<rp id="mwYmQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYmU">たく</rt><rp id="mwYmY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYmc">緻<rp id="mwYmg">(</rp><rt id="mwYmk">み</rt><rp id="mwYmo">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYms">足<rp id="mwYmw">(</rp><rt id="mwYm0">あし</rt><rp id="mwYm4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYm8">手<rp id="mwYnA">(</rp><rt id="mwYnE">て</rt><rp id="mwYnI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYnM">纏<rp id="mwYnQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYnU">まと</rt><rp id="mwYnY">)</rp></ruby>ひのうちに<ruby id="mwYnc">捕<rp id="mwYng">(</rp><rt id="mwYnk">とら</rt><rp id="mwYno">)</rp></ruby>はれずに<ruby id="mwYns">濟<rp id="mwYnw">(</rp><rt id="mwYn0">す</rt><rp id="mwYn4">)</rp></ruby>む、<ruby id="mwYn8">推<rp id="mwYoA">(</rp><rt id="mwYoE">すゐ</rt><rp id="mwYoI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYoM">察<rp id="mwYoQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYoU">さつ</rt><rp id="mwYoY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYoc">者<rp id="mwYog">(</rp><rt id="mwYok">しや</rt><rp id="mwYoo">)</rp></ruby>、<ruby id="mwYos">若<rp id="mwYow">(</rp><rt id="mwYo0">も</rt><rp id="mwYo4">)</rp></ruby>しくは<ruby id="mwYo8">打<rp id="mwYpA">(</rp><rt id="mwYpE">だ</rt><rp id="mwYpI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYpM">算<rp id="mwYpQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYpU">さん</rt><rp id="mwYpY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYpc">者<rp id="mwYpg">(</rp><rt id="mwYpk">しや</rt><rp id="mwYpo">)</rp></ruby>よりは、ずつとその<ruby id="mwYps">謎語<rp id="mwYpw">(</rp><rt id="mwYp0">なぞ</rt><rp id="mwYp4">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwYp8">近<rp id="mwYqA">(</rp><rt id="mwYqE">ちか</rt><rp id="mwYqI">)</rp></ruby>づける、して、<ruby id="mwYqM">彼<rp id="mwYqQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYqU">かれ</rt><rp id="mwYqY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYqc">等<rp id="mwYqg">(</rp><rt id="mwYqk">ら</rt><rp id="mwYqo">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYqs">失<rp id="mwYqw">(</rp><rt id="mwYq0">うしな</rt><rp id="mwYq4">)</rp></ruby>つてゐる<ruby id="mwYq8">廣<rp id="mwYrA">(</rp><rt id="mwYrE">くわう</rt><rp id="mwYrI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYrM">濶<rp id="mwYrQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYrU">くわつ</rt><rp id="mwYrY">)</rp></ruby>な<ruby id="mwYrc">眼<rp id="mwYrg">(</rp><rt id="mwYrk">がん</rt><rp id="mwYro">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYrs">界<rp id="mwYrw">(</rp><rt id="mwYr0">かい</rt><rp id="mwYr4">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYr8">立<rp id="mwYsA">(</rp><rt id="mwYsE">りつ</rt><rp id="mwYsI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYsM">派<rp id="mwYsQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYsU">ぱ</rt><rp id="mwYsY">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwYsc">保<rp id="mwYsg">(</rp><rt id="mwYsk">ほ</rt><rp id="mwYso">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYss">持<rp id="mwYsw">(</rp><rt id="mwYs0">ぢ</rt><rp id="mwYs4">)</rp></ruby>していかれるのである。が、<ruby id="mwYs8">成<rp id="mwYtA">(</rp><rt id="mwYtE">せい</rt><rp id="mwYtI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYtM">功<rp id="mwYtQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYtU">こう</rt><rp id="mwYtY">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYtc">機<rp id="mwYtg">(</rp><rt id="mwYtk">き</rt><rp id="mwYto">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYts">械<rp id="mwYtw">(</rp><rt id="mwYt0">くわい</rt><rp id="mwYt4">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYt8">捉<rp id="mwYuA">(</rp><rt id="mwYuE">とら</rt><rp id="mwYuI">)</rp></ruby>へんには、<ruby id="mwYuM">彼<rp id="mwYuQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYuU">かれ</rt><rp id="mwYuY">)</rp></ruby>はまた<ruby id="mwYuc">啻<rp id="mwYug">(</rp><rt id="mwYuk">たゞ</rt><rp id="mwYuo">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwYus">冷靜<rp id="mwYuw">(</rp><rt id="mwYu0">しづか</rt><rp id="mwYu4">)</rp></ruby>にその<ruby id="mwYu8">智<rp id="mwYvA">(</rp><rt id="mwYvE">ち</rt><rp id="mwYvI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYvM">覺<rp id="mwYvQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYvU">かく</rt><rp id="mwYvY">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYvc">働<rp id="mwYvg">(</rp><rt id="mwYvk">うご</rt><rp id="mwYvo">)</rp></ruby>かすばかりでなく、それ〲<ruby id="mwYvs">適<rp id="mwYvw">(</rp><rt id="mwYv0">てき</rt><rp id="mwYv4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYv8">當<rp id="mwYwA">(</rp><rt id="mwYwE">たう</rt><rp id="mwYwI">)</rp></ruby>な<ruby id="mwYwM">時<rp id="mwYwQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYwU">じ</rt><rp id="mwYwY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYwc">機<rp id="mwYwg">(</rp><rt id="mwYwk">き</rt><rp id="mwYwo">)</rp></ruby>に<ruby id="mwYws">於<rp id="mwYww">(</rp><rt id="mwYw0">おい</rt><rp id="mwYw4">)</rp></ruby>て<ruby id="mwYw8">隨<rp id="mwYxA">(</rp><rt id="mwYxE">ずゐ</rt><rp id="mwYxI">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYxM">分<rp id="mwYxQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYxU">ぶん</rt><rp id="mwYxY">)</rp></ruby>と<ruby id="mwYxc">大<rp id="mwYxg">(</rp><rt id="mwYxk">だい</rt><rp id="mwYxo">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYxs">膽<rp id="mwYxw">(</rp><rt id="mwYx0">たん</rt><rp id="mwYx4">)</rp></ruby>に、<ruby id="mwYx8">他人<rp id="mwYyA">(</rp><rt id="mwYyE">ひと</rt><rp id="mwYyI">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwYyM">容<rp id="mwYyQ">(</rp><rt id="mwYyU">よう</rt><rp id="mwYyY">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYyc">貌<rp id="mwYyg">(</rp><rt id="mwYyk">す</rt><rp id="mwYyo">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwYys">讀<rp id="mwYyw">(</rp><rt id="mwYy0">どく</rt><rp id="mwYy4">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwYy8">破<rp id="mwYzA">(</rp><rt id="mwYzE">は</rt><rp id="mwYzI">)</rp></ruby>せねばいけぬのである。</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Chapter+XLII.+Shows+the+Divining+Arts+of+a+Perceptive+Mind+%3Cruby%3E%E7%AC%AC%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%A0%E3%81%84%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E5%9B%9B%E5%8D%81%E4%BA%8C%3Cruby%3E%E7%AB%A0%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%97%E3%82%84%E3%81%86%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%80%80%3Csmall%3E%E8%A6%BA%E3%82%8A%E3%81%AE%E6%97%A9%E3%81%8D%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%AE%E9%80%8F%E8%A6%96%E8%A1%93%3C%2Fsmall%3E&amp;rft.btitle=The+Egoist%3A+A+Comedy+in+Narrative+%3Cruby%3E%E6%88%91%E6%84%8F%E3%81%AE%E4%BA%BA%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%82%A8%E3%82%B4%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B9%E3%83%88%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E&amp;rft.place=Kanda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=332-333&amp;rft.pub=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E5%9C%8B%E6%B0%91%E6%96%87%E5%BA%AB%E5%88%8A%E8%A1%8C%E6%9C%83%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.date=1918-06-15&amp;rft.aulast=Meredith&amp;rft.aufirst=George&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F953545%2F1%2F171&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwYzM"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwYzQ"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwYzU"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-551" id="cite_note-551" data-mw-footnote-number="504"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwYzY"><a href="#cite_ref-551" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwYzc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwYzg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-551" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3641" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwYzk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFJūichiya1934" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Jūichiya, Gisaburō (18 April 1934).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwYzo">澄んだ三宅</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYzs">[</span>The Transparent Miyake<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYzw">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1234791/1/99" class="external text" id="mwYz0"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwYz4">ちりがみ文章</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwYz8">[</span><i id="mwY0A">Some Writing on Waste Paper</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY0E">]</span> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kōjimachi" title="Kōjimachi" id="mwY0I">Kōjimachi</a>, Tokyo: Kouseikaku. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY0M">&nbsp;</span>181.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwY0Q">彼に向ふと、自分の獨りが目立つ。現在もさうだ。彼は何よりも自然だ。自分はさうはゆかない。彼は暫く書かなかつた。書かないで、生活の整理をやつてゐた。それも淡々としてやつてゐた。三宅の現在書く小說には、此の態度がよく出てゐる。世の中は廣い。私の書くやうな獨りの多いものが好きな人もあるらしい。三宅の最近のやうな小說は食ひ足りないと云つた趣味の人も多いらしい。然し三宅の書くものには噓はない。彼は平氣で正直になれる男だ。他人が苦しまねばゆけぬところへ、易々といつてゐるのだ。他人が大袈裟に發見するものを、無雜作に洞察してゐるのだ。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY0U">[</span>Whenever I face him, my lone self sticks out, even right now. He is more natural than anything else, which does not work for me. He has not written for some time now, and whilst not writing, he was still sorting out his life. He was doing it so nonchalantly too. This attitude is well apparent in Miyake’s current novel. In life it is vast. There seem to be people who like the many kinds of loners that I would write. There seem to be many people whose interests have shown that novels like Miyake’s recent ones leave something to be desired. But there are no lies in what Miyake writes. He is a man who can be composed and candid. He speaks with ease where others cannot but struggle, and he discerns with simplicity what others discover with hyperbole.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY0Y">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E6%BE%84%E3%82%93%E3%81%A0%E4%B8%89%E5%AE%85&amp;rft.btitle=%E3%81%A1%E3%82%8A%E3%81%8C%E3%81%BF%E6%96%87%E7%AB%A0&amp;rft.place=K%C5%8Djimachi%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=181&amp;rft.pub=Kouseikaku&amp;rft.date=1934-04-18&amp;rft.aulast=J%C5%ABichiya&amp;rft.aufirst=Gisabur%C5%8D&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1234791%2F1%2F99&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwY0c"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwY0g"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwY0k"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-553" id="cite_note-553" data-mw-footnote-number="505"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwY0o"><a href="#cite_ref-553" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwY0s"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwY0w">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-553" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3650" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwY00" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFChen2009" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Chen, Tien-shi (30 September 2009). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://kanagawa-u.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/4476/files/LawJ%20vol.2-3.pdf" class="external text" id="mwY04">"Mulling over the Issue of Statelessness" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwY08">無国籍問題を考える</bdi></a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwY1A">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwY1E">Kanagawa law journal</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwY1I">神奈川ロージャーナル</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwY1M">2</b>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwY1Q"><span lang="ja" id="mwY1U">神奈川大学大学院法務研究科</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwY1Y">: 32.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Kanagawa+law+journal&amp;rft.atitle=Mulling+over+the+Issue+of+Statelessness+%E7%84%A1%E5%9B%BD%E7%B1%8D%E5%95%8F%E9%A1%8C%E3%82%92%E8%80%83%E3%81%88%E3%82%8B&amp;rft.volume=2&amp;rft.pages=32&amp;rft.date=2009-09-30&amp;rft.aulast=Chen&amp;rft.aufirst=Tien-shi&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fkanagawa-u.repo.nii.ac.jp%2Frecord%2F4476%2Ffiles%2FLawJ%2520vol.2-3.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwY1c"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwY1g"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwY1k"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-555" id="cite_note-555" data-mw-footnote-number="506"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwY1o"><a href="#cite_ref-555" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwY1s"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwY1w">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-555" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3660" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwY10" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFYōko1924" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Yōko, Sakai (1 August 1924). Saitō, Sajirō (ed.). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1790850/1/52" class="external text" id="mwY14"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwY18"><ruby id="mwY2A">繪<rp id="mwY2E">(</rp><rt id="mwY2I">ゑ</rt><rp id="mwY2M">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwY2Q">夜<rp id="mwY2U">(</rp><rt id="mwY2Y">よる</rt><rp id="mwY2c">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwY2g">何<rp id="mwY2k">(</rp><rt id="mwY2o">なに</rt><rp id="mwY2s">)</rp></ruby>をするでせう　<small id="mwY2w">（推薦）</small></bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY20">[</span>What Do Paintings Do at Night? <small id="mwY24">(recommended)</small><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY28">]</span>. <i id="mwY3A">Kinnohoshi</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwY3E">金の星</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwY3I">6</b> (8). Tabata, Tokyo: Kinnohoshi Co: 83.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwY3M">「あなたを<ruby id="mwY3Q">繪<rp id="mwY3U">(</rp><rt id="mwY3Y">ゑ</rt><rp id="mwY3c">)</rp></ruby>のお<ruby id="mwY3g">國<rp id="mwY3k">(</rp><rt id="mwY3o">くに</rt><rp id="mwY3s">)</rp></ruby>へお<ruby id="mwY3w">連<rp id="mwY30">(</rp><rt id="mwY34">つ</rt><rp id="mwY38">)</rp></ruby>れしませう。<ruby id="mwY4A">繪<rp id="mwY4E">(</rp><rt id="mwY4I">ゑ</rt><rp id="mwY4M">)</rp></ruby>のお<ruby id="mwY4Q">國<rp id="mwY4U">(</rp><rt id="mwY4Y">くに</rt><rp id="mwY4c">)</rp></ruby>はそれは〱<ruby id="mwY4g">樂<rp id="mwY4k">(</rp><rt id="mwY4o">たの</rt><rp id="mwY4s">)</rp></ruby>しい<ruby id="mwY4w">所<rp id="mwY40">(</rp><rt id="mwY44">ところ</rt><rp id="mwY48">)</rp></ruby>です。そこへ<ruby id="mwY5A">行<rp id="mwY5E">(</rp><rt id="mwY5I">ゆ</rt><rp id="mwY5M">)</rp></ruby>けば、もうけつして<ruby id="mwY5Q">悲<rp id="mwY5U">(</rp><rt id="mwY5Y">かな</rt><rp id="mwY5c">)</rp></ruby>しい<ruby id="mwY5g">事<rp id="mwY5k">(</rp><rt id="mwY5o">こと</rt><rp id="mwY5s">)</rp></ruby>もなく、そして<ruby id="mwY5w">何<rp id="mwY50">(</rp><rt id="mwY54">な</rt><rp id="mwY58">)</rp></ruby>んでも<ruby id="mwY6A">思<rp id="mwY6E">(</rp><rt id="mwY6I">おも</rt><rp id="mwY6M">)</rp></ruby>ひ<ruby id="mwY6Q">通<rp id="mwY6U">(</rp><rt id="mwY6Y">どほ</rt><rp id="mwY6c">)</rp></ruby>りになるんです。あなたはお<ruby id="mwY6g">母<rp id="mwY6k">(</rp><rt id="mwY6o">かあ</rt><rp id="mwY6s">)</rp></ruby>さまにも<ruby id="mwY6w">會<rp id="mwY60">(</rp><rt id="mwY64">あ</rt><rp id="mwY68">)</rp></ruby>ふ<ruby id="mwY7A">事<rp id="mwY7E">(</rp><rt id="mwY7I">こと</rt><rp id="mwY7M">)</rp></ruby>が<ruby id="mwY7Q">出<rp id="mwY7U">(</rp><rt id="mwY7Y">で</rt><rp id="mwY7c">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwY7g">來<rp id="mwY7k">(</rp><rt id="mwY7o">き</rt><rp id="mwY7s">)</rp></ruby>ます」つて<ruby id="mwY7w">云<rp id="mwY70">(</rp><rt id="mwY74">い</rt><rp id="mwY78">)</rp></ruby>つたのよ。お<ruby id="mwY8A">孃<rp id="mwY8E">(</rp><rt id="mwY8I">ぢやう</rt><rp id="mwY8M">)</rp></ruby>さんはそりや<ruby id="mwY8Q">行<rp id="mwY8U">(</rp><rt id="mwY8Y">ゆ</rt><rp id="mwY8c">)</rp></ruby>きたがつたのよ。だけど、<ruby id="mwY8g">繪<rp id="mwY8k">(</rp><rt id="mwY8o">ゑ</rt><rp id="mwY8s">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwY8w">國<rp id="mwY80">(</rp><rt id="mwY84">くに</rt><rp id="mwY88">)</rp></ruby>には<ruby id="mwY9A">繪<rp id="mwY9E">(</rp><rt id="mwY9I">ゑ</rt><rp id="mwY9M">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwY9Q">中<rp id="mwY9U">(</rp><rt id="mwY9Y">なか</rt><rp id="mwY9c">)</rp></ruby>のものでなければいかれないでせう。だからあたし、お<ruby id="mwY9g">孃<rp id="mwY9k">(</rp><rt id="mwY9o">ぢやう</rt><rp id="mwY9s">)</rp></ruby>さんに<ruby id="mwY9w">肖<rp id="mwY90">(</rp><rt id="mwY94">せう</rt><rp id="mwY98">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwY-A">像<rp id="mwY-E">(</rp><rt id="mwY-I">ざう</rt><rp id="mwY-M">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwY-Q">畫<rp id="mwY-U">(</rp><rt id="mwY-Y">ぐわ</rt><rp id="mwY-c">)</rp></ruby>をかいてもらふやうに<ruby id="mwY-g">云<rp id="mwY-k">(</rp><rt id="mwY-o">い</rt><rp id="mwY-s">)</rp></ruby>つたの。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY-w">[</span>“I shall take you to the Land of Paintings. It is a very happy place. If you go there, you will never be sad any more, and everything will be as you wish. You will also be able to see your mother,” I said. Mistress really wanted to go. But in the Land of Paintings, you would have to be something already in a painting. So I asked Mistress to have her portrait painted.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY-0">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Kinnohoshi&amp;rft.atitle=%3Cruby%3E%E7%B9%AA%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%82%91%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%81%AF%3Cruby%3E%E5%A4%9C%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%82%88%E3%82%8B%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E4%BD%95%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%AA%E3%81%AB%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%82%92%E3%81%99%E3%82%8B%E3%81%A7%E3%81%9B%E3%81%86%E3%80%80%3Csmall%3E%EF%BC%88%E6%8E%A8%E8%96%A6%EF%BC%89%3C%2Fsmall%3E&amp;rft.volume=6&amp;rft.issue=8&amp;rft.pages=83&amp;rft.date=1924-08-01&amp;rft.aulast=Y%C5%8Dko&amp;rft.aufirst=Sakai&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1790850%2F1%2F52&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwY-4"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwY-8"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwY_A"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-556" id="cite_note-556" data-mw-footnote-number="507"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwY_E"><a href="#cite_ref-556" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwY_I"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwY_M">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-556" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3666" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwY_Q" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFChikamatsu1939" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Chikamatsu, Shūkō (9 August 1939).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwY_U">吉野路</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1687444/1/99" class="external text" id="mwY_Y"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwY_c">旅こそよけれ</bdi></a>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwY_g"><span lang="ja" id="mwY_k">冨山房百科文庫</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwY_o"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY_s">&nbsp;</span>79. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanda,_Tokyo" title="Kanda, Tokyo" id="mwY_w">Kanda, Tokyo</a>: Fuzambo. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwY_0">&nbsp;</span>186.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E5%90%89%E9%87%8E%E8%B7%AF&amp;rft.btitle=%E6%97%85%E3%81%93%E3%81%9D%E3%82%88%E3%81%91%E3%82%8C&amp;rft.place=Kanda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E5%86%A8%E5%B1%B1%E6%88%BF%E7%99%BE%E7%A7%91%E6%96%87%E5%BA%AB%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pages=186&amp;rft.pub=Fuzambo&amp;rft.date=1939-08-09&amp;rft.aulast=Chikamatsu&amp;rft.aufirst=Sh%C5%ABk%C5%8D&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1687444%2F1%2F99&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwY_4"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwY_8"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZAA"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-557" id="cite_note-557" data-mw-footnote-number="508"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZAE"><a href="#cite_ref-557" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZAI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZAM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-557" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3672" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZAQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFKatagiri1929" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Katagiri, Ryūko (15 September 1929).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZAU">鬼と佛の共に棲む世</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZAY">[</span>A World Where Demons and Buddhas Coexist<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZAc">]</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1028899/1/223" class="external text" id="mwZAg"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwZAk">日本婦人の使命と其の修養</bdi></a> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZAo">[</span><i id="mwZAs">Japanese Women’s Missions and Their Cultivation</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZAw">]</span> (in Japanese). Tashōgoe, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gifu" title="Gifu" id="mwZA0">Gifu</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gifu_Prefecture" title="Gifu Prefecture" id="mwZA4">Gifu</a>: <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwZA8"><span lang="ja" id="mwZBA">忠誠婦德會</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwZBE">. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZBI">&nbsp;</span>427.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZBM">「<ruby id="mwZBQ">貴方<rp id="mwZBU">(</rp><rt id="mwZBY">あなた</rt><rp id="mwZBc">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwZBg">事<rp id="mwZBk">(</rp><rt id="mwZBo">じ</rt><rp id="mwZBs">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZBw">情<rp id="mwZB0">(</rp><rt id="mwZB4">ぜう</rt><rp id="mwZB8">)</rp></ruby>を<ruby id="mwZCA">聞<rp id="mwZCE">(</rp><rt id="mwZCI">き</rt><rp id="mwZCM">)</rp></ruby>くと<ruby id="mwZCQ">眞<rp id="mwZCU">(</rp><rt id="mwZCY">まこと</rt><rp id="mwZCc">)</rp></ruby>にお<ruby id="mwZCg">氣<rp id="mwZCk">(</rp><rt id="mwZCo">き</rt><rp id="mwZCs">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwZCw">毒<rp id="mwZC0">(</rp><rt id="mwZC4">どく</rt><rp id="mwZC8">)</rp></ruby>ですから、ここまで<ruby id="mwZDA">乘<rp id="mwZDE">(</rp><rt id="mwZDI">の</rt><rp id="mwZDM">)</rp></ruby>つて<ruby id="mwZDQ">來<rp id="mwZDU">(</rp><rt id="mwZDY">き</rt><rp id="mwZDc">)</rp></ruby>た<ruby id="mwZDg">汽<rp id="mwZDk">(</rp><rt id="mwZDo">き</rt><rp id="mwZDs">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZDw">車<rp id="mwZD0">(</rp><rt id="mwZD4">しや</rt><rp id="mwZD8">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZEA">賃<rp id="mwZEE">(</rp><rt id="mwZEI">ちん</rt><rp id="mwZEM">)</rp></ruby>はそれで<ruby id="mwZEQ">拂<rp id="mwZEU">(</rp><rt id="mwZEY">はら</rt><rp id="mwZEc">)</rp></ruby>はなくてもよい<ruby id="mwZEg">事<rp id="mwZEk">(</rp><rt id="mwZEo">こと</rt><rp id="mwZEs">)</rp></ruby>にしてあげますが、これから<ruby id="mwZEw">先<rp id="mwZE0">(</rp><rt id="mwZE4">さき</rt><rp id="mwZE8">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwZFA">又<rp id="mwZFE">(</rp><rt id="mwZFI">また</rt><rp id="mwZFM">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZFQ">買<rp id="mwZFU">(</rp><rt id="mwZFY">か</rt><rp id="mwZFc">)</rp></ruby>はなければいかれますまい。もう<ruby id="mwZFg">外<rp id="mwZFk">(</rp><rt id="mwZFo">ほか</rt><rp id="mwZFs">)</rp></ruby>にお<ruby id="mwZFw">金<rp id="mwZF0">(</rp><rt id="mwZF4">かね</rt><rp id="mwZF8">)</rp></ruby>は<ruby id="mwZGA">少<rp id="mwZGE">(</rp><rt id="mwZGI">すこ</rt><rp id="mwZGM">)</rp></ruby>しもありませんか？」</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZGQ">[</span>“I am truly sorry to hear of your situation, so I will let you go without paying the fare for the train you took here, but you will have to pay from this point on. Do you have any money left?”<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZGU">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E9%AC%BC%E3%81%A8%E4%BD%9B%E3%81%AE%E5%85%B1%E3%81%AB%E6%A3%B2%E3%82%80%E4%B8%96&amp;rft.btitle=%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%AC%E5%A9%A6%E4%BA%BA%E3%81%AE%E4%BD%BF%E5%91%BD%E3%81%A8%E5%85%B6%E3%81%AE%E4%BF%AE%E9%A4%8A&amp;rft.place=Tash%C5%8Dgoe%2C+Gifu%2C+Gifu&amp;rft.pages=427&amp;rft.pub=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E5%BF%A0%E8%AA%A0%E5%A9%A6%E5%BE%B7%E6%9C%83%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.date=1929-09-15&amp;rft.aulast=Katagiri&amp;rft.aufirst=Ry%C5%ABko&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1028899%2F1%2F223&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZGY"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZGc"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZGg"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-558" id="cite_note-558" data-mw-footnote-number="509"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZGk"><a href="#cite_ref-558" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZGo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZGs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-558" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3678" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZGw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFNakano1939" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Nakano, Hideto (25 August 1939).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZG0">九　<ruby id="mwZG4">鮒<rp id="mwZG8">(</rp><rt id="mwZHA">ふな</rt><rp id="mwZHE">)</rp></ruby></bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1720656/1/73" class="external text" id="mwZHI"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwZHM">黃色い虹</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi" title="Nihonbashi" id="mwZHQ">Nihonbashi</a>, Tokyo: Dōwa Shunjūsha. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZHU">&nbsp;</span>125.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E4%B9%9D%E3%80%80%3Cruby%3E%E9%AE%92%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%B5%E3%81%AA%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E&amp;rft.btitle=%E9%BB%83%E8%89%B2%E3%81%84%E8%99%B9&amp;rft.place=Nihonbashi%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=125&amp;rft.pub=D%C5%8Dwa+Shunj%C5%ABsha&amp;rft.date=1939-08-25&amp;rft.aulast=Nakano&amp;rft.aufirst=Hideto&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1720656%2F1%2F73&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZHY"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZHc"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZHg"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-559" id="cite_note-559" data-mw-footnote-number="510"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZHk"><a href="#cite_ref-559" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZHo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZHs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-559" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3684" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZHw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFHirayama1943" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Hirayama, Rokō (20 May 1943).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZH0">里けしき</bdi>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/1133534/1/72" class="external text" id="mwZH4"><bdi lang="ja" id="mwZH8">大石夫妻</bdi></a> (in Japanese). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanda,_Tokyo" title="Kanda, Tokyo" id="mwZIA">Kanda, Tokyo</a>: Ten'yū Shobō. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZIE">&nbsp;</span>133.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E9%87%8C%E3%81%91%E3%81%97%E3%81%8D&amp;rft.btitle=%E5%A4%A7%E7%9F%B3%E5%A4%AB%E5%A6%BB&amp;rft.place=Kanda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pages=133&amp;rft.pub=Ten%27y%C5%AB+Shob%C5%8D&amp;rft.date=1943-05-20&amp;rft.aulast=Hirayama&amp;rft.aufirst=Rok%C5%8D&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F1133534%2F1%2F72&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZII"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZIM"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZIQ"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-561" id="cite_note-561" data-mw-footnote-number="511"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZIU"><a href="#cite_ref-561" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZIY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZIc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-561" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3698" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZIg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFInnes2009" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammond_Innes" title="Hammond Innes" id="mwZIk">Innes, Ralph Hammond</a> (10 June 2009). "III. The darkness of the engine-room" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZIo">三　行手に魔の岩礁が……</bdi>. <i id="mwZIs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wreck_of_the_Mary_Deare" title="The Wreck of the Mary Deare" id="mwZIw">The Wreck of the Mary Deare</a></i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZI0">メリー・ディア号の遭難</bdi> (in Japanese). Translated by Takahashi, Yasukuni. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Setagaya" title="Setagaya" id="mwZI4">Setagaya</a>, Tokyo: Gutenberg21. <q id="mwZI8">I didn't know what to do. He seemed calm and in control of the situation, and yet I knew that he had gone physically beyond the limits of endurance—mentally, too, perhaps. "We've got to get clear of The Minkies," I told him. "Once we're clear of The Minkies we're all right." I let go of the wheel and started for the companion ladder. "I'm going to start the engines."<span class="cs1-kern-right" id="mwZJA"></span></q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZJE">私はどうしてよいか分からなかった。彼は平静で、状況を把握しているように思われはしたものの、私はすでに肉体的に忍耐の限界を越えており、たぶん精神的にもそうだったろう。<br id="mwZJI">「ミンキー礁を迂回しなけりゃだめだ。ミンキー礁さえかわしてしまえばもう大丈夫だ」<br id="mwZJM">私は舵輪を放し、昇降梯子の方へ行きかけた。「エンジンをかけてくる」</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=III.+The+darkness+of+the+engine-room+%E4%B8%89%E3%80%80%E8%A1%8C%E6%89%8B%E3%81%AB%E9%AD%94%E3%81%AE%E5%B2%A9%E7%A4%81%E3%81%8C%E2%80%A6%E2%80%A6&amp;rft.btitle=The+Wreck+of+the+Mary+Deare+%E3%83%A1%E3%83%AA%E3%83%BC%E3%83%BB%E3%83%87%E3%82%A3%E3%82%A2%E5%8F%B7%E3%81%AE%E9%81%AD%E9%9B%A3&amp;rft.place=Setagaya%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.pub=Gutenberg21&amp;rft.date=2009-06-10&amp;rft.aulast=Innes&amp;rft.aufirst=Ralph+Hammond&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZJQ"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZJU"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZJY"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-562" id="cite_note-562" data-mw-footnote-number="512"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZJc"><a href="#cite_ref-562" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZJg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZJk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-562" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3704" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZJo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFHirano2018" class="citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remi_Hirano" title="Remi Hirano" id="mwZJs">Hirano, Remi</a> (November 2018). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/11505457/1/1" class="external text" id="mwZJw">"ecojin interview REMI HIRANO"</a>. <i id="mwZJ0">ecojin</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZJ4">エコジン</bdi> (in Japanese). <b id="mwZJ8">67</b>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_the_Environment_(Japan)" title="Ministry of the Environment (Japan)" id="mwZKA">Ministry of the Environment</a>: 4.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=ecojin&amp;rft.atitle=ecojin+interview+REMI+HIRANO&amp;rft.volume=67&amp;rft.pages=4&amp;rft.date=2018-11&amp;rft.aulast=Hirano&amp;rft.aufirst=Remi&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.ndl.go.jp%2Fpid%2F11505457%2F1%2F1&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZKE"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZKI"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZKM"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-564" id="cite_note-564" data-mw-footnote-number="513"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZKQ"><a href="#cite_ref-564" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZKU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZKY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-564" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3713" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZKc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFAlexanderHara" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Alexander, Meg; Hara, Chieko. <i id="mwZKg">The Reluctant Bride</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZKk">予期せぬ求婚</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZKo">[</span><i id="mwZKs">An Unexpected Proposal</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZKw">]</span> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZK0">&nbsp;</span>1. HarperCollins Japan. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZK4">&nbsp;</span>100. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwZK8">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZLA">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-4-596-97144-9" title="Special:BookSources/978-4-596-97144-9" id="mwZLE"><bdi id="mwZLI">978-4-596-97144-9</bdi></a>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZLM">ミスター・ソールトンて とっても すてきな青年ねぇ もうっ レティシアったら もっと彼に愛想よくしなけりゃだめじゃない<br id="mwZLQ">どうして わたしが？<br id="mwZLU">彼は あのアイシャム卿の弟ですよ 結婚相手としては申し分ないでしょう？<br id="mwZLY">母様 わたしには オリヴァー・ウェルズって人がいるのよ<br id="mwZLc">あんな人 ただの地方のお金持ちってだけじゃないの</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZLg">[</span>Mr Salton is a very fine young man. You must be welcoming to him, Letitia.<br id="mwZLk">Why must I?<br id="mwZLo">He is Lord Isham’s younger brother. He would make a most suitable husband for you, no?<br id="mwZLs">But Mother! I’ve already got Oliver Wells!<br id="mwZLw">He is just some rich local, now isn’t he?<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZL0">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+Reluctant+Bride+%E4%BA%88%E6%9C%9F%E3%81%9B%E3%81%AC%E6%B1%82%E5%A9%9A&amp;rft.pages=100&amp;rft.pub=HarperCollins+Japan&amp;rft.isbn=978-4-596-97144-9&amp;rft.aulast=Alexander&amp;rft.aufirst=Meg&amp;rft.au=Hara%2C+Chieko&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZL4"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZL8"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZMA"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-566" id="cite_note-566" data-mw-footnote-number="514"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZME"><a href="#cite_ref-566" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZMI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZMM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-566" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3722" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZMQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFNeels" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betty_Neels" title="Betty Neels" id="mwZMU">Neels, Betty</a>. "Chapter One" <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZMY">１</bdi>. <i id="mwZMc">When Two Paths Meet</i> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZMg">大聖堂のある町</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZMk">[</span><i id="mwZMo">The Town with a Cathedral</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZMs">]</span> (in Japanese). Translated by Tsukada, Yumiko. HarperCollins Japan. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwZMw">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZM0">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-4-302-10429-1" title="Special:BookSources/978-4-302-10429-1" id="mwZM4"><bdi id="mwZM8">978-4-302-10429-1</bdi></a>. <q id="mwZNA"><span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwZNE"></span>'Really, Katherine, you must control the children! This is surely proof that you are quite unsuitable for any kind of responsible job. I can only hope that you will learn something from us while you are living here.'<span class="cs1-kern-right" id="mwZNI"></span></q> <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZNM">「キャサリン、子供たちをちゃんと監督しなきゃだめじゃないか！　おまえはまったく責任ある仕事に向いてないな。ここにいる間に、少しはそういうことも覚えたほうがいいと思うがね」</bdi></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Chapter+One+%EF%BC%91&amp;rft.btitle=When+Two+Paths+Meet+%E5%A4%A7%E8%81%96%E5%A0%82%E3%81%AE%E3%81%82%E3%82%8B%E7%94%BA&amp;rft.pub=HarperCollins+Japan&amp;rft.isbn=978-4-302-10429-1&amp;rft.aulast=Neels&amp;rft.aufirst=Betty&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZNQ"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZNU"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZNY"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-567" id="cite_note-567" data-mw-footnote-number="515"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZNc"><a href="#cite_ref-567" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZNg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZNk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-567" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3728" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZNo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFBai2014" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Bai, Yongchuan (28 March 2014).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZNs">三、母校の小使となる</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZNw">[</span>3, I Became a Janitor at My Alma Mater<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZN0">]</span>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZN4">報恩一途　白永傳回想録</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZN8">[</span><i id="mwZOA">All for Requital: A Memoir of Bai Yongchuan</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZOE">]</span> (in Japanese). I-Mei Multimedia e-Content Production &amp; Marketing Co., Ltd. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZOI">&nbsp;</span><span class="nowrap" id="mwZOM">20–</span>21.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZOQ">以上の外に校長宿舎の外庭掃除、風呂焚き、土曜、日曜午後、祭日は学校の周囲の生垣の剪定、樹木の整形等も小使の仕事、大人でも大変なことなのに十四、五の子供にはなかなか荷重な仕事だった。恩師の言葉を思い出し、辛いけれど克服せねばだめだ、どんなに働いても命をとられることはないといろいろ自分を励まし精一杯何でもよく工夫して成し遂げた。働けば働く程体はめきめき強くなって仕事をする楽しみまで覚えるようになった。</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZOU">[</span>Other than the above, as a janitor, I also cleaned the garden outside the principal’s accommodation, heated the baths, and on Saturday and Sunday afternoons and holidays, pruned the hedges around the school, shaped the trees and such, all of which would be hard enough for an adult, let alone a fourteen-, fifteen-year-old for whom it was a real burden. I remembered a former teacher’s words, psyched myself up in various ways, like telling myself that I had to overcome it even though it was tough, that it wouldn’t kill me no matter how much I worked, and I figured it out with all my might and pulled it off. My body got stronger and stronger the more I worked, and it got to the point where I came to enjoy working.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZOY">]</span></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E4%B8%89%E3%80%81%E6%AF%8D%E6%A0%A1%E3%81%AE%E5%B0%8F%E4%BD%BF%E3%81%A8%E3%81%AA%E3%82%8B&amp;rft.btitle=%E5%A0%B1%E6%81%A9%E4%B8%80%E9%80%94%E3%80%80%E7%99%BD%E6%B0%B8%E5%82%B3%E5%9B%9E%E6%83%B3%E9%8C%B2&amp;rft.pages=20-21&amp;rft.pub=I-Mei+Multimedia+e-Content+Production+%26+Marketing+Co.%2C+Ltd.&amp;rft.date=2014-03-28&amp;rft.aulast=Bai&amp;rft.aufirst=Yongchuan&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZOc"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZOg"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZOk"></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-568" id="cite_note-568" data-mw-footnote-number="516"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwZOo"><a href="#cite_ref-568" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwZOs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwZOw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-568" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3734" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwZO0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><cite id="CITEREFAmano2025" class="citation book cs1 cs1-prop-script cs1-prop-foreign-lang-source">Amano, Seiju (10 December 2025).  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZO4">第四十八章　『ひみつのレシピ』</bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZO8">[</span>Chapter 48: “Secret Recipe”<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZPA">]</span>.  <bdi lang="ja" id="mwZPE"><ruby id="mwZPI">十<rp id="mwZPM">(</rp><rt id="mwZPQ">じゅっ</rt><rp id="mwZPU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZPY">歳<rp id="mwZPc">(</rp><rt id="mwZPg">さい</rt><rp id="mwZPk">)</rp></ruby>の<ruby id="mwZPo">最<rp id="mwZPs">(</rp><rt id="mwZPw">さい</rt><rp id="mwZP0">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZP4">強<rp id="mwZP8">(</rp><rt id="mwZQA">きょう</rt><rp id="mwZQE">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZQI">魔<rp id="mwZQM">(</rp><rt id="mwZQQ">ま</rt><rp id="mwZQU">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZQY">導<rp id="mwZQc">(</rp><rt id="mwZQg">どう</rt><rp id="mwZQk">)</rp></ruby><ruby id="mwZQo">師<rp id="mwZQs">(</rp><rt id="mwZQw">し</rt><rp id="mwZQ0">)</rp></ruby></bdi> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZQ4">[</span><i id="mwZQ8">The Strongest 10-Year-Old Magician</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZRA">]</span>. <span title="Japanese-language text" id="mwZRE"><span lang="ja" id="mwZRI">ヒーロー文庫</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Japanese-language_text" id="mwZRM"> (in Japanese). Vol.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwZRQ">&nbsp;</span>11. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiyoda,_Tokyo" title="Chiyoda, Tokyo" id="mwZRU">Chiyoda, Tokyo</a>: Imagica Infos.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=%E7%AC%AC%E5%9B%9B%E5%8D%81%E5%85%AB%E7%AB%A0%E3%80%80%E3%80%8E%E3%81%B2%E3%81%BF%E3%81%A4%E3%81%AE%E3%83%AC%E3%82%B7%E3%83%94%E3%80%8F&amp;rft.btitle=%3Cruby%3E%E5%8D%81%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%98%E3%82%85%E3%81%A3%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E6%AD%B3%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%95%E3%81%84%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%E3%81%AE%3Cruby%3E%E6%9C%80%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%95%E3%81%84%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E5%BC%B7%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%8D%E3%82%87%E3%81%86%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E9%AD%94%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%BE%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E5%B0%8E%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%A9%E3%81%86%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E%3Cruby%3E%E5%B8%AB%3Crp%3E%28%3C%2Frp%3E%3Crt%3E%E3%81%97%3C%2Frt%3E%3Crp%3E%29%3C%2Frp%3E%3C%2Fruby%3E&amp;rft.place=Chiyoda%2C+Tokyo&amp;rft.series=%3Cspan+title%3D%22Japanese-language+text%22%3E%3Cspan+lang%3D%22ja%22%3E%E3%83%92%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AD%E3%83%BC%E6%96%87%E5%BA%AB%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fspan%3ECategory%3AArticles+containing+Japanese-language+text&amp;rft.pub=Imagica+Infos&amp;rft.date=2025-12-10&amp;rft.aulast=Amano&amp;rft.aufirst=Seiju&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AJapanese+conjugation" class="Z3988" id="mwZRY"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_uses_Japanese-language_script_(ja)" id="mwZRc"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_Japanese-language_sources_(ja)" id="mwZRg"></span></li>
